#: dialog/vcskeeve.msg:201 dialog/vcwalace.msg:140
msgid "Never mind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:172
msgid ""
"Oh gods -- may the spirit of the Founder guide you. If you're the Chosen One, we're\n"
" going to need it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:173
msgid "Uun Ga."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:174
msgid "Have a safe journey."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:175 dialog/acwarior.msg:175
msgid "????"
msgstr "????"

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:176
msgid "We're doomed! You have failed your quest."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:177
msgid "You cannot continue like this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:182
msgid "You are evil. The Chosen One is evil!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:183
msgid "They come to our village from the east, but their goods are poor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:300
msgid "Hello, Chosen One. Nice to see you again. I pray that your holy quest is going well. Is there something I can help you with?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:301
msgid "Chosen One, our people are dying. You must hurry your search for the holy GECK. What may I do to aid you in this most holy of quests?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:302
msgid "We are running out of time, Chosen One. Please, finish your holy quest soon. We cannot afford to wait much longer. If there's anything I can do to help you to save us, let me know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:303
msgid ""
"Chosen One, our village is almost dead... you're our only hope. Is there anything\n"
" I could tell you that would aide you in our salvation?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:400
msgid "Is there anything you could tell me about Kaga?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:401
msgid "[The villager stares at you, wide-eyed, then slowly steps away from you while glancing around nervously.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:402
msgid "Alright, I guess not."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:1107 dialog/acvillgr.msg:1108
msgid ""
"He heals us with his herbs and magic. He is in the northern part\n"
" of our village."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:1109 dialog/kchild.msg:1109 dialog/kcitizen.msg:1109
msgid ""
"It is a magic powder which will heal you, but will make you\n"
" sleepy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acvillgr.msg:1111 dialog/acwarior.msg:1111 dialog/kchild.msg:1111
#: dialog/kcitizen.msg:1111
msgid "He guards the bridge leading into our village."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:100
msgid "You see a tribesman."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:101
msgid "You see a tribeswoman."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:150
msgid ""
"Before you stands a large warrior of your village, wearing\n"
" pants fashioned from animal hides."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:152
msgid "Hello, Chosen One, can I help you in your quest?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:153
msgid "I'm just looking around the village one last time before I leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:155
msgid "Could you tell me where I can find more healing powder?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:156
msgid "Gods give you speed to bring back Eden before it is too late."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:159
msgid ""
"Oh, you're testing me. Go see Hakunin in the northern corner of the village. He makes our\n"
" medicines."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:161
msgid ""
"Well, I've seen them when Mynoc has us guard the bridge, but he does all the dealing.\n"
" Talk to him at the Great Bridge."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:163
msgid "Could tell me where the Great Bridge is located?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:165
msgid ""
"Chosen One? The Great Bridge is at the southern end of the village. You know,\n"
" you've been there many times."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:172
msgid ""
"Ah, dull one. They say you are the Chosen One. I must say the spirit\n"
" of the Founder works in strange ways."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:173
msgid "Oon Ga."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:174
msgid " Have a safe journey, dull one -- for our sake."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:176
msgid "You betray us. You must die."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:177
msgid "A traitor to your own people!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:179
msgid "Death to the evil one!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:180
msgid ""
"They are nothing to us! They scavenge the dying corpse\n"
" of the wastes to live."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:300
msgid "Hello again, Chosen One. May the warrior spirits protect and guide you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:301
msgid "Are you having difficulties, Chosen One? You must not fail us - please hurry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:302
msgid "Why do you wait so long? We must have the GECK soon. Chosen One, our village is dying."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:303
msgid "Chosen One, our village is almost dead. Why have you not brought the holy GECK to us yet?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:970 dialog/template.msg:970
msgid "That is my name."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:971 dialog/template.msg:971
msgid "You are talking to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:972
msgid "What a silly question. That's me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:980 dialog/ahmonk.msg:404 dialog/gcharold.msg:293
#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:321 dialog/template.msg:980 dialog/vclynett.msg:823
msgid "I don't know anything about that."
msgstr "Jag vet ingenting om det."

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:981
msgid "Sorry. No clue."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:982 dialog/template.msg:982
msgid "Never heard of it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:1107 dialog/acwarior.msg:1108
msgid ""
"He heals us with his herbs and magic. He is in the northern\n"
" part of our village."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/acwarior.msg:1109
msgid ""
"It is a magic powder which will heal you, but will make\n"
" you sleepy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:100
msgid "You see the Elder of your village."
msgstr "Du ser din bys Äldste."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:101
msgid "It is the Elder."
msgstr "Det är den Äldste."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:102
msgid ""
"The Elder is just that - old, older than you can remember. Still, she has the\n"
" strength and fire to lead the village through these hard times."
msgstr ""
"Den Äldste är just det - gammal, äldre än du kan minnas. Ändå har hon\n"
" styrkan och glöden som krävs för att leda byn genom dessa svåra tider."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:103
msgctxt "aeld1"
msgid ""
"Congratulations, Chosen One, you have survived the Temple of Trials. Are\n"
" you ready for your quest?"
msgstr ""
"Gratulerar, Utvalde, du har överlevt Prövningarnas Tempel. Är\n"
" du redo för ditt uppdrag?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:104
msgid "What were you doing - trying to get me killed in the temple?"
msgstr "Vad höll du på med? Försökte du få mig dödad i templet?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:105 dialog/dcvic.msg:2505 dialog/hcfrank.msg:129
#: dialog/tribec1.msg:470 dialog/vclynett.msg:828
msgid "Of course."
msgstr "Självklart."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:106
msgid "I'd like to think about it some more."
msgstr "Jag skulle vilja tänka på det lite mer."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:107
msgctxt "aeld2a"
msgid ""
"I am proud of you, Chosen. You have overcome much. Now. You must go find Vault\n"
" 13. Vault 13. Bring the GECK home. GECK. Here is a shiny bottle. Vic gave us this. Vic.\n"
" He is a trader in Klamath. Klamath. Go to Vic. Find Vault 13. Find GECK. Come home. Do\n"
" your best, child."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:112
msgctxt "aeld2b"
msgid "You not find vault. Find vault! Vault 13."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:113 dialog/ahhakun.msg:225 dialog/dcderek.msg:306
#: dialog/dcfred.msg:363 dialog/dcfred.msg:373 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:328
#: dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:273 dialog/hcseymor.msg:158 dialog/kcsulik.msg:231
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:751 dialog/kcsulik.msg:792
msgid "Uh."
msgstr "Eh."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:114
msgctxt "aeld3"
msgid "Chosen One, do you wish us all dead? You must find the Vault!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:115
msgid "I'm sorry, Elder. I will not fail."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:116
msgid "Yeah, yeah. Stop yelling."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:117
msgctxt "aeld4"
msgid "Chosen One, why are you here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:118
msgid "I know where Vault 13 is!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:119
msgid "I am ready for the holy quest."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:120 dialog/ahelder.msg:125
msgid "I need some more info."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:121 dialog/ahelder.msg:130
msgid "I'm not going to get myself killed!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:122
msgid "What was I supposed to do again?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:123
msgid "I'm going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:124
msgctxt "aeld5"
msgid ""
"That is good news, but not enough to save us. You must come back soon with the\n"
" GECK or our people will die!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:126
msgid "Fine, I'm going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:127
msgctxt "aeld6"
msgid ""
"You survived. The Chosen One cannot be weak or we are all doomed. Are you\n"
" prepared for your quest?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:128
msgid "I've passed the test. Of course, I'm ready."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:129 dialog/bcrebecc.msg:136
msgid "I need to think about this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:131
msgctxt "aeld7"
msgid ""
"Pay attention. Find the holy Vault 13 and bring back the GECK. Vic, the trader\n"
" from Klamath, brought us the flask from the holy Thirteen. Start your search with him.\n"
" The disk will remind you of your task. May the gods of the Vault watch over you."
msgstr ""
"Lyssna noga. Hitta det heliga Valv 13 och ta tillbaka GECK. Vic, handlaren\n"
" från Klamath, gav oss flaskan från det heliga Tretton. Börja din sökning hos honom.\n"
" Disken kommer att påminna dig om din uppgift. Må Valvets gudar vaka över dig."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:133
msgid "Before I go, I have some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:134
msgid "Goodbye. I will not fail the tribe."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:135
msgctxt "aeld8"
msgid "Very well. See me when you decide - but do not wait too long."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:137
msgctxt "aeld9"
msgid "I cannot help much. So much has been lost from the Long Ago. What wisdom do you seek?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:138
msgctxt "aeld9b"
msgid "What do you need?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:139
msgid "Tell me more about the GECK."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:140
msgid "How do I get to Klamath?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:141
msgid "Where is Vault 13?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:142
msgid "On second thought, I don't need any help now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:143
msgctxt "aeld10"
msgid ""
"It is a holy artifact - the Garden of Eden Creation Kit. The disks promise it\n"
" will make our lands green and our village prosperous. It will save us. More, I do not know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:144
msgid "There's more I want to know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:146
msgctxt "aeld11"
msgid "Klamath is to the east."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:147
msgid "There are other things I would learn."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:148
msgid "I am ready. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:149
msgctxt "aeld12"
msgid ""
"The holy Thirteen? I cannot help you. Only the Vault Dweller knew. His tales have\n"
" the sound of a perilous journey. "
msgstr ""
"Det heliga Tretton? Jag kan inte hjälpa dig. Bara Valvinvånaren visste. Hans berättelser har\n"
" toner av en farofylld resa."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:150
msgid "I see. There is much I need to know."
msgstr "Jag förstår. Det är mycket jag behöver veta."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:151
msgid "Goodbye, Elder."
msgstr "Adjö, Äldste."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:152
msgctxt "aeld13"
msgid ""
"Being a coward will kill us all! Including you. You passed\n"
" the Temple Trials. We have faith in you. We need you."
msgstr ""
"Att vara en fegis kommer att döda oss alla! Inklusive dig. Du klarade\n"
" tempelutmaningarna. Vi har förtroende för dig. Vi behöver dig."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:153
msgid "Not so fast, old woman. I need time to think about this!"
msgstr "Inte så fort, gamla tant. Jag behöver tid att tänka på det här!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:154
msgid "As you wish, Elder."
msgstr "Som du vill, Äldste."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:155
msgctxt "aeld14a"
msgid "You've betrayed us. You will perish."
msgstr "Du har förrått oss. Du kommer att förgås."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:156
msgctxt "aeld14b"
msgid "You are a traitor!"
msgstr "Du är en förrädare!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:157
msgctxt "aeld14c"
msgid "Why do you do this?"
msgstr "Varför gör du så här?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:158
msgctxt "aeld14d"
msgid "I knew you had the soul of darkness!"
msgstr "Jag visste att du hade mörkrets själ!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:159
msgctxt "aeld15"
msgid ""
"Then take this flask. It is from the holy Vault 13. Vic, a trader in Klamath,\n"
" brought it to us. He may know where the vault is. You may also need some of what they\n"
" call money. Here."
msgstr ""
"Ta då den här flaskan. Den är från det heliga Valv 13. Vic, en handlare i Klamath,\n"
" tog den till oss. Han kanske vet var valvet är. Du kan också behöva lite av vad de\n"
" kallar pengar. Här."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:160
msgid "Uh... What was my quest again?"
msgstr "Eh... Vad var mitt uppdrag nu igen?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:161
msgid "Is there more you can tell me?"
msgstr "Finns det något mer du kan berätta för mig?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:162
msgid "Wish me luck, Elder, and I will not fail you."
msgstr "Önska mig lycka till, Äldste, och jag ska inte svika dig."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:163
msgctxt "aeld16"
msgid "Find Vic in Klamath. We are counting on you."
msgstr "Hitta Vic i Klamath. Vi räknar med dig."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:164
msgctxt "aeld17"
msgid ""
"It's good to see you again, Child. I don't mean to be abrupt but I see you\n"
" haven't completed your quest to find the holy Thirteen. Please, let's not waste time\n"
" talking. The need of our people is great. Go find the Vault!"
msgstr ""
"Det är skönt att se dig igen, mitt barn. Jag menar inte att vara abrupt men jag ser att du\n"
" inte har slutfört ditt uppdrag att hitta det heliga Tretton. Snälla, låt oss inte slösa tid\n"
" med att prata. Vårt folks behov är stort. Gå och hitta Valvet!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:165 dialog/bcdalia.msg:108 dialog/bcjones.msg:129
#: dialog/ccquincy.msg:113 dialog/fcfmatt.msg:114 dialog/ocariel.msg:106
#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:119 dialog/ocgoris.msg:187 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:128
#: dialog/ocjul.msg:114 dialog/ocjul.msg:120 dialog/ockerith.msg:109
#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:111 dialog/ocmatt.msg:150 dialog/octhearn.msg:108
#: dialog/scdocjub.msg:120 dialog/scmira.msg:195 dialog/shtandi.msg:306
msgid "Me go now."
msgstr "Jag gå nu."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:166 dialog/ccgguard.msg:143 dialog/vcstark.msg:129
msgid "All right, I'm going."
msgstr "Okej, jag går nu."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:167
msgid "I will not fail you elder."
msgstr "Jag kommer inte att svika dig, äldste."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:168
msgid "I'm working on it, Ok?"
msgstr "Jag jobbar på det, Ok?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:169
msgctxt "aeld18"
msgid ""
"Once again you return without the GECK. Our crops begin to fail us, Chosen. Our\n"
" need becomes greater with the passage of time. Go find the holy Thirteen!"
msgstr ""
"Ännu en gång återvänder du utan GECK. Våra grödor börjar svika oss, Utvalde. Vårt\n"
" behov blir större med tidens gång. Gå och hitta det heliga Tretton!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:170
msgid "Ok, me go now."
msgstr "Okej, jag gå nu."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:171
msgid "Yes, Elder."
msgstr "Ja, Äldste."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:172
msgid "I will not fail you or our people, Elder."
msgstr "Jag kommer inte att svika dig eller vårt folk, Äldste."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:173
msgid "Look. If you think you can do better... "
msgstr "Hörru. Om du tror att du kan göra det bättre... "

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:174
msgctxt "aeld19"
msgid ""
"Chosen One, things are not well here. We need the GECK if our village is to\n"
" survive. Our people grow weak with hunger and our food reserves will not last much\n"
" longer. Please, find the holy Thirteen and return to us. Go now."
msgstr ""
"Utvalde, saker och ting är inte bra här. Vi behöver GECK om vår by ska kunna\n"
" överleva. Vårt folk blir svaga av hunger och våra matreserver räcker inte mycket\n"
" längre. Snälla, hitta det heliga Tretton och återvänd till oss. Gå nu."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:176
msgid "Very well. I'm on my way."
msgstr "Javisst. Jag är på väg."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:177
msgid "I will do my best to find the GECK and save our village."
msgstr "Jag ska göra mitt bästa för att hitta GECK och rädda vår by."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:178
msgid "Don't push me, old woman. I'm doing my best."
msgstr "Pressa mig inte, gamla tant. Jag gör mitt bästa."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:179
msgctxt "aeld20"
msgid ""
"Child, our need is greater than ever before. Our people sicken, the brahmin\n"
" are dying, and our food is all but gone. The blight of the land can only be cured with\n"
" the GECK. Go, find the GECK and save our people."
msgstr ""
"Mitt barn, vårt behov är större än någonsin tidigare. Vårt folk är sjukt, brahminerna\n"
" är döende, och vår mat är nästan slut. Landets fördärv kan bara botas med\n"
" GECK. Gå, hitta GECK och rädda vårt folk."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:181 dialog/scmerk.msg:262 dialog/vcconnar.msg:153
msgid "I'm on my way."
msgstr "Jag är på väg."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:182
msgid "Forgive me Elder. I will find the GECK without delay."
msgstr "Förlåt mig, Äldste. Jag ska hitta GECK utan dröjsmål."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:183
msgid "Yeah, yeah. You're beginning to sound like a broken disk..."
msgstr "Ja, ja. Du börjar låta som en trasig disk..."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:200
msgctxt "eeld1"
msgid "Chosen One! How did you get here?"
msgstr "Utvalde! Hur kom du hit?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:201
msgid "Uhh... duh?"
msgstr "Ehh... öh?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:202 dialog/tribec7.msg:219
msgid "I've come to rescue you."
msgstr "Jag har kommit för att rädda dig."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:203
msgid "What the hell's going on here?"
msgstr "Vad i helvete är på gång här?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:204
msgctxt "eeld2"
msgid "You monster! Have you come to kill me, too?"
msgstr "Ditt monster! Har du kommit för att döda mig också?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:205
msgid "Uhhh?"
msgstr "Ehhh?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:206
msgid "No, it's me, the Chosen One!"
msgstr "Nej, det är jag, den Utvalde!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:207
msgid "Oh, shut up, you old bitch! It's me, your Chosen One."
msgstr "Håll käften, din gamla kärring! Det är jag, din Utvalde."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:208
msgctxt "eeld3"
msgid "Oh, gods... Listen - go down. Find machine that makes power. Kill machine. Kill bad men. Kill everybody! You kill, we go home. Also, if you not have GECK then look for GECK here. Must have GECK to save village! Freedom is nothing without home to return to. Understand? Oh, gods."
msgstr "Åh, gudar... Lyssna - gå ner. Hitta maskin som gör ström. Döda maskinen. Döda onda män. Döda allihop! Du dödar, vi går hem. Och om inte du ha GECK, leta efter GECK här. Måste ha GECK för att rädda by! Frihet är ingenting utan hem att återvända till. Förstått? Åh, gudar."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:209
msgid "Uh -huh!"
msgstr "A-ha!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:210
msgctxt "eeld4"
msgid "Careful, do not touch the glow wall. I think the machine that feeds it is beneath us. Destroy it so we may escape. How did you get here?"
msgstr "Försiktigt, rör inte glödväggen. Jag tror att maskinen som matar den är under oss. Förstör den så att vi kan fly. Hur kom du hit?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:211
msgid "I have a ship. "
msgstr "Jag har ett skepp. "

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:212
msgctxt "eeld5"
msgid "Men came to our village in flying machines and took us. There were others, too - from the holy Thirteen! I thought we were saved. I thought we were going to heaven. (sigh)"
msgstr "Män kom till vår by i flygande maskiner och tog oss. Det var andra också - från det heliga Tretton! Jag trodde att vi var räddade. Jag trodde att vi skulle komma till himlen. (suck)"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:213 dialog/ahhakun.msg:289
msgid "And then?"
msgstr "Och sedan?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:214
msgctxt "eeld5a"
msgid ""
"Then they brought us here, to hell. They have killed most of us with something they call effeevee. They will kill us all before they are through!\n"
" Do you know what must be done, Chosen One?"
msgstr ""
"Sen förde de oss hit, till helvetet. De har dödat de flesta av oss med något de kallar effeevee. De kommer att döda oss alla innan de är klara!\n"
" Vet du vad som måste göras, Utvalde?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:215
msgid "Effeevee?"
msgstr "Effeevee?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:218
msgctxt "eeld6"
msgid "If you destroy the machine, we will find the ship. Hurry, there are not many of us left. "
msgstr "Om du förstör maskinen, hittar vi skeppet. Skynda er, vi är inte många kvar. "

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:219 dialog/ahhakun.msg:249 dialog/kcardin.msg:272
#: dialog/nclabish.msg:736 dialog/tribec4.msg:231
msgid "What happened?"
msgstr "Vad hände?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:221
msgctxt "eeld7"
msgid "You must destroy the machine and kill the devils in this place. We will meet you outside! And Chosen One, if you have not found the GECK, seek it here. Our freedom is nothing if we cannot save our village. Now go!"
msgstr "Du måste förstöra maskinen och döda djävlarna på denna plats. Vi möter dig utanför! Och Utvalde, om du inte har hittat GECK, sök den här. Vår frihet är ingenting om vi inte kan rädda vår by. Gå nu!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:223
msgctxt "eeld8"
msgid "I am still the Elder. Remember your place! Apologize or I will not help you anymore."
msgstr "Jag är fortfarande den Äldste. Minns din plats! Be om ursäkt, annars hjälper jag dig inte mer."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:224
msgid "Sorry, you're not an old bitch. What's going on?"
msgstr "Ledsen, du är inte en gammal kärring. Vad är det som händer?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:225
msgid "Like you could help me in there? Fuck off and die."
msgstr "Som om du kunde hjälpa mig där inne? Dra åt helvete och dö."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:226
msgctxt "eeld9"
msgid "Go away. You are no better than these devils. I weep you were named the Chosen One."
msgstr "Gå härifrån. Du är inte bättre än de här djävlarna. Jag gråter över att du utsågs till den Utvalde."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:227
msgctxt "eeld10"
msgid "Why are you here? Every minute you waste another of our people could be killed. And don't forget the GECK! We must have it."
msgstr "Varför är du här? Varje minut du slösar kan leda till att någon annan av oss dödas. Och glöm inte GECK! Vi måste ha den."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:228
msgid "Nuh??"
msgstr "Nä??"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:229
msgid "Where was I supposed to go?"
msgstr "Var skulle jag gå?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:230
msgid "Just wanted to annoy you. I'm on it. Don't worry."
msgstr "Jag ville bara reta dig. Jag jobbar på det. Oroa dig inte."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:231
msgctxt "eeld11"
msgid "(sigh) Go below. Kill. Smash machines. Go now!"
msgstr "(suck) Gå ner. Döda. Krossa maskiner. Gå nu!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:232
msgctxt "eeld12"
msgid "Listen this time! Go to the levels below us. Find the machine that makes power. Stop it and we can escape. The men here are not true to the Vault dream. They are evil. Also, if you have not yet found the GECK, seek it here. Our freedom is nothing if our village cannot be saved. Now go!"
msgstr "Lyssna den här gången! Gå till våningarna under oss. Hitta maskinen som gör ström. Stoppa den så kan vi fly. Männen här är inte trogna till Valv-drömmen. De är onda. Och om du ännu inte har hittat GECK, sök den här. Vår frihet är ingenting om vår by inte kan räddas. Gå nu!"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:233 dialog/bcrebecc.msg:160 dialog/ccatech.msg:143
#: dialog/cccook.msg:141 dialog/ccdoctor.msg:124 dialog/ccncomp.msg:133
#: dialog/cctech1.msg:143 dialog/cctech2.msg:145 dialog/hcbnkgrd.msg:117
#: dialog/ncmyrgrd.msg:426 dialog/ocdar.msg:119 dialog/ocdar.msg:133
#: dialog/octhearn.msg:118 dialog/ocvaldis.msg:118
msgid "Got it."
msgstr "Jag förstår."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:234
msgctxt "eeld13"
msgid "That is what they call it. They stick needles into our skin, like stimpaks, but then terrible things happen. Then... (chokes up)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:235 dialog/gcbrain.msg:381 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:139
#: dialog/rcjane.msg:174
msgid "Then what?"
msgstr "Sen då?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:236
msgid "This is going to make me sick, isn't it?"
msgstr "Det här kommer att få mig att må illa, eller hur?"

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:237
msgctxt "eeld13a"
msgid "Then the skin bubbles like maggots beneath it. Boils grow and burst. Blood runs from your ears and your tongue swells. Those who are lucky choke to death. Those who are not..."
msgstr "Sedan bubblar huden som om det vore likmaskar under den. Bölder växer och spricker. Blodet rinner ur öronen och tungan sväller. De som har tur kvävs till döds. De som inte har det..."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:238
msgid "They'll pay."
msgstr "De kommer att få betala för det här."

#: dialog/ahelder.msg:239
msgid "That certainly was disgusting. What am I supposed to do?"
msgstr "Det var verkligen äckligt. Vad ska jag göra?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:100
msgid "Before you stands Hakunin, the village shaman. He appraises you with his crazy eyes from somewhere in the world only he inhabits...."
msgstr "Framför dig står Hakunin, byns shaman. Han betraktar dig med sina galna ögon från någonstans i den värld som bara han lever i....."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:101
msgid "You see Hakunin lying on the ground. He's badly wounded."
msgstr "Du ser Hakunin ligga på marken. Han är svårt skadad."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:102
msgid "You see Hakunin. He's very near death."
msgstr "Du ser Hakunin. Han är mycket nära döden."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:103
msgid "Hakunin is badly burned. He smells like roast chicken, looks like burnt meatloaf, and you don't know how he's managed to stay alive this long."
msgstr "Hakunin är svårt brännskadad. Han luktar grillad kyckling, ser ut som bränd köttfärslimpa och du förstår inte hur han har lyckats hålla sig vid liv så här länge."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:104
msgctxt "hak001"
msgid "Greetings, Chosen. Why does the earth before me warm to the touch of your passing?"
msgstr "Var hälsad, Utvalde. Varför värms jorden framför mig vid beröringen av din passage?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:105 dialog/ahhakun.msg:112
msgid "Uh? "
msgstr "Eh? "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:106 dialog/ahhakun.msg:113
msgid "I've come to say goodbye. I'm leaving on my holy quest. "
msgstr "Jag har kommit för att säga adjö. Jag ger mig av på mitt heliga uppdrag. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:107 dialog/ahhakun.msg:114
msgid "I'm heading out. I was hoping just this once you'd talk like a real person. "
msgstr "Jag är på väg ut. Jag hoppades att du för en gångs skull kunde prata som en riktig person. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:108 dialog/ahhakun.msg:115
msgid "You are doing just way too many drugs. I'm outta here. "
msgstr "Du tar alldeles för många droger. Jag sticker härifrån. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:109 dialog/ahhakun.msg:178
msgid "I'm hurt. Can you heal me?"
msgstr "Jag är skadad. Kan du läka mig?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:110 dialog/ahhakun.msg:116
msgid "There were some pretty nasty plants infesting your garden- I've taken care of them for you."
msgstr "Det fanns några ganska otäcka växter i din trädgård- jag har tagit hand om dem åt dig."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:111
msgctxt "hak001a"
msgid "Please reveal to clouded eyes the purpose of your passage."
msgstr "Vänligen avslöja för grumlade ögon syftet med din passage."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:117
msgctxt "hak002"
msgid "The Earth sings with the news of a champion upon the land.... Perhaps, before you go, you would bestow a kindness?"
msgstr "Jorden sjunger med nyheten om en ärad kämpe i vårt land.... Kanske, innan du går, kan du skänka en vänlighet?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:118 dialog/epac17.msg:801 dialog/tribec1.msg:532
#: dialog/tribec8.msg:301 dialog/tribec8.msg:319
msgid "Sure. What do you need?"
msgstr "Visst. Vad behöver du?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:119
msgid "It depends... what'll you give me?"
msgstr "Det beror på... Vad tänker du ge mig?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:120
msgctxt "hak002a"
msgid "The views of the world are many - a lesson you will learn soon.... Perhaps, before you reap the experiences of life, you would bestow a kindness?"
msgstr "Världens vyer är många - en lektion du snart kommer att lära dig.... Kanske, innan du skördar livets erfarenheter, skulle du skänka en vänlighet?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:121
msgid "Did you just ask me to do you a favor? If so, sure, why not?"
msgstr "Bad du mig just att göra dig en tjänst? Om så är fallet, varför inte?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:122
msgid "I'll do something for you, but since I have to work this hard just to understand you, this task will cost."
msgstr "Jag ska göra något för dig, men eftersom jag måste arbeta så här hårt bara för att förstå dig, kommer den här uppgiften att kosta."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:123
msgctxt "hak003"
msgid "A blessing on you, for you are truly a child of nature. Would you please use your special talents and rid my garden of the plants of dark soul?"
msgstr "En välsignelse över dig, för du är verkligen ett naturens barn. Kan du vara snäll och använda dina speciella talanger och befria min trädgård från den mörka själens växter?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:124
msgid "Uh-huh. "
msgstr "Aha. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:125
msgid "Nuh-uh. Youuu. Giv. Hed hurt."
msgstr "Näe. Duuu. Ge me. Huve ont."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:126
msgctxt "hak004"
msgid "May your aura grace my presence when you are... Oh, come to my door when you're done and I'll give you something good."
msgstr "Må din aura pryda min närvaro när du är... Åh, kom till min dörr när du är klar så ska jag ge dig något välgörande."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:127 dialog/fcdrwong.msg:541
msgid "Urgh."
msgstr "Urgh."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:128
msgctxt "hak005"
msgid "The plants of dark soul have infested my garden again. Many seasons have touched my bones and I am too frail for that fight which is eternal in nature. I ask that you be my champion."
msgstr "Den mörka själens växter har angripit min trädgård igen. Många årstider har berört mina ben och jag är för bräcklig för den kamp som är evig till sin natur. Jag ber att du ska vara min ärekämpe."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:129
msgid "I don't think so. I need to start my quest right away."
msgstr "Jag tror inte det. Jag måste påbörja mitt uppdrag direkt."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:130
msgid "I know you're not a bad guy, but I've got a headache already, so I think I'll have to pass."
msgstr "Jag vet att du inte är en ond snubbe, men jag har redan huvudvärk, så jag tror att jag måste avstå."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:131
msgid "Forget it. I'm the future leader of this tribe and it would be undignified for me to do your gardening for you."
msgstr "Glöm det. Jag är den framtida ledaren för denna stam och det skulle vara ovärdigt för mig att göra ditt trädgårdsarbete åt dig."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:132
msgid "I'd be honored, holy one."
msgstr "Det vore en ära, o helige."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:133
msgid "Did you just ask me to weed your garden? If that's the case, okay."
msgstr "Bad du mig just att rensa ogräs i din trädgård? Om så är fallet, okej."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:134
msgid "For a price."
msgstr "För ett pris."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:135
msgctxt "hak006"
msgid "To ask payment for a gift will bring you less than the gift itself. I will give you such and add the lesson of your self-disappointment at the receiving."
msgstr "Att begära betalning för en gåva kommer att ge dig mindre än gåvan själv. Jag ska ge dig en sådan och lägga till lärdomen om din självbesvikelse vid mottagandet."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:136
msgid "Good enough. Where's the garden?"
msgstr "Det räcker gott och väl. Var är trädgården?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:137
msgid "You know, a nice gift would be to SPEAK ENGLISH!"
msgstr "Du vet, en trevlig present skulle vara att PRATA SVENSKA!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:138
msgid "What if I give you a lesson in disappointment and leave right now? Bye."
msgstr "Vad sägs om att jag ger dig en lektion i besvikelse och går nu? Hej då."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:139
msgid "Well, if that's your attitude, I don't think I'm interested. Goodbye."
msgstr "Om det är din inställning är jag nog inte intresserad. Hejdå."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:140
msgctxt "hak006a"
msgid "If we speak the same words, do we mean the same thing? Do words always carry the same touch of a soul?"
msgstr "Om vi säger samma ord, menar vi då samma sak? För ord alltid samma beröring till en själ?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:141
msgid "Oh, yeah. Much better. And the lesson I learned is to shut up and just ask where the garden is."
msgstr "Just ja. Mycket bättre. Och läxan jag lärde mig är att hålla tyst och bara fråga var trädgården är."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:142
msgid "Let's try the word, \"goodbye.\" It means I'm leaving. "
msgstr "Låt oss prova orden \"hej då\", som betyder att jag tänker gå. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:143
msgctxt "hak007"
msgid "Surely you remember it is to the northeast, foolish one."
msgstr "Du minns ju att det är åt nordost, din dåre."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:144 dialog/dclara.msg:531 dialog/vcmelind.msg:125
#: dialog/vcmelind.msg:132
msgid "Thank you for your help."
msgstr "Tack för din hjälp."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:145
msgid "Thanks. I actually understood that."
msgstr "Tack. Jag förstod faktiskt det där."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:146
msgid "Are you calling me a fool? I don't think I want to help you, after all. "
msgstr "Kallar du mig en dåre? Jag tror inte att jag vill hjälpa dig, trots allt. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:147
msgid "I'll be back for my payment soon."
msgstr "Jag kommer tillbaka för min betalning snart."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:148
msgctxt "hak008"
msgid "The burden you carry now will grow ever heavier."
msgstr "Den börda du bär nu kommer att bli allt tyngre."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:149
msgctxt "hak009"
msgid "May the gods bless your efforts, Chosen. May your aura grace my presence when the earth breathes clean again."
msgstr "Må gudarna välsigna dina ansträngningar, Utvalde. Må din aura pryda min närvaro när jorden andas rent igen."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:150
msgid "I take it you want to see me again when I'm done... You could have just said so, you know."
msgstr "Jag antar att du vill träffa mig igen när jag är klar... Du kunde bara ha sagt det, vet du."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:152
msgctxt "hak010"
msgid "Ha! The founder's spirit lives in you. Focus in to fortify the self to expand the greatness to enable such to touch the world. Of course, the rewards will be more than those of the spirit. "
msgstr "Ha! Grundarens anda lever i dig. Fokusera på att stärka dig själv för att utöka din storhet och göra det möjligt för dig att beröra världen. Naturligtvis kommer belöningarna att vara mer än andens. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:153
msgid "Sounds good. I'll be back when I'm done."
msgstr "Det låter bra. Jag kommer tillbaka när jag är klar."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:154
msgid "So, I'm getting an actual thing in payment. Good enough. See ya later."
msgstr "Så jag får en riktig sak i betalning. Det låter bra. Syns senare."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:155
msgid "I think you've been playing with those plants way too much. To avoid your fate, I'm staying away from the garden."
msgstr "Jag tror att du har lekt med växterna alldeles för mycket. För att undvika ditt öde håller jag mig borta från trädgården."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:156
msgctxt "hak011"
msgid "Time can neither be wasted or saved- it must always be now. The actions create the fabric of your life."
msgstr "Tid kan varken slösas bort eller sparas - den måste alltid vara nu. Det är handlingarna som väver ditt livs tyg."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:157
msgid "Uh, right. Like I said, I've got to go. Goodbye. "
msgstr "Ja, just det. Som jag sa, jag måste gå. Hej då."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:158
msgid "You know, talking to you makes me wonder about that time can't be wasted idea. I'm outta here. "
msgstr "Att prata med dig får mig att fundera på idén om att tid inte kan slösas bort. Jag sticker härifrån. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:159
msgid "If only I had your wisdom, wise one. Forgive me- of course I'll take care of it for you."
msgstr "Om jag bara hade din visdom, du vise. Förlåt mig - naturligtvis ska jag ta hand om det åt dig."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:160
msgctxt "hak012"
msgid "You may bear the mantle of the Chosen, but your dark soul cries from within."
msgstr "Du må bära den Utvaldes mantel, men din mörka själ skriker inifrån."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:161
msgid "I beg your forgiveness, holy one. How can I cleanse my soul? "
msgstr "Jag ber om din förlåtelse, du helige. Hur kan jag rena min själ? "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:162
msgid "That's right, Hakunin, and you'd be a real wise man not to forget it."
msgstr "Det stämmer, Hakunin, och du skulle vara en riktigt klok man om du inte glömde det."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:163
msgid "My head aches from within listening to you. I'm gone."
msgstr "Mitt huvud värker inifrån när jag lyssnar på dig. Jag är borta."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:164
msgid "Booka!"
msgstr "Booka!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:165
msgctxt "hak013"
msgid "Cleanse your soul as you would banish demons from my garden."
msgstr "Rena din själ som du skulle fördriva demoner från min trädgård."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:166
msgid "It shall be done, wise one. I will come seek your forgiveness after I have purified your garden."
msgstr "Det ska ske, du vise. Jag kommer och söker din förlåtelse efter att jag har renat din trädgård."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:167
msgid "You're trying to say that weeding your garden will be good for me, right? Well, okay, I'll give it a try."
msgstr "Du försöker säga att det är bra för mig att rensa ogräs i din trädgård, eller hur? Okej, jag ska ge det ett försök."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:168
msgid "I kinda like my soul the way it is. Bye."
msgstr "Jag gillar faktiskt min själ som den är. Hej då."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:169
msgid "I'm not worthy. I'll take my leave now."
msgstr "Jag är inte värdig. Jag ska ta min avsked nu."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:170
msgctxt "hak014"
msgid "Chosen, once again the wholeness of your being is like a land blessed."
msgstr "Utvalde, än en gång är helheten av din varelse som ett välsignat land."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:171 dialog/ahhakun.msg:181 dialog/ahhakun.msg:184
#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:211 dialog/ahmonk.msg:422 dialog/ahmonk.msg:702
#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:202 dialog/dcchcgrd.msg:166 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:512
#: dialog/ecfarmer.msg:104 dialog/echomest.msg:104 dialog/generic.msg:200
#: dialog/kcbhcust.msg:208 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:141 dialog/tribec6.msg:132
#: dialog/vclynett.msg:811 dialog/vcvltgrd.msg:131 dialog/vicencom.msg:139
#: dialog/vicencom.msg:165 dialog/vicencom.msg:251
msgid "Thank you."
msgstr "Tack."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:172
msgid "You mean I'm better, right?"
msgstr "Du menar att jag mår bättre, eller hur?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:173
msgctxt "hak015"
msgid "To make one whole instills a sense of fullness that you would be well to understand, Chosen."
msgstr "Att göra en människa hel ger en uppfyllande känsla som du skulle må bra av att förstå, Utvalde."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:174
msgid "Wait, don't tell me. I'm better and you felt good doing it, right? Thanks."
msgstr "Vänta, säg det inte. Jag mår bättre och du mådde bra av att göra det, eller hur? Tack för det."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:175
msgid "You are wise and kind, Holy One."
msgstr "Du är vis och vänlig, O Helige."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:176
msgctxt "hak017"
msgid "In what way may I touch the chosen soul, Seed of the Dweller?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:177
msgid "Uh, where exactly is your garden?"
msgstr "Eh, var exakt ligger din trädgård?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:179
msgid "Oh, nothing. Goodbye."
msgstr "Åh, ingenting. Hej då."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:180
msgctxt "hak018"
msgid "Ahh. You return the spirit of the Dweller to the world and bring a smile to the soul of an old man in passing. For this, I give you powders of healing. Remember, they fog the mind as they cleanse the body."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:182
msgctxt "hak018a"
msgid "And also, will I mix the broc flower with the xander root together whenever you bring both to me. May your pathways be true and your heart follow suit. "
msgstr "Och dessutom kommer jag att blanda brocblomman med xanderroten när du ger mig båda. Må dina vägar gå rätt fram och ditt hjärta följa därefter. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:183
msgid "Where can I find these things?"
msgstr "Var kan jag hitta dessa saker?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:185
msgid "I'm almost sorry to go. I can just about understand you now. Bye."
msgstr "Jag är nästan ledsen att jag måste gå. Jag kan nästan förstå dig nu. Hej då."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:186
msgctxt "hak019"
msgid "Ah, Chosen, my garden is well- how is yours?"
msgstr "Åh, Utvalde, min trädgård är välskött- hur är din?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:187 dialog/hczaius.msg:126
msgid "I'm all right."
msgstr "Jag mår bra."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:188 dialog/fcdrfung.msg:172
msgid "I need healing."
msgstr "Jag behöver läkning."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:189
msgid "Where did you say the plants were?"
msgstr "Var sa du att växterna var?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:190
msgid "I don't have a garden- what the hell are you talking about this time?"
msgstr "Jag har ingen trädgård- vad i helvete pratar du om den här gången?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:191
msgid "I'd like you to make some healing powder for me."
msgstr "Jag vill att du gör lite läkande pulver åt mig."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:192
msgid "Oh, never mind. I've got to go."
msgstr "Åh, glöm det. Jag måste gå."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:193
msgid "Ow?"
msgstr "Aj?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:194
msgid "Ooog! Bak!"
msgstr "Fnys! Bårt!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:195
msgctxt "hak020"
msgid "The pleasure of these words fills me. Alas, the gods whisper for my ear. Goodbye."
msgstr "Njutningen av dessa ord fyller mig. Ack, gudarna viskar för mitt öra. Adjö."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:197
msgid "Still mixing the herbs, huh? See you later."
msgstr "Du blandar fortfarande örterna, va? Vi ses senare."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:198
msgctxt "hak021"
msgid "We all have gardens. May your journeys act as tending. Be well. I must seek audience with the gods now."
msgstr "Vi har alla trädgårdar. Må dina resor fungera som trädgårdsarbete. Ha det bra. Jag måste be om gudarnas uppmärksamhet nu."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:199 dialog/dcsheila.msg:210 dialog/dctyler.msg:394
#: dialog/hcencha.msg:141 dialog/hczaius.msg:156
msgid "See ya."
msgstr "Vi ses."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:200
msgid "I'm betting you carry your audience with you wherever you go. Be well."
msgstr "Jag slår vad om att du har din publik med dig vart du än går. Ha det så bra."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:201
msgctxt "hak022"
msgid "Look to the north, Chosen, and the way will be open."
msgstr "Titta norrut, Utvalde, och vägen kommer att vara öppen."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:202 dialog/ahhakun.msg:208 dialog/cccook.msg:153
#: dialog/sccarkid.msg:116
msgid "Okay. Thanks."
msgstr "Okej. Tack."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:203
msgctxt "hak023"
msgid "I am honored to serve the Chosen."
msgstr "Jag är ärad att få tjäna den Utvalde."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:204
msgctxt "hak024"
msgid "Such is life. Two creates a third. You will need both xander root and broc flower for the healing powder."
msgstr "Sådant är livet. Två skapar en tredje. Du behöver både xanderrot och brokblomma för det helande pulvret."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:205
msgid "Oh. Thanks"
msgstr "Åh. Tack"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:206
msgid "Poo."
msgstr "Bajs."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:207
msgctxt "hak025"
msgid "May this be of no use."
msgstr "Må detta vara utan nytta."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:209 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:115 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:118
msgid "Uh!"
msgstr "Uh!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:210
msgctxt "hak026"
msgid "You are well."
msgstr "Du mår bra."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:212
msgid "No lessons? No incomprehensible speeches? You sure you're okay?"
msgstr "Inga lektioner? Inga obegripliga tal? Är du säker på att du är okej?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:213
msgctxt "hak027"
msgid "Welcome, Chosen. Bless us with words that the GECK will be found soon. Our village ails, our need is great, our time, short."
msgstr "Välkommen, Utvalde. Välsigna oss med ord om att GECK kommer att hittas snart. Vår by lider, vårt behov är stort, vår tid, kort."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:214 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:116 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:119
#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:111 dialog/kcsulik.msg:324 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:107
msgid "Nuh."
msgstr "Nä."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:215
msgid "And your ability to speak normally, non-existent. I'm still trying."
msgstr "Och din förmåga att tala normalt, obefintlig. Jag försöker fortfarande."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:216
msgid "I'm on it. "
msgstr "Jag jobbar på det. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:217
msgid "Get off my back, old man. I'm doing the best I can."
msgstr "Låt mig vara, gamla gubbe. Jag gör så gott jag kan."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:218
msgid "I'm still looking, holy one. I hope to have the GECK soon."
msgstr "Jag letar fortfarande, helige. Jag hoppas ha GECK snart."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:219
msgctxt "hak028a"
msgid "May the Earth cushion the steps you must take."
msgstr "Må Jorden dämpa stegen du måste ta."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:220
msgctxt "hak028b"
msgid "May the Waters soothe your journey."
msgstr "Må Vattnet lugna din resa."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:221
msgctxt "hak028c"
msgid "May the Wind guide you to your goal."
msgstr "Må Vinden leda dig till ditt mål."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:222
msgctxt "hak028d"
msgid "May the Fire toast your bottom until you get this done."
msgstr "Må Elden bränna din rumpa tills du får det här gjort."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:224
msgid "Say what?!"
msgstr "Vad sa du?!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:226
msgid "Huh?!"
msgstr "Va?!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:227
msgctxt "hak029"
msgid "Welcome back, Chosen. I see by your face the salvation of the GECK is not yet ours. Be tireless as the ant before our reserves run out. You are our last hope."
msgstr "Välkommen tillbaka, Utvalde. Jag ser på ditt ansikte att GECKs räddning ännu inte är vår. Var lika outtröttlig som myran innan våra lager tar slut. Du är vårt sista hopp."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:228 dialog/ahhakun.msg:234 dialog/ahhakun.msg:239
#: dialog/ecbhead.msg:138 dialog/ecbhead.msg:140 dialog/ecbhead.msg:1138
#: dialog/ecbhead.msg:1140 dialog/kcsulik.msg:114 dialog/kcsulik.msg:120
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:758 dialog/kcsulik.msg:950 dialog/kcsulik.msg:958
#: dialog/ncboxer.msg:207 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:149 dialog/scfelix.msg:112
#: dialog/scwestin.msg:124
msgid "Uh-huh."
msgstr "Aha."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:229
msgid "I'm trying. I'd like to see the ant covering the miles I am."
msgstr "Jag försöker. Jag skulle vilja se myran ta sig an lika många kilometer som jag gör."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:230
msgid "I'm doing my best."
msgstr "Jag gör mitt bästa."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:231
msgid "I'll double my efforts, holy one. I will not let you down."
msgstr "Jag ska fördubbla mina ansträngningar, heliga. Jag kommer inte att svika dig."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:232
msgid "Yeah, yeah. I've heard it all before."
msgstr "Ja, ja. Jag har hört allt det här förut."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:233
msgctxt "hak030"
msgid "Chosen - the village cries in desperation. The children are weak with hunger. Please, we cannot hold out much longer."
msgstr "Utvalde - byn skriker i desperation. Barnen är svaga av hunger. Snälla, vi kan inte hålla ut mycket längre."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:235
msgid "I'm trying. I'm trying! Give me a break!"
msgstr "Jag försöker. Jag försöker! Ta det lugnt!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:236
msgid "I'll find the GECK, holy one. You have my word."
msgstr "Jag ska hitta GECK, helige man. Du har mitt ord."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:237
msgid "I'll do my best to find the GECK."
msgstr "Jag ska göra mitt bästa för att hitta GECK."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:238
msgctxt "hak031"
msgid "Chosen, the sands of time are but a few grains. Please. Bring the GECK soon and make the future of the village like the beach of the ocean. Quickly, before the last grain falls."
msgstr "Utvalde, tidens sand är bara några få korn. Snälla. Ta med GECK snart och gör byns framtid som stranden vid havet. Skynda, innan det sista kornet faller."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:240
msgid "All right. I'm off to find it."
msgstr "Okej, då. Jag ska leta reda på det."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:241
msgid "Life's a beach, huh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:242
msgid "I will find the GECK, holy one. I will not let our people down."
msgstr "Jag ska hitta GECK, helige man. Jag tänker inte svika vårt folk."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:243
msgctxt "hak032"
msgid "Chosen, the spirits of our ancestors guide me to a world of dreams that I may touch thoughts. Our village suffers without the holy GECK. Your hands hold our lives as a father holds his children."
msgstr "Utvalde, våra förfäders andar leder mig till en värld av drömmar där jag kan röra vid tankar. Vår by lider utan den heliga GECK. Dina händer håller våra liv som en far håller sina barn."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:244
msgctxt "hak033"
msgid "Once again my spirit touches you from the void, Chosen. Our crops fail, our reserves are meager. Return to us with the GECK. Your failure is our last light."
msgstr "Ännu en gång berör min ande dig från tomrummet, utvalde. Våra grödor vissnar, våra reserver är magra. Återvänd till oss med GECK. Ditt misslyckande är vårt sista ljus."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:245
msgctxt "hak034"
msgid "Chosen. The village weakens. It is harder to touch your dreams. You must hurry or we will all..."
msgstr "Utvalde. Byn försvagas. Det är svårare att röra vid dina drömmar. Du måste skynda dig, annars kommer vi alla..."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:246
msgctxt "hak035"
msgid "Chosen? Chosen? Do you hear me? The village dies. All of our futures die, too. We have little left in both time and essence... Hurry. Hurry..."
msgstr "Utvalde? Utvalde? Hör du vad jag säger? Byn dör. Alla våra framtider dör också. Vi har lite kvar av både tid och essens... Skynda. Skynda..."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:247
msgctxt "hak101"
msgid "Chosen - the shadow of darkness arrived before you."
msgstr "Utvalde - mörkrets skugga kom före du gjorde."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:248
msgid "Owwww!"
msgstr "Ajjjj!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:250
msgid "You look bad. Let me help."
msgstr "Du ser illa ut. Låt mig hjälpa."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:251
msgctxt "hak102"
msgid "Child of Nature, how could we put such a burden on your shoulders? (sigh) Your people have been taken."
msgstr "Naturens barn, hur kunde vi lägga en sådan börda på dina axlar? (suck) Ditt folk har blivit bortfört."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:252
msgid "Uhh?"
msgstr "Ehhh?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:253
msgctxt "hak103"
msgid "Yes. Gone. Many dark souls came, riding the metal birds like a flock of hungry chittick bugs, hiding their evil in shiny skins. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:254
msgid "Ooo! Shiny Purty!"
msgstr "Ååå! Glänsig snyg!"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:255
msgctxt "hak104"
msgid "No! Not shiny pretty! They kidnapped our people and took them to the southwest."
msgstr "Nej! Inte glänsande snygg! De kidnappade vårt folk och förde dem sydvästerut."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:256 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:346
msgid "Ow."
msgstr "Aj."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:257
msgctxt "hak105"
msgid "Yes. Great sadness and pain. I stand between worlds to tell you, Chosen. Save your people."
msgstr "Ja. Stor sorg och smärta. Jag står mellan världarna för att berätta för dig, Utvalde. Rädda ditt folk."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:258 dialog/dcvicgrd.msg:434 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:123
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:105 dialog/kcsulik.msg:118 dialog/kcsulik.msg:323
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:926 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:106 dialog/scvortis.msg:111
msgid "Uh?"
msgstr "Eh?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:259
msgctxt "hak106"
msgid "Chosen, please let my words touch you. Go southwest. South and west. Save our people. Save our people."
msgstr "Utvalde, låt mina ord beröra dig. Gå sydväst. Syd och väst. Rädda vårt folk. Rädda vårt folk."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:260
msgid "Uh-huh.."
msgstr "Aha."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:261
msgctxt "hak107"
msgid "Thank the ancestors. Now my soul may join the eternal song. Safe journey, Chosen."
msgstr "Tacka förfäderna. Nu kan min själ ansluta sig till den eviga sången. Säker resa, Utvalde."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:262
msgid "Go?"
msgstr "Gå?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:263
msgctxt "hak108"
msgid "Go!..."
msgstr "Gå!..."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:264 dialog/dcsheila.msg:200 dialog/dcsheila.msg:212
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:232 dialog/rclou.msg:120
msgid "Bye bye."
msgstr "Hej då."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:265
msgctxt "hak109"
msgid "Dark souls came. They took everyone."
msgstr "Mörka själar kom. De tog allihop."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:266
msgid "Dark souls? What do you mean?"
msgstr "Mörka själar? Vad menar du?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:267
msgctxt "hak110"
msgid "A rush of wind came. On it were great dragonflies that spat flame. Evil men crawled from the beasts' bellies and brought death to our warriors."
msgstr "En vindpust kom. På den fanns stora trollsländor som spottade eld. Onda män kröp ut ur djurens magar och förde död över våra krigare."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:268
msgid "Our warriors couldn't stop them?"
msgstr "Kunde inte våra krigare stoppa dem?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:269
msgctxt "hak112"
msgid "The spirit was willing, but the spearheads were weak. The evil ones burned our warriors with the lights of hell."
msgstr "Anden var villig, men spjutspetsarna var svaga. De onda brände våra krigare med skärseld."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:270
msgid "They killed everyone?"
msgstr "Dödade de alla?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:271
msgctxt "hak113"
msgid "All were dead or taken. My spirit returned to flesh only to reveal the truth to the Chosen."
msgstr "Alla blev dödade eller tillfångatagna. Min ande återvände till köttet bara för att avslöja sanningen för Den Utvalde."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:272
msgid "What happened to the ones taken?"
msgstr "Vad hände med de som togs?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:273
msgctxt "hak114"
msgid "The beasts swallowed all, then took to the winds."
msgstr "Odjuren svalde alla och gav sig sedan iväg för vinden."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:274
msgid "Uh, which way were the winds that they followed going?"
msgstr "Eh, åt vilket håll blåste vindarna som de följde?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:275
msgctxt "hak115"
msgid "Did you never listen when I taught you the yearly dance of the wind spirits? South, of course."
msgstr "Lyssnade du aldrig när jag lärde dig vindandarnas årliga dans? Söderut, så klart."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:276
msgid "Your descriptions were so vivid and powerful, great Hakunin, that I was often stricken senseless for the duration of your lessons."
msgstr "Dina beskrivningar var så levande och kraftfulla, store Hakunin, att jag ofta blev helt hänförd under dina lektioner."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:277
msgid "Oh, those winds. Of course. "
msgstr "Åh, de vindarna. Såklart. "

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:278
msgctxt "hak116"
msgid "Yes, they traveled the wind south. I overheard the dark souls speaking. They planned to rest their beasts at a place named Navarro before crossing the great basin of our earth-mother's tears."
msgstr "Ja, de färdades med vinden söderut. Jag hörde de mörka själarna tala. De planerade att vila sina bestar på en plats som heter Navarro innan de korsade den stora funt fylld med vår jordmoders tårar."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:279
msgid "What shall I do?"
msgstr "Vad skall jag göra?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:280
msgid "Basin of tears?"
msgstr "Tårarnas funt?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:281
msgctxt "hak117"
msgid "For me, nothing. Chosen, you must seek the fold of the dark ones and rescue our people."
msgstr "För mig, ingenting. Utvalde, du måste söka de mörkas flock och rädda vårt folk."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:282 dialog/dccaesar.msg:323
msgid "I will try."
msgstr "Jag ska försöka."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:283
msgctxt "hak118"
msgid "You are the Chosen. You must do."
msgstr "Du är den Utvalde. Du måste göra det."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:284
msgid "Hakunin?"
msgstr "Hakunin?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:285
msgid "First time I understood what you meant."
msgstr "Första gången jag förstod vad du menade."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:286
msgctxt "hak120"
msgid "An ocean of tears, cried by a mother for her children."
msgstr "Ett hav av tårar, gråtit av en mor för sina barn."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:287
msgid "Oh, the ocean. But what shall I do?"
msgstr "Åh, havet. Men vad skall jag göra?"

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:288
msgctxt "hak121"
msgid "A strange mist stole their minds and sent them to the land of Sleep. The evil ones walked among the dreamers, yet did not dream."
msgstr "En märklig dimma stal deras sinnen och skickade dem till Sömnens land. De onda vandrade bland drömmare, men drömde inte."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:290
msgctxt "hak122"
msgid "Too many seasons and too many wounds, Chosen. Instead, you must listen."
msgstr "För många årstider och för många sår, Utvalde. Istället måste du lyssna."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:300
msgid "Those who steal carry a great burden. Remember this, Chosen One."
msgstr "De som stjäl bär på en stor börda. Kom ihåg detta, Utvalde."

#: dialog/ahhakun.msg:301
msgid "You must now pay for your sins, Chosen One."
msgstr "Du måste nu betala för dina synder, Utvalde."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:100
msgid "You see the Abbot, the spiritual leader of the Abbey."
msgstr "Du ser Abboten, Klostrets andlige ledare."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:101
msgid "There's something about this monk that leads you to believe he's rather important."
msgstr "Det är något med den här munken som får dig att tro att han är ganska viktig."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:200 dialog/amonk1.msg:200 dialog/amonk4.msg:200
msgid "Welcome traveler."
msgstr "Välkommen resenär."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:202 dialog/amonk1.msg:202
msgid "We are the guardians of knowledge."
msgstr "Vi är kunskapens väktare."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:203
msgid "I'm sorry, but knowledge of our books is of no use to you."
msgstr "Jag är ledsen, men kunskap om våra böcker är inte till någon nytta för dig."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:300
msgid "Welcome to the Abbey, traveler. How can I help you?"
msgstr "Välkommen till Klostret, resenär. Hur kan jag hjälpa dig?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:301 dialog/amonk4.msg:301
msgid "What can you tell me about your order?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:302
msgid "Have you ever heard of a device called a GECK?"
msgstr "Har du någonsin hört talas om en apparat som kallas GECK?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:303 dialog/amonk5.msg:305
msgid "Do you know where I could find Vault 13?"
msgstr "Vet du var jag kan hitta Vault 13?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:401
msgid "Okay. I'd like to know something else."
msgstr "Okej. Jag skulle vilja veta något annat."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:402
msgid "Hmm... that *does* sound familiar. Why, yes, I recall Brother Thomas mentioning something about that recently. I'm sorry, but I don't recall exactly what he said."
msgstr "Hmm... det låter *faktiskt* bekant. Ja, jag minns att broder Thomas nämnde något om det nyligen. Jag är ledsen, men jag minns inte exakt vad han sa."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:403
msgid "That's fine. Just point me to Brother Thomas and I'll go ask him."
msgstr "Det är okej. Peka bara ut var broder Thomas är så frågar jag honom."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:405 dialog/vcdrtroy.msg:352
msgid "Well, thanks anyway."
msgstr "Nåväl, tack ändå."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:406
msgid ""
"I'm afraid I won't be able to do that. You see, I am under the impression that Brother Thomas is no longer among\n"
" the living. But, fortunately for you, he was one of our most reliable transcribers. I'm sure whatever articles he came\n"
" across concerning the information you seek has been transcribed into our computers."
msgstr ""
"Jag är rädd att jag inte kommer att kunna göra det. Du förstår, jag har fått intrycket att broder Thomas inte längre är bland\n"
" de levande. Men lyckligtvis för er var han en av våra mest pålitliga transkriberare. Jag är säker på att alla artiklar han kom över\n"
" om informationen du söker har transkriberats till våra datorer."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:407
msgid "Wait a second, you're \"under the impression\" that Brother Thomas is dead? Where I come from, death is a pretty clear cut thing. So, is he dead, or isn't he?"
msgstr "Vänta lite, du \"har fått intrycket\" att broder Thomas är död? Där jag kommer ifrån är döden en ganska tydlig sak. Så, är han död, eller är han inte?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:408
msgid ""
"Brother Thomas has been missing for several days, ever since he went down to the caverns below the Abbey. [He sighs wearily.]\n"
" You see, some of the Abbey's residents claimed to have seen a huge beast lurking down there, and Brother Thomas was quite skeptical.\n"
" He took it upon himself to go dispel these rumors, yet, as it turns out, his disappearance has only further validated them."
msgstr ""
"Broder Thomas har varit försvunnen i flera dagar, ända sedan han gick ner till grottorna under Klostret. [Han drar en utmattad suck.]\n"
" Du förstår, några av Klostrets invånare påstod sig ha sett ett enormt odjur lura där nere, och broder Thomas var ganska skeptisk.\n"
" Han tog på sig att gå och skingra dessa rykten, men det visar sig att hans försvinnande bara har bekräftat dem ytterligare."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:409
msgid "Hmmm. Maybe I should take a look what's down there. *I AM* the chosen one after all..."
msgstr "Hmmm. Jag kanske borde ta en titt på vad som finns där nere. *JAG ÄR* den utvalde trots allt..."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:410
msgid "I'm adventurous. I can take a look."
msgstr "Jag är äventyrlig. Jag kan ta en titt."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:411
msgid ""
"You'd really do that? Perhaps while you're down there, you could look for a certain book. You see, it was last\n"
" known to be in Brother Thomas's possession, and it's very important to us, as it was passed down by our founders.\n"
" If you could retrieve that book, I would be most grateful. In fact, I'd grant you full access to our computers, so you\n"
" can look for whatever you desire."
msgstr ""
"Skulle du verkligen göra det? När du är där nere kanske du kan leta efter en viss bok. Du förstår, den var senast\n"
" i broder Thomas ägo, och den är mycket viktig för oss, eftersom den ärvdes genom leden från våra grundare.\n"
" Om du kunde hämta den boken, skulle jag vara mycket tacksam. Jag skulle ge dig full tillgång till våra datorer, så att du\n"
" kan leta efter vad du än önskar."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:412
msgid "It's a deal. I'll be back soon."
msgstr "Det är en överenskommelse. Jag kommer snart tillbaka."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:413
msgid "Maybe, let me think about this some more..."
msgstr "Kanske, låt mig tänka på det här lite mer..."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:414
msgid "Thank you. Please let me know if you find the book."
msgstr "Tack så mycket. Låt mig veta om du hittar boken."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:415 dialog/ahmonk.msg:426
msgid "Ok, bye."
msgstr "Okej, hej då."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:416
msgid "Hello, my friend."
msgstr "Hej, min vän."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:417
msgid "I've killed your beast, and I've got your book."
msgstr "Jag har dödat ditt odjur och jag har din bok."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:418
msgid "Excellent! Let me have it!"
msgstr "Utmärkt! Låt mig ta den!"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:420
msgid "Not so fast. How much is it worth to you?"
msgstr "Inte så fort. Hur mycket är den värd för dig?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:421
msgid ""
"[He takes the book from you and caresses its cover as if to sooth it.] You have done us a great service. You now\n"
" have full access to our computers in the library. Tell Brother Paul I grant you permission to access our files."
msgstr ""
"[Han tar boken från dig och smeker dess omslag som för att lugna den.] Du har gjort oss en stor tjänst. Du har nu\n"
" full tillgång till våra datorer i biblioteket. Säg till broder Paul att jag ger dig tillstånd att använda våra filer."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:423
msgid "You want money for it? Fine, here's $250. Go see Brother Paul for access to the computers."
msgstr "Vill du ha pengar för den? Visst, här är $250. Gå till broder Paul för att få tillgång till datorerna."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:424
msgid "Thanks for the money, bye."
msgstr "Tack för pengarna, hej då."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:425
msgid "You should look on a second floor computer, now that you have full access there."
msgstr "Du borde titta igenom en dator på andra våningen, nu när du har full tillgång dit."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:430
msgid "What is the purpose of your order?"
msgstr "Vad är syftet med er grupp?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:431
msgid "What is the history behind the Abbey?"
msgstr "Vad är historien bakom Klostret?"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:432
msgid "Hmm, I don't have any questions at the moment."
msgstr "Hmm, jag har inga frågor just nu."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:433
msgid ""
"Our holy mission is to read, copy and take care of our sacred books of knowledge and other relics of the lost age.\n"
" It is our hope that with this knowledge we are able to create a Memorabilia that might one day help humanity emerge from\n"
" its self-imposed Dark Age. Any information that we come across is recorded, lest it be lost like so much was in the\n"
" great Flame Deluge."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:434
msgid ""
"After the Great War, the guiding hands of fate directed our ancestors to this old Abbey in the mountains. Due to\n"
" its remote location, the monastery survived the Flame Deluge mostly unscathed. As our ancestors explored the building,\n"
" they discovered an extensive library of books. And not just religious texts, oh no, this library contained the gamut of\n"
" written works, from literary classics, to scientific encyclopedias."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:435
msgid "What happened then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:436 dialog/ccmandr.msg:285 dialog/ncrenesc.msg:423
msgid "I've heard enough."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:437
msgid ""
"They soon realized the true treasure trove of wisdom stored within those books--especially the scientific tomes.\n"
" Here were the chronicles of a fallen civilization. A lost age. There were a few who thought it might be best to\n"
" destroy this knowledge, for fear that it would once again guide humanity towards apocalypse. But it was eventually\n"
" decided that they would instead dedicate themselves to ensuring the preservation of the books, to be released when,\n"
" and if, the world was ready for it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:438
msgid "(More)"
msgstr "(Mer)"

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:439
msgid ""
"And so, utilizing a small printing press, they began making copies of the books, and also transcribing them\n"
" into the Abbey's computers to preserve them digitally, should the physical books ever be destroyed. Over the long years,\n"
" others have come across the Abbey, and some have elected to stay and live out their lives in the tranquil quiet of our mountain home."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:440 dialog/dcstory1.msg:162 dialog/epac10.msg:3015
#: dialog/epac10.msg:3042 dialog/scdocjub.msg:151 dialog/scdocjub.msg:157
msgid "Thanks for the story."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:441
msgid "Where did your ancestors come from?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:442
msgid "They never told where they originally came from. We suspect that they came here originally from the east."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:443
msgid "Well, thanks for the story."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:444
msgid "Do you need any help here at the monastery?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:445
msgid "I found out what's wrong with your water pump."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:446
msgid "Do you know anything about the original founders?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:447
msgid ""
"I do not know all the names of our founders, but the most important one I am aware of is Miller.\n"
" Before the Great War he was an electrical engineer working for the United States government. Shortly thereafter,\n"
" he converted to Catholicism and made an oath with himself that we would spend the rest of his life preserving the\n"
" knowledge of the past. His greatest fear was that this knowledge would be lost forever and thus needed to be preserved\n"
" so that future generations may benefit."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:448
msgid "You must be quite knowledgeable having read so much."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:449
msgid ""
"I have indeed read much in my life. Yet you might be disappointed at the limitations of my knowledge. You see,\n"
" we record and preserve. We are forbidden to act upon the wisdom of these books, therefore our understanding of the text is quite limited."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:450
msgid "Wait, you're telling me that you just blindly transcribe these books without even trying to comprehend them?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:451
msgid ""
"As I've said, it is our job to preserve this knowledge, not to understand it. Before this knowledge can be\n"
" returned to mankind, he must first prove to have risen above his tendency of mass genocide. That's the only way to\n"
" ensure that history does not repeat itself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:452
msgid ""
"Well, I've got news for you: that day's never going to come. And while you're hoarding all this knowledge in your\n"
" little mountain paradise here, people out in the wasteland are struggling every day to survive. In fact, my entire tribe\n"
" is on the brink of destruction. The knowledge contained in these books could help cure diseases, improve crops, and greatly\n"
" increase the chance of humanity's survival."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:453
msgid ""
"Ah, well I suppose you make a good point. But it just seems like the information stored here could help out a lot\n"
" of people. Even if you don't think the world's ready for this knowledge, I don't see why *you* can't at least try to learn from it.\n"
" Otherwise, what's the point of keeping it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:454
msgid ""
"I understand your frustration with our ways, but you must understand that this is the way things have always been\n"
" for us. To alter things now, after so many years... that would be blasphemous against our faith. No, I feel we must continue\n"
" to live by the rules set by our ancestors."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:455
msgid ""
"I understand your frustration with our ways, but you must understand that this is the way things have always been\n"
" for us. To alter things now, after so many years... that would be blasphemous against our faith. Still, I shall consider\n"
" your words. I sense great wisdom in you, wanderer. It is a pity I have met very few like you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:456
msgid "Thanks. I'd like to know something else though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:457
msgid "Very well. I'd like to know something else though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:501
msgid "You gain %d experience points for bringing back the book."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:600
msgid "I fixed your broken waterpump."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:601
msgid ""
"That is great news, indeed. That waterpump had been acting up for quite some time. Those merchants said they\n"
" could take care of it, but they didn't seem to be making much progress. It's a good thing you came along. Thank you again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:602
msgid "I expect some money for this you know. Now cough it up!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:603 dialog/ncftully.msg:2014
msgid "No problem. I have some other questions though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:604
msgid "I'm glad to be of assistance. Take care."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:605
msgid "[Frowns.] I see. Fine, here, take these coins. Now go, and stop bothering me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:606
msgid "Thank you, *father*."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:700
msgid "Uhh... no I seem to have misplaced it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:701
msgid ""
"What!? [He sighs deeply.] It is most unfortunate that you were unable to recover that book. But you say you've\n"
" killed the beast? Hm, then it should be safe to send our own people down to continue searching for it. Anyway, for your\n"
" service, I shall grant you access to our computers. Go see Brother Paul for the access key."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:800
msgid ""
"Actually, yes. Our main water pump has been acting up for some time, and now it finally seems to have broken down\n"
" completely. If you know anything about machinery, do you think you could take a look and see if something could be done?\n"
" There are a few merchants already working on it. I fear that little progress has been made though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:801
msgid "I'm happy to help. I'll report back on the progress."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:802
msgid "Sure, I'll be glad to help... for a price of course."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:803
msgid "Actually on second thought, let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:804
msgid ""
"What!? Oh, fine. If that's the kind of person you are, then you shall receive payment for your service. Here's\n"
" 25 coins to begin with.  Please let me know if something can be done. [The man sighs as he hands you the coins]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:805
msgid "Hey, no need for the sighing. You think everything in life comes for free? Now, let me get to work."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:806
msgid "Really? Please, do tell."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:807
msgid "The motor gave out and fried all the connectors. I'm going to Vault City to get a new part."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:808
msgid "Oh thank you. You are indeed a great help. Please report back once you install the new part."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:809
msgid "I will. Be back soon."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:900
msgid "You explain to the Abbot that while the information they hold could lead to mankind's annihilation, it could also lead to mankind's salvation."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:901
msgid "You learn about the original founder of the Abbey."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1000
msgid "I killie scary monster down in cave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1010
msgid "Really? That's great. That is very brave of you. You're a big boy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1011
msgid "Really? That's great. That is very brave of you. You're a big girl."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1012
msgid "(smile) I know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1020
msgid "Did you happen to find a book lying there? A friend of mine had it, and he went missing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1021
msgid "I find book. Here, it heavy and no pitchers inside."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1022
msgid "I no find book. Sorree. I go look now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1030
msgid "I find book."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1031
msgid "That's great. Thanks. You're one special guy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1032
msgid "That's great. Thanks. You're one special gal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1033
msgid "YAY."
msgstr "JIPPIE."

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1100
msgid ""
"I was down there earlier. I saw a few dead bodies, so I'm guessing one of them belonged to your missing monk. If\n"
" it makes you feel any better, I killed the thing responsible for his death."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1110
msgid ""
"Ah... so it's as I feared. Brother Thomas shall be dearly missed. You have my thanks for ridding us of whatever\n"
" wasteland beasts lurked down there. However, I... I don't suppose you found a book while you were down there. It's a very\n"
" important book that was last known to be in Brother Thomas's possession."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1111
msgid "No, but I suppose I could go back and check."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1112
msgid "Do you mean this book?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1113
msgid "Before I go, let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:1411
msgid "Very interesting. I have to go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:4091
msgid "So no one else has even bothered to go down there and check on him? What if he's simply trapped down there somehow, and he's slowly starving to death?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:4092
msgid "I suppose that's possible, but you must understand. We are a peaceful people. The thought of going up against one of those wasteland monsters is terrifying to us. We're simply not equipped for such confrontations. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:4177
msgid "I've killed the beast."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:4188
msgid "Excellent! And how about the book; were you able to recover it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ahmonk.msg:6020
msgid "If you truly want to show your gratitude, how about some money for my trouble?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/aichest.msg:100 dialog/aivase.msg:100
msgid "You see a simple vase."
msgstr "Du ser en enkel vas."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:101
msgid "You see a small chest."
msgstr "Du ser en liten kista."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:102 dialog/aivase.msg:101
msgid "You see a sun-baked clay vase."
msgstr "Du ser en solblekt lervas."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:103
msgid "You see a chest for the shaman's herbs."
msgstr "Du ser en kista för shamanens örter."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:104
msgid "You deftly steal from the shaman's things."
msgstr "Du stjäl skickligt från shamanens saker."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:105
msgid "You skillfully lock the chest."
msgstr "Du låser skickligt kistan."

#: dialog/aichest.msg:106
msgid "You skillfully unlock the chest."
msgstr "Du låser skickligt upp kistan."

#: dialog/amonk1.msg:100 dialog/amonk2.msg:100 dialog/amonk3.msg:100
#: dialog/amonk4.msg:100
msgid "You see a monk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk1.msg:101 dialog/amonk2.msg:101 dialog/echlyppl.msg:106
msgid "You see a holy woman."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk1.msg:103 dialog/amonk2.msg:103
msgid "You see a regular Abbey nun."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk1.msg:203 dialog/atribal.msg:202 dialog/dccustmr.msg:304
#: dialog/dcg2grd.msg:274 dialog/dcg2grd.msg:300 dialog/dcorphan.msg:271
#: dialog/dcorphan.msg:282 dialog/dcorphan.msg:291 dialog/dcorphan.msg:303
#: dialog/dcpengrd.msg:235 dialog/dcrebdor.msg:213 dialog/dcstory2.msg:115
#: dialog/echomkid.msg:210 dialog/kctorr.msg:276 dialog/ocsandy.msg:139
msgid "Hi."
msgstr "Hej."

#: dialog/amonk1.msg:205
msgid "I hope you enjoy your stay here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:200 dialog/amonk3.msg:202 dialog/atribal.msg:200
#: dialog/atribal.msg:205 dialog/tribec8.msg:104
msgid "Greetings."
msgstr "Hälsningar."

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:201 dialog/atribal.msg:201
msgid "Welcome to the Abbey."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:202
msgid "You should talk to our leader if you wish to gain any information."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:203
msgid "Good day... or is it night already?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:204
msgid "There's so much work that must be done."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk2.msg:205
msgid "Life here at the Abbey is a peaceful one. Something rare in these wretched wastes."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:101
msgid "You see a nun."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:102
msgid "This monk looks like he knows a thing or two about computers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:103
msgid "This nun looks like she knows a thing or two about computers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:200
msgid "Don't break anything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:201
msgid "Sorry, I'm rather busy at the moment."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:203
msgid "Feel free to look around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:204
msgid "We copy the knowledge for the future generations."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:205
msgid "These old books are very fragile."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:206
msgid "Copying books is pretty hard work."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk3.msg:208
msgid "There's much to copy down from these books."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:101
msgid "This monk looks like a trader."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:203
msgid "Go play somewhere else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:300
msgid "Hi, how can I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:400
msgid "Our holy mission is to collect and preserve the sacred relics of the forgotten past. Anyone is welcome here, as long as they don't damage anything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:401
msgid "Who is your leader?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:402
msgid "What kind of relics?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:403
msgid "He can be found on the third floor. If you wish to learn more about our order, he is the one to talk to."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:404
msgid "All sorts, but most of our Memorabilia consist of ancient tomes. So much information can be obtained from those texts. It is our mission to preserve this knowledge so that a future generation may use it to build a new world of peace and joy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk4.msg:406 dialog/amonk5.msg:403 dialog/bckarla.msg:105
#: dialog/ccdrgrd.msg:125 dialog/ccgguard.msg:130 dialog/fctnkbar.msg:115
#: dialog/fctnkbar.msg:121 dialog/fctnkbar.msg:127 dialog/fctnkbar.msg:130
#: dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:115 dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:120 dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:125
#: dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:127 dialog/fctnkmer.msg:115 dialog/fctnkmer.msg:121
#: dialog/fctnkmer.msg:127 dialog/fctnkmer.msg:130 dialog/fsface.msg:130
#: dialog/fsface.msg:135 dialog/fsface.msg:140 dialog/fsface.msg:219
#: dialog/gsterm.msg:740 dialog/kcardin.msg:301 dialog/kcardin.msg:390
#: dialog/kcdunton.msg:520 dialog/kcsally.msg:391 dialog/ocdar.msg:114
#: dialog/ocdar.msg:123 dialog/ocsandy.msg:127 dialog/scelise.msg:147
#: dialog/scelise.msg:172 dialog/scelise.msg:174 dialog/scjohn.msg:109
#: dialog/shtandi.msg:232 dialog/shtandi.msg:283
msgid "Ok."
msgstr "Ok."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:100
msgid "You see a computer monk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:101
msgid "You see Brother Paul."
msgstr "Du ser Broder Paul."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:102
msgid "This monk looks like a computer geek."
msgstr "Den här munken ser ut som en datanörd."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:202
msgid "Now, did I backup those computer files today..."
msgstr "Så, säkerhetskopierade jag de där datorfilerna idag..."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:203
msgid "I'm sorry, but I don't have time for someone of your intelligence."
msgstr "Jag är ledsen, men jag har inte tid med någon med din intelligens."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:300 dialog/dcrebecc.msg:220 dialog/dctyler.msg:371
#: dialog/epac11.msg:402 dialog/epac12.msg:300 dialog/epac17.msg:120
#: dialog/hceric.msg:131 dialog/ncethwri.msg:431 dialog/nckitty.msg:350
#: dialog/nclabish.msg:260 dialog/ncmcgee.msg:370 dialog/qcgensci.msg:157
#: dialog/scskeete.msg:141 dialog/vcandy.msg:247 dialog/vcandy.msg:281
#: dialog/vcbarcit.msg:151 dialog/vcdrtroy.msg:285 dialog/vcgenfam.msg:157
#: dialog/vckohl.msg:178 dialog/vcwrkcit.msg:151
msgid "Yes?"
msgstr "Ja?"

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:301
msgid "You guys sure have a lot of computers here."
msgstr "Ni har verkligen många datorer här."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:303
msgid "Tell me about your leader."
msgstr "Berätta om er ledare."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:304
msgid "Do you have any info about a GECK?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:307
msgid "I am in need of some specific information."
msgstr "Jag behöver lite specifik information."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:400
msgid ""
"Yes, we have. Too many, in my opinion. I can't express to you the tedium of having to back up all these files\n"
" each and every day. There's just so much information to preserve, but, of course, it must be done."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:401
msgid "Of course. Anyway, I have some other questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:402
msgid "We are an independent community. Anyone is welcome as long as they behave themselves."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:404
msgid "The Abbot is a good spiritual leader, but he's been a little cranky since we lost Brother Thomas to the beast."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:405
msgid "What kind of beast?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:406
msgid ""
"I haven't seen it, personally--there's nothing in the world that could get me to go down there and explore those\n"
" caverns--but if I had to guess, I'd say it's probably just some overgrown radscorpion."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:407
msgid "If you haven't seen it, then what makes you think it's a radscorpion?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:408
msgid "Because I've heard sounds echoing up from the caves--the sounds of snapping claws and skittering legs."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:409 dialog/dcflick.msg:431 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:196
#: dialog/hcmarcus.msg:317 dialog/tribec2.msg:161 dialog/vclynett.msg:831
msgid "Right."
msgstr "Just det."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:410
msgid "In fact, we do. Take a look on that computer over there. Here, you can use this card to access our encrypted files. [He hands you an access card.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:411
msgid "Wow, thanks a lot!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:412
msgid "I don't know anything about Vault 13, but there is Vault City down south. Maybe they have the info you need."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:414
msgid ""
"That computer near me should have the information you seek, but you'd need an access card to use it.\n"
" We're very selective with who we give access to, but if you speak to the Abbot, perhaps he'll grant you permission."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:415 dialog/rcjane.msg:231 dialog/scwestin.msg:170
msgid "Ok, thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:420
msgid "I'm guessing you've read a lot of books in your time. So I'm curious, what's the most fascinating thing you could tell me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:421
msgid "Hmm, let's see. Did you know a notch in a tree will remain the same distance from the ground as the tree grows?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:422
msgid "Sure. If I come across anything like that, I'll be sure to let you know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:423
msgid "Right... Well, I have some other questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:424
msgid "Would you? I'd appreciate that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:425
msgid "No problem. I have some other questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:426
msgid "Any time. Well, see you around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:430
msgid "I found some information about Botany that might interest you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:431
msgid "Really?! That's great. Please, do tell immediately."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:432
msgid ""
"Fascinating! I shall take this holodisk and add it to the computer database immediately. I appreciate you\n"
" taking the time to find this for me. Thank you for collecting this for me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:433
msgid "Well you see... Understanding habitat destruction and species extinction is dependent on an accurate and complete catalog of plant systematics and taxonomy. And then this means that..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:434
msgid "Any time. I have some other questions though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:435 dialog/vilann.msg:202
msgid "No problem. See you around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:436
msgid "Fascinating! I appreciate you taking the time to find this for me. Please go and upload this information to our computers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:437
msgid "No problem, I'll do that now. See you around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:500
msgid "Stop that, moron!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:550
msgid "That computer near me should have some information about it. You now have access, so take a look for yourself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:600
msgid "The Abbot gave me permission to access the computers here."
msgstr "Abboten gav mig tillåtelse att använda datorerna här."

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:601
msgid "Ah yes, I heard about what you did. Thanks for taking care of that situation. Here is the access key. (He hands you the key.) Enjoy!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:602 dialog/hcdorgrd.msg:282 dialog/ncbrkmn.msg:307
msgid "Thanks. See you around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:650
msgid "Greetings traveler! I am Brother Paul and I am in charge of the collection of information for the Abbey. What can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:651
msgid "Nice to meet you, Paul. I have some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4210
msgid "Uh, no, I can't say I knew that. That's... interesting."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4211
msgid "And did you know a cucumber is 96% water?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4212
msgid "Wow, 96%, huh? Fascinating. But, um, what's a cucumber?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4213
msgid ""
"I've never seen one, but I've read about them. [He looks around nervously and lowers his voice.] I know we're\n"
" not supposed to actually study these books, but when I was transcribing a book on botany, I just couldn't help but get\n"
" sucked into it. The world of plants is simply captivating. Perhaps, if, during your travels, you happen upon some botany\n"
" information, you could bring it to me? I'd be most grateful. Of course, it'd have to be our secret."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4220
msgid "I don't think I want to contribute to your plant obsession. Sorry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/amonk5.msg:4221
msgid "Oh, well then. Fine, forget I asked."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/arbridge.msg:100
msgid ""
"You are standing at the Great Bridge, passageway from\n"
" your village to the vast Wasteland."
msgstr ""
"Du står vid Den Stora Bron, passage från\n"
" din by till det vidsträckta Ödelandet."

#: dialog/arcaves.msg:100
msgid ""
"You are in a dark, musty temple. The shadows seem to\n"
" play tricks with your eyes, and you can hear the faint sound of movement."
msgstr ""
"Du befinner dig i ett mörkt, unket tempel. Skuggorna tycks\n"
" spela ett spratt för dina ögon och du kan höra det svaga ljudet av rörelser."

#: dialog/arvillag.msg:100
msgid "You are once more in the village of your birth, Arroyo."
msgstr "Du är återigen i din födelseby, Arroyo."

#: dialog/aswell.msg:100
msgid "The well has not worked in a while. It needs to be repaired."
msgstr "Brunnen har inte fungerat på ett tag. Den behöver repareras."

#: dialog/aswell.msg:101
msgid "The well is working fine."
msgstr "Brunnen fungerar bra."

#: dialog/atribal.msg:100
msgid "You see a Tribal."
msgstr "Du ser en Stammedlem."

#: dialog/atribal.msg:101
msgid "You see a strong looking man."
msgstr "Du ser en man som ser stark ut."

#: dialog/atribal.msg:204
msgid "Are you from the Arroyo tribe?"
msgstr "Är du från Arroyo-stammen?"

#: dialog/atribal.msg:206
msgid "Nice outfit!"
msgstr "Snygg klädsel!"

#: dialog/atribal.msg:207
msgid "Hello, fellow tribal!"
msgstr "Hallå, stamkompis!"

#: dialog/atribal.msg:500
msgid "Don't mess with my stuff!"
msgstr "Rör inte mina saker!"

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:100 dialog/bcjohn.msg:100 dialog/bcrobert.msg:100
#: dialog/bcsara.msg:100 dialog/dcaddct2.msg:100 dialog/fcdocsqa.msg:101
#: dialog/kctrapr.msg:102 dialog/scjohn.msg:100
msgid "You see a squatter."
msgstr "Du ser en ockupant."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:101
msgid "You see Bill, the squatter."
msgstr "Du ser Bill, ockupanten."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:102
msgid "You see a middle aged man wearing worn clothing."
msgstr "Du ser en medelålders man som bär slitna kläder."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:103
msgid "Sorry, stranger. I don't have time to chat with you."
msgstr "Ledsen, främling. Jag har inte tid att prata med dig."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:104
msgid "Hey, I said I don't have time to chat. Please go away."
msgstr "Hörru, jag sa att jag inte har tid att prata. Var snäll och försvinn."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:105
msgid "Thanks for helping Rebecca. That was a fine thing you did."
msgstr "Tack för att du hjälpte Rebecca. Det var bra gjort av dig."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:106
msgid "Leave me alone. I'm no threat to you."
msgstr "Lämna mig ifred. Jag är inget hot mot dig."

#: dialog/bcbill.msg:107
msgid "All right, all right. I'm moving."
msgstr "Javisst, javisst. Jag rör på mig."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:100 dialog/kcattend.msg:106 dialog/kcbgirl.msg:106
#: dialog/vilann.msg:100
msgid "You see a young woman."
msgstr "Du ser en ung kvinna."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:101
msgid "You see Chrissy, Rebecca's daughter."
msgstr "Du ser Chrissy, Rebeccas dotter."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:102
msgid "You see a pretty young woman. She looks confident and able to handle herself in a fight."
msgstr "Du ser en vacker ung kvinna. Hon ser självsäker ut och kan ta hand om sig själv i en strid."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:103
msgid "If you're here to try and rape me, you're going to be wearing your balls as a bow tie. Get it?"
msgstr "Om du är här för att försöka våldta mig, kommer du bära dina kulor som en fluga. Fattar du?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:104
msgid ""
"Let me guess. The guys are tired of me kicking them where it hurts, so they sent you in here to\n"
" do something obscene. Well, I can hurt you just as bad; I just need to kick higher. Get it?"
msgstr ""
"Låt mig gissa. Killarna är trötta på att jag sparkar dem där det gör ont, så de skickade in dig hit för att\n"
" göra något hemskt. Jag kan skada dig lika illa, jag behöver bara sparka högre. Fattar du?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:105
msgid "Bow tie?"
msgstr "Fluga?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:107 dialog/bccrissy.msg:125
msgid "What go on here? Who you?"
msgstr "Vad hända här? Vem du?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:109 dialog/bccrissy.msg:117 dialog/bccrissy.msg:127
msgid "I'd like to know who you are and what is going on here."
msgstr "Jag skulle vilja veta vem du är och vad som pågår här."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:110
msgid ""
"Yeah. A fancy piece of cloth worn around the neck for decoration. It's like a scarf, but for\n"
" men. Now, just imagine me kicking you SO hard that you end up wearing your dangly about your neck. Get\n"
" it?"
msgstr ""
"Japp. Ett tjusigt tygstycke som bärs runt halsen som dekoration. Det är som en rosett, men för\n"
" män. Tänk dig nu att jag sparkar dig så hårt att det slutar med att du bär dina dinglisar runt halsen. Fattar du\n"
" det?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:111
msgid "Me understand. You no hurt me."
msgstr "Jag förstå. Du inte göra mig illa."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:112
msgid "I got the picture; please don't hurt me."
msgstr "Jag fattar; snälla gör mig inte illa."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:113
msgid "Okay, so why are you here?"
msgstr "Okej, så varför är du här?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:115
msgid "Me want know what go on here? Who you?"
msgstr "Jag veta vill vad händer här? Vem du?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:118
msgid "Really? Awesome! Let's go."
msgstr "Verkligen? Grymt! Nu kör vi."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:120
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In a nutshell, my name is Chrissy and I'm from the Squat. I was out exploring last week when I\n"
" found that entrance out there. I thought it might be an abandoned mine or something, so I decided to\n"
" check it out. Well, it's not a mine; it's a secret entrance into Vault 15. The vault is being\n"
" used as a base for a band of raiders called the Khans. They caught me snooping around and their leader, Darion, had me locked up in here."
msgstr ""
"Kort och gott, heter jag Chrissy och jag kommer från Squat. Jag var ute och utforskade förra veckan när jag\n"
" hittade den där ingången där ute. Jag tänkte att det kunde vara en övergiven gruva eller något, så jag bestämde mig för att\n"
" kolla upp det. Men det är ingen gruva, det är en hemlig ingång till Valv 15. Valvet\n"
" används som en bas för ett band av plundrare som kallas Khans. De kom på mig med att snoka runt och deras ledare, Darion, låste in mig här."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:121
msgid "Okay. Me take you home."
msgstr "Okej. Jag dig tar hem."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:122
msgid "All right, I'll take you home."
msgstr "Okej, jag tar dig hem."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:123
msgid ""
"Well, I'll be damned. Today must be my lucky day. To what do I owe the pleasure of seeing you\n"
" again?"
msgstr ""
"Ja, det var som fan. Idag måste vara min turdag. Vad förskaffar mig nöjet att få träffa dig\n"
" igen?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:128
msgid "Please take me to my mother, Rebecca."
msgstr "Snälla ta mig till min mamma, Rebecca."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:129
msgid ""
"My knight in shining armor returns. Well, it would shine if you'd clean it every once in a\n"
" while. Oh, and you might want to consider bathing yourself as well. So, what can I do for you?"
msgstr ""
"Min riddare i skinande rustning återvänder. Ja, den skulle glänsa om du gjorde rent den lite\n"
" då och då. Och du kanske skulle överväga att bada dig själv också. Så, vad kan jag göra för dig?"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:130 dialog/ccatech.msg:105 dialog/cccomp2.msg:105
#: dialog/ccomp2.msg:105 dialog/cctech1.msg:105 dialog/cctech2.msg:105
msgid "Me just say hi. Me go now."
msgstr "Jag bara säga hej. Jag gå nu."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:131
msgid "Just thought I'd say hello. I'll be going now."
msgstr "Jag tänkte bara säga hej. Jag ska gå nu."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:132
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Hey, I know I have a smart mouth, but I want you to know that I'm very grateful for you saving\n"
" my butt. Thanks very much!"
msgstr ""
"Hej, jag vet att jag är uppkäftig, men jag vill att du ska veta att jag är mycket tacksam för att du räddade\n"
" livhanken på mig. Tack så mycket!"

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:133 dialog/ccxarn.msg:176 dialog/fcfmatt.msg:194
#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:146
msgid "You welcome."
msgstr "Det så lite."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:134 dialog/dcpetey.msg:165 dialog/dcrebecc.msg:402
#: dialog/dcslave.msg:464 dialog/fcfmatt.msg:195 dialog/ocdalia.msg:148
#: dialog/vcconnar.msg:140
msgid "You're welcome."
msgstr "Det var så lite."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:135
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"The people of the Squat are protecting these guys by helping them keep the vault a secret, but they\n"
" don't know what's really going on here. Darion told us that the vault was being repaired so we could have\n"
" a safe place to live with lots of food and water, but it's all a lie. I've been in there and looked\n"
" around. The vault is dead, and the food and water machines don't work. Our food and water's been coming\n"
" from the spoils\n"
" of raids against caravans."
msgstr ""
"Folket i Squat skyddar de här snubbarna genom att hjälpa dem att hålla valvet hemligt, men de\n"
" vet inte vad som verkligen pågår här. Darion berättade för oss att valvet reparerades så att vi kunde ha\n"
" en säker plats att bo på med massor av mat och vatten, men det är bara en lögn. Jag har varit där inne och tittat\n"
" runt. Valvet är dött och mat- och vattenmaskinerna fungerar inte. Vår mat och vatten har kommit\n"
" från bytet\n"
" från räder mot karavaner."

#: dialog/bccrissy.msg:136
msgid ""
"Look, I've got to go home and warn everyone about what's really going on here. We can't help these\n"
" monsters. Will you take me home?"
msgstr ""
"Jag måsteta mig hem och varna alla för vad som verkligen pågår här. Vi kan inte hjälpa de här\n"
" monstren. Kan du ta mig hem?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:100
msgid "You see a young woman in tattered clothing."
msgstr "Du ser en ung kvinna i trasiga kläder."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:101 dialog/ocdalia.msg:101
msgid "You see Dalia."
msgstr "Du ser Dalia."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a young woman in tattered clothing. She seems very alert, and watches her surroundings\n"
" carefully."
msgstr ""
"Du ser en ung kvinna i trasiga kläder. Hon verkar mycket alert och iakttar sin omgivning\n"
" noggrant."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:103 dialog/bcdalia.msg:140
msgid "Hi. I'm Dalia. What can I help you with?"
msgstr "Hej. Jag heter Dalia. Vad kan jag hjälpa dig med?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:104
msgid "Nothing, just say hi."
msgstr "Inget, bara säg hej."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:105
msgid "Uh, who you?"
msgstr "Öh, vem du?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:106 dialog/ocjimmy.msg:119
msgid "What you do here?"
msgstr "Vad du gör här?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:107
msgid "You look like guard."
msgstr "Du ser ut som vakt."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:109 dialog/bcjones.msg:113 dialog/ocgordon.msg:176
#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:113
msgid "Just saying hello."
msgstr "Säger bara hej."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:111 dialog/dccustmr.msg:204 dialog/ecslaver.msg:108
#: dialog/mcjo.msg:153 dialog/ncmcgee.msg:395 dialog/rcascgrd.msg:187
msgid "What are you doing?"
msgstr "Vad är det du gör?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:112
msgid "You look like you're guarding that trail."
msgstr "Du ser ut som om du vaktar den där stigen."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:113 dialog/echermit.msg:114 dialog/hcghoul.msg:183
#: dialog/ncmyrgrd.msg:458 dialog/ocjul.msg:136 dialog/ocmatt.msg:126
msgid "I'll be going now."
msgstr "Jag ska gå nu."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:114
msgid "Well, hello to you. Now, I'm sorry, but you should go."
msgstr "Ja men, hej på dig. Jag är ledsen, men du borde gå."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:115 dialog/cccook.msg:105
msgid "Me want talk."
msgstr "Jag prata vill."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:116 dialog/scwesgrd.msg:105
msgid "Ok, me go."
msgstr "Ok, ja' gå."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:117
msgid "I want to talk to you."
msgstr "Jag vill prata med dig."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:119
msgid "I said I'm Dalia. Look, I don't mean to be rude, but I don't want to talk to anyone right now. Okay?"
msgstr "Jag sa att jag heter Dalia. Jag vill inte vara oförskämd, men jag vill inte prata med någon just nu. Okej?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:120 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:283 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:334
#: dialog/dcvicgrd.msg:333 dialog/dcvicgrd.msg:463 dialog/ocgordon.msg:141
msgid "Okay, bye."
msgstr "Okej, hej då."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:121
msgid "Just little more."
msgstr "Bara mer lite."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:122
msgid "Then I'll leave."
msgstr "Då går jag."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:123
msgid "I just want to ask you a question."
msgstr "Jag vill bara ställa en fråga till dig."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:124
msgid "I like the fresh air, I like the trees, so I'm standing here. Do you have a problem with that?"
msgstr "Jag gillar den friska luften, jag gillar träden, så jag står här. Har du något problem med det?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:125 dialog/bcjones.msg:108 dialog/ocdave.msg:139
#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:108
msgid "Sorry, me go."
msgstr "Ledsen, jag gå."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:126
msgid "No, not problem. Me ask you something."
msgstr "Nej, inte problem. Jag fråga dig något."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:127
msgid "I don't have a problem, but I am curious about something."
msgstr "Jag har inget problem, men jag är nyfiken på en sak."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:128
msgid "Sorry, I'll be going then."
msgstr "Ledsen, jag ska gå då."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:129
msgid ""
"No, I'm not guarding the trail. There's nothing in this hole worth guarding. I told you, I'm\n"
" enjoying the fresh air. Now go away."
msgstr ""
"Nej, jag vaktar inte stigen. Det finns inget i det här hålet som är värt att vakta. Jag sa ju att jag\n"
" njuter av den friska luften. Försvinn nu."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:130
msgid "You nice talk to. Me talk more."
msgstr "Du trevlig prata med. Jag prata mer."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:131
msgid "Sorry me bother. Me go."
msgstr "Ledsen jag stör. Jag gå."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:132
msgid "But we're having such a nice conversation, why stop?"
msgstr "Men vi har ett så trevligt samtal, varför sluta?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:133
msgid "I guess it's time to leave."
msgstr "Jag antar att det är dags att gå."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:134
msgid "Oh no, it's the pest again. Look, I have nothing to say to you. Go away!"
msgstr "Åh nej, det är skadedjuret igen. Jag har inget att säga till dig. Gå din väg!"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:137
msgid "I have no quarrel with you. Leave me be."
msgstr "Jag har inget otalt med dig. Låt mig vara i fred."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:141
msgid "Person go by here? In hurry?"
msgstr "Person som förbi här? Bråttom?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:142 dialog/bcdalia.msg:143 dialog/ccquincy.msg:105
#: dialog/dcderek.msg:314 dialog/dctyler.msg:443 dialog/fcronmey.msg:110
#: dialog/hcliz.msg:112 dialog/hcmanson.msg:140 dialog/hcminers.msg:143
#: dialog/hcminers.msg:147 dialog/hcphil.msg:118 dialog/hcrsuper.msg:111
#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:124 dialog/hcrsuper.msg:129 dialog/hcsuper.msg:111
#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:124 dialog/hcsuper.msg:129 dialog/ncwriply.msg:434
#: dialog/nhmyron.msg:530 dialog/rccshtnd.msg:104 dialog/scelise.msg:123
#: dialog/scggcap.msg:111 dialog/scgunthr.msg:154
msgid "Nothing."
msgstr "Ingenting."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:144
msgid "Did you see someone go by here in a hurry?"
msgstr "Såg du någon ha bråttom förbi här?"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:145
msgid "I see people go by here every day. I really don't pay much attention to them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:146
msgid "Me not have time for you crap."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:148
msgid "Girl life at stake. Young girl. Someone daughter. You please help?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:149
msgid "I don't have time for your crap."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:150
msgid "Fine, bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:151
msgid ""
"Look, a young girl's life is at stake here. The daughter of a worried mother. Can you please\n"
" help me out?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:152
msgid ""
"I don't give a radrat's ass... I'm sorry. I'm just a gun who was hired to stand here and guard\n"
" this trail. Other than that, I don't know what's going on around here. I had a daughter once, though,\n"
" and... yeah, some guy went by here. I let him through because he knew the proper sign... just like the\n"
" sign you gave me. Go on. I'm outta here. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:153
msgid "Thanks. Me no forget this, Dalia."
msgstr "Tack. Jag inte glömma det här, Dalia."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:154
msgid "Thanks. I won't forget this, Dalia."
msgstr "Tack. Jag kommer inte att glömma det här, Dalia."

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:155 dialog/bcdalia.msg:157
msgid "Then go the hell away and leave me be!"
msgstr "Dra åt helvete då och låt mig vara!"

#: dialog/bcdalia.msg:156 dialog/bcdalia.msg:158 dialog/bcdarion.msg:104
#: dialog/bcjones.msg:167 dialog/bczeke.msg:109 dialog/bczeke.msg:111
#: dialog/bczeke.msg:149 dialog/bczeke.msg:153 dialog/bczeke.msg:155
#: dialog/bscomp2.msg:105 dialog/bscomp2.msg:107 dialog/bscomp3.msg:107
#: dialog/bscomp3.msg:109 dialog/bscomp3.msg:111 dialog/bscomp4.msg:107
#: dialog/bscomp4.msg:110 dialog/bscomp4.msg:113 dialog/bscomp5.msg:105
#: dialog/bspower.msg:110 dialog/ccncomp.msg:141 dialog/ccxarn.msg:141
#: dialog/ncstulit.msg:472 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:170 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:175
#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:228 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:230 dialog/oscomptr.msg:122
#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:123 dialog/oscomptr.msg:126 dialog/shtandi.msg:137
msgid "Done."
msgstr "Färdigt."

#: dialog/bcdardog.msg:100
msgid "You see a dog."
msgstr "Du ser en hund."

#: dialog/bcdardog.msg:101
msgid "You see Darion's dog."
msgstr "Du ser Darions hund."

#: dialog/bcdardog.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see an animal with a lot of fur and four legs. If a dog could grin evilly, you would swear\n"
" this one is doing it."
msgstr ""
"Du ser ett djur med mycket päls och fyra ben. Om en hund kunde flina ondskefullt, skulle du svära\n"
" på att den här gör det."

#: dialog/bcdargrd.msg:101
msgid "You see one of Darion's personal guards."
msgstr "Du ser en av Darions personliga vakter."

#: dialog/bcdargrd.msg:102
msgid "He has armor, weapons, and a bad attitude - not the type of guy who likes your company."
msgstr "Han har rustning, vapen och en dålig attityd - inte den sortens snubbe som gillar ditt sällskap."

#: dialog/bcdarion.msg:100
msgid "You see an older man."
msgstr "Du ser en äldre man."

#: dialog/bcdarion.msg:101
msgid "You see Darion, leader of the New Khans."
msgstr "Du ser Darion, ledare för New Khans."

#: dialog/bcdarion.msg:102
msgid "You see an older man with thin, gray hair. He seems to be in good shape for his age."
msgstr "Du ser en äldre man med tunt, grått hår. Han verkar vara i god form för sin ålder."

#: dialog/bcdarion.msg:103
msgid ""
"So, here you are at last. The savior of the downtrodden, the righter of wrongs, the icon of\n"
" hope for humanity. What a dumb-ass! Well, before you start any boring speeches, I'd just like to say\n"
" that I'm not fucking interested. Let's just cut to the chase and get this over with. Baddog, kill!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:100 dialog/bcgengrd.msg:101 dialog/bckarla.msg:100
#: dialog/bcphil.msg:100
msgid "You see a Khan raider."
msgstr "Du ser en Khan-plundare."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:102
msgid "You see a tough looking person with armor, weapons, and a bad attitude. It must be a Khan."
msgstr "Du ser en tuff person med rustning, vapen och en dålig attityd. Det måste vara en Khan."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:103
msgid "What the... I don't think I know you. Who the hell are you?"
msgstr "Vad i...? Jag tror inte att jag känner dig. Vem fan är du?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:104
msgid "I got my ID right here! Let me show ya."
msgstr "Jag har mitt ID här! Jag ska visa dig."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:105
msgid "The name's... umm... Pat, and I'm new here."
msgstr "Jag heter... ehh... Pat, och jag är ny här."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:106
msgid "All right, wise-ass. Take your best shot."
msgstr "Okej, lustigkurre. Gör ett bra försök."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:107
msgid "Oh yeah. Sorry. Didn't recognize you at first. Go on about your business."
msgstr "Jaha. Jag är ledsen. Kände inte igen dig först. Fortsätt med vad du höll på med."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:108
msgid "Hey, I'm not as stupid as you look."
msgstr "Jag är inte så dum som du ser ut."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:109
msgid "You're not dead yet? Shit."
msgstr "Är du inte död än? Skit också."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:110
msgid "Man, Darion doesn't pay me enough to stand around here and do nothing."
msgstr "Asså, Darion betalar mig inte tillräckligt för att bara stå här och inte göra något."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:111
msgid "Sometimes I sit and think about absolutely nothing."
msgstr "Ibland sitter jag och tänker på absolut ingenting."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:112
msgid "I generally don't care what anyone else thinks."
msgstr "Jag bryr mig i allmänhet inte om vad någon annan tycker."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:113
msgid "Ignorance is bliss... I think."
msgstr "Okunnighet är lycka... tror jag."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:114
msgid "When's the next caravan passing through? I could use some action."
msgstr "När passerar nästa karavan? Jag skulle behöva lite mer spänning."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:115
msgid "I could use a break."
msgstr "Jag skulle behöva en rast."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:116
msgid "Damn, I still hurt from that bitch Chrissy kicking me."
msgstr "Fan, jag har fortfarande ont efter att den där slynan Chrissy sparkade mig."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:117
msgid "Hey, we never get any new blood around here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:118
msgid "So when are we going to get out of this stupid place?"
msgstr "När ska vi dra iväg från det här dumma stället?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:119
msgid "I don't know about you, but I think this sucks."
msgstr "Jag vet inte vad du tycker, men jag tycker att det här suger."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:120
msgid "There ain't nothin' to kill around here."
msgstr "De' e ju inge' att döda härikring."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:121
msgid "Where's the damn bathroom?"
msgstr "Var fan är toaletten?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:122
msgid "Hey, we never get a break around here. Isn't there some law or something?"
msgstr "Vi får aldrig nån rast här. Finns det ingen lag eller nåt?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:123
msgid "We should start up a government like in the old days."
msgstr "Vi borde starta en regering som förr i tiden."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:124
msgid "Man, I wonder what it was like to be President back then?"
msgstr "Asså, jag undrar hur det var att vara president på den tiden?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:125
msgid "I bet you could do anything you wanted if you were President."
msgstr "Jag slår vad om att du skulle kunna göra vad du ville om du var president."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:126
msgid "I think my father would be proud of me today. Too bad I killed him."
msgstr "Jag tror att min pappa skulle vara stolt över mig idag. Synd att jag dödade honom."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:127
msgid "I HATE RATS! HATE HATE HATE!"
msgstr "JAG HATAR RÅTTOR! HATAR HATAR HATAR!"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:128
msgid "Hey, is that new armor you have on? How do you rate getting new armor?"
msgstr "Är det ny rustning du har på dig? Vad tycker du om att ha ny rustning?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:129
msgid "This damn vault smells. Don't you hate it?"
msgstr "Det här jäkla valvet stinker. Visst hatar du det?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:130
msgid "Hey, who is it we're supposed to be keeping an eye open for?"
msgstr "Hörru, vem är det vi ska hålla ögonen öppna efter?"

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:131
msgid "All I do is stand, stand, stand."
msgstr "Allt jag gör är att stå, stå, stå."

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:132
msgid "I think we should just waste everyone upstairs and say to hell with this place."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:133
msgid "What the hell is your problem with rats?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:134
msgid "Have you ever pulled one of the legs off of a rat?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:135
msgid "I like guns, yeah! GUNS I LIKE! GUNS: I REALLY, REALLY LIKE THEM!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:136
msgid "Hey, is anyone listening to me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:137
msgid "Oh well, I just talk to keep myself sane anyway."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:138
msgid "Hey, anyone remember what was in a Long Island Ice Tea?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:139
msgid "Yeah, vodka, rum, tequila, triple sec, lime, and Nuka."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:140
msgid "Hey, look -- the lights came on. What the..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:141
msgid "Darion said he'd get the damn lights fixed. I guess he came through."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:142
msgid "I don't think the generator just fixes itself, does it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:143
msgid "That was kind of weird; now I can see. Jesus, this place looks like shit!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:144
msgid "Wow, it's bright in here. Where's the dimmer control?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcgengrd.msg:145 dialog/ccqmstr.msg:106 dialog/dcatkslv.msg:307
#: dialog/dcslvrun.msg:200 dialog/mcprotec.msg:152 game/cmbatai2.msg:2347
#: game/cmbatai2.msg:2548 game/cmbatai2.msg:3148 game/cmbatai2.msg:12148
#: game/cmbatai2.msg:32646 game/cmbatai2.msg:36147 game/cmbatai2.msg:36248
#: game/cmbatai2.msg:36347 game/cmbatai2.msg:36448 game/cmbatai2.msg:36547
#: game/combatai.msg:2347 game/combatai.msg:2548 game/combatai.msg:3148
#: game/combatai.msg:12148 game/combatai.msg:32646 game/combatai.msg:36147
#: game/combatai.msg:36248 game/combatai.msg:36347 game/combatai.msg:36448
#: game/combatai.msg:36547 game/combatai.msg:36854
msgid "Die!"
msgstr "Dö!"

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:101
msgid "You see John, the squatter."
msgstr "Du ser John, ockupanten."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:102
msgid "You see a middle-aged man wearing worn clothing."
msgstr "Du ser en medelålders man som bär slitna kläder."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:103
msgid "Sorry, stranger, I don't have time to chat with you."
msgstr "Ledsen, främling, jag har inte tid att prata med dig."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:104 dialog/scjohn.msg:104
msgid "Why no talk?"
msgstr "Varför prata inte?"

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:105
msgid "Okay, wavy."
msgstr "Okej, vågigt."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:106 dialog/scjohn.msg:106
msgid "All right, see ya."
msgstr "Okej, vi ses."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:107 dialog/scjohn.msg:107
msgid "Wait a minute. Why won't you talk to me?"
msgstr "Vänta lite nu. Varför vill du inte prata med mig?"

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:108
msgid ""
"We're a very private community here, and we don't want any trouble or interference from outside\n"
" sources. Please just leave us be."
msgstr ""
"Vi är ett mycket privat samhälle här, och vi vill inte ha några problem eller störningar från utomstående\n"
" källor. Snälla, låt oss bara vara."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:110 dialog/scjohn.msg:110
msgid "Hello... and good bye."
msgstr "Hej... och hej då."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:111
msgid "Thank you for all that you've done. I apologize for the cold shoulder earlier."
msgstr "Tack för allt du har gjort. Jag ber om ursäkt för det kalla bemötandet tidigare."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:112
msgid "Screw you, asshole!"
msgstr "Fan ta dig, skitstövel!"

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:113
msgid "Damn, I hate it when that happens."
msgstr "Fan, jag hatar när det händer."

#: dialog/bcjohn.msg:114
msgid "Take that! Yeah, that'll show ya."
msgstr "Ta den där! Ja, det ska du få se."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:100 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:100
msgid "You see a short man carrying a book in his hands."
msgstr "Du ser en kort man som bär en bok i sina händer."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:101
msgid "You see Doc Jones, the doctor."
msgstr "Du ser Doc Jones, doktorn."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:102
msgid "You see a short man with a book called \"So, You Want to be a Doctor.\""
msgstr "Du ser en kort man med en bok som heter \"Så, Du Vill bli Läkare.\""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:103
msgid "Hello, I'm Doc Jones. You can call me Doc. What can I help you with?"
msgstr "Hej, jag är Doc Jones. Du kan kalla mig Doc. Vad kan jag hjälpa dig med?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:104 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:104
msgid "Got owie. You fix?"
msgstr "Har aj-aj. Du fixa?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:105 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:105
msgid "Feel icky. You fix?"
msgstr "Mår dåligt. Du fixa?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:106 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:106
msgid "Me gimp, you fix?"
msgstr "Jag lam, du fixa?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:107 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:107
msgid "Got questions. Okay?"
msgstr "Har frågor. Okej?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:109 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:109
msgid "I'm injured. Can you help me?"
msgstr "Jag är skadad. Kan du hjälpa mig?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:110 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:110
msgid "I feel ill. Can you help me?"
msgstr "Jag känner mig sjuk. Kan ni hjälpa mig?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:111 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:111
msgid "I'm crippled. Can you help me?"
msgstr "Jag är handikappad. Kan du hjälpa mig?"

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:112 dialog/ccdoctor.msg:201 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:112
msgid "I wanted to ask you some questions."
msgstr "Jag vill ställa några frågor till dig."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:114
msgid ""
"Why, certainly. Here, we'll give you a shot of this -- this'll sting a bit -- now a bandage,\n"
" and there, you're all set."
msgstr ""
"Javisst. Här, vi ger dig en spruta av det här -- det här kommer att svida lite -- nu ett bandage,\n"
" och där, nu är allt klart."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:115 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:115
msgid "Me thank. Bye."
msgstr "Jag tacka. Hej då."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:116 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:116
msgid "Thanks, Doc. I feel much better."
msgstr "Tack, Doc. Jag känner mig mycket bättre."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:117
msgid ""
"Why, certainly. Here, you'll need to drink this -- all of it, I know it tastes foul. Now, just\n"
" lie down on the bed over there, and I'll wake you in the morning."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:118 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:118
msgid "Me feel good. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:119
msgid "Thanks Doc, that did the trick."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:120
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, but I don't have the proper facilities to perform surgery. I'd suggest you go to one\n"
" of the bigger cities and see a surgeon. Try Vault City. It's north of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:121
msgid "Okay. Bye"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:122 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:122
msgid "All right. Thanks anyway."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:123 dialog/dccaesar.msg:182 dialog/dcmaggie.msg:173
#: dialog/dcrebecc.msg:241 dialog/dctubby.msg:171 dialog/kcjenny.msg:290
#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:114 dialog/ocgoris.msg:122 dialog/ocjimmy.msg:118
#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:123 dialog/qcmartin.msg:126 dialog/rcdrjohn.msg:154
msgid "What would you like to know?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:124
msgid "You work Darion?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:125 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:125
msgid "You leave here when want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:126
msgid "What you know about Darion?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:127 dialog/ocdalia.msg:117 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:127
msgid "How you be here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:128
msgid "You say Darion got doggie?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:130 dialog/bczeke.msg:123
msgid "Do you work for Darion?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:131 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:130
msgid "Can you leave here if you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:132
msgid "What can you tell me about Darion?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:133 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:132
msgid "How did you come to be here in the first place?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:134
msgid "You mentioned Darion has a dog?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:135 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:133
msgid "Thanks for the information. I'll be heading out now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:136
msgid ""
"Well, yes and no. It's not by choice. I'm a prisoner here. Darion is getting up there in years\n"
" and he needs a dedicated physician to look after him. The Khans keep me here for his needs. I'd rather\n"
" be here for the people in the town above. They have no medical help at all, and there is a lot I can\n"
" do to aid them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:137 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:135
msgid "Okay. Need know more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:139 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:137
msgid "That's very commendable of you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:140 dialog/ocmatt.msg:153
msgid "I see. I'll be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:141
msgid "They're squatters! Let 'em die. Get on with your life."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:142
msgid ""
"No, I'm pretty much trapped here. I can't even leave to refill my medical supplies. Darion\n"
" sends out for anything I need."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:143 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:141
msgid "Me got it. Go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:144 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:142
msgid "Need ask more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:145
msgid "I guess you just aren't a trustworthy enough person to be allowed freedom."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:146
msgid "All right. I'm sorry, but I have to get going."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:147 dialog/bcjones.msg:158
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:148
msgid ""
"Darion is a mental case, plain and simple. He's got more spooks in his head than his dog has\n"
" fleas. As far as I can figure it, he was a member of another gang called the Khans. They kidnapped\n"
" this girl, Tandi, and held her for ransom. Her father didn't take kindly to that, and hired some merc\n"
" to get her back. Darion was the only one to come out alive."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:149 dialog/ocjimmy.msg:149 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:147
msgid "Uh... what you said."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:150 dialog/ocariel.msg:133 dialog/ocgordon.msg:134
#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:148
msgid "Got go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:151
msgid "Uh-huh. Well, I'll be leaving now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:152
msgid "Wow; I'm impressed with your knowledge."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:153
msgid "Sounds like my kind of guy."
msgstr "Låter som min typ av kille."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:154
msgid ""
"I was kidnapped. I was traveling from Vault City to New Reno for a well-deserved vacation. Went\n"
" to bed one night and woke up bound and gagged the next morning. A week or so later, I was here. Been\n"
" here ever since."
msgstr ""
"Jag blev kidnappad. Jag var på väg från Valvstaden till Nya Reno för en välförtjänt semester. Gick\n"
" till sängs en kväll och vaknade bunden och med munkavle nästa morgon. Runt en vecka senare var jag här. Har varit\n"
" här sedan dess."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:155 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:632 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:153
msgid "Ugh."
msgstr "Ugh."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:156 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:154
msgid "Thanks. Me be leave now."
msgstr "Tack. Jag gå nu."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:157
msgid "The weak are often the prey of the strong."
msgstr "De svaga är ofta de starkas byte."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:159
msgid "Interesting, but I need to get going."
msgstr "Intressant, men jag måste gå."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:160
msgid ""
"Yeah, he's got a dog. Personally, I think it's the meanest, most vile creature on the face of\n"
" the earth. It seems to love Darion, though, so I guess it can't be all that bad."
msgstr ""
"Ja, han har en hund. Personligen tycker jag att det är den elakaste, mest avskyvärda varelsen på\n"
" jorden. Den verkar dock älska Darion, så jag antar att den inte kan vara så illa."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:161 dialog/shtandi.msg:204
msgid "Me ask more."
msgstr "Frågar mer."

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:162
msgid "Uh, bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:163
msgid "I see. Well, thanks for the warning."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:164
msgid "Ah. Well, I've got to go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:165 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:158
msgid "I'll not help someone like you. Go away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:166
msgid "Okay, well, you take care, and come back if you need anything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:168
msgid ""
"Now he's paranoid. He believes that Tandi is out to get him. He's obsessed with revenge, and he\n"
" wants Tandi dead. He's riddled with guilt 'cause he hid and lived, rather than dying with his\n"
" gang... and the list goes on and on."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:200
msgid "Darion is dead."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:201
msgid "Dar-e-on dead."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:202
msgid "He is!? Oh, this is wonderful news."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:203 dialog/epac12.msg:250
msgid "What are you going to do now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:204
msgid "What yoo do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:205
msgid ""
"Well, I see no reason to return to my old life. The town above us doesn't have any medical assistance, so I think\n"
" I will go up and help them. Thank you again for freeing me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:206
msgid "Of course. See you later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:210
msgid "I still need to pack a few things. I'll see you on the outside."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:220
msgid ""
"Hey there, good to see you again! Everyone here really appreciates what you have done. I personally am glad\n"
" to be out of there. Working for Darion was a nightmare."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:221
msgid "Glad I could help. So, tell me a little bit more about yourself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:222
msgid "Alright, see you around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:230
msgid ""
"Well you see, I'm originally from the New California Republic, but I realized I had a gift for medical practices.\n"
" So I trained as much as I could under the NCR medical staff, and once I had learned all I could, I decided to try and\n"
" learn more by making my way to Vault City. I was lucky enough to meet Dr. Troy while he was tending an injured citizen\n"
" outside the vault, and long story short, he agreed to finalize my training in Vault City. I had just finished my training\n"
" and was heading out when Darion captured me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:231
msgid "That's terrible. Well, I hope everything works out for you now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:240
msgid "I hope so too. I think I can put my medical skills to good use here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:250
msgid "Thanks again for everything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcjones.msg:251
msgid "It feels good to be helping civilized people again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bckarla.msg:101
msgid "You see Karla, a Khan."
msgstr "Du ser Karla, en Khan."

#: dialog/bckarla.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a tough-looking woman in metal armor. She would be pretty, if it were not for the scars\n"
" that line her face."
msgstr ""
"Du ser en tuff kvinna i metallrustning. Hon skulle vara söt, om det inte vore för ärren\n"
" som kantar hennes ansikte."

#: dialog/bckarla.msg:103
msgid "Talk to Phil, shit head."
msgstr "Prata med Phil, din skitstövel."

#: dialog/bckarla.msg:104
msgid "Talk to Phil, bitch."
msgstr "Prata med Phil, slyna."

#: dialog/bckarla.msg:106
msgid "That little bitch is dead."
msgstr "Den lilla slynan är död."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:101
msgid "You see Phil, a Khan guard."
msgstr "Du ser Phil, en Khanvakt."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:102
msgid "You see a tough-looking young man in metal armor. He is heavily armed."
msgstr "Du ser en tuff ung man i metallrustning. Han är tungt beväpnad."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:103
msgid ""
"I should shoot you dead, but I'm kind of curious about what you could possibly have to say to\n"
" me."
msgstr ""
"Jag borde skjuta ihjäl dig, men jag är lite nyfiken på vad du kan tänkas ha att säga till\n"
" mig."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:104
msgid "Me look for spy. Go this way."
msgstr "Jag leta spion. Gå den här vägen."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:105
msgid "Me look for missing girl. You know where find?"
msgstr "Jag leta försvunnen flicka. Vet du var hitta?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:106
msgid "Me come here accident. Go now."
msgstr "Jag kom hit misstag. Gå nu."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:107
msgid "Screw you. Me shoot you dead."
msgstr "Fan ta dig. Jag skjuta dig död."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:108
msgid "Uh, we talk this out?"
msgstr "Eh, vi prata om det här?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:109
msgid "I'm looking for an eavesdropper who came this way."
msgstr "Jag letar efter en tjuvlyssnare som kom den här vägen."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:110
msgid "I'm looking for a missing girl. Seen her?"
msgstr "Jag letar efter en försvunnen flicka. Har du sett henne?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:111
msgid "Sorry, took the wrong trail by accident. Gotta go."
msgstr "Förlåt, jag råkade ta fel spår av misstag. Måste gå."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:112
msgid "Up yours and have a bullet breakfast, asshole."
msgstr "Kör upp den och ät en frukost av kulor, skitstövel."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:113
msgid "I think we can talk this out like two civilized beings."
msgstr "Jag tror att vi kan prata ut om det här som två civiliserade varelser."

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:114
msgid "Ah, that would be me. Now that you've found me, what's next?"
msgstr "Ah, det skulle vara jag. Nu när du har hittat mig, vad händer härnäst?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:115
msgid "Why you spy Rebecca?"
msgstr "Varför du spioner Rebecca?"

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:116
msgid "Now me know not be shooting wrong person. Thanks!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:117
msgid "Nothing, me go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:118
msgid "Why are you spying on Rebecca?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:119
msgid "Just wanted to make sure I'm shooting the right person. Thanks, and have a nice day!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:120
msgid "Hmm. Nothing, I guess I'll be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:121
msgid ""
"I can't believe that you think you can just waltz in here and get answers to your questions!\n"
" Oh, what the hell, you're about to die anyway and I feel generous. We've got her kid locked in the\n"
" back room and have been having some fun with her. That bitch, Rebecca, has been trying to find her, so\n"
" we've been keeping an eye open to make sure she doesn't get too close."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:122 dialog/bcphil.msg:148
msgid "You sicky in head. Me fix by remove head."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:123 dialog/bcphil.msg:149
msgid "What you mean have fun with girl?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:124
msgid "Oh, that explain. Me leave now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:125 dialog/bcphil.msg:151
msgid "You are one sick puppy. I think I'll put you to sleep now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:126 dialog/bcphil.msg:152
msgid "Fine, have fun and I'll be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:127 dialog/bcphil.msg:153
msgid "Hand over the girl and we can all leave here alive."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:128
msgid "Think about it as you die, stupid."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:131
msgid "Why in the hell should I do that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:132
msgid "It's good for your eternal soul."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:133
msgid ""
"Because I'm the worst thing that you could ever fear happening to you. Hand her over or feel\n"
" the pain."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:134
msgid ""
"Because if we fight, one of us will die. I don't want to die any more than you do, so let's end\n"
" this peacefully. Okay?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:135
msgid "Screw that noise."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:138
msgid "That sounds like a challenge. I'll take it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:141
msgid ""
"Hmm... I... Yeah, Okay. Here's the key to her cell; she's in the back room of the shack. Take her\n"
" and get out, but don't come back. If I see you again, we'll see who lives and who dies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:142
msgid "Let's see who comes out of this alive."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:143
msgid "Thanks, you did the right thing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:144
msgid "The only way you're leaving here is feet first, in a box."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:147
msgid "You mean the one locked up in back that we've been having fun with? No, I haven't seen her."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:150
msgid "Oh. Me leave now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:154
msgid "So, you've returned. Let's see who comes out on top."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcphil.msg:155
msgid "We killed that bitch Chrissy, and now it's your turn to die!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:100
msgid "You see an older woman."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:101 dialog/dcrebecc.msg:101
msgid "You see Rebecca."
msgstr "Du ser Rebecca."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see an older woman. Although she appears to have lived a hard life, she has not lost any of\n"
" her natural beauty."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:103
msgid "Hi, I'm Rebecca. Can we talk privately, please?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:104
msgid "What talk about?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:105 dialog/bcrebecc.msg:114
msgid "Why need talk private?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:107
msgid "No. Me leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:108 dialog/bcrebecc.msg:135
msgid "Sorry, not interested."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:109
msgid "What do you want to talk to me about?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:110
msgid "Sure, where can we go for privacy?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:111 dialog/bcrebecc.msg:117
msgid "Why the need for privacy?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:112
msgid ""
"(whispering) My daughter is missing and I need help finding her. I can't talk about it here,\n"
" though. Can we go somewhere private?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:115 dialog/fctnkbar.msg:106 dialog/fctnkgmr.msg:107
#: dialog/fctnkmer.msg:106
msgid "No, me go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:116
msgid "All right, let's go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:118
msgid "No thanks, I don't want to get involved."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:119
msgid ""
"(whispering) You may think I'm crazy but I get the feeling I'm being watched all the time. It's\n"
" rather disturbing, and I'm a bit on edge because of it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:120
msgid "Okay, we go private."
msgstr "Okej, vi gå privat."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:121
msgid "No time for sicky in head."
msgstr "Ingen tid för sjuk i huvudet."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:122
msgid "All right; where can we go to talk?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:123
msgid "Sorry, I don't like the sound of this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:124
msgid "Thanks; we can go to my tent."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:126
msgid "We should be able to talk here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:127
msgid "Okay, what problem?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:128
msgid "Me got questions first."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:129
msgid "Okay, so what's so important?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:130
msgid "I have some questions for you, first."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:131
msgid ""
"I have a daughter named Chrissy who's a bit of a tomboy. She likes to run around, explore,\n"
" and pretty much stick her nose into things. Chrissy's a good kid, though. She doesn't\n"
" cause trouble, she's always home on time and she's shown herself to be a very responsible young lady.\n"
" I let her do as she pleases most of the time. Last week Chrissy didn't come home. I've asked\n"
" around, and nobody's seen or heard from her. I tried to find her myself, but Zeke, he's... sort of the\n"
" mayor here... stopped me. He said it wasn't safe for me to go out looking on my own; he'd have some of\n"
" his men do it. They couldn't find her, either, and said that maybe the slavers got her."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:132
msgid "No, not get involved."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:133
msgid "Need think before decide."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:134
msgid "Ok, me seem be hero type lately."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:137
msgid "All right, Rebecca. I'll try to help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:138 dialog/tribec1.msg:364
msgid "If I help you, what's in it for me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:140 dialog/cccook.msg:115
msgid "What go on here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:141
msgid "Who boss?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:142
msgid "Me try find Vault 13. You know where is?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:143
msgid "Tell about vault."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:144
msgid "Tell about Darion."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:145
msgid "Thanks. We talk you problem?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:146 dialog/cccook.msg:120 dialog/vcmacrae.msg:117
#: dialog/vcmacrae.msg:135
msgid "What's going on around here?"
msgstr "Vad är på gång häromkring?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:147
msgid "Who's in charge around here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:148
msgid "I'm looking for Vault 13. Do you know anything about it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:149
msgid "Tell me about the vault."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:150
msgid "So tell me about Darion."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:151
msgid "Thanks Rebecca. Let's talk about your problem now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:152
msgid ""
"We call this place the 'Squat' because it was settled by the homeless of many cities. It's not\n"
" much, but it's all we have. To the west is a city called the NCR. They've known about us for quite some\n"
" time, and never offered us any kind of help or hindrance. Now, they are suddenly claiming this area as their\n"
" ancestral home, and they want it back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:154
msgid "What here they want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:156
msgid "What is here that they want so badly?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:157
msgid ""
"Well... there is a vault here; I think it's number 15. They want to loot it for any of the old\n"
" technology that may still be there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:158
msgid "Ah. Me understand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:159
msgid "I knew there had to be something here other than the waste-of-flesh inhabitants."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:161
msgid "That explains a lot. You've been very helpful. I need to ask some more questions, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:162
msgid ""
"That would be Zeke. He runs everything up here. You can find him in the building over there.\n"
" ::points north-east::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:163
msgid "Thanks. Ask more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:164
msgid "Thank you. I need to ask you some more questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:165
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, I have no idea. I would ask about it in NCR. They've taken a great interest in\n"
" vaults lately."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:166 dialog/ccxarn.msg:116
msgid "Okay, me do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:167
msgid "All right, I will."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:168
msgid ""
"Well... we're not supposed to talk about it, but since I need your help... The vault is being\n"
" repaired by Darion. He's our benefactor. When it's fully functional, we're all supposed to move in\n"
" where we'll be safe from raiders, slavers, and such. So far he has the food and water systems up, but\n"
" that's about it."
msgstr ""
"Så... Vi får inte prata om det, men eftersom jag behöver din hjälp... Valvet håller på att\n"
" reparerat av Darion. Han är vår välgörare. När det är fullt fungerande, ska vi alla flytta in.\n"
" där vi kommer att vara säkra från plundrare, slavhandlare och liknande. Än så länge har han mat- och vattensystemen uppe, men\n"
" det är typ allt."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:169
msgid "Me see. Need know more."
msgstr "Förstår. Behöva veta mer."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:170
msgid "I need to know more."
msgstr "Jag behöver veta mer."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:171
msgid ""
"There's not much to say, really. Darion keeps to himself and never leaves the vault. If he has\n"
" anything to say, he says it through Zeke. I've only met him once, and he seemed like a nice guy."
msgstr ""
"Det finns inte mycket att säga, egentligen. Darion håller sig för sig själv och lämnar aldrig valvet. Om han har\n"
" något att säga, så säger han det genom Zeke. Jag har bara träffat honom en gång, och han verkade vara en trevlig kille."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:173
msgid "Nice guys finish last. I wonder what he's up to?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:175
msgid "That's okay. You are very helpful."
msgstr "Det är okej. Du är väldigt hjälpsam."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:176
msgid "I have nothing to give you other than my undying gratitude."
msgstr "Jag har inget annat att ge dig än min eviga tacksamhet."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:177
msgid "That's more than enough. I'll help you."
msgstr "Det är mer än tillräckligt. Jag tänker hjälpa dig."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:178
msgid "It'll take more than that to buy my help."
msgstr "Det krävs mer än så för att köpa min hjälp."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:179
msgid "What the hell, I'll help you."
msgstr "Vad fan, jag tänker hjälpa dig."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:180
msgid ""
"Thank you so much. I'll never be able to repay you for this. I'll wait here until you bring...\n"
" Hey, there was someone outside listening to us! I saw their shadow on the tent wall. They just ran off\n"
" that way! ::points north-east:: They must have heard everything!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:181
msgid "Me stop, no get away!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:182
msgid "You no worry, me find girl."
msgstr "Du inte oroa, hittar flicka."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:183 dialog/ccquincy.msg:130
msgid "Ooops."
msgstr "Ojdå."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:184
msgid "I'll try and stop them."
msgstr "Jag ska försöka stoppa dem."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:185
msgid "They won't stop me from finding your daughter."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:186
msgid "Oh well. Shit happens."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:187
msgid "Please, just go away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:188
msgid "Have you thought things through?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:189
msgid "Me ask questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:190
msgid "No, still think."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:191
msgid "No, I'm still considering everything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:192
msgid "I want to ask you some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:193
msgid "Have you changed your mind? Will you help me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:194
msgid "Sorry, no."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:195
msgid "Me help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:196
msgid "Yes, I'll help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:197
msgid ""
"You must be the person who saved my daughter. I can never repay you for your kindness. Thank you.\n"
" Please wait here, I need to talk to Chrissy and then I'd like to talk to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:198
msgid ""
"You saved my daughter. I can never repay you for your kindness. Thank you.\n"
" Please wait here, I need to talk to Chrissy and then I'd like to talk to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:200
msgid ""
"My daughter has told me everything. I find it hard to believe that Darion is such a monster\n"
" after all he's been doing for us. And to think, we've been helping him hide his operations as a raider.\n"
" I can guarantee you we won't stand for it any longer. I've already talked to Zeke, and he wants to see\n"
" you. You should go see him now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:201
msgid ""
"I find it hard to believe that Darion is such a monster after all he's been doing for us. And to\n"
" think, we've been helping him hide his operations as a raider. I can guarantee you we won't stand for\n"
" it any longer. I'll talk to Zeke and explain everything. I'm sure he'll want to see you. You should go\n"
" talk to him later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:203
msgid "I hope you find Chrissy soon."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:204
msgid "Me looking."
msgstr "Letar."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:205
msgid "I'll continue to search for her."
msgstr "Jag kommer att fortsätta leta efter henne."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:206
msgid "Thanks for everything you've done for me."
msgstr "Tack för allt du har gjort för mig."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:207
msgid ""
"I can't explain why, but I don't believe the slavers took her. I've an uneasy feeling that\n"
" something else is going on. And then there's this feeling that I'm being followed. I've had it ever\n"
" since I talked to Zeke about Chrissy. I need someone to help me find my daughter. Will you help me,\n"
" please?"
msgstr ""
"Jag kan inte förklara varför, men jag tror inte att slavhandlarna tog henne. Jag har en obehaglig känsla av att\n"
" något annat år på gång. Och så känner jag mig förföljd. Jag har haft det ända\n"
" sedan jag pratade med Zeke om Chrissy. Jag behöver nån som hjälper mig att hitta min dotter. Vill du hjälpa mig,\n"
" snälla?"

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:208
msgid ""
"They keep sending people here to try and talk us out of our home, but they don't understand\n"
" that we have nowhere else to go. We don't have the skills necessary to survive on our own if we leave\n"
" here."
msgstr ""
"De fortsätter skicka hit folk för att övertyga oss om att lämna vårt hem, men de förstår inte\n"
" att vi inte har någon annanstans att ta vägen. Vi har inte de färdigheter som krävs för att överleva på egen hand om vi flyttar\n"
" härifrån."

#: dialog/bcrebecc.msg:209
msgid ""
"You know, it's kind of funny that they managed to get something that complex fixed, but not the\n"
" lights. The damn place is lit by torches. Anyway, Darion doesn't want anyone to know what's going on\n"
" with the vault. He's afraid that someone will take it all away from us if they find out. So, we're told\n"
" to drive off anyone who shows up here -- especially the NCR."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:101
msgid "You see Roberta, a squatter."
msgstr "Du ser Roberta, en husockupant."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:102 dialog/bcsara.msg:102
msgid "You see a middle aged woman wearing worn clothing."
msgstr "Du ser en medelålders kvinna som bär slitna kläder."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:103
msgid "Oh, my. I'm sorry, but I have nothing to say to you. Please go away."
msgstr "Åh, herre. Jag är ledsen, men jag har inget att säga till dig. Var snäll och gå härifrån."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:104
msgid "Please go away. I don't want to be bothered."
msgstr "Snälla, gå härifrån. Jag vill inte bli störd."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:105
msgid "Thanks for helping out Rebecca. I was wrong about you."
msgstr "Tack för att du hjälpte Rebecca. Jag hade fel om dig."

#: dialog/bcrobert.msg:106 dialog/bcsara.msg:106
msgid "I'm no threat to you. Please don't kill me."
msgstr "Jag är inget hot mot dig. Snälla, döda mig inte."

#: dialog/bcsara.msg:101
msgid "You see Sara, a squatter."
msgstr "Du ser Sara, en husockupant."

#: dialog/bcsara.msg:103
msgid "Please don't bother me; I'm really busy right now."
msgstr "Var snäll och stör mig inte, jag är väldigt upptagen just nu."

#: dialog/bcsara.msg:104
msgid "Please go away. There's nothing here for you."
msgstr "Snälla, gå härifrån. Det finns inget här för dig."

#: dialog/bcsara.msg:105
msgid "Thanks for helping out Rebecca. It was a wonderful thing for you to do for a stranger."
msgstr "Tack för att du hjälpte Rebecca. Det var underbart av dig att göra det för en främling."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:100
msgid "You see an older squatter."
msgstr "Du ser en äldre husockupant."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:101
msgid "You see Zeke, a squatter."
msgstr "Du ser Zeke, en husockupant."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:102
msgid "You see an older man with thinning, white hair."
msgstr "Du ser en äldre man med tunt, vitt hår."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:103
msgid ""
"My name's Zeke, stranger. I'm sorry, but I don't have time to talk to you -- and I don't think\n"
" there's anything in this town for you, anyway. You should move on."
msgstr ""
"Jag heter Zeke, främling. Jag är ledsen, men jag har inte tid att prata med dig -- och jag tror inte\n"
" att det finns något för dig i den här stan. Du borde gå vidare."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:104 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:752 dialog/gcbrain.msg:501
#: dialog/ncwriply.msg:631 dialog/ocariel.msg:141 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:234
#: dialog/ockerith.msg:124 dialog/vcgatgrd.msg:188
msgid "Uh, okay."
msgstr "Eh, okej."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:106
msgid "All right, I'll leave."
msgstr "Okej, jag ska gå."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:107
msgid "I just wanted to ask a couple of questions."
msgstr "Jag ville bara ställa ett par frågor."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:108
msgid ""
"Well, I think you'll find that we're all out of answers here. Why don't you come back when we\n"
" get a shipment in?"
msgstr ""
"Jag tror att du kommer att upptäcka att vi har slut på svar här. Varför kommer du inte tillbaka när vi\n"
" får in en leverens?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:110
msgid ""
"Hello, again. I still don't have any answers for you, stranger. Why don't you take a hint and\n"
" get the duck out of fodge?"
msgstr ""
"Hej, igen. Jag har fortfarande inga svar åt dig, främling. Varför hajar du inte och\n"
" hrar åt delvete?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:112
msgid ""
"Rebecca has told me what you did for her. I want to apologize for the treatment you received\n"
" here. You certainly didn't deserve it. What can I help you with?"
msgstr ""
"Rebecca har berättat vad du gjorde för henne. Jag vill be om ursäkt för den behandling du fick\n"
" här. Du förtjänade det verkligen inte. Vad kan jag hjälpa dig med?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:114
msgid "Nothing. Wavy."
msgstr "Inget. Vinkis."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:115
msgid "I've got some questions for you."
msgstr "Jag har några frågor till dig."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:116
msgid "Nothing for now, thanks."
msgstr "Inget för tillfället, tack."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:118
msgid "You work for Darion?"
msgstr "Jobbar 'u för Darion?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:119
msgid "What you do about raiders?"
msgstr "Vad gör ni åt plundrare?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:120
msgid "Where vault door?"
msgstr "Var valvdörr?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:121
msgid "Anything else go on here?"
msgstr "Något annat händer här?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:122 dialog/ocsandy.msg:114
msgid "Me leave now."
msgstr "Jag gå nu."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:124
msgid "What do you intend to do about the raiders?"
msgstr "Vad tänker du göra åt plundrarna?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:125
msgid "Where is the vault entrance?"
msgstr "Var är ingången till valvet?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:126
msgid "Is there anything else going on around here?"
msgstr "Är det något annat på gång här?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:127
msgid "I guess that's it. I'll be going now."
msgstr "Jag antar att det var allt. Jag ska gå nu."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:128
msgid ""
"Yes, I do. I act as the middle man between him and the people up here. I'm not very happy about\n"
" the fact, now that I know what he's up to."
msgstr ""
"Ja, det gör jag. Jag agerar mellanhand mellan honom och folket här uppe. Jag är inte särskilt glad över\n"
" det faktumet, nu när jag vet vad han håller på med."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:131
msgid ""
"Nothing. They have the guns, they control the water, and they control the food. That means\n"
" they are in charge. Period. We have no skills and no means of support without the backing of Darion.\n"
" How can we turn against him? We're at his mercy."
msgstr ""
"Ingenting. De har vapnen, de kontrollerar vattnet och de kontrollerar maten. Det betyder\n"
" att de bestämmer. Punkt slut. Vi har inga färdigheter och inget stöd utan Darions hjälp.\n"
" Hur kan vi vända oss mot honom? Vi är utlämnade till hans nåd."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:132
msgid "Hmm. Me think me understand."
msgstr "Hmm. Jag tro förstå."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:133
msgid "Hmm. I see."
msgstr "Hmm. Jag förstår."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:134
msgid ""
"It's behind that door over there, but it's locked from the other side and trapped, too. I don't have\n"
" any means of opening it... Wait a minute. I found this key card some time ago, and I have no idea what\n"
" it is for. Rebecca says that you found some sort of door where they were holding Chrissy. Maybe this\n"
" card will open it. Here, take it."
msgstr ""
"Den är bakom dörren där borta, men den är låst från andra sidan och kopplad tillfällor också. Jag har inte\n"
" något sätt att öppna den... Vänta lite nu. Jag hittade det här nyckelkortet för ett tag sedan, och jag har ingen aning om vad\n"
" det är till för. Rebecca säger att du hittade nån sorts dörr där de höll Chrissy. Kanske det här\n"
" kortet kan öppna den. Här, ta det."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:135 dialog/scwesgrd.msg:132
msgid "Me thank you."
msgstr "Jag tack dig."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:136
msgid "Thanks. I'll give it a try."
msgstr "Tack. Jag ska försöka med det."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:137
msgid ""
"There's a city west of here called NCR. They claim Vault 15 is their ancestral home and they want it\n"
" back. They've been sending people here trying to talk us into leaving but we aren't going for it. This is the only home we know."
msgstr ""
"Det finns en stad västerut som heter NKR. De hävdar att Valv 15 är deras förfäders hem och de vill ha det\n"
" tillbaka. De har skickat hit folk för att försöka övertala oss att ge oss av, men vi går inte med på det. Det här är det enda hem vi känner till."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:138
msgid "You maybe make deal NCR?"
msgstr "Du kanske gör möte NKR?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:139
msgid "Would you consider making a deal with NCR?"
msgstr "Kan ni tänka er att arrangera ett möte med NKR?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:140
msgid "That all depends. What did you have in mind?"
msgstr "Det beror helt på. Vad hade du tänkt dig?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:141
msgid "Join NCR tribe. Learn from elders. Give NCR you permission enter vault. Both happy."
msgstr "Gå med NKR-stam. Lär från de äldste. Ge NKR er tillstånd gå i valvet. Båda glada."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:142
msgid ""
"Join NCR, let them annex your territory, and give them access to the vault. In return, they can teach you all the skills\n"
" you need to survive on your own and offer you their protection."
msgstr ""
"Gå med i NKR, låt dem annektera ert territorium och ge dem tillgång till valvet. I gengäld kan de lära er alla färdigheter\n"
" ni behöver för att överleva på egen hand och erbjuda er sitt skydd."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:143
msgid ""
"Not bad... I like it. You've got yourself a deal if you can get NCR to agree to it as well. But...\n"
" Look, someone has to take care of Darion and his cronies. It should be done now before they realize what has happened\n"
" and have time to prepare for an attack. Why not get this over with and take Darion out now?\n"
" You'll have the element of surprise on your side."
msgstr ""
"Inte illa... Jag gillar det. Vi går med på det om du kan få NKR att acceptera det också. Men...\n"
" Lyssna, någon måste ta hand om Darion och hans kumpaner. Det bör göras nu innan de inser vad som har hänt\n"
" och har tid att förbereda sig för en attack. Varför inte få det här överstökat och ta Darion nu?\n"
" Du har överraskningsmomentet på din sida."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:144
msgid "You right, me take care of."
msgstr "Du rätt, jag löser."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:145
msgid "Me not sure."
msgstr "Jag inte säker."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:146
msgid "Yeah, I guess it has to be done."
msgstr "Ja, jag antar att det måste göras."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:147 dialog/ccmaster.msg:150 dialog/gcharold.msg:289
#: dialog/ncorvill.msg:673 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:334 dialog/scofjack.msg:147
#: dialog/vclynett.msg:824
msgid "I don't know."
msgstr "Jag vet inte."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:148
msgid "Excellent. Good luck to you, and thank you."
msgstr "Utmärkt. Lycka till och tack så mycket."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:150
msgid ""
"Well, take the time to think about it, but know this -- until Darion is out of the picture, I\n"
" have no choice but to maintain things around here as they are. It's for the safety of everyone\n"
" concerned. That means no deal and you are still persona non grata. Understand?"
msgstr ""
"Ta dig tid att tänka på det, men vet detta -- tills Darion är ute ur bilden, har\n"
" jag inget annat val än att behålla saker här som de är. Det är för alla berördas\n"
" säkerheten. Det betyder inget avtal och du är fortfarande persona non grata. Förstått?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:152
msgid "Hi. I'm still waiting for a final resolution to our troubles. In other words, kick Darion's ass!"
msgstr "Hej. Jag väntar fortfarande på en slutgiltig lösning på våra problem. Med andra ord, spöa Darion!"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:154
msgid ""
"You've done it, friend! We're no longer under Darion's yoke. Thank you! I'm ready to accept your deal with NCR now.\n"
" Just have them send one of their reps by and I'll seal the deal."
msgstr ""
"Du har gjort det, min vän! Vi släpar inte längre Darions ok. Tack så mycket! Jag är redo att acceptera ditt avtal med NKR nu.\n"
" Be dem bara skicka en av sina representanter så ska jag signera avtalet."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:156
msgid "Thanks for the chance of a new life. We all owe you."
msgstr "Tack för att du gav oss chansen till ett nytt liv. Vi står alla i din skuld."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:157
msgid "Just go away. I have nothing to say to you."
msgstr "Bara gå härifrån. Jag har inget att säga till dig."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:158
msgid ""
"Wait, before you go... I found this key card some time ago, and I have no idea what it's for.\n"
" Rebecca says that you found some sort of entrance where they were holding Chrissy. Maybe this card will\n"
" open it. Here, take it."
msgstr ""
"Vänta, innan du går... Jag hittade det här nyckelkortet för ett tag sen, och jag har ingen aning om vad det är till för.\n"
" Rebecca säger att du hittade nån sorts ingång där de höll Chrissy. Kanske det här kortet kommer\n"
" öppna den. Här, ta det."

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:160 dialog/ccatech.msg:109 dialog/cctech1.msg:109
#: dialog/cctech2.msg:109 dialog/fcfmatt.msg:110 dialog/mcbaltha.msg:163
#: dialog/ockerith.msg:104 dialog/rcmodjes.msg:129 dialog/vcandy.msg:204
msgid "What can I help you with?"
msgstr "Vad kan jag hjälpa dig med?"

#: dialog/bczeke.msg:161
