msgid "The name doesn't ring a bell, but then again I don't keep track of who comes in and out of town. Check with Becky. Everyone ends up going through there. She might know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:240
msgid "If you didn't come to the Den for a specific reason you should probably leave. It's not very safe around here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:243
msgid "I can handle myself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:244 dialog/dclara.msg:253 dialog/dclara.msg:342
#: dialog/dcmetzge.msg:432 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:461 dialog/dcrebecc.msg:334
#: dialog/dcrebecc.msg:342 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:323 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:416
#: dialog/dcvicgrd.msg:298 dialog/dcvicgrd.msg:313 dialog/ocgordon.msg:140
#: dialog/vcgatgrd.msg:143 dialog/vcoldjoe.msg:118
msgid "Okay, thanks."
msgstr "Okej, tack."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:250
msgid "No doubt. Otherwise you probably wouldn't have made it here alive."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:251
msgid "Uh, yes, so I heard. You said that already."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:260
msgid "Well it depends on what you're good at. There is something I'm curious about. If you can find out, I'll pay you a bit."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:261
msgid "As I said, I'm looking for more information on a certain something... or someplace. I'll pay of course."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:262
msgid "Sure what's that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:263 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:524 dialog/epac9.msg:212
#: dialog/fcoz7.msg:149 dialog/fsface.msg:143 dialog/scmerk.msg:208
msgid "Maybe later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:270
msgid "Let me know if you change your mind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:280
msgid ""
"Well, there's a church east of here. Metzger has some people guarding whatever\n"
" is inside. Find out what and I'll pay you $200."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:281
msgid "That was easy. I already know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:290
msgid "Thanks. Don't get in a fight... yet. I have a plan."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:292
msgid "I'll be right back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:300 dialog/dcsmitty.msg:461 dialog/dctubfri.msg:261
#: dialog/epac17.msg:411 dialog/epac17.msg:532 dialog/rcascort.msg:131
#: dialog/rcmarge.msg:151
msgid "What's that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:301 dialog/dclara.msg:391
msgid "Raw chemical compounds in large crates."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:302 dialog/dclara.msg:392
msgid "Big containers holding chemicals of some kind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:303
msgid "Let me check again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:310
msgid "That makes sense actually. Thanks. Here's your money."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:311 dialog/qcbird.msg:122 dialog/rcdrjohn.msg:224
msgid "Why is that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:312 dialog/hcenchb.msg:125 dialog/hczaius.msg:152
#: dialog/scvortis.msg:170
msgid "No problem. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:320
msgid "I've seen caravans from Vault City come in and then some of it gets picked up by caravans from New Reno."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:321
msgid "So? Why does that make sense?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:340
msgid "New Reno is the drug capital around here. They have to get the raw materials to make their drugs from somewhere, right? It seems like they're getting some, or all of it, from Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:350
msgid "Not sure exactly. Somewhere to the south I think. I've never been there, I just see their caravans stop by once in a while - once in a long while."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:351 dialog/gcbrain.msg:506
msgid "Oh, okay. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:360
msgid "You looking for some more quick and easy cash? $50. Easy money."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:362 dialog/ncrenesc.msg:700
msgid "Make it quick."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:370
msgid "I need you to check with Metzger to see if he'd be okay if Tyler and I settled some old matters. He'll understand what I mean."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:371
msgid "Why do you want me to ask?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:372
msgid "If I get a chance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:380
msgid "Because I don't want Tyler to see any of my people going into or out of Metzger's place. I don't want to tip our hand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:381
msgid "Don't you get it? If Tyler sees me all of a sudden talking to Metzger he might catch wind of something fishy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:382 dialog/dcsheila.msg:179
msgid "We'll see."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:390
msgid "So did you find out what's in there?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:400
msgid "So did you talk to him yet? What did he say?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:401
msgid "He said yes. If you win, you can have their job, like before."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:402 dialog/dclara.msg:474 dialog/dcmetzge.msg:264
msgid "Na."
msgstr "Na."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:410
msgid "Great. I was hoping as much. I hear he's been complaining about them lately. Here's your money."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:411
msgid "I assume there's something else now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:420
msgid "I have one more job for you. I'm not sure how you'll do it, but since you were able to get inside maybe they trust you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:421
msgid "I snuck inside."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:422 dialog/dcrebecc.msg:481 dialog/hctyphon.msg:124
#: dialog/hiwell.msg:140 dialog/vcdrtroy.msg:164 dialog/vcmclure.msg:332
#: dialog/vcrandal.msg:211 dialog/vcstark.msg:349
msgid "What is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:430
msgid "I'm sure you can figure something out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:431
msgid "Okay, what is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:440
msgid ""
"We can't take them at their present strength. They have extra funding\n"
" and slightly outnumber us. If you can find some kind of weakness we could use\n"
" to balance out the odds or something we can exploit..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:441
msgid "Huh? Find a weakness? How am I supposed to do that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:443
msgid "Consider it done."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:450
msgid "We'll give you $150. There's no way we can get close enough to find out by ourselves."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:451
msgid "If I get around to it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:460
msgid "I don't know. That's why I'm asking you to help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:461 game/proto.msg:674 game/skill.msg:1005
msgid "I'll try."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:462
msgid "This is pointless."
msgstr "Det här är meningslöst."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:470
msgid "Did you find anything?"
msgstr "Hittade du något?"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:471
msgid "Yes. They're having a party tonight."
msgstr "Ja. De ska ha fest ikväll."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:473
msgid "Gra."
msgstr "Gra."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:480
msgid ""
"Excellent! They're sure to leave a skeleton crew. Those should be good\n"
" odds. We'll take out those at the party after we hit the church."
msgstr ""
"Utmärkt! De kommer säkert att lämna ett skelett av personal. Det borde vara bra\n"
" odds. Vi ger oss på de som är på festen efter att vi har slagit till mot kyrkan."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:481
msgid "And my money?"
msgstr "Och mina pengar?"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:490
msgid ""
"I don't think so. You'll have to come with us if you want your money. You\n"
" won't have to fight but just to be sure it's not a trap. We'll give you $300 total."
msgstr ""
"Jag tror inte det. Du måste följa med oss om du vill ha dina pengar. Du\n"
" behöver inte slåss, men bara för att vara säker på att det inte är en fälla. Vi ger dig $300 totalt."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:491 dialog/ecravpty.msg:179
msgid "You ready?"
msgstr "Är du redo?"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:492
msgid "Okay, let's do it."
msgstr "Okej, då gör vi det."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:493
msgid "Give me a bit to get ready."
msgstr "Ge mig lite tid att göra mig redo."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:494
msgid "No way. Keep your money!"
msgstr "Inte en chans. Behåll dina pengar!"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:500
msgid "Okay, but we've got to act soon so don't take too long or we'll ruin our chance."
msgstr "Okej, men vi måste agera snart, så ta inte för lång tid på dig, för då förstör vi vår chans."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:510
msgid "You don't have to fight. Easy money."
msgstr "Du behöver inte slåss. Lättförtjänta pengar."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:511
msgid "Well, have you changed your mind?"
msgstr "Nå, har du ändrat dig?"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:512
msgid "Let's go. I'm ready."
msgstr "Nu kör vi. Jag är redo."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:513
msgid "Okay, I'll be right back."
msgstr "Okej, jag kommer strax tillbaka."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:515
msgid "Uk"
msgstr "Uk"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:520
msgid "Because of you we blew our chance."
msgstr "På grund av dig sumpade vi vår chans."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:521
msgid "Coward!"
msgstr "Ynkrygg!"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:522
msgid "You get nothing."
msgstr "Du får ingenting."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:523
msgid "It was probably a trap anyhow."
msgstr "Det var nog en fälla ändå."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:524
msgid "Sorry, you're not reliable."
msgstr "Tyvärr, du är inte pålitlig."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:525
msgid "I can't trust you."
msgstr "Jag kan inte lita på dig."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:532
msgid "Special thanks to you!"
msgstr "Ett särskilt tack till dig!"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:533
msgid "I've finally paid Tyler back for what he did to my brother."
msgstr "Jag har äntligen givit igen för mot Tyler för vad han gjorde mot min bror."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:534
msgid "Thank you again."
msgstr "Tack igen."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:540
msgid "Now that Metzger's dead, I don't know what'll happen."
msgstr "Nu när Metzger är död vet jag inte vad som kommer att hända."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:541
msgid "Maybe we should just pack up."
msgstr "Vi kanske bara ska packa ihop."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:542
msgid "Did you hear Metzger died? I don't know what to do now."
msgstr "Hörde du att Metzger dog? Jag vet inte vad jag ska göra nu."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:543
msgid "What's going to happen to the Den now? Maybe something better."
msgstr "Vad kommer att hända med Lyan nu? Kanske något bättre."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:544
msgid "This could actually be for the better."
msgstr "Detta kan faktiskt vara till det bättre."

#: dialog/dclara.msg:550 dialog/ectrader.msg:136 game/cmbatai2.msg:1682
#: game/cmbatai2.msg:36082 game/combatai.msg:1682 game/combatai.msg:36082
msgid "Bastard!"
msgstr "Din jävel!"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:551 dialog/mcmiria.msg:150 dialog/ncboxer.msg:342
#: game/combatai.msg:18147
msgid "Bitch!"
msgstr "Subba!"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:560
msgid "Thanks. Here's your money and $100 extra."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:570
msgid "Did you kill Tyler and his guards? How are we supposed to prove ourselves to Metzger? He'll never hire us now. That was our only chance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:571
msgid "We don't have any work. Someone killed off Metzger's guards and now he won't talk to us. He thinks we did it. Oh well."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:573
msgid "Too bad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:574
msgid "That was me, and you're next."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:575
msgid "Oh. Okay, bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:576
msgid "Uhr?"
msgstr "Uhr?"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:590
msgid "I told you we would go together. Since no one was there to watch the place, it got ransacked and now Metzger's madder than hell."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:591
msgid "I told you to find a weakness, not kill them! Since no one was there to watch the place, it got ransacked and now Metzger's madder than hell."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:592
msgid "Damn it! I told you to ask Metzger, not to kill them! Since no one was there to watch the place, it got ransacked and now Metzger's madder than hell."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:593
msgid "Damn it! I told you not to attack them! Since no one was there to watch the place, it got ransacked and now Metzger's madder than hell."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:594
msgid "Oh, well, I've got to go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:595
msgid "That's a shame."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:596
msgid "You're next, bitch."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:597
msgid "Hmph!"
msgstr "Hmph!"

#: dialog/dclara.msg:598
msgid "You next."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:610
msgid "You really know how to screw things up, don't you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:611
msgid "We don't need any more of your help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:612
msgid "Go bother someone else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:613
msgid "Metzger better not take anything out on us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:614 dialog/wsterm3b.msg:173 dialog/wsterm3b.msg:177
msgid "I'm sorry. I can't help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:615
msgid "Can't talk. I'm trying to figure out what to do now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:616
msgid "I hope Metzger doesn't think we were involved."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:617
msgid "What are we going to do now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:618
msgid "We better leave soon in case Metzger thinks we killed his guards."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:619
msgid "You ever been to New Reno? Maybe we'll head there - or north."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:650
msgid "Alright! Let's go! Everyone follow me!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:700
msgid ""
"Alright, we took care of the skeleton crew here at the church, but there still is Tyler and his cronies over in the Residential area.\n"
" They should be pretty drunk by now and we can easily catch them off guard. You ready to finish this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:720
msgid "Well, don't stray too far. We need to finish this tonight or we'll do it without you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:721
msgid "I'll be back shortly."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclara.msg:730
msgid "We did it. I can't believe it! We're heading back to the church to take charge. Meet us back there for your reward."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:100
msgid "You see a middle aged man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:101
msgid "He is unshaven and reeks of alcohol."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:102
msgid "*hickup* Do I know you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:103
msgid "It's 11 O'clock. Do you know where your children are?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:104
msgid "(Looks at you sleepily) What? *hickup* It's 11 already?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:105
msgid "Actually no it isn't, I just wanted to say that. But seriously, do you know where your children are?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:106
msgid "Actually yeah it is, but that's not important right now. Seriously though, do you know where your children are?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:107
msgid "*hickup* I have children? *hickup* Oh yeah, I do. He..or is it she..*hickup* should be around here somewhere."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:108
msgid "Wow, you're such a drunk. Well, good thing I am working on a way to get your child out of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:109
msgid "(Ignores what you just said.) Yeah that's great. *hickup* Now let me get back to this drink."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:110
msgid "You are a hero to all fathers out there. Keep it up!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:111
msgid "zzzZZZZzzz..."
msgstr "zzzZZZZzzz..."

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:112
msgid "zZZZZzzZZzzz..."
msgstr "zZZZZzzZZzzz..."

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:113
msgid "*mumbles*"
msgstr "*mumlar*"

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:114
msgid "Can't you see I'm drinking here? *hickup*"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:115
msgid "Don't bother me. *hickup*"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:116
msgid "Actually it is a little before 11 O'clock, but that's not important right now. Seriously though, do you know where your children are?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclbfthr.msg:117
msgid "Actually it is a little past 11 O'clock, but that's not important right now. Seriously though, do you know where your children are?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:100 dialog/dcpeasnt.msg:400 dialog/mcchild.msg:100
#: dialog/mcjonny.msg:100 dialog/vilchild.msg:100
msgid "You see a small boy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:101
msgid "You see Little Bobby."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:102
msgid "He is wearing dirty clothing and has bruises on his neck and face."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:103
msgid "He is wearing new clothing and has a smile on his face."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:104
msgid "Hi mister! My name's Bobby and I live here with my Dad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:105
msgid "Hi miss! My name's Bobby and I live here with my Dad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:106
msgid "I see. Well tha-"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:107
msgid ""
"Are you here 'cause my dad owes you money? I don't know if he's here or not. But if I knew where he was,\n"
" I'd tell you, 'cause maybe you'd beat him up so bad he wouldn't ever come home again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:108
msgid "This sounds horrible, Bobby. Your father has no right to treat you that way -- no parent does."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:109
msgid "Hah! I'd beat my son too if he didn't listen to me. Your father sounds like a good man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:110
msgid ""
"[His eyes light up.] You aren't like the others that come through here. I like you. [He sighs heavily.]\n"
" I wish my dad was more like you. Sometimes I think about running away. Some of my friends don't have homes, and they say\n"
" it's not so bad. As long as they bring Mr. Flick enough things, they get to eat once a day. But Mr. Flick doesn't sound very\n"
" nice either -- actually, he sounds a lot like my dad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:111
msgid "You're a meanie! Go away. I don't like you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:112
msgid ""
"There's gotta be something that can be done about this. Can you think of any adults in this town that'd be willing to\n"
" look after you -- or any of these homeless kids?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:113
msgid ""
"[Bobby shrugs.] Maybe Mom? I don't mean *my* mom -- my mom's dead -- but there's a lady that people call Mom. I dunno why.\n"
" Maybe 'cause she's really nice? She's got a diner on the other side of town. [He points to the Northeast.] My homeless friends go\n"
" there and she sneaks them free food. I wish Dad would take me there, 'cause she knows how to make rat taste really yummy!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:114
msgid "Hmm, I *am* feeling a bit hungry. Perhaps I'll go pay Mom a visit. You take care of yourself, Bobby."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:115
msgid "You're such a little brat. I better leave now before I kick the shit outta you. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:116
msgid ""
"Guess what, Bobby? I spoke with Mom, and she's going to be opening up a nice big new home where you and all your\n"
" homeless friends are welcome to go live together. It's going to be in the big building that's right across the street from here.\n"
" She said she'll have it all set up in a couple days."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:117
msgid ""
"[A huge smile lights up the boy's face.] Really? That's great! [He hugs you.] I can't wait to live there with all my\n"
" friends! I'm so excited! Thanks again mister, you're the best!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:118
msgid ""
"[A huge smile lights up the boy's face.] Really? That's great! [He hugs you.] I can't wait to live there with all my\n"
" friends! I'm so excited! Thanks again miss, you're the best!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:119
msgid "You're welcome kid. See you around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:120
msgid "Hi again! Did you talk to the Mom lady?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:121
msgid "Don't worry Bobby, I'm working on it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:122
msgid "You help Bobby find a better life."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:123
msgid "Hi again! Thanks for everything. I love this new place. Mom is such a great lady!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:124
msgid "I love this new place. Mom is such a great lady!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:125
msgid "I'm so excited! Time to pack my stuff."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:126
msgid "I wonder if dad will notice I am gone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:127
msgid "This is going to be so much better."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:200
msgid "I don't like you. Go away!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:210
msgid "It sounds like you're not too fond of your dad. Mind if I ask why?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:211
msgid "You little brat, what gives you the right to talk about your dad like that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:220
msgid ""
"Cause my dad's not very nice. He leaves me home alone all the time, and when he *is* home, he's always drunk or\n"
" he says he's flying on Jet, which is a lie 'cause I never see him fly anywhere. Sometimes, he brings a\n"
" girlfriend home -- he's got lots of girlfriends -- and he makes me go outside for awhile, even if its the middle of the night\n"
" and it's cold or raining."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:221
msgid "That's-"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dclilbby.msg:230
msgid ""
"Oh! And sometimes he tells me to take things from people in secret. He says it's a game and that he gives it back later,\n"
" but I don't' believe him. But if I don't do it, then he gets real mad and his eyes get all scary looking, and he hurts me.\n"
" See? [He lifts up his shirt sleeve, revealing a nasty bruise on his arm.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:100
msgid "You see the owner of the saloon."
msgstr "Du ser ägaren till salongen."

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:101
msgid "You see Becky."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:150
msgid "This looks like the owner."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:151
msgid "This is Becky, owner of this place."
msgstr "Det här är Becky, ägaren av det här stället."

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:153
msgid "Hello, stranger, and welcome to my saloon. I'm Becky."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:154
msgid "Hello, I am "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:155
msgid ". What's there to do around here?"
msgstr ". Vad finns det att göra här omkring?"

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:156
msgid "Hi, I'm "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:157
msgid ". Can I ask some questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:159
msgid "Mag gah."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:160
msgid "Run along. I don't need your kind here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:162 dialog/dcslvgrt.msg:343 dialog/fcjuavki.msg:178
#: dialog/scmerk.msg:251
msgid "Screw you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:163 dialog/ncorvill.msg:292
msgid "I'm going."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/dcmaggie.msg:164
msgid "Sorry, no offense was meant. Can I ask something?"
msgstr ""

