#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:100 dialog/ectravlr.msg:100
msgid "You see a traveler."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:101
msgid "This person seems to be looking for something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:200
msgid "It's a slaver! Kill him!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:201
msgid "Kill the oppressor!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:202
msgid "Kill the evil slaver!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:203
msgid "Down with slavery! Kill the slavers!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:250
msgid "Hello there!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:251
msgid "Hey stranger!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:300
msgid "Hey stranger, what are you doing out in these parts?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:301
msgid "I'm lost."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:302
msgid "Just wandering around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:303
msgid "Not much. What are you doing out here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:304
msgid "Looking for people to kill."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:306
msgid "huh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:307
msgid "Um, I think I need to be going now. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:310
msgid ""
"I wish I could help you, but I've been wandering these parts\n"
" for so long, I'm not certain where anything is any more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:311
msgid "Why are you wandering around here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:312
msgid "What are you doing out here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:313 dialog/vcmacrae.msg:141
msgid "Well, good luck to you."
msgstr "Nåväl, lycka till."

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:314
msgid ""
"Ah, well, good luck to you. Oh, by the way, watch out for the\n"
" Den. They like to sell people there."
msgstr ""
"Ja, lycka till. Åh, förresten, se upp för\n"
" Lyan. De gillar att sälja folk där."

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:315
msgid "The Den?"
msgstr "Lyan?"

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:316
msgid "Sell people?"
msgstr "Sälja människor?"

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:317
msgid "Sure, whatever. Bye."
msgstr "Visst. Hej då."

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:320
msgid ""
"Seems people around these parts like to keep slaves. I'm here to\n"
" try and free them slaves. And if a slaver or two dies in the process, no biggie."
msgstr ""
"Folk här gillar visst att ha slavar. Jag är här för att\n"
" försöka befria slavarna. Och om en slavhandlare eller två dör under processen, är det ingen stor grej."

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:321
msgid "What's wrong with owning slaves? I'd own some if I could find them."
msgstr "Vad är det för fel med att äga slavar? Jag skulle äga några om jag kunde hitta dem."

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:322
msgid "I'll keep my eyes out for the bastards."
msgstr "Jag ska hålla ögonen öppna efter de jävlarna."

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:323
msgid "Killing is never justified."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:324
msgid "Kill? I'll help you kill them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:330
msgid ""
"Really? That's great. Well, I have to head out and look for more\n"
" slaves to free."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:331
msgid "Good luck."
msgstr "Lycka till."

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:335
msgid ""
"No, sometimes you need to kill a few people to save many. Sacrifices\n"
" of the land. Besides, they're slavers; it's not like they are real people."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:336
msgid "Yeah, you're right. Well, I've gotta go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:337
msgid "Really? Well, to me you're dead meat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:340
msgid "You bastard! I'll kill you for that!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:341
msgid "You bitch! I'll kill you for that!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:342
msgid "Not if I kill you first!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:350
msgid ""
"Yeah. They attack small groups of people. Any that live go to the\n"
" auction blocks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:351
msgid "That's horrible. I'll remember to watch out for them. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:355
msgid ""
"The Den's a town. They specialize in slavery and all sorts of\n"
" evil. They're no good at all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:356 dialog/gcwooz.msg:741
msgid "Thanks for the information. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:360
msgid "Just looking to shut down the slave routes."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:362
msgid "Oh, ok. Good luck to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:370
msgid "Try slavers. They make really good kills. Nice and messy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:371
msgid "Cool. Thanks for the info."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecabolst.msg:372
msgid "You're here. I'd rather kill you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:100 dialog/ecsirlau.msg:100
msgid "A man in power armor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:101
msgid "Arthur, son of Uther Pendragon."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:102
msgid "His fly is down."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:103
msgid ""
"Hail, travelers. My name is Arthur, son of Uther Pendragon, from the Brotherhood of Steel. We\n"
" are on quest for the Holy Hand Grenade of Antioch. Hast thou seen it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:104
msgid "Holy what of who?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:105
msgid "Player Response"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:106
msgid "Unga."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:107
msgid "No time to talk. We're on quest."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:108
msgid "We seek the Holy Hand Grenade of Antioch."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:109
msgid "For the Brotherhood of Steel!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:110
msgid "Hmm... African or European swallow?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:111
msgid "Hey now! That's not yours, is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:112
msgid "I'm warning you. Keep your hands to yourself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:113
msgid "That's it. Enough is enough."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:114
msgid ""
"The Holy Hand Grenade of Antioch? Why, 'tis only the greatest hand held, anti-personnel weapon\n"
" of its kind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:115
msgid "Why do you search for such a terrible weapon?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:116
msgid ""
"We of the Brotherhood of Steel seek to find this most devastating weapon of our ancestors, and\n"
" secure it from those who would abuse the power of the Holy Hand Grenade of Antioch."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:118
msgid ""
"Well... because the Brotherhood of Steel is dedicated to protecting the weak and defenseless, and\n"
" this thing could really hurt someone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:120
msgid "Umm... because it's really the only moral thing to do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:122
msgid ""
"Wha... um... Look now, we're really quite busy. Are you going to help us or not? Have you seen\n"
" the Holy Hand Grenade of Antioch or not?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:125
msgid ""
"Well, why didn't you just say so? If you could just tell us where, we'll be off and you can get\n"
" back to whatever it is you were doing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:126
msgid "[You point in a random direction.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:127
msgid "Right then. Thank you for your help. Something for your trouble."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:128
msgid "Wait! I am also on a quest. I seek the holy GECK. Have you seen it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:129
msgid "Well then, no sense in continuing this conversation. We're off."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:131
msgid "Bloody peasant!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:133
msgid ""
"GECK, you said? Why yes, we have two of them. Don't need another one. Thanks all the same\n"
" though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:134
msgid "Since you have two of them, maybe you could give me one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:135
msgid ""
"No. No. Couldn't do that. Wouldn't be right to end your quest that easily. There's some more\n"
" of them that way. Go get your own. [He points in a direction about the same way you pointed when you\n"
" told him where the Holy Hand Grenade of Antioch was.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:200
msgid "Do you speak the king's tongue?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:201
msgid "Hellooo."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:202
msgid "Hey, I'm over here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:203
msgid "If you could spare a moment of your time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:204
msgid "Ahem."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:205
msgid "Now come on. Don't ignore me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:206
msgid "Pleeeease! I need to ask you something important."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:207
msgid "Well, we must continue our quest for the Hand Grenade of Antioch. Come, Patsy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:300
msgid "Our quest has been fulfilled!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ecarthur.msg:301
msgid "Arthur, at your service."
msgstr ""

