msgstr ""

#: dialog/fstnkcmp.msg:109
msgid "-Fuel Tanks: Empty- -Cargo Hold: Empty- -Navigation Computer: Non Functional- -Mooring Lines: Attached-"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/fstnkcmp.msg:112
msgid "-Fuel Tanks: Full- -Cargo Hold: Empty- -Navigation Computer: Non Functional- -Mooring Lines: Attached-"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/fstnkcmp.msg:115
msgid "ERROR: Fuel Tanks Empty."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/fstnkcmp.msg:116
msgid "ERROR: Navigation Computer non Functional."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/fstnkcmp.msg:117
msgid "-Fuel Tanks: Empty- -Cargo Hold: Empty- -Navigation Computer: Functional- -Mooring Lines: Attached-"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/fstnkcmp.msg:118
msgid "-Fuel Tanks: Full- -Cargo Hold: Empty- -Navigation Computer: Functional- -Mooring Lines: Attached-"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/fstnkcmp.msg:119
msgid "You see a PoseidoNet Navigation Computer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/fstnkcmp.msg:129
msgid "[You run through the casting-off sequence quickly, and the ship rockets away from the rig.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/fstnkcmp.msg:131
msgid "Navigation Computer on-line."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/fstnkcmp.msg:200
msgid "WARNING: Submarine still active. Proceeding would result in the ship's destruction."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:100
msgid "You see an unusually large molerat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:101
msgid "You see The Brain."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a huge, albino molerat. It seems to have a swollen cranium and is particularly\n"
" intelligent looking."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:110
msgid "You are even more foolish than most of your kind to cross me. Now you must die."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:120
msgid "I don't know how you got in here -- but you must be able to find your way out the same way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:121
msgid "I don't have time for your pestering. I'm planning a way to take over the world. Go away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:122
msgid "Don't bother me. I won't warn you again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:123
msgid "That's it. Zomak! Kill him for me!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:130
msgid ""
"Renewal is at hand. But it won't get any closer unless you get moving on repairing our Atomic\n"
" Reactor. (to himself) Humans... they're so disappointing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:131
msgid "Repair the Atomic Reactor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:132 dialog/gcbrain.msg:610
msgid "Oh yeah. Well, I'll be going then. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:140
msgid "I smell one of my Talismans on you, but I don't remember giving you one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:141
msgid "I found it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:142
msgid "Uh, you must have forgotten."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:143
msgid "It's just my aftershave. Old Mice -- do you like it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:144
msgid "I killed one of your drones and took it from his still warm corpse."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:145
msgid "I got it from a village near Vault City. The people there said your followers left these with them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:150
msgid "Are you ready to become one of us?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:151
msgid "I was born ready. Where do I sign up?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:152
msgid "You mean become a giant rat?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:153
msgid "I don't want any part of what you are."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:154
msgid "Just who are us, uh, I mean, you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:160
msgid ""
"In order to survive, both Gecko and Vault City will need to cooperate. Vault City needs the\n"
" power from our Atomic Reactor in order to expand, and we need Vault City's medical technology. Unless\n"
" we cooperate, both cities will stagnate. Vault City needs to help us to repair our power plant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:161
msgid "How are you going to get them to do that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:170
msgid ""
"I am known simply as The Brain. A tribute to my genius. Few things within Gecko, and only a few more\n"
" without, escape my notice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:171 dialog/gcbrain.msg:621
msgid "But you're just a giant rat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:172 dialog/gcbrain.msg:622
msgid "You said something about joining you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:180
msgid ""
"I don't care where you got it. The real question is whether you intend to join us and wear it\n"
" in earnest. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:181
msgid "Join you? What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:182
msgid "I'd rather clean your cage than join you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:183
msgid "That depends. Vault City's patrols keep getting attacked by molerats. I assume you're behind this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:184
msgid "Why of course I am. All part of my grand scheme to take over the world. I wouldn't expect your deficient human brain to understand. But alas, what concern is it of yours?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:185
msgid "I just want your molerats to stop attacking Vault City's patrols."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:186
msgid "Do you? Interesting... Alright, I propose a deal, human. I shall comply with your request, *if* you complete a certain task for me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:187 dialog/ncsalvat.msg:316 dialog/vcdrtroy.msg:172
msgid "What do you want me to do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:188
msgid "Look, we had a deal -- I repair the reactor, and you call off your creatures. I did my part of the bargain, now it's your turn."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:189
msgid "The reactor is repaired, yes. But is it optimized? No, I'm afraid not. I said I'd call off my molerats when you *complete* the task. Getting it half-done isn't good enough."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:190
msgid ""
"Well, as part of my plan to rule the world, I intend to reward my ghoul followers by finding a\n"
" way to restore their humanity."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:191
msgid "How are you going to do that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:200
msgid ""
"When I unite Gecko and Vault City under my rulership, I will dedicate Vault City's medical labs\n"
" to finding a way to reverse the effects of radiation that turned the people into ghouls. They will be\n"
" renewed, reborn as humans once again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:201
msgid "That doesn't sound so bad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:210
msgid ""
"The Ankh is a symbol of life. Once I've given you this talisman you'll be one of us. And your\n"
" comrades will be more likely to help you along the path towards Renewal. But be careful who you show\n"
" it to."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:211
msgid "Are you ready to accept Renewal and wear my Ankh Talisman?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:212
msgid "OK, I'll take your Ankh Talisman."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:213
msgid "I don't want to Renew. I like myself just the way I am. I don't want your talisman."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:214
msgid "Renewal? What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:220
msgid "Those fools in Vault City have only signed their death warrants by destroying our reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:221
msgid "Now I have to think of another way to take over the world. Just get out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:222
msgid "I've had enough of your clumsy meddling. Zomak! Kill this fool for me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:230
msgid ""
"Repairing the reactor was an excellent first step. One more step is needed to ensure the\n"
" survival of both Gecko and Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:231 dialog/gcbrain.msg:641
msgid "One more step?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:232
msgid "Aren't you the concerned citizen all of a sudden."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:233
msgid "I think I've heard more than enough. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:234
msgid "Just why is a giant talking rat so concerned about all of this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:240
msgid ""
"You have done well. Both Vault City and Gecko have reason to rejoice. With our reactor working\n"
" at top efficiency, my plan to take over the world may near fruition. Now you may leave. I have work to\n"
" do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:241
msgid "Well, I sure didn't do it for you. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:242
msgid "Big plans for an overbred rat. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:250
msgid ""
"Well, the reactor's running -- but not very efficiently. We need to use Vault City's central\n"
" computer to analyze our reactor's output report."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:251
msgid ""
"Vault City's central computer. I'm sure that openminded people like that would be happy to help\n"
" a giant mutated rat and a city full of ghouls."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:252
msgid "How do you propose to make that happen?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:260
msgid ""
"Concerned citizen? In a way. In order to take over the world, I have to make sure that there's\n"
" something worth taking over. I need to build a strong powerbase using Gecko and Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:261
msgid "A rat plotting to take over the world?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:270
msgid ""
"Well, despite your feelings about a rodent ruling the world, the actions I propose would benefit\n"
" thousands of Vault City and Gecko's citizens. You may not care for me or my motives, but the results\n"
" are still well worth working towards."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:271
msgid "Why don't you tell me about this last step, and I'll think about helping."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:272
msgid ""
"It makes my flesh crawl to think that I've already helped you in some way. I'm leaving.\n"
" Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:280
msgid ""
"Well, they will let you if you can show them how much it benefits them. We have an economic\n"
" report that proves that optimizing the Gecko atomic power plant will directly benefit Vault City. I'll\n"
" let our comrades here in Gecko know of your mission."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:281
msgid ""
"They'll give you the Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator if you can prove that doing so benefits Vault City. I have prepared\n"
" an economic report that details just how much repairing our power plant benefits Vault City. I'll let\n"
" our comrades here in Gecko know of your mission."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:282
msgid "That's great, but who in Vault City would even think of reading such a thing?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:283
msgid ""
"Why don't you talk to that old windbag, that stinking sack Festus, in the power plant and\n"
" see if he can dredge some useful information out of his rotting skull. He may know of a means of optimzing the power plant.\n"
" I'll let our comrades here in Gecko know of your mission."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:284
msgid "That sounds like a good idea. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:290
msgid ""
"I think that McClure is the only Councilmember in Vault City with enough brains to be able to\n"
" see past his prejudices. He'll make sure you get what you need."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:291
msgid "No way, no how, am I going to be your message boy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:292
msgid "Well, I guess it's worth a shot. Where do I get the disk?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:300
msgid ""
"You need to go up above, to the junkyard. Look for a ghoul named Gordon. He has the Economic\n"
" Data Disk that you need. You'll have my talisman, so he'll know to give you the disk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:301
msgid "What talisman?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:310
msgid "You're sure you want to consign all the citizens of both cities to a slow death?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:311
msgid "Well, I guess not. Okay, tell me where to get the disk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:312
msgid "Better a slow death than to be ruled by a rat. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:320
msgid ""
"(Sniff, sniff) Hmmm, I smell the distinctive aroma of Cheezy Poofs on you. You don't happen to\n"
" have some to spare do you? I just love Cheezy Poofs."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:321
msgid "Hmm, nope. No Cheezy Poofs here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:322
msgid "I guess I could spare some Cheezy Poofs."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:330
msgid "Now you're one of us. Soon, I will take over the world and all of you will be Renewed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:331
msgid "Uh, yeah. Whatever you say."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:332
msgid ""
"That's it. That's enough. This stops right here. Someone's gotta stomp you out of existence --\n"
" and that someone's me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:340
msgid ""
"Well, then, I suppose we have nothing more to say to one another. But you know that I cannot\n"
" allow you to leave here alive, unless you're one of us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:341
msgid "I'd rather die than join you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:342
msgid "Hmm, maybe I've been hasty in my judgment."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:343
msgid "Bring it on, Willard."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:350
msgid "You fool. Zomak! Kill this intruder for me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:360
msgid ""
"You humans have such limited tolerances. I would have remained a normal rat if you humans\n"
" hadn't done your best to destroy the world. If it weren't for the radiation, I wouldn't be\n"
" what I am today."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:361
msgid "And what's that, exactly?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:370
msgid "Now that everything's been explained for you, are you ready to join us?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:371
msgid "Well, I suppose so."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:372
msgid "I'm convinced, alright. Convinced that I've got to get out of this nuthouse."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:380
msgid ""
"I was just one of many normal rats in an advanced research lab. Then, one day, there were\n"
" explosions. Our cages were broken open, and we were doused with some sort of fluid from a huge vat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:390
msgid ""
"I crawled outside. As I began to heal, I noticed that I had changed. I tried to communicate with\n"
" people, but they all just tried to kill me. Humans are just too violent to survive under their own\n"
" leadership -- but that's another story. The first step is to repair the reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:391
msgid "Repair the reactor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:400
msgid ""
"You must get a Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator from Vault City in order to repair the Gecko reactor. If you don't,\n"
" then Vault City will no doubt attack Gecko. Of course, by destroying the reactor, they will doom\n"
" themselves in the long run, as well."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:401
msgid "Doom themselves? How do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:402
msgid "Why would Vault City give me a part for the Gecko Atomic power plant?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:410
msgid ""
"You have to show them that it's in their own best interest to do so. People are easily\n"
" manipulated through self-interest."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:411
msgid "I don't think the people in Vault City will give me a part for your atomic power plant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:420
msgid "But right now, don't you have something to do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:421
msgid "Uh, I guess I better get going on that atomic power plant thing. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:422
msgid "I sure do. I need to get the heck out of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:430
msgid "My nose is quite keen. I'm certain that you have Cheezy Poofs. Give me some right now. Please."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:431
msgid "The only way you're getting my Cheezy Poofs is from my cold and lifeless fingers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:432
msgid "Oh, hey. What's this in my pocket? I guess I do have some Cheezy Poofs after all. Whaddya know?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:440
msgid ""
"(crunch, munch, crunch) Mmmm, I love Cheezy Poofs, they're so, well, uh, Cheesy. For that, you\n"
" get to be a member of my special cult, and you can help me take over the world."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:441
msgid ""
"(crunch, munch, crunch) Mmmm, I love Cheezy Poofs, they're so, well, uh, Cheesy. I was wise to\n"
" allow you to join my cult. Isn't there something you should be doing right now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:442 dialog/gcbrain.msg:443
msgid "(crunch, munch, crunch) Mmmm, I love Cheezy Poofs, they're so, well, uh, Cheesy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:450
msgid "So be it. Zomak! Kill this fool for me. But be careful with the Cheezy Poofs!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:460
msgid ""
"You have to use the Reactor Data disk on Vault City's Central Computer. You can either sneak\n"
" in and use it or, if you have the Economic Data disk, you can go to McClure."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:461
msgid "Economic Data disk?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:463
msgid ""
"Just bring the Analyzed Reactor Data disk to Festus and he'll input the data to get the\n"
" reactor running efficiently."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:464
msgid ""
"Well, once you get a Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator from Vault City, bring it back\n"
" to the reactor. Then you can try to convince that pompous slug Festus to install the part, or use the\n"
" repair robot to install the part, or you could even install the part yourself, of course - so long as\n"
" someone does it we'll be all right."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:465
msgid "How can I get the part from Vault City?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:466
msgid "Oh, I see. Well, thanks for the information. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:467
msgid ""
"Festus is the geezer that runs the atomic power plant. He's old, crotchety, and cantankerous, but\n"
" he does actually know something about running the plant. His offices are over on the far southeast part\n"
" the plant. Bring the data disk to him and he'll know how to use it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:468
msgid "Oh, I get it. Okay. Thanks. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:500
msgid ""
"(musing to himself) So many things pass away. Times are not what they were. (sigh) I feel that my\n"
" sole remaining kin has died. Mad, though he was, I wish it were not so. I had hoped that\n"
" he might find some happiness even in his dotage. (to you) Well, enough of my sad musings."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:504
msgid ""
"A Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator. That's the part that you need to get from\n"
" Vault City. Then you need to bring it back here and get it installed in the reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:505
msgid "Get it installed in the reactor? How can I do that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:510
msgid ""
"The reactor's optimization data has been recorded on the disk you have by Vault City's\n"
" Central Computer. Now all you have to do is to bring the disk to that pompous windbag, Festus.\n"
" Or I suppose that you could just use the disk on the reactor robot control terminal, if you can't\n"
" bear talking to Festus."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:511
msgid "Festus? Who's he?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:512
msgid "Oh, okay. Thanks. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:600
msgid ""
"Renewal is at hand. But it won't get any closer unless you get moving on\n"
" repairing our atomic reactor. (to himself) Humans... they're so disappointing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:601
msgid ""
"Renewal is almost here, but it won't get any closer unless you use the\n"
" Reactor's Data disk on Vault City's Central Computer. Phah! One would think that\n"
" even a human could understand that much."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:602
msgid ""
"You're so close to providing the means for Renewal to all of us. If you'd\n"
" only give the Reactor Data disk that you've had analyzed to Festus."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:603
msgid ""
"You know that you need to get the Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator\n"
" from Vault City in order to install it in our atomic reactor. Sometimes I think\n"
" that Renewal will never arrive as long as I have to depend upon humans."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:604
msgid "Repair the reactor? What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:605
msgid "Use the Reactor Data disk? Just how am I going to do that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:606
msgid "I have to give it to Festus?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:607
msgid "A Hydro-whatsits? Huh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:608
msgid "What's that about the reactor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:609 dialog/gcbrain.msg:640
msgid "Give it to who?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:611
msgid "You need to get that Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator installed before the plant is operational again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:620
msgid ""
"I am known simply as The Brain. A tribute to my genius. Few things within\n"
" Gecko, and only a few more without, escape my notice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:630
msgid ""
"The actions I propose would benefit thousands of Vault City and Gecko's\n"
" citizens. You may not care for me, or my motives, but the results are still well\n"
" worth working toward."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:631
msgid "You've received the Reactor Data disk, now you have to use it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:632
msgid "You've had the Reactor Data disk analyzed, now you have to do something with it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:633 dialog/gcbrain.msg:653
msgid ""
"Our atomic reactor needs a part if we have any hope of getting it to run\n"
" efficiently."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:634
msgid ""
"You've acquired the data that we need to optimize the atomic reactor. Now,\n"
" all you have to do is give it to Festus."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:635
msgid "Why don't you tell me about whatever it is that you're proposing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:636 dialog/gcbrain.msg:655
msgid "Use the Reactor Data disk? How am I going to do that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:637 dialog/gcbrain.msg:656
msgid "Well, I figured that, but what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:638 dialog/gcbrain.msg:658
msgid "A part? What kind of part?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:639
msgid "Why don't you tell me about this last step and I'll think about helping."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:650
msgid ""
"Well, despite your feelings about a rodent ruling the world, the actions I\n"
" propose would benefit thousands of Vault City and Gecko citizens. You may not care\n"
" for me or my motives but the results are still well worth working towards."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:651
msgid "You've received the Reactor Data disk, now you have to do something with it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:652
msgid "You've had the Reactor Data disk analyzed, now you have to use it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:654
msgid "Why don't you tell me about those actions that you're proposing?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:657 dialog/gclenny.msg:6051 dialog/hcchad.msg:144
#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:147 dialog/ncchiwri.msg:305 dialog/ncchrwri.msg:305
#: dialog/ocdave.msg:113 dialog/scsherif.msg:125 dialog/vcstark.msg:360
msgid "Like what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:659
msgid "Why don't you tell me about this last step and I'll think about helping?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:670
msgid ""
"The reactor, always the reactor (sigh). Come back when you've made some\n"
" progress on it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:671
msgid "Come back later. I'm communing with a higher power, or something (sheesh)."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:672
msgid "Look, if you don't call off the attacks, the people in the village could end up enslaved by Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:700 dialog/vilann.msg:402
msgid "I have nothing more to say to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:701
msgid "Alright you ugly son-of-a-bitch, now I've got a new deal for you: Either you call off your rodents, or I swear to you I'll blow the damn reactor!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:702
msgid "All right, all right... Consider it done. Just, don't touch the reactor. (mumbles) Damn psychotic humans..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:703
msgid "Now that we're in agreement, what were you saying about the optimization?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:704
msgid "It's settled then. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:705
msgid "You came to an agreement about the molerats with The Brain."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:706
msgid "Vault City's patrols keep getting attacked by molerats. I assume you're behind this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:707
msgid "You ask for my assistance, yet you leave a task half-finished. (to himself) Typical human. (to you) Optimize the reactor, then, and only then, shall I assist you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:708
msgid "That depends. What is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:709
msgid "Listen here, you radioactive rat. You're really starting to piss me off. You said your \"kin\" had kicked the bucket... Well, I want you to know -- it was me, who finished him off. And now I think I'll finish the job of rendering your kind extinct."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:710
msgid "Listen here, you radioactive rat. You're really starting to piss me off. I think it's time I put a stop to this madness."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:711
msgid "I need to think this over."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:712
msgid "Most interesting... and here I thought you were concerned for the well-being of Vault City. Anyway, the safety of that village is integral to my plan. Therefore, I shall grant your request, human."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:713
msgid "It seems to me, that because you have fixed and optimized the reactor, you deserve my help. What is it that you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:714
msgid "Thank you! What were you saying about the optimization?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:715
msgid "Thank you! Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:716
msgid "It appears that Gordon has already given you this Economic Data Disk that I speak of. Take it to Vault City immediately."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:717 dialog/hcphil.msg:222 dialog/scmerk.msg:172
#: dialog/vclynett.msg:732 dialog/vclynett.msg:747
msgid "I'm on it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:718
msgid "Umm... yeah, maybe later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:719
msgid "You *must* get a Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator from Vault City in order to repair the Gecko reactor. If you don't, then Vault City will no doubt attack Gecko. If you help me, I will fulfill your request. So... will you join us?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:720
msgid "Very well, I shall help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:721
msgid "No, screw you rat brain! I've had enough of this. Time to die!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcbrain.msg:4211
msgid "Uh, I guess I better go get that disk from Gordon. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc.msg:100
msgid "You get no response from the guard."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:100
msgid "Halt, mutant wastelander! We are searching the area for an enemy of the Enclave. Identify yourself immediately."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:101
msgid "Who are you calling a mutant, asshole? You want an enemy? You've got one -- right here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:102
msgid "Look, I'm just a simple traveler. I've never even heard of the Enclave. This person you're looking for must be pretty dangerous, because you guys look like you mean business."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:103
msgid "That's enough for me. Kill him."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:104
msgid "Oh, this will be fun!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:105
msgid "Oh yeah, they're dangerous alright, and we suspect them to be fleeing Gecko. For all we know, you're the one we're looking for."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:106
msgid "Well I'm sure glad I'm not, because you don't look like anyone I'd want to mess with. But listen, if there's a dangerous person on the loose around here, I should really be getting back to my family so I can warn them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:107
msgid "All right, I give up. Let's party!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:108
msgid "You're not going anywhere just yet. Have you ever been to Gecko?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:109
msgid "Yeah, of course I have. Lovely place. I mean, the locals are hideous and it kinda smells and there's all that radiation and stuff, but it sure is fun to mess around on the computers. Ha! You should have been there when I was messing with this one jackass--you know, he looked a lot like you fellas."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:110
msgid "Gecko? Hell no, this is as close as I get. Don't you know that place is full of them ugly-ass ghouls? Why do you ask?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:111
msgid "OK, I believe you. Fan out, men. Search the area. We gotta find this person."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:112
msgid "No. I don't believe you. This is our man, boys!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:113
msgid "No. I don't believe you. This is our woman, boys!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:114
msgid "Whoa! Whoa! Just hold on a second. Why don't you believe me? What am I supposed to have done?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:115
msgid "Somebody hacked into the Enclave computer network from the Poseidon Oil Reactor. We're trying to track him down."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:116
msgid "Hacked into it!? Well, that couldn't have been me. I'm just a tribal. Hell, I don't even know how to use a -- what did you call it? Kom-pu-tor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:200
msgid "Gecko? Hell no, this is as close as I get. Don't you know that place is full of them ugly-ass ghouls? It's bad enough that I have to watch over my Uncle Lenny, here. Why do you ask?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:201
msgid "Urgh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenc2.msg:202
msgid "Me kill baddies!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcenclen.msg:100
msgid "You have entered a large plain just outside of Gecko. There are people here wearing some high-tech armor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:100
msgid "You see a particularly unkempt ghoul."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:101
msgid "You see Festus, the atomic power plant supervisor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a glum looking ghoul with a particularly rancid appearance. He smells like an\n"
" infected wound."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:110
msgid "Aren't you just as stupid as they get? Hah, hah, hah."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:111
msgid "Are you dumb or what? Hah, hah, hah. You look just like a Vault City person."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:112
msgid "Well, you're pretty dumb, aren't you? You should head on over to Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:113
msgid "I just have so many important things to do. Why don't you get back to Vault City, where you belong?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:114
msgid "Hah, hah, hah. You just have such a stupid look on your face."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:120
msgid ""
"Hello there. I'm Festus. I run the whole reactor. Without me, this whole town would be shut\n"
" down. I'm a very busy man. They really overwork me here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:121
msgid ""
"I've got so much to do here. I could really use a break. But, you know, nobody else can run the\n"
" atomic power plant. I'm harnessing the power of the atom, you know. Really tires a fellow out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:123
msgid "I understand that the reactor isn't running very well. Is that true?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:124
msgid "Why do you look -- and smell -- as though you're falling apart?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:125
msgid "Well, I wouldn't want to take up your valuable time. I'll just be on my way. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:130
msgid "I sure have the reactor running smoothly now. I'm just that good."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:131
msgid "The reactor's running pretty good now, all right. Could still do with a tiny bit of a tuneup mebbe, but I'd say it's a pretty good job all the same."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:132
msgid "More work? What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:133
msgid "Well, nothing's ever perfect. Goodbye, Festus."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:141
msgid "Well, I supervise the atomic power plant. Really, though, I run the whole thing by myself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:142
msgid ""
"Yup, I run the whole thing -- in a supervisory capacity. All by myself. It would be impossible if\n"
" I just weren't so darn good at it. It's a gift, really..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:143
msgid "By yourself? What are all those other people in the next room doing then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:144
msgid "You must know quite a bit about atomic power, then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:145
msgid "Well, I don't want to keep you from your work. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:150
msgid ""
"Wastrels. That's all they are. They don't really understand what needs to be done. They're just\n"
" placeholders. It irks me that they think they know something about atomic power plants. Why, if it\n"
" weren't for me..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:151 dialog/gcfestus.msg:161
msgid "Hmm. What did you say you do here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:152 dialog/gcfestus.msg:162
msgid "Ah, yes. Well, I'd better be going now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:160
msgid ""
"Know about atomic power? Well, I almost invented it. I know more about atomic power than anyone\n"
" alive. If it's atomic power -- I'm your man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:170
msgid ""
"You know, I really do run the whole thing. It's pretty tough. But I do have many years of\n"
" experience. I'm all pro when it comes to running atomic power plants."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:171
msgid "You must be very good at your job."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:172
msgid "I'm sure you are. Uh, I better be going now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:180
msgid ""
"Most people think it's easy. They think that just anyone can run an atomic reactor. But it's\n"
" not for the untrained or faint of heart. I'm harnessing the power of the atom here!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:181
msgid "I'm impressed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:182
msgid "Well, I wouldn't want to keep you. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:190
msgid ""
"It sure would be nice to have some help. But, you see, no one else is qualified to do what I do.\n"
" They don't even understand the basics of what I do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:191
msgid "How could anyone hope to keep up with you? You're above everyone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:192
msgid "You're really special, no doubt about it. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:200
msgid ""
"You know I am. I can tell that you really understand things like this. If I weren't so busy here\n"
" I'd run Gecko. And let me tell you, I'd run it right."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:201
msgid "You'd run the town, too?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:202
msgid "Arrrrrgh! I'm leaving now. I am. Don't try to stop me. Goodbye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:210
msgid ""
"Well, there wouldn't be any of this trading with Broken Hills for uranium ore. We'd just trade\n"
" them power for it, instead. They could run their city using the power of the atom."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:211
msgid "Wouldn't you have to run powerlines across miles and miles of hazardous desert?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:212
msgid "Do you smell something? Something foul? I better leave. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:220
msgid ""
"Well, I suppose so. Then we'd have them buy giant batteries from us. Yes, that's the beauty of\n"
" it. Then they'd have to buy the batteries from us, too. And that's just to start; I have other big\n"
" plans, like..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:221
msgid "You're a politician, too? It's incredible that your talents cover such diverse fields."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:222
msgid "Is something rotting in here? I think I need some fresh air. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:230
msgid ""
"I'm just multi-faceted. Really, I'm very good at whatever I try. Seldom is there anyone better.\n"
" Of course, I just happen to prefer running the atomic power plant. But, if I wanted to, I could do\n"
" anything else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:231
msgid ""
"I can't believe that everyone in Gecko doesn't see your true worth. I'm going to go tell them\n"
" right now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:232
msgid "Must break free. Strength fading. Must leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:240
msgid "What brings you to this part of my atomic reactor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:241
msgid "Well, I have a part that you can use to fix the reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:242 dialog/gcskeetr.msg:204 dialog/rcfannie.msg:132
msgid "Uh, I was just looking around. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:250
msgid ""
"You know, I'm not so sure that this is the right part after all. Maybe you should take it back\n"
" to Vault City to check. I don't think I can help you with this, after all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:251
msgid "I'm sure it's the right part. I have great confidence in your abilities."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:252 dialog/gcfestus.msg:262 dialog/gcfestus.msg:272
msgid "I guess you're right. I better find another way to install the part."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:260
msgid ""
"I don't think that those people in Vault City really like us all that much. I wouldn't put it\n"
" past them to booby-trap this part. Maybe it only looks like the right part, and it's really a bomb!\n"
" You can't fool me that easily. I'm not installing this thing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:261
msgid ""
"With your technical expertise, if it were a bomb, you would already know it. Please just\n"
" install the part."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:270
msgid ""
"Okay, I'm here. But I'm still not sure that this isn't the right part, or that it's not a trap\n"
" somehow. You know, I'm much too valuable to waste. Maybe I should just let someone else do this...\n"
" later... much later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:271
msgid ""
"It needs to be done now. And you're the only person that can do it right. Come on, all of Gecko\n"
" depends on you!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:300
msgid ""
"Well, it sure uses a lot of uranium. And it leaks some. You know, I've asked somebody to fix it,\n"
" but no one listens to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:301
msgid "I've heard that it's leaking radiation into the groundwater. Is that true?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:302
msgid "I thought you were the expert. Why don't you fix it? Just what do you do here anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:310
msgid ""
"Well, that's possible, but I don't think it would do any harm to anything. It's underground,\n"
" after all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:311
msgid ""
"I think you may be wrong. Vault City's been complaining that your atomic reactor has been\n"
" tainting their water with radiation."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:312 dialog/gczomak.msg:251
msgid "Well, if you say so. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:320
msgid ""
"Not possible. No one would know more about it than me. They're just looking for someone to blame\n"
" for their problem. We don't even draw from the same aquifer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:321
msgid "You sound sure. But so did they."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:330
msgid ""
"Well, they're just a bunch of amateurs when it comes to atomic power. I'm the real expert here.\n"
" You can take what I say to the bank. If there were any banks left, that is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:331
msgid "Well, I guess you know what you're talking about. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:332
msgid "I'm not as sure as you are. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:340
msgid "You have a spare Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator on you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:341
msgid "You actually know what that is?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:342
msgid "Of course. Are you ready to install it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:350
msgid "Surprised? I told you that I know all about atomic power plants. You shoulda listened to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:351
msgid "Well, since you know what it is, you must know how to install it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:352
msgid "I think I've listened to you too much already. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:360
msgid ""
"Of course I do. Why, that's just plain simple for someone of my experience and talent. I was\n"
" weaned on Magnetosphere Regulators as a pup, you know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:361
msgid "That's great. Could you install it for me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:370
msgid ""
"Well, I guess I could install it. I'm certainly the only one that could install it right.\n"
" Installing a Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator is pretty tricky."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:371
msgid "Here's the Regulator. I knew I could count on you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:372
msgid "On second thought, I think I'd better find another way. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:380
msgid ""
"I guess I could install it. But, you know, installing a Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator\n"
" is pretty tricky. And it's dangerous. Not that I'm afraid for myself. But who could run the atomic\n"
" power plant if something were to happen to me? I'm sorry, I can't help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:381
msgid "I should have known you'd chicken out. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:390
msgid "Can't help you now. I'm too busy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:391
msgid "Come back next week. I may have some time then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:392
msgid "Uh, you have the wrong part anyway. Yeah, that's it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:393
msgid "Sorry, I'm too busy to help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:394
msgid "I can't betray Gecko by endangering myself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:400
msgid ""
"Oh yeah. Heh, heh. Sure, it's the right part. It's just, uh, a more primitive model than I'm\n"
" used to. That's all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:401
msgid "Good. Then go ahead and install it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:410
msgid ""
"I guess they'd know better than to try and fool me with a bomb. I'm certain that they know just\n"
" who they're dealing with here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:411
msgid ""
"They spoke of you often in Vault City. Usually in hushed tones of reverence. Now, just install\n"
" the damn part."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:420
msgid "Okay, that's got it. Hey! I did it. I really am that good."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:421
msgid "Damn, I'm good."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:422
msgid "It was difficult, but I did it. I'm a hero."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:423
msgid "I deserve a raise for the work I do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:424
msgid "Gecko sure owes me now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:425
msgid "Did you see me out there? Never even faltered."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:431
msgid "I heard that you take care of parts requisitions and I need one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:432
msgid "I just wondered what you do here. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:440
msgid "You? What do you need one for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:441
msgid ""
"Well, the guys in the other room need it. But I told them I wanted to get it from you just so\n"
" that I could see you in action."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:442
msgid "I just need one. Come on, be a pal. Just give me one. Okay?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:443
msgid ""
"I just think you'd better give me one. Working in a power plant, sometimes people have accidents.\n"
" Understand me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:444
msgid "I need one for- Hey, isn't that Fershlubiner Widget Activator running in the red?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:450
msgid "Well, okay. Here's your Part Requisition Form. I guess you have your reasons for needing it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:451
msgid ""
"Well, okay. Here's your... Hey? Where'd I put that darn thing? It must be here somewhere... Hmm, I guess\n"
" I can't find it right now. It'll turn up, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:453
msgid "Oh, well. Maybe I'll come back later, then. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:460
msgid ""
"I don't care what you want. Those Part Requisition Forms are for official business only. They\n"
" only entrust them to key personnel. That's why I have them. Get me? Key personnel, only. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:461
msgid "Yeah, I get you. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:462
msgid "Well, you'll get yours. Maybe not today, but soon. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:470
msgid ""
"Uh, well, it's supposed to be that way. I've got plenty of important work to do. If that's all\n"
" you came in for..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:471
msgid "Well, actually I need a Part Requisition Form."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:472 dialog/kcdunton.msg:138
msgid "I guess I don't need anything after all. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:480
msgid ""
"What do you mean? Oh, well, I guess I've been working pretty darn hard lately. Haven't had time\n"
" to really take care of myself the way I should. Maybe the radiation just affects me a little\n"
" differently."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:481
msgid "Uh, well... maybe you should consider bathing or something, to take care of the funk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:490
msgid ""
"Well, I guess I should. Whenever I bathe, though, a lot of my skin sloughs off and all my scabs\n"
" break open. And another thing, my fingernails keep tearing..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:491
msgid "Hold on! Wait! I think I've heard enough. Uh, let's back up a little."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:500
msgid "Festus leaves and then comes back. He is still carrying the part."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:520
msgid "Festus gives you back the part."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:530
msgid "Festus leaves and then comes back. He looks very pleased about something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:600
msgid "I have a reactor data disk that may help you optimize the reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:610
msgid "Okay, give it to me and I'll see what I can do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:630
msgid "No, I think I'll keep it for now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:640
msgid "Okay. Looks good. Thanks for all your help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:650
msgid "Sure. No problem."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:700
msgid "You convinced Festus to help you with the power plant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:800
msgid ""
"I mean that the reactor's running now, but it sure could run better. I mean better by a long country mile, if we jist had a smidge more data. Now if you could\n"
" get the optimization data, we'd be cooking with gas, uh, well, you know what I mean."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:801
msgid "Optimization data? Where would I get that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:802
msgid ""
"Well, you could probably get the information from the Vault City central\n"
" computer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:803
msgid "Well, let me see what I can do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:804
msgid "Hmm, that's a thought."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:805
msgid ""
"That's only going to happen when a paper dog successfully chases an asbestos\n"
" cat through hell. Goodbye, Festus."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:806
msgid ""
"I bet a clever one like you could jist sneak in there and use a\n"
" holodisk with the reactor performance information on the central computer. Then\n"
" sneak the disk right back here. That'd do it. I'd do it myself, but I'm just too\n"
" valuable here to leave, even for a moment."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:807
msgid "I hate to leave a job only half-done."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:808
msgid "Hmm, I don't think I could get away with that. Sorry, Festus. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:809
msgid ""
"That just might work. I guess some of my cleverness is rubbing off on\n"
" you. Good, good. Say, you should prolly bring it to a feller named McClure. From\n"
" what I hear, he's the only one there that'd bend an ear about anything but Vault\n"
" City's precious citizens."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:810
msgid ""
"Councilman McClure is the man to see. OK, thanks for the tip. I guess I'll do it\n"
" then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:811
msgid ""
"Gee, I'd just love to get locked up in Vault City for being a mutie sympathizer. No\n"
" thanks, Festus. You're on your own. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:812
msgid ""
"That's the spirit. I was a-hopin' you'd say that. Great. Just use this disk here\n"
" on Vault City's central computer and then git it right back here. We'll use less uranium, the\n"
" core won't leak so bad, and this Vault City won't have any reason to come exterminate us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:813
msgid "I sure don't want to see Gecko destroyed. I'll do it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:814
msgid "I just don't think I'm up to that. Sorry, Festus. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:815
msgid ""
"I sure wish I could spare the time to go do it myself but I can't. All I can say is\n"
" thanks, kid. You'll be doing all of us here a big favor. (sniff, sniff) You make me so\n"
" proud."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:816
msgid ""
"Well, I better get going. Goodbye, Festus. I'll be back with the data you need just\n"
" as soon as I can."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:817
msgid "Don't just lollygag there. Get that data."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:818
msgid "Don't just stand there. The reactor's not gonna keep workin' forever."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:819
msgid "Get moving and get that optimization data, like you said you would."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:820
msgid "Plenty of time to chat *after* we optimize the reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:821
msgid ""
"Go to Vault City and trade McClure the Econ disk for the reactor data we need. Get\n"
" it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:822
msgid "Come on now. Get that disk to McClure."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:823
msgid "Vault City? Job undone? Ring any bells in that hollow between your ears?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:824
msgid "Hurry up!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:825
msgid ""
"Thanks for getting the data we needed from Vault City to optimize this leaky old beast.\n"
" You're a sly one, no denying it, by cracky. Almost as good a job as I could have done myself.\n"
" 'Course... if'n you wanna actually *finish* the dang job, just use that disk on the Robot Control Terminal.\n"
" Understand me? Well, OK then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:826
msgid "Well, I didn't like leaving the job only half-done. Goodbye, Festus."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:827
msgid "Yeah, I bet you would have done it. You festering windbag. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:828
msgid "You're a peach. There's no doubt about it. I knew you'd do it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:829
msgid "You make me so proud."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:830
msgid "Thanks. Now let me get back to my important work."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfestus.msg:831
msgid "Keep that up and you may get to be just like me someday."
msgstr ""

