#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:268
msgid "I'd like to Renew into a smoothy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:269
msgid "I swear I've seen things fly over us at night."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:280
msgid "I love you, man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:281 dialog/gcfolk.msg:306 dialog/rcgenpes.msg:145
msgid "You're the best."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:282
msgid "Nuke Vault City 'til it glows!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:283
msgid "./~ 99 syringes of RadAway on the wall, 99 syringes... ./~"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:284
msgid "./~ I've been working on the re-act-or, all the live-long day... ./~"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:285
msgid "Before you, I wouldn't trust a smoothskin at all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:286
msgid "I guess some of you smoothies are okay after all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:287
msgid "We ought to go get Chester to drink with us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:288
msgid "When I Renew, I want to turn out just like you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:289
msgid "Sure glad our reactor's running."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:290
msgid "I must be drunk. Wooz is starting to make sense to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:291
msgid "I think I saw an apple once... or was it a banana?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:300
msgid "The reactor is working so good you can almost hear it hum."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:301
msgid "Thanks for working things out with Vault City for us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:302
msgid "We're going to have so much power now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:303
msgid "Not much longer until we can trade power to Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:304
msgid "Gosh, we're going to need a lot of Copper from Redding now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:305
msgid "The reactor is working great now. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:307
msgid "Thanks for fixing up our atomic reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:308
msgid "Reactor's purring, just as nice as you please. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:320
msgid "Renew, comrade. Renew!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:321
msgid "You are one of us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:322
msgid "Hello, comrade. Renewal is at hand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:323
msgid "We will all be one soon."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:324
msgid "He knows all. Worship his sleek fur."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:325
msgid "Damn cultists. Get out of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:326
msgid "Renew this (makes hand gesture), asshole."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:327
msgid "I've got your Renewal right here, pal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:328
msgid "Can't turn around these days without stepping on another damn cultist."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:329
msgid "You'll never catch me worshipping some damn oversized rat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:340
msgid "You ought to go see Lenny about those wounds."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:341
msgid "You look all banged up. Go see Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:342
msgid "You shouldn't wrestle with a deathclaw. Go see Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:343
msgid "Lenny's in Harold's office. You should have him take a look at those wounds."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:344
msgid "How'd you get all torn up like that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:345
msgid "Ouch. You should go see Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:346
msgid "Lenny's in the settlement; go have him take a look at your injuries."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcfolk.msg:347
msgid "I'd sure hate to see the other guy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:100
msgid "You see another ghoul. He appears to be preoccupied."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:101
msgid "You see Gordon of Gecko."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:102
msgid "You see a very nicely dressed ghoul with his hair slicked back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:110
msgid "I have no time for stupid people."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:111
msgid "I have important work to do. Get out of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:112
msgid "You're just as stupid as the rest of them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:113
msgid "This isn't the room for remedial reading lessons."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:114
msgid "Too much inbreeding among smoothskins, I guess."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:120
msgid "Hello there. My name's Gordon. Gordon of Gecko."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:121
msgid "Hello again "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:122
msgid "Hello, Gordon. I'm "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:123
msgid "Nice to meet you. I'm "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:124
msgid "Gordon, what did you say you did here again?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:125
msgid "I'm just checking in on all my friends. Nice to see you again. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:130
msgid "I look for opportunities."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:131
msgid "Opportunities? Like what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:135
msgid "I look for ways of maximizing my potential worth."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:136
msgid "Hmm, sounds like greed to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:140
msgid ""
"I am greedy. But most people misunderstand greed. Greed is a powerful driving force. Throughout\n"
" history, mankind's greatest achievements were driven by men that wanted to better their positions.\n"
" Driven by greed. Greed, for lack of a better word, is good."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:141
msgid "I'll take your word for that, Gordon. But what does greed have to do with Gecko?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:150
msgid ""
"So far, not much. But in greed lies Gecko's salvation. I have important information about the\n"
" survival of Gecko, but I can't get anyone to listen to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:151
msgid "What kind of information?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:160
msgid ""
"Well, I've calculated that if our reactor was running properly, we could generate an enormous\n"
" amount of excess power -- far more than Gecko needs."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:161
msgid "Yeah, so?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:170
msgid ""
"Well, now that you've helped to repair our atomic power plant I have a much better chance of\n"
" getting what I want. Maximizing my potential."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:171
msgid "Maximizing your potential? What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:172
msgid "Is this greed talking again, Gordon?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:180
msgid ""
"I've also found out, from a very reliable source, that Vault City cannot expand without\n"
" additional power."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:181
msgid "Vault City can't expand?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:182
msgid "A very reliable source? Who?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:190
msgid ""
"Vault City, you see, has enough power for their current needs -- as long as they're careful. But\n"
" the Vault power plant that they use was never designed for the increased load their city is putting on\n"
" it. It's at peak capacity right now. Without more power, they can't expand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:191
msgid "I don't see how that helps you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:200
msgid ""
"Well, if our power plant's working better, we could trade our excess power and technical\n"
" expertise to Vault City in exchange for medical technology. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:210
msgid ""
"Without more power Vault City will burn out their reactor within 15 years. If Gecko's reactor\n"
" isn't repaired, we won't last half that time. Without medical technology, all of us Ghouls are going\n"
" to die off in the next 20 years, anyway. Everyone loses if Vault City and Gecko don't cooperate."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:211
msgid "So you're just a good Samaritan huh? Somehow, I don't buy that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:220
msgid ""
"Not at all. I've got my end covered. I'd be the natural choice to administer this project.\n"
" Greed is my driving force, but thousands of lives are saved by it. Greed is good. At least it would be,\n"
" if I could get anyone in Vault City to read my economic data."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:221
msgid "I don't think I'd want to see you administering anything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:222
msgid "Hmm, I might be able to show the data to someone in Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:223
msgid ""
"I bet Councilman McClure in Vault City would love to get his hands on that data. He seems\n"
" like someone who's ruled by reason more than prejudice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:224
msgid "What a great story, Gordon. You're the best. (chuckle) I'll remember that one. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:230
msgid ""
"I tally up economic data on Gecko's economy and report it to Harold. But he usually doesn't\n"
" listen to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:231
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that. Economic data on what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:232
msgid "Well, I'm sure Harold's pretty busy. See you later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:240
msgid ""
"One night, I heard a voice calling to me from the reactor pit over there. A voice out of the\n"
" shadows. I didn't know what to think at first, but what the voice said sure made a lot of sense. Its\n"
" figures all check out, too. Don't know who or what the voice is, but the facts all tally up just like\n"
" it said. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:241
msgid "What did the voice say?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:250 dialog/gcgordon.msg:260
msgid "Mostly on ways of maximizing potential worth. My potential worth. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:251 dialog/gcgordon.msg:261
msgid "Your potential worth? Sounds to me like you're just greedy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:271
msgid ""
"I just don't buy your idea that greed is good. I bet you'd just sell off portions of whatever\n"
" you were supposed to administer and take off with the money. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:272
msgid "Because you left out the most important part of your plan. A partner -- namely, me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:280
msgid ""
"Well, I have all the relevant economic data on a disk. You may have it, if you promise to show\n"
" the data to someone in Vault City that can understand and make use of the data it contains. But be\n"
" discreet with it... not everyone there will be happy you talked to us ghouls."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:281
msgid "I don't think I want to be stuck with your disk. Thanks anyway. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:282
msgid "Okay, I'll take the disk. I'm sure that I can put it into the right hands. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:290
msgid "Humph, I don't need your help. You're just a tribal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:291
msgid "Well, I guess not all the bigots live in Vault City, do they, Gordie old boy? Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:300
msgid ""
"Our atomic power plant is still barely operational. You must not take the information to\n"
" Vault City yet."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:301
msgid "I don't think they'd be very receptive to ghoul data in Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:302
msgid "No, I haven't yet... but I will. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:303
msgid ""
"Delivering that data to Vault City is only one of the many steps you need to take. Our atomic power\n"
" plant is still barely operational and needs to be fixed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:304
msgid "I will get right on it. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:305
msgid "Yeah, maybe some other time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:310
msgid ""
"Thanks for fixing our atomic power plant. The next step in old Gordon of Gecko's plan is working\n"
" nicely. Greed is a wonderful thing. You should be proud to be a part of this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:311
msgid "Greed is good; right, Gordon? Well, I've got plans of my own to work on. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:320
msgid "We're doomed. We're all doomed. Nothing can save us now. Just go away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:321
msgid "Just get away from me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:322 dialog/gcharold.msg:179 dialog/vcmclure.msg:261
msgid "Okay, goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:330
msgid ""
"I really owe you. Now I can get everything I've ever wanted. All at Gecko and Vault City's\n"
" expense. Just as soon as I'm ratified as the new foreman. Yessir, that Harold's really out on his ass\n"
" now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:331
msgid "Uh, yeah. Whatever, Gordon. (you roll your eyes). Well, I guess I'll be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:332
msgid ""
"You just better watch yourself, Gordon. The trip down is usually a lot faster than the trip up.\n"
" Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:340
msgid "I see you have the symbol. Are you here for the information?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:341
msgid "The symbol?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:342
msgid "The information?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:343
msgid "Of course. I wear the symbol proudly, and I need the information right away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:344
msgid "Shhh. Not now, brother. We're being watched. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:350
msgid "You wear the symbol of Renewal. You are one of us. Renew, comrade! Renew!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:351
msgid "Yes, I am one of us. Reno, uh, Renew!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:352
msgid "I just found this. What is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:353
msgid "I picked this off a corpse. What the heck is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:360
msgid "Did he send you for the data disk?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:361
msgid "Yes, of course I'm here for the disk. Hand it over right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:362 dialog/gcgordon.msg:371 dialog/gcgordon.msg:402
msgid "What disk?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:370
msgid ""
"Ah, well, there can never be too many in our cause. More comrades means a better chance for old\n"
" Gordon here to get what he wants. Are you here for the disk?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:372
msgid "I think the radiation has fried your brain. I'm leaving. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:380
msgid ""
"Here it is, but don't let the wrong person know that you have it. Give it only to Councilman\n"
" McClure in Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:381
msgid "Yes, of course. Uh, Renew, brother."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:382
msgid ""
"I'm not bringing any ghoul disk into Vault City -- they'd put my head on a stick for that.\n"
" Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:390
msgid ""
"It's the economic data disk that proves that Gecko and Vault City must both work together in\n"
" order for either of us to survive. Are all of you smoothskins such smallbrains?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:391
msgid "Oh, yes, that disk; sure I'll take it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:392
msgid ""
"That sounds like really complicated stuff, all right. Too much for a pinhead like myself to\n"
" understand. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:400
msgid ""
"Ah, of course. (wink, wink) We have all \"found\" the symbol. Renew, comrade! Are you here for the\n"
" disk?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:401
msgid "Yes, I am. Where is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:403
msgid "No, not really. I think I'd better leave now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:410
msgid "A corpse? Which one of us died?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:411
msgid "Uh, I mean it was given to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:412
msgid ""
"Which one died? You're all dead. You're friggin ghouls, aren't you? One of your ghoul friends\n"
" gave it to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:413
msgid "Well, you should really ask which one of you I haven't killed. By the way -- you're next."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:414
msgid "No, you misunderstood me. I said I joined the corps. Renew brother!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:420
msgid ""
"The facts speak for themselves. If you show it to someone with an open enough mind, the data\n"
" will do all the convincing they'll need."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:421
msgid "Well, okay. I'll try it. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:422 dialog/rcmarion.msg:263
msgid "I'll think about it. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:500
msgid ". What do you do here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:501
msgid ". See you later, Gordon. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcgordon.msg:600
msgid "Thanks for the information Gordon. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:100
msgid "You see a glowing ghoul with a concerned look on his face."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:101
msgid "You see Hank the glowing ghoul, a worker here in the power plant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:102
msgid "You see a glowing ghoul monitoring some power plant gauges."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:110
msgid ""
"Hello, I'm Hank. I take care of the inside of the reactor core. Not that much ever needs to be\n"
" done there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:111
msgid ""
"Hello, nice of you to visit me again. Feels nice and toasty this close to the core. Most\n"
" smoothies don't care for that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:112
msgid "Hi, Hank. I need to get inside the Core."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:113
msgid "Hank, I have a coolant report from Harold that you need to see. Here you go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:114
msgid "Hi there, Hank. I'm just taking the tour. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:120
msgid ""
"Heh, heh. I wouldn't advise that, smoothy. You'd fry into a crisp. Me, I like the warmth, but I\n"
" wouldn't recommend it for you. Quite a bit of heat and radiation in there. That's why the smoothies\n"
" that built this place included a maintenance bot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:121
msgid "Maintenance bot?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:122 dialog/gclumpy.msg:272
msgid "Oh, thanks. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:130
msgid ""
"Let me look this over. According to this, our coolant level is way too high. I would've thought\n"
" that turning off the coolant would lead to immediate meltdown but I guess not. I'd better go turn off\n"
" the coolant right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:131
msgid ""
"That report said our coolant level was too high. I should turn off the coolant now, don't you\n"
" think?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:132
msgid "Good thinking, Hank. I better be going. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:133
msgid ""
"On second thought, maybe you should wait a moment on that. Let me check with Harold before you\n"
" turn off the coolant. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:140
msgid ""
"Yeah, the smoothies that built this place didn't want to fry either, so they included a robot.\n"
" It was designed to perform maintenance tasks by remote control from that terminal over there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:141
msgid "That's perfect. I can use that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:142
msgid "I'll have to check that out. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:150
msgid "Nice part you got there. Just what we need."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:151
msgid "Glad you like it. Want to install it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:152
msgid "Thanks, I really like it too. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:160
msgid ""
"I'd like to help you out, but I wouldn't know how to install something like that. I mostly just\n"
" watch the gauges here. Try Festus. He's the resident parts genius -- just ask him."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:161
msgid "Where is Festus?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:162 dialog/gchank.msg:172
msgid "Is there any other way?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:163 dialog/gczomak.msg:242 dialog/gczomak.msg:271
#: dialog/vcgatgrd.msg:199
msgid "Okay. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:170
msgid "You talk to Festus about installing that part yet?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:171
msgid "Where is he?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:173
msgid "Not yet. Maybe I'll go do that now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:180
msgid ""
"Festus is out the way you came in. He's in the control room. Can't miss him... he's the smelly,\n"
" whiny one tottering about underneath that huge ego. He should be able to help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:190
msgid ""
"Well, if you could control the maintenance robot, it might be able to install it. Or, you could\n"
" just walk in there and install it yourself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:191
msgid "Maintenance robot?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:192
msgid "Install it myself?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:200
msgid ""
"Well, it hasn't worked too well, lately. It kept overheating. We don't need to use it anyway, so\n"
" we didn't bother to fix the heat shielding on it. If you can figure out the control codes and don't run\n"
" it for too long, you may be able to get it to do what you want."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:210
msgid "Thanks for fixing the reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:211
msgid "Is it cooler in here lately?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:212
msgid "Thanks for helping us out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:220
msgid "I've never heard her hum like that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:221
msgid "Purring like a kitten."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:222
msgid "Runs better than ever."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:230
msgid "Just stay out of the way and don't touch anything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:231
msgid "How'd you get in here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:232
msgid ""
"Why don't you take a little walk through those doors. Glowing pit, pretty-pretty. Heh, heh,\n"
" heh."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gchank.msg:300
msgid "You tricked Hank into starting a meltdown."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:100
msgid "You see a particularly leathery-looking Ghoul."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:101
msgid "You see Harold."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:102
msgid "You see a very old but still spry-looking ghoul."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:103
msgctxt "hld1a"
msgid "I gotta tell ya, ol' Harold's a bit slow on the draw hisself. The two of us talkin' wouldn't get a whole lot done."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:104
msgctxt "hld1b"
msgid "Ahh, ain't you cute. I just don't have time to try understanding ya right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:105
msgctxt "hld1c"
msgid "Heh heh, ain't you a kick. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:106
msgctxt "hld2a"
msgid "Hello there, smoothskin. The name's Harold. I help keep this town running."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:107
msgctxt "hld2a1"
msgid "Whatcha need, youngster?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:108
msgctxt "hld2b"
msgid "Well, golly-be-damned, smoothskin. You did us a great favor helping out our power plant. The name's Harold. I keep this town running."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:109
msgctxt "hld2c"
msgid "Mighty kind o' ya helping us out with the atomic power plant. We're in your debt. Now, what can this cranky-old carcass do for ya?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:110
msgctxt "hld2d"
msgid "You are somethin'. Just like the original. What can old Harold do for ya, Vault Dweller? "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:111
msgctxt "hld2e"
msgid "Haven't you done enough harm, smoothskin? What do you want now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:112
msgid "Smoothskin? Why did you call me that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:113
msgid "Vault Dweller? I'm not a Vault Dweller."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:114
msgid "Hello, Harold. What do you do here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:115
msgid "Is there someplace I can barter or re-supply here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:116
msgid "Is that a tree growing out of your head?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:117
msgid "You must know if there's something called a Garden of Eden Creation kit here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:118
msgid "Harold, I'd like to know where I can get some healing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:119
msgid "I know you're probably still mad, but you mentioned the Master. My ancestor killed him."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:120
msgid "Hello, Harold. Just passing through. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:121
msgctxt "hld3"
msgid "Wha-whatever it takes to keep this place together. Better job on it than me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:122
msgid "This place is coming apart?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:123
msgid "You don't sound so good."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:124
msgctxt "hld3a"
msgid "Yep, but I'm doing great for being dead! I never get tired of the looks when I tell that one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:125
msgid "Ahh, right....So you say the place is falling apart?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:126
msgid "Dead, you say? Well, in that case you're doing great. So good you can answer my next question."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:127
msgctxt "hld4a"
msgid "Well, sorta. Our atomic reactor's a mite... sensitive. The people I got running it mean well, but... well, they are not the sharpest tools in the shed. If you know what I mean."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:128
msgctxt "hld4b"
msgid "Well, we're doing better now you've fixed our reactor. I'd never thought anybody'd get those idjits in Vault City to help us out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:129
msgctxt "hld4c"
msgid "You know, it's not so bad now. You fix the power plant, then you get the info we need to make it good-as-new. Golly-be-damned, ain't you somethin'?!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:131
msgid "I didn't want to see Vault City destroy your town."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:132
msgid "Well, I didn't want to see Vault City destroy your town. Besides it was in their best interest to fix your power plant as well."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:133
msgid "Well, since it's in Vault City's best interest to fix up your reactor, it wasn't too hard to get the Optimization info from them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:134
msgid "I don't like to complete any job only half-way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:135
msgid "Well, I'd love to stay and chat with you but I've got things to do and places to go. Good luck."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:136
msgctxt "hld5"
msgid "Well, technically... it's a thingie."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:137
msgid "Okay, what does it do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:138
msgctxt "hld6"
msgid "Need a little time on the whetstone yourself, huh? I mean they are not too bright. Here's an example. The other day I get a report. On it, it says the main coolant valve should be shut down. That woulda caused a meltdown that would make the Grand Canyon look like a pig wallow."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:139
msgid "That sounds bad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:140
msgctxt "hld7"
msgid "Uh, yeah, that would be bad. Now, I got things fixed up in time, but we came close to the end there. They need someone to watch out for 'em."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:141
msgid "Good thing you're here to help them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:142
msgctxt "hld8"
msgid "Who'd a thought I'd be making things right? Although if we don't get a Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator pretty damn quick, there is gonna be trouble."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:143
msgid "What the hell is Hydra-magna-whateveraltor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:144
msgid "Hmm, sounds like a real problem all right. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:145
msgid "Trouble? What kind of trouble?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:146
msgid "Well, I've taken enough of your valuable time. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:147
msgctxt "hld9"
msgid "Heck, if it weren't for you, them damn idjits in Vault City woulda laid us out for the big dirt nap."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:148
msgid "I couldn't let Vault City kill all of you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:149
msgid "Happy to help out, Harold. Let me ask you about something else, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:150
msgctxt "hld11a"
msgid "Mighty kind a'ya. Not many smoothskins would do that for a town full of ghouls. Kinda reminds me of a smoothie I knew, way back when."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:151
msgctxt "hld11b"
msgid "You know, you're a lot like the Vault Dweller."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:152
msgid "Another smoothie? What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:153
msgid "Thanks. I'm hoping to live up to my ancestor. Let me ask you something else while I'm here that might help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:154
msgid "Happy to help. Let me ask you about something else though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:155
msgid "Well, all in a day's work really. I need to be going now, though. People to save, monsters to slay, disasters to avert, you know, all that sort of thing. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:156
msgctxt "hld14"
msgid "You cut with the dull edge of the knife, don't ya? You don't look like an orange peel left in the sun all day. Your skin's still soft and purty. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:157
msgid "Got me there. I'll try to make my next question a little more worthwhile."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:158
msgid "Oh. Yeah. Hey, let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:159
msgid "You just better not be getting any funny ideas about my soft skin."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:160
msgid "Uh, well, I better be going. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:161
msgctxt "hld15"
msgid "Funny ideas? Well, you mean like skinning you alive with a rusty, dull, old knife and then grafting your still-warm, wet, glistening, oh-so-soft, skin over my crusty-rotten gook?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:162
msgid "Hey! You just keep the hell away from me. I'm getting out of here while I still have my skin!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:163
msgid "Yeah, that's exactly what I meant. Good call."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:164
msgctxt "hld16"
msgid "Well, you don't have anything to worry about....can't find my knife."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:165
msgid "How 'bout I change the subject with another question?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:166
msgid "Well, you just better keep your grubby mitts off my skin. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:167
msgctxt "hld17"
msgid "More skin! ... Need more skin! (chuckles) What happ'n? Drop your sense of humor in the dust on the way into town?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:168
msgid "I've got a lot on my mind, all right? I need some more information."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:169
msgid "I think I'll go look for it. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:170
msgctxt "hld18"
msgid "I just let a big fart and it still doesn't cover your stink. Why don't you just drift outta here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:171
msgid "Okay, but first I wanted to apologize for the way I acted earlier."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:172
msgid "Put a sock in it ya smelly old ghoul. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:173
msgctxt "hld19"
msgid "That's a start, but you're gonna have to do better."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:174
msgid "I don't know what else to say. I guess I just don't deal well with things that are new to me. I am sorry, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:175
msgid "Okay, how 'bout this? If I had jerky that looked half as bad as you do I'd burn it just to keep from poisoning any scavengers that might happen upon it. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:176
msgctxt "hld20a"
msgid "Well, alright. But you'd better stop being a bonehead. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:177
msgctxt "hld20b"
msgid "Well, I tell ya youngster. Nice try but yer still an idjit. Maybe this'll be the lesson you need. You are outta here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:178
msgid "I'm sorry. Now that we've got that settled. Let me ask you something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:180
msgctxt "hld21a"
msgid "I'd rather look like this than look like you and have to be you. You are a bonehead. Get the hell outta here. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:181
msgctxt "hld21b"
msgid "You're like that bad booger ya can't shake off your finger. But I'm still shaking.... Oh look, there ya go!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:182
msgctxt "hld21c"
msgid "Well, look what the wind pooped in. My favorite turd. Why don'tcha just squish on outta here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:183
msgctxt "hld21d"
msgid "Wanna know how to keep an idjit in suspense?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:184
msgctxt "hld21e"
msgid "Hey, I was hoping you'd show up. You won a prize for bein' the biggest jerk. There's a party in your honor ten miles north of town. Better hurry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:185
msgctxt "hld26"
msgid "Their best interest? What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:186
msgid "Well, according to some economic data I got hold of Vault City is much better off if they help you to repair your power plant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:187
msgid "I mean, it's always better to try to get along with others."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:188
msgid "Uh, nothing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:189
msgid "Wow, it's much later than I thought it was. I better be going. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:190
msgctxt "hld27"
msgid "Economic data? You didn't give them that information th-that Gordon keeps flapping his yap about, did you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:191
msgid "Uh, yes I did. Why?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:192
msgid "Uh, no, of course not."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:193
msgctxt "hld28"
msgid "Yeah, well, I'm sure some bonehead, very much like yourself, said the same thing about the Master."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:194
msgid "Sounds like a great story. Wish I had time to hear it but I gotta go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:195
msgid "The Master? My ancestor killed him!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:196
msgctxt "hld29"
msgid "Nothing, huh? I'm not buyin' it. You just put us in a bind. Why don't you skedaddle while I thinka what to do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:197
msgid "Uh, sorry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:198
msgid "Yeah, sure. Why don't you just do that. Geez, try to help some people...."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:199
msgctxt "hld30"
msgid "Why?! Now Vault City knows just how much we need uranium ore from Broken Hills. They could cut off them shipments and we'd be finished."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:200
msgid "Oh, it can't be as bad as all that. They seemed like reasonable people to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:201
msgid "I didn't know that was what they'd use the information for. I'm sorry. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:202
msgctxt "hld31"
msgid "Well, I sure hope not. Those idjits in Vault City hate ghouls. They'd cut off our ore shipments from Broken Hills in a white-hot minute. Then they'd set the terms. Wouldn't be long until Gecko'd be a slave camp."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:203
msgid "Oh, I'm sure they wouldn't do that. They seem pretty reasonable."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:204
msgid "Well, it's a good thing I didn't tell them anything like that then. Heh, heh. Hey, let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:205
msgid "Well, shit happens. Sometimes it happens to you. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:206
msgctxt "hld32"
msgid "Reasonable? Reasonable! Well, I'm sure people said the Master was reasonable, too. What a bonehead. Get the hell out. Now!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:207
msgid "Maybe they have the right idea. Maybe it's time to put an end to freaks like you. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:208
msgid "Uh, well, I uh, that is. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:209
msgctxt "hld33"
msgid "Well, you might try talking to Wooz over in the Harp. You can't miss it - it's just across the way. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:211 dialog/gcharold.msg:217 dialog/gcharold.msg:220
msgid "Thanks, that's all I need to know for now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:212
msgctxt "hld34"
msgid "Jealous? His name's Herbert. I talk to him when I get lonely... Heh heh. Just kiddin'... His name's Bob."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:213
msgid "Right... Well, maybe you or Bob will know the answer to this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:214
msgid "Thanks, that's way more than I need to know for now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:215
msgctxt "hld35"
msgid "A Garden of Eden Creation Kit? A GECK, right? I seem to remember Vaults had those. Don't know where you'd find one today. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:218
msgctxt "hld36"
msgid "Just talk to my assistant, Lenny. He'll be able to fix ya right up."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:221
msgctxt "hld37"
msgid "Another smoothskin. Had a lot of respect for that one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:222
msgid "Who was that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:223
msgctxt "hld38"
msgid "Well, I could probably remember if I wasn't dead. I never get tired of that joke. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:224
msgid "Maybe you don't..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:225
msgctxt "hld38a"
msgid "Well, to be honest, can't remember the name. But they wore a funny suit. Kinda like the one you're wearing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:226 dialog/gcharold.msg:229
msgid "I'm wearing the Vault Suit that my ancestor wore. It's a totem of my holy quest."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:227
msgid "Oh, this old thing?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:228
msgctxt "hld38b"
msgid "No lie?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:230
msgid "No lie, Harold."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:231
msgctxt "hld39"
msgid "That so? Well, well, well. That explains a thing or two. I wondered why you looked familiar. I'm not losing the last coupla marbles I got left."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:232
msgid "We really look alike?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:233
msgid "Tell me what the Vault Dweller was like."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:234
msgctxt "hld40"
msgid "Yea, it looked just like that. Come to think of it, it had a 13 on it too. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:235
msgid "Actually, this is the suit of my ancestor, the Vault Dweller."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:236
msgctxt "hld41"
msgid "There is a resemblance. Near as I can remember, anyways. You know, your ancestor saved the whole darn lot of us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:237
msgid "The Vault Dweller saved all of the ghouls?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:238
msgid "Thanks. It's nice to know. Look, I have to run off for a bit. I'll see you later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:239
msgctxt "hld42"
msgid "Jumpin' to conclusions, youngster. That's gonna get your ass shot off someday. All of us. Saved every two-legged-shuffler on the dang planet. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:240
msgid "I didn't realize that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:241
msgid "I think I've heard enough for now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:242
msgctxt "hld43"
msgid "Well. Now ya do. And what happened next? For a thank you, the damn high-and-mighty Vaulties booted the Vault Dweller out. I always wondered what happened after that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:243 dialog/qcmartin.msg:124
msgid "I can tell you what happened."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:244
msgid "Enough reminiscing let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:245
msgctxt "hld44"
msgid "Well, I'd sure like to hear that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:246
msgid "The legend of the Vault Dweller starts with the Vault casting him out into the dry Wastes.... [You tell Harold the story of your ancestor]...and so that's why I'm looking for Vault 13 now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:247
msgctxt "hld45"
msgid "Thanks for telling. I sure was curious all these years. You sure got your work cut out for ya. Huh, ya know...."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:248
msgid "Know what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:249
msgid "I've taken enough of your time already. I better be going. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:250
msgctxt "hld46a"
msgid "Well, I been saving these for a rainy day, but it sounds like you're gonna need'em more than I ever will. Here, take these."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:251
msgctxt "hld46b"
msgid "I was gonna give you some healing supplies but damn me if I didn't do that already. I tell you, gettin' old's hell on the memory."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:252
msgid "Thanks. Let me ask you about something though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:253
msgid "Thanks for everything. I better be going though. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:254
msgctxt "hld48a"
msgid "Without a functional Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator we're leaking radioactive coolant into the groundwater. Now that means, anyone using that water is not gunna need a night-light to take a midnight piss. Also, we need more fuel because our power plant is not burnin' it very efficiently."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:255
msgctxt "hld48b"
msgid "We need a Hydroelectric Magnetosphere Regulator and it needs to be installed soon or we have got some real problems. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:256
msgid "Sounds bad. Where would you get a Hydro magnetosomething-or-other?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:257
msgid "What happens if you don't get the part?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:258
msgid "Who do you buy your fuel from?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:259
msgid "Sorry to hear it. Let me ask you about something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:260
msgid "I think I'm going to have to leave you to your troubles for right now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:261
msgctxt "hld49"
msgid "Well, I'm certain those ornery bastards in Vault City have one. Not that they'd share. Hell, even if we had one of those thingies, I'm not so certain Festus could install the dang thing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:262
msgid "Vault City wouldn't give you the part? Even if it means that the groundwater won't be polluted anymore?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:263
msgid "Sounds like you've got a lot on your mind. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:264
msgctxt "hld50"
msgid "If we don't get it, you can bet those boneheads from Vault City will shut down our power plant, permanently."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:265
msgid "What will you do then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:266
msgctxt "hld51"
msgid "We get our fuel from the Broken Hills. That's a mining community some ways south."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:267
msgid "Interesting. Where would you get one of those Hydro magnetosomething-or-others?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:268
msgid "What happens if you don't get that Hydro-part?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:269
msgid "Hmm, I think I should let you figure this out on your own. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:270
msgctxt "hld52"
msgid "Take dirt naps. Vault City doesn't play nice. They'll just come up here and kill all of us if we don't get that part. Well, at least I'll have a tree for a monument."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:271
msgid "What was the name of that part again?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:272
msgid "Sounds like you need that Hydro-thingy pretty badly. Let me ask you something else right now, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:273
msgid "Sounds like trouble. I need to run off and see what I can do. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:274
msgctxt "hld53"
msgid "Well, they'd only help us if they thought it was in their own best interest to do so. Huh. Not much chance of that happening."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:275
msgid "Hmm, you may be right. Still if someone could convince them that they should help you..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:276
msgctxt "hld54"
msgid "They shoot ghouls on sight. Makes conversation a bit tricky."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:277
msgid "I wonder if someone else could tell them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:278
msgid "Yes, it would. Right now I've got another question."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:279
msgid "Hey, you never know. I'll see you later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:280
msgid "To the north"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:281
msgid "To the northwest"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:282
msgid "To the west"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:283
msgid "To the southwest"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:284
msgid "To the south"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:285
msgid "To the southeast"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:286
msgid "To the east of here"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:287
msgid "To the northeast"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:288 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:344 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:333
msgid "I don't understand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:290 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:335
msgid "That hurts."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:291 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:347 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:336
msgid "That really hurts."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:292 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:337
msgid "That's got to hurt."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:294 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:316 dialog/wsterm1b.msg:132
#: dialog/wsterm4c.msg:202 dialog/wsterm4c.msg:225
msgid "Yes"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:295 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:317 dialog/wsterm1b.msg:133
#: dialog/wsterm4c.msg:203 dialog/wsterm4c.msg:226
msgid "No"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:296
msgid "Why do you talk to me this way?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:297
msgid "You're not nice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:298
msgid "Thank you. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:299 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:322 dialog/kcsulik.msg:3014
#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:324
msgid "This is good."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:300 dialog/kcsulik.msg:3015 dialog/qcgencit.msg:121
#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:325
msgid "This isn't good."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:301 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:326
msgid "I have a good feeling about this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:302 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:325 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:327
msgid "I have a bad feeling about this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:303 dialog/kcsulik.msg:3018
msgid "These people are crazy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:304 dialog/nhmyron.msg:538
msgid "I didn't learn anything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:305
msgid "I learned something"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:306 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:330
msgid "Is everyone else crazy here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:307 dialog/kcsulik.msg:3020 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:331
msgid "There must be another way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:309 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:332 dialog/kcsulik.msg:3022
msgid "Try this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:311
msgid "I'm scared."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:312
msgid "I'm worried."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:313
msgid "I found something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:314 dialog/hcmarcus.msg:338
msgid "I got lucky."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:315 dialog/kcsulik.msg:3034
msgid "You need to fix this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:316 dialog/kcsulik.msg:3035
msgid "You need to turn this on."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:317 dialog/kcsulik.msg:3036
msgid "You need to unlock this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:318 dialog/kcsulik.msg:3037
msgid "You need to open this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:319 dialog/kcsulik.msg:3038
msgid "Maybe we should come back here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:320
msgid ""
"No, lie. I'll make sure the reactor gets fixed. One way or another. Hmm,\n"
" I wonder if I can get Festus to do it. Oh well, goodbye for now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcharold.msg:321
msgid "Hey Harold, I got that part you need to fix your reactor. I am going to go and try to get it installed in the reactor. I'll report back when I am done. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:100
msgid "You see a ghoul with a shaved head."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:101
msgid "You see Jeremy, the ghoul in charge of supplies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:102
msgid "You see a tall, thin ghoul who seems to be very busy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:110
msgid ""
"Hello there. My name's Jeremy. I'm in charge of the all-powerful supply cabinet here. I keep\n"
" track of all our stored supplies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:111
msgid ""
"Hello again. Come to visit the all-powerful supply cabinet, or do you just need something from\n"
" storage?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:112
msgid "All-powerful?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:113
msgid "I need something from storage."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:114
msgid "I don't need anything. I was just looking around. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:120
msgid ""
"Well, if you want something from storage you need a Request Authorization Form. Do you have a\n"
" Request Authorization Form?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:121
msgid "Yes, I do. Here it is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:122
msgid "Uh, no I don't. Where do I get a Request Form?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:130
msgid "Well, this looks like it, all right. What do you need?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:131
msgid "I need a 3-step plasma-transformer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:132
msgid "I need a 3-step plasma-transformer. Want to know what I need it for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:133
msgid "I need a moss-covered, three-handled gredunza."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:140
msgid "I think I have one right here in this cabinet. Ah, yes. Here it is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:141 dialog/gcjerem.msg:151
msgid "Hmm, not the latest model, but it'll have to do. Thanks. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:150
msgid "I don't even want to know. I think I have one right here in this cabinet. Ah, yes. Here it is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:160
msgid "Can't help you now. I'm way too busy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:161
msgid "You see, it's all about stuff."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:162
msgid "You see, it's all about ideas."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:163
msgid "You see, it's all about words."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:164
msgid "You see, it's all about Natas."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:165
msgid "You see, it's all about bald-headed monkeys."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:166
msgid "You see, it's all about secrets."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:167
msgid "You see, it's all about marketing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:170
msgid "Okay, maybe not all-powerful. But it's pretty damn important. What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:171
msgid "I need something from Storage."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:172
msgid "Uh, nothing. I was just looking around. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:180
msgid "I can't believe what they let in here these days."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:181
msgid "Dumb as they come, aren't you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:182
msgid "Don't walk into the reactor pit."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:183
msgid "Uh, I'm too busy to read you a story right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:184
msgid "Keep moving... go ahead. That's a good smoothskin."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:190
msgid "You need a what? Well, there's a waiting list for those. Need anything else?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:191
msgid "Uh, I guess I'll just settle for a 3-step plasma transformer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:192
msgid "Damn. Nope, nothing else will do. I'll just have to come back. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:200
msgid ""
"Hmm, you're not a friend of Skeeter's, are you? He's always trying to get me to give him\n"
" valuable supplies. Then he just pulls the stuff apart and breaks it. I wouldn't trust him to fix a\n"
" toaster."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:201
msgid "Uh, well, actually I was getting it for Skeeter."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:202
msgid ""
"Skeeter who? I just need to bring this part over to the reactor control-room to fix the... Hey,\n"
" look! Is that a rat over there?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:203
msgid "I don't know what they're going to do with the thing. I'm just picking it up."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:210
msgid ""
"I should have expected that. How the hell did Skeeter get anyone to authorize him getting a\n"
" part, though? I just hope he doesn't blow anything up this time. Oh well. Not my business, I suppose."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:211
msgid "Uh, the part? I need to pick it up now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:220
msgid ""
"Well, you could get one from either Harold back in the settlement, or you could get one from\n"
" Festus right here in the main reactor control room. I don't care who you get it from, as long as you\n"
" get it. No Request Authorization, no parts -- that's the way it works."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:221
msgid "Did you get your Request Authorization form yet? Gotta have the form before I can give you any parts."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:222
msgid "Oh, okay. Well, I better go get one, then. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcjerem.msg:300
msgid "Actually, I think I'll get it later. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:100
msgid "You see an especially short, older ghoul."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:101
msgid "You see Lenny, Harold's assistant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:102
msgid "You see a short, older ghoul. He appears to be preoccupied."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:110
msgid "Hello there, my name's Lenny. H'how can I h'help you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:111
msgid "Hello ag'gain. How c'can I help you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:112
msgid "I hear that you're the Descendant of the Vault Dweller. You know, I met the Vault Dweller once."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:113
msgid ""
"Hello there. I j'just can't g'get over h'how much you look like the Vault Dweller. Wh'what\n"
" c'can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:114
msgid "Grenny? Heewo."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:116 dialog/gclenny.msg:151 dialog/gclenny.msg:164
msgid "I'm wounded. Can you help me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:117 dialog/gclenny.msg:152 dialog/gclenny.msg:165
msgid "One of my friends is hurt. Can you help them?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:118
msgid "My friends are hurt. Can you help them?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:119
msgid "Lenny, have you ever heard of something called a Garden of Eden Creation Kit?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:120
msgid "You met my ancestor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:121
msgid "I'm just looking around. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:122
msgid "Can you provide healing?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:125
msgid "Yes. What do you need?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:126
msgid "I guess I don't need anything right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:130
msgid "Y'you sh'shouldn't have left your village. G'go home now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:131
msgid "Home? Goobye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:140
msgid "Y'you sh'should go home."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:141
msgid "I c'can't take time for you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:142
msgid "Sh'shoo. Go away!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:150
msgid ""
"A G'garden of Eden C'creation K'kit? I heard that Vault City had one of those. That's the only\n"
" one I've ever heard of, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:153
msgid "Well, my ancestor, the Vault Dweller, said that Vault 13 owes us one. I need to find it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:154 dialog/gclumpy.msg:263 dialog/kcsulik.msg:806
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:823
msgid "I guess that's all I need to know. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:160
msgid "W'well, I h'help H'harold mostly. Wh'when people get hurt, I h'help them out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:161
msgid "Help Harold do what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:163
msgid "You can heal people?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:166
msgid "I'll have to keep that in mind, if I get hurt. Thanks. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:170
msgid "L'let me t'take a look at that. I th'think I c'can help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:171 dialog/gclenny.msg:182
msgid "Isn't this going to cost me anything?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:172
msgid "Thanks, Lenny. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:173
msgid "Thanks, Lenny. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:174
msgid "I c'can h'help you. B'but it'll c'cost you $30. F'for supplies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:175
msgid "I don't think I need your help right now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:180
msgid "Well, your f'friend c'could use a little h'help. I c'can h'help them though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:181
msgid "L'look's like you f'found some kind of trouble to g'get into. I c'can fix them up, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:183
msgid "Thanks Lenny. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:184
msgid "Thanks Lenny. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:185
msgid "Your f'friend is hurt. I can f'fix 'em up f'for $30. I n'need the m'money for s'supplies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:186
msgid ""
"What have you f'folks been up to. L'looks l'like you c'could really use some healing. I\n"
" n'need to charge you $60 to heal everyone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:187
msgid "Your f'friend looks ok to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:190
msgid "W'well. I didn't actually m'meet the V'vault Dweller. But I saw 'em. Once. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:191
msgid "You saw the Vault Dweller? Where?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:192
msgid "Oh, I see. Well, I've got places to go, things to kill. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:200
msgid "Well, b'before the W'war I w'was a doctor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:201
msgid "Before the war? But that must have been almost 160 years ago."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:202
msgid "Oh; well, that explains it. Thanks. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:210
msgid ""
"That's t'true. B'but the radiation seems to have g'given us g'ghouls a longer life-span.\n"
" 'Course, it took almost everything else away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:211
msgid "Took things away?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:212
msgid "Everything seems to have good and bad mixed together. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:220
msgid "W'well, y'yes. We look l'like f'friggin' f'freaks. We d'don't have any skin, for Chrisakes."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:221
msgid "Well, I guess you have seen better days."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:222
msgid "As a group, you're not the most attractive bunch on the planet. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:230
msgid "Y'you c'could say that. I'd trade in all those years to b'be a n'normal person again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:231
msgid "Well, not much hope of that, I suppose."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:232
msgid "I bet you would. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:240
msgid ""
"If those f'fools in Vault City w'would share their medical technology, I'm sure we could\n"
" c'cleanse the excess r'radiation and heal ourselves."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:241
msgid "They won't help you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:242 dialog/kcbob.msg:202 dialog/vcmoore.msg:114
msgid "I think I've heard enough. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:250
msgid ""
"Y'you've been to Vault City? Then you t'tell me wh'what you think the chances of g'getting\n"
" h'help from those bigots is. M'might as well watch a p'paper dog chase an asbestos c'cat through hell."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:251
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that, but I think you're right. Let me ask you about something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:252
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:260
msgid ""
"N'no. L'life's too short -- heh, heh -- well, for m'most people -- to sweat the s'small stuff.\n"
" Know what? It's all small stuff. This is f'free."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:261
msgid "Thanks Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:270
msgid ""
"I'it w'was a long time ago. In a place called N'necropolis. A lot of us g'ghouls lived there.\n"
" One day, I saw someone running through the city."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:271
msgid "Running?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:272
msgid "Well, I think I've had enough of your hazy memories for now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:280
msgid ""
"Yes, running. You see, we ghouls c'can't run too much anymore. So, I knew it was an outsider when I saw\n"
" them. They ran by so close I could have touched them. I wish that I had joined the Vault Dweller...."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:281
msgid "You wanted to join my grandsire?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:282
msgid "Yeah, as though my ancestor would let a fleshless freak like you do anything with them. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:283
msgid "Uh, well, I'd love to hear the whole story but I've got things to do. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:290
msgid "Yes. I h'had the chance of a lifetime and I blew it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:292
msgid "Well, those are the breaks. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:300
msgid ""
"L'later, I h'heard that the Vault Dweller had fixed our water system. The V'vault Dweller saved\n"
" us -- all of us. Do you understand? It didn't matter that we were ghouls. For once it didn't matter.\n"
" We w'were people again. W'worth saving."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:301
msgid "My ancestor was the founder of our tribe. That memory is revered amongst my people."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:302
msgid "Well, I'm only interested in saving my tribe. The rest of the world can fend for itself. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:310
msgid ""
"Later, I heard that the Vault Dweller destroyed the source of the m'mutant army. The Vault\n"
" D'dweller saved all of us. Human and ghoul alike... I could have been a part of that, but I lacked the\n"
" c'courage. I've never forgiven m'myself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:311
msgid "I am following in my ancestor's footsteps. Would you like another chance? Will you join me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:312
msgid ""
"I'm sure that the work you do here amongst the ghouls has value and meaning. It was good to\n"
" hear of my ancestor. Let me ask you something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:313
msgid ""
"Well, a lot of people are cowards deep down inside. It's not something to be overly ashamed of.\n"
" You're just weak. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:314
msgid ""
"Often the right path is not obvious. We all have our special purpose here. Thanks for telling\n"
" me of my ancestor. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:320
msgid ""
"I'm h'happier than a bull b'brahmin in a pasture-full o' cows! I'd b'be honored to j'join you.\n"
" I m'may be old and I cain't m'move t'too darn fast, leastwasy not for too long, b'but I kin sure p'patch you up when y'you need it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:321
msgid "I am glad that you can join me. I'm sure that your healing skills will come in handy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:322
msgid ""
"Hmm, this might be too arduous for one of your advanced age. I think\n"
" you should stay here. I'm sorry. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:330
msgid "I have work to do here. I c'cannot join you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:331
msgid "You are n'not at all like your ancestor. Y'you disgrace their m'memory."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:332
msgid "Y'you have m'much to learn about life. I d'do not like what y'you have learned so far."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:333
msgid "I am saddened to hear that you cannot join me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:334
msgid ""
"Jeez, you'd think a piece of rotting meat like you would leap at the chance to get out of this\n"
" glowing cesspool of a town. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:340
msgid "I h'help H'harold administer the town. Th'there's always more p'paperwork to do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:341
msgid "What else did you say you did here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:342 dialog/gclumpy.msg:193 dialog/gclumpy.msg:252
#: dialog/kcdunton.msg:312 dialog/kcdunton.msg:322 dialog/kcsulik.msg:223
#: dialog/rcmarge.msg:176 dialog/rcmarge.msg:179 dialog/rcmarge.msg:182
msgid "I guess that's all I need to know for now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:350
msgid ""
"You d'didn't have enough m'money... b'but I helped y'you out anyway. J'jist c'cant stand to see\n"
" p'people in p'pain."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:351
msgid "I can't thank you enough, Lenny. I need some more information from you, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:352
msgid "Thanks, Lenny. I definitely owe you one. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:360
msgid "There are s'so many p'people here. You d'don't need my h'help, anymore. G'good-luck to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:370 dialog/gclenny.msg:2100
msgid ""
"I never th'thought I'd live to see the d'day when I'd be ashamed to b'be p'part of what you're\n"
" doing. You're a d'disgrace to the Vault Dweller's m'memory. B'dee-ya, b'dee-ya, goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:371
msgid ""
"Y'know, I th'thought it w'would be nice to t'travel around with y'you. But you're j'jist an\n"
" ornery and c'cantankerous as a bull b'brahmin with a c'cactus up its ass. And you don't s'smell much\n"
" b'better, either. B'dee-ya, b'dee-ya, goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:372
msgid "I'm sorry to see you go, Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:373
msgid ""
"You can't handle it, huh? Well, you better just drag your half-rotten carcass away before I make\n"
" up my mind as to whether snuffing you is worth a cartridge or not."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:374
msgid ""
"*Burp* Yeah, whatever. I guess you've got other things to do, like spending all of your free\n"
" time trying to remember what it was like to have skin that didn't look like three month old roadkill\n"
" in July. Get out of here, you fucking freak."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:380 dialog/gclenny.msg:1000
msgid "Wh'what d'do you w'want me to do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:381
msgid "Lenny, I know you're really trying. But please get out of my way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:382
msgid "I need you to fight differently, Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:383 dialog/kcsulik.msg:883
msgid "I need you to wait here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:384
msgid "Physician, heal thyself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:385
msgid "I need some healing, Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:386
msgid "I need you to heal some of our friends here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:387
msgid "I need you to heal us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:388
msgid "How are you doing, old-timer?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:389
msgid "I don't need anything else from you right now, Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:400
msgid "You want me to f'fight d'differently?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:401 dialog/kcsulik.msg:891
msgid "I want you to change your distance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:402 dialog/kcsulik.msg:892
msgid "I want you to use your best weapon."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:403
msgid "I want you to use your best armor"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:404
msgid "I want you to fight differently."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:410
msgid "H'how, f'far do you want m'me to be? You know it's hard for me to c'catch up."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:411
msgid "I want you to stay only a short distance away from me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:412
msgid "I want you to stay at medium distance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:413
msgid "I want you to stay at long distance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:414
msgid "I need you to scout ahead."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:420
msgid "Wh'what d'do you want me to d'do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:421
msgid "I want you to fight defensively for now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:422
msgid "I need you to fight normally."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:423
msgid "I need you to fight aggressively."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:430
msgid "I g'guess you c'can teach an old d'dog new tricks. What a k'kick."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:431
msgid "I j'jist c'can't seem to g'get the hang of it, somehow."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:440
msgid ""
"Oh, Okay. I'll w'wait right here until you g'get back. G'give me a chance to r'rest my aching\n"
" j'joints."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:441
msgid "You do that, Lenny. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:442
msgid "You should wait here; oh, and another thing..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:450
msgid "I g'gotta g'get a b'bigger g'gun."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:451
msgid "Use your best weapon, Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:461
msgid "Put your best armor on, Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:462
msgid "Lenny, after you put on your best armor, there's something else I need you to do for me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:470 dialog/gclenny.msg:1300
msgid "That's a g'good idea. I w'was wondering when we'd s'stop for that. I'm h'hurtin' fer c'certain."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:471
msgid "Y'you ought to l'let m'me take a l'look at those w'wounds o' yours."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:472
msgid "Seems l'like someone n'needs m'me to sow 'em up ag'gain."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:473
msgid "Go ahead and heal yourself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:474
msgid "Heal yourself, and then there's something else I need you to do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:475
msgid "Go ahead and heal me, please."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:476
msgid "Heal me, and then there's something else I need you to do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:477
msgid "Go ahead and heal us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:478
msgid "Heal us, and then there's something else I need you to do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:480
msgid "I c'cain't d'do that. I'm not really much of a scout."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:481
msgid "Oh, okay. Never mind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:490 dialog/gclenny.msg:1700
msgid "I'll s'stick c'close to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:491
msgid "Stay close now, Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:492
msgid "Stay close, and there's something else I need you to do for me too."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:500 dialog/gclenny.msg:1800
msgid "I g'guess we d'don't want to m'make too easy a t'target huh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:501
msgid "Don't get too close, Lenny. I want to make them work at hitting us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:502
msgid "Don't close up too much. There's something else I need you to do for me, too."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:510 dialog/gclenny.msg:1900
msgid "Okay, I'll s'stay a b'bit farther off. S'seems like people mostly want to k'kill you, anyways."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:511
msgid ""
"I need you to keep back for your own safety. It has absolutely nothing to do with the way you\n"
" smell."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:512
msgid "Before we spread out I need you to do something else for me, as well."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:520
msgid "I've g'gotten pretty g'good at looking out f'fer myself o'er the years."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:521
msgid "I just need you to be careful when we get into fights."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:522
msgid "I want to make sure that nothing happens to you. Heck, you're an antique. One more thing, though..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:530
msgid "Only way to d'do it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:531
msgid "Just fight the way you normally would, and we should be fine."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:532
msgid "Just loosen up and fight normally. One more thing..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:540
msgid "I c'can't do that. J'jist fighting at all is about all th'these old b'bones kin handle."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:541 dialog/shtandi.msg:229
msgid "OK. Never mind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:1100
msgid "I'm d'doing fine."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:1200
msgid "I have a minor w'wound but I can keep g'going."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:1400
msgid "I need healing now or I'm g'gonna die."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:1500
msgid ""
"Oh, okay. I'll w'wait right here until you g'get back. G'give me a chance to r'rest my aching\n"
" j'joints."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:2000
msgid "There are s'so many p'people here. You d'don't need my h'help anymore. G'good-luck to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:2200
msgid "I w'wasn't sure you'd come back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:2300
msgid "What's with the rush all the time?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:2301
msgid "Oh, sorry. I'll get out of your way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:2302
msgid "Rush, rush, rush. OK, take it easy, I'm moving. Sorry, I didn't mean to get in your way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:2303
msgid "I'm sorry, I just can't move any faster. I'll get out of your way then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:2304
msgid "Oh, okay, I'll lurch out of your way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:2305
msgid "I'll just stagger over here then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:2306
msgid "I don't mean to be an obstacle."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:2307
msgid "Oh, sorry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:3000
msgid "Too many bad things happen around you. I am leaving before something happens to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:3001
msgid "I'm not going to help a childkiller. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:3002
msgid "You scare me with your bloodlust. I will not follow you anymore."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:3003
msgid "I don't want anything to do with a slaver. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:3004
msgid "You are a traitor! You destroyed our powerplant. I will not help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:3005
msgid "I d'don't want anything to d'do with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:4000
msgid "Well, okay, but I sure don't want to be left all alone here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:4001
msgid "All right, if you think it's really a good idea."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:4002
msgid "Well, I don't like to use weapons unless I really have to, but I suppose I could use a knife, I think. I can use a pistol, at least I used to be able to. If I really had to, I think I could handle a submachine gun. If only they weren't so loud. I'm a healer, not a fighter."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:4003
msgid "Gosh I hope I won't need that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:4004
msgid "Well, I don't like to use weapons unless I really have to, but I suppose I could use a knife, I think. I can use a spear, at least I used to be able to. If I really had to, I think I could handle a rifle. If only they weren't so loud. I'm a healer, not a fighter."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:5000
msgid "I think I m'might have a b'broken limb."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:5001
msgid "I think I m'might be r'radiated."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:5002
msgid "I think I m'might be p'poisoned."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:5100
msgid "I'm f'feeling a b'bit warm now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:5101
msgid "That's b'better."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6000
msgid "I need a professional opinion, Lenny. What do you know about managing a heart condition?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6001
msgid "Can you tell me anything about these pills I found, Doc?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6010
msgid "What seems to be the t'trouble? Your t'ticker ain't g'givin' out on you now, is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6011
msgid "No, I was actually wondering if there was anything we could do for Cassidy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6012
msgid "No. I'm going to murder an infirmed old man and I was trying to come up with something more creative than sneaking up and popping a paper bag."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6013
msgid "Just chalk it up to academic curiosity, I guess."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6020
msgid "Heh. No need to get t'tetchy, now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6021
msgid "Well, mostly, it's just c'common sense stuff. Eatin' right, steerin' c'clear of the harder c'chems, that sorta thing. K'keepin' stress to a m'minimum. B'basically, livin' m'more like an old l'lady, and less like... well, us. Heh. O'course, the b'best thing you could d'do would probably be to t'tamp it down with some c'cardiac regulators, m'maybe some v'vasodilators."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6022
msgid "Cardiac what now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6023
msgid "Hmm. Heart pills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6030
msgid "Let's see, now... (Lenny mutters to himself as he reads over the label.)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6040
msgid "Heart pills. I guess what they're p'puttin' out in Vault City and NCR these d'days ain't much different than w'what we were usin' b'back before the w'war. Strong m'medicine. G'get a fella on that stuff, he'd have the h'heart of a m'mutant m'marathon runner. Heck, if he minded his d'doc and took 'em r'regular-like, he could probably live on hot b'buttered chems and n'not have to worry about it skippin' a s'single b'beat. Uh, n'not that I'd recommend that sort o' thing, of course. D'doctors orders are always supposed to be c'clean livin' and p'plenty of r'roughage, right?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6041
msgid "Uh, right. Thanks, Lenny. Let me ask you about something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6042
msgid "Are they dangerous at all? Any side-effects to look out for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6043
msgid "Do you think these could help Cassidy?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6050
msgid "They could be j'just the thing, now that you m'mention it. In fact, I think they w'would be. He'd hafta be careful about a c'coupla' things, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6052
msgid "I knew there'd be a catch."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6060
msgid "Nothin' that'd be likely to c'come up t'too often. They've been known to c'cause dizziness. And y'you shouldn't t'take 'em with g'grapefruit juice, though I d'don't think that's gonna be m'much of a p'problem, these days. Unless that's what those l'lumpy g'green things are supposed to be. Hmmm... (Lenny puts a hand to his chin and stares off into space)."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6061
msgid "Lenny?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6070
msgid "S'sorry. Oh! One more b'big one. Unless you're l'lookin' to meet a l'less-than-d'dignified end, you *do not* want to g'go mixin' those things with N'new Reno p'pep pills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6071
msgid "Pep... pills?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6072
msgid "Bad reaction, then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6080
msgid "Ayup. Y'know, for when your l'little t'trooper won't st'stand at attention? T'technical n'name for 'em was \"PDE-5 inhibitors\" but t'times bein' what they are, and N'new Reno bein' what IT is... Anywho, where was I?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6081
msgid "Ayup. Y'know, for when a man's l'little t'trooper won't st'stand at attention? T'technical n'name for 'em was \"PDE-5 inhibitors\" but t'times bein' what they are, and N'new Reno bein' what IT is... Anywho, where was I?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6082
msgid "Oh, yeah. You g'get those two into your s'system together, and KER-BLAM! Your heart'll explode like a b'blood s'sausage. I remember d'doin' p'post-mortems on m'more than one poor g'geezer who was t'too b'busy sowing his oats to r'read a w'warning label."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6083
msgid "Blood Sausage?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6084
msgid "Huh. Good to know. Thanks a lot, Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6090
msgid "Oh. Heh. Musta b'been a little before your t'time. Sorry. Anything else I can d'do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6091
msgid "Well, since you asked..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclenny.msg:6092
msgid "Nope, that'll do. Thanks, Lenny."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:100
msgid "You see a very glum-looking human."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:101
msgid "You see Lumpy, Skeeter's friend and assistant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:102
msgid "You see a very thin, saggy-eyed, and unhappy-looking human."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:110
msgid "You're in worse shape than I am. Poor moron."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:111
msgid "I don't have time enough to spend talking to morons."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:112
msgid "You ain't much smarter than the brahmin I watch."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:113
msgid "You don't quite have a full deck, do ya?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:114
msgid "By God, you are just as dumb as you look."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:120
msgid "Hello there. My name's Lumpy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:121
msgid "That's sort of an unusual name. How did you come by it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:123
msgid "That's nice, Lumpy. Uh, I've got to be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:130
msgid "Well, my real name's John -- but everyone here just calls me Lumpy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:131
msgid "Why Lumpy?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:132
msgid "Well, who can blame them. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:140
msgid ""
"Hello there. Ever notice that each brahmin has its own personality? Well, if you watch them as\n"
" long as I have, you sure notice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:141
msgid "Yup. Downright fascinating. That's what they are."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:142
msgid "Moo moos."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:144
msgid "That's really interesting. Who are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:145
msgid "I'm curious about some things."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:146
msgid "Nice to meet you. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:150
msgid ""
"Hello there. You're probably here to see Skeeter. I don't really take care of the technical\n"
" stuff. I'm just here to help out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:151
msgid "Keeter. Heh, heh, heh."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:152 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:125
msgid "Who're you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:155
msgid "Oh, okay. I'll talk to Skeeter then. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:160
msgid "Hello there. Since you've already invited yourself in -- what can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:161 dialog/ncboxer.msg:211
msgid "Me hungry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:162
msgid "Uh, I was wondering where Skeeter is?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:164
msgid "Oh, sorry. I didn't mean to barge in. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:170
msgid "I guard the brahmin or help Skeeter in his workshop."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:171 dialog/gclumpy.msg:245 dialog/gclumpy.msg:261
msgid "Who's Skeeter?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:173
msgid "I think that's all I need to know for now. Goodbye, Lumpy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:180
msgid ""
"Well, it's sort of a joke. You see, they usually call people like you and me smoothskins. But I\n"
" was treated so poorly by other Smoothskins down in Vault City that everyone here figured that I must\n"
" be more lumpy than they are."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:181
msgid "Why were you treated poorly in Vault City?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:182
msgid "That explains a lot. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:190
msgid ""
"Well, Skeeter's sort of a mechanic. He'll take apart almost anything that you bring him. Gets\n"
" most of them back together too, sooner or later. Sometimes things end up working better than they did\n"
" before."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:191
msgid "Where can I find Skeeter?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:192 dialog/gclumpy.msg:292 dialog/gcrdesk.msg:141
#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:152 dialog/gcrdesk.msg:171 dialog/gcrdesk.msg:181
#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:192 dialog/kcsulik.msg:822 dialog/rcmarion.msg:174
msgid "Interesting. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:200
msgid ""
"Well, they said I wasn't human enough for them. I'm sorta radiation resistant -- perfect for\n"
" here. But they didn't like it. Treated me like dirt."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:210
msgid ""
"One day I just couldn't take it anymore. I figured that dying out in the Wastes was better than\n"
" living with those assholes in Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:211
msgid "How'd you end up here, then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:220
msgid ""
"Well, a caravan from Broken Hills found me and brought me here. I've been here ever since. One\n"
" thing about the ghouls here is that they care more about what kind of person you are inside. It's like\n"
" a big family."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:221
msgid "Broken Hills? Where are those?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:222 dialog/kcmaida.msg:305 dialog/kcmaida.msg:313
msgid "Interesting. Let me ask you something else, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:223
msgid "It's great that you're happy here. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:224
msgid "A family of freaks. I don't think I want to hear anything else from you. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:230
msgid ""
"Broken Hills is where we get all the uranium that we need for the atomic reactor from. From what\n"
" I understand, the uranium is mined by mutants down there. But they have humans trade the stuff for\n"
" them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:231
msgid "Why do they have humans trade the stuff for them?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:241
msgid "Aren't you the curious one? Well, okay. What do you want to know?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:242
msgid "What do you want to know now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:243
msgid "What's all that junk in the yard?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:246
msgid "Anything unusual going on around here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:250
msgid ""
"Well, because they trade uranium to Vault City, too. Vault City treats anyone that's not a pure\n"
" strain human just like lepers. So, Broken Hills uses human traders. Some guy named Chad, I think."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:251
msgid "Chad, huh? I'll keep that in mind. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:260
msgid ""
"Well, some of this junk is left over from when they were building the reactor -- before the war.\n"
" The rest of this stuff? I just don't know. Skeeter collects all kinds of stuff."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:262
msgid "Interesting. I have another question for you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:270
msgid "Well he's right here. Just open your eyes and look around a bit. Sheesh."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:271
msgid ""
"Well, Skeeter's usually in his workshop. Just south of the unfinished reactor. Can't almost\n"
" never drag him out of there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:273
msgid "I don't know where Skeeter's been recently."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:280
msgid "Well, I mostly stick to my business, but sometimes I think I hear things late at night."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:281
msgid "Hear things? Like what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:282
msgid "Aw, come on. You can tell me what you heard. I won't tell anybody."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:283
msgid "Me too, but I figure they're just voices inside my head."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:290
msgid ""
"Well, I'm not sure, mind you. But I think I've heard people, at least I thought it was people.\n"
" Coming and going from the reactor pit late at night."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:291
msgid "People? Every night?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:300
msgid ""
"I can't tell you. People would think I'm nuts. Probably just the wind blowing through the junk,\n"
" anyway."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:301
msgid "I tell you I didn't hear anything. Now stop pestering me about it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:302
msgid "Okay. Let me ask you something else, then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:310
msgid ""
"(Looks closely into your eyes) You hear voices inside your head? Do they tell you how much\n"
" better you are than everyone else? Do they tell you that someday people will kneel before your\n"
" greatness? (smiles and nods)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:311
msgid "Uh, no. Not really."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:312
msgid "Uh, yeah. Sure I do. Doesn't everyone?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:320
msgid "Good thing. I was really beginning to worry about you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:321
msgid "Well, thanks for your concern. Let me ask you some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:322
msgid "Uh, yeah. Well, I think I need to be moving on. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:330
msgid ""
"I kinda had you pegged for that type when I first saw you, but I wasn't sure. Get out of here,\n"
" you frigging nutcase!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:331 dialog/qcbird.msg:127
msgid "Uh, yeah. Whatever. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:332
msgid "Well, one of us is a nutcase -- I just think you're confused as to which one of us it is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:340
msgid ""
"Well, I don't know if they were people or what, but usually it's just every couple of nights.\n"
" Noises coming and going from the reactor pit. I don't know what's going on, and I don't want to know,\n"
" either."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:341
msgid "I guess I can't blame you. No telling what might be down there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:342 dialog/rclou.msg:151 dialog/rcmcgrew.msg:118
#: dialog/vcgreg.msg:225 dialog/vcwalace.msg:184 dialog/vcwalace.msg:286
msgid "Thanks for the information. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:343
msgid "Isn't the reactor pit too radioactive for anything to live in it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:350
msgid "No, this part of the reactor wasn't completed when the war started."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gclumpy.msg:351
msgid "Oh, I see. Hmm, tell me something else, then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:103
msgctxt "powr1"
msgid "ENCLAVE here. Why isn't your video feed working?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:104
msgid "Uh, it's working just fine. I can see you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:105
msgid "It's broken."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:106
msgid "We're working on the visual link right now. I just wanted to test it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:107
msgid "(Logoff.)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:108
msgctxt "powr2"
msgid "Who the hell is this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:109
msgid "Uh, we're all fine here. How are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:110
msgid "This is caau, rit, sss, pu-, -ear me. Over."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:111
msgid "I'm the Chosen One, so you just better watch your language."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:112
msgid "This is Unit Three reporting in."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:113
msgctxt "powr3_c"
msgid "Well, your unit still doesn't appear to be operational, Pal. Who is this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:114
msgctxt "powr3a"
msgid "That didn't make a damn bit of difference. I'm still not gettin' a damn thing. Who are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:115
msgid "Please repeat. Over."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:116 dialog/gcpacoff.msg:121
msgid "I could tell you but then I'd have to kill you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:117 dialog/gcpacoff.msg:122 dialog/gcpacoff.msg:162
msgid "I'm the Chosen One."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:118 dialog/gcpacoff.msg:123
msgid "Well, that's not unusual, is it? Nothing works right anymore."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:119 dialog/gcpacoff.msg:124
msgid "That's for me to know and you to find out. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:120
msgctxt "powr3b_b"
msgid "What are you talking about? Who-who is this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:125
msgctxt "powr4a_a"
msgid "The President! I, uh..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:126
msgctxt "powr4b_b"
msgid "Oh? A wise guy, huh? Look, I'm tracing you right now, pal. We'll see how smart you feel with internal security all over your fricking ass. Dickhead!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:127
msgctxt "powr4c_a"
msgid "Now, I've had enough of your bullshit. How would you like to play dodge-the-plasma with the Assault Squad? Huh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:128
msgid "Hey, I'm sorry, I didn't mean to upset you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:129
msgid "I've got your trace for you, and I can show you just where to shove it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:130
msgid "You're putting a trace on me? Well, I'm putting a trace on you too, pal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:131
msgid "I'd love to stick around and talk to all of your pals about that bridal shower you've been planning but I've got better things to do with my time. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:132
msgid "Well, I, uh, I've got to be going. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:133
msgctxt "powr5_a"
msgid "Try the gain."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:134
msgid "There... that should do it. Any better?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:135
msgid "Gain? What am I supposed to gain? I keep pretty active; I don't think I can gain anything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:136
msgid "I'll just try back later. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:137
msgctxt "powr6_a"
msgid "Chosen One, huh? Well, uh, pardon me for not blowing sunshine up your ass, but I'm a little too busy for this, your highness."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:138
msgid "Kneel before me and I may spare your life. Gee, I like the sound of that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:139
msgid "I no longer insist upon genuflecting. A slight bow to kiss my ring should be sufficient."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:140
msgid "Uh, I meant I was the one *chosen* to fix the comm-unit. Seems like nothing works anymore."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:141
msgid "Well, I think I've had just about enough of your insolence. Goodbye, peasant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:142
msgctxt "powr7_a"
msgid "Unit Three? I thought you were still at Navarro base?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:143
msgid "Navarro base? Oh yeah, Navarro base. That's where we are. Sure. I knew that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:144
msgid "No, we had to get out of there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:145
msgid "Your signal's breaking up. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:146
msgctxt "powr8_a"
msgid "Huh, ain't it the truth. Just don't let anyone who's got the President's ear hear that. You'll be making cattle-runs to New Reno 'til the end of time, pal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:147 dialog/gcpacoff.msg:196
msgid "The President?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:148
msgid "Only got two legs. I'd be pretty tired by the time I got there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:149
msgid "Well, no rest for the wicked. I better get back to fixing this. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:150
msgctxt "powr9_a"
msgid "Yeah, that's a new one. Since my video's working you can see I'm rolling on the floor here. It does seem like everything's a damn secret though, huh? All the special ops on the mainland. I don't see how anything gets done."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:151
msgid "On the mainland? Why, where are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:152
msgid "Well, it's like that all over."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:153
msgctxt "powr10_a"
msgid "Yeah, you know how unhappy he gets when people complain. He takes it personal, like it's a loyalty thing. Maybe that just goes with being the President of the United States. Or what's left of 'em."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:154
msgid "The President of the United States?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:155
msgid "I didn't vote for him. I thought he was too interested in getting laid. I prefer a candidate that's too old to get it up anymore--keeps their mind on the job more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:156
msgid "Maybe so. You know, I better get back to work. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:157
msgctxt "powr11"
msgid "Oh, very funny. But you'd have a great place to recover from your run -- at least from what I hear."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:158
msgid "So you're not in New Reno then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:159
msgid "Well, I better get back to work. Gotta get this link fixed. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:160
msgctxt "powr12"
msgid "The President of the United-fucking-States-of-America. Who'd you think I was talking about? Who the fu - Who is - What - I should kick your fucking ass, who is this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:161
msgid "I'm the Chosen One. Kiss my... feet."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:163
msgid "I'm the President. You're in a heap of trouble."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:164
msgid "You're not important enough for that information."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:165
msgid "Uh, I better be going. Lots of work to do here. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:166
msgctxt "powr13"
msgid "This is ENCLAVE main comm. ...But you should know that. Who are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:167
msgid "Oh, I'm just... hey, you ever notice that cooked gecko tastes kind of like brahmin butt. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:168
msgid "I'm the Chosen One and you'll learn to remember that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:169
msgid "Nobody important. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:170
msgctxt "powr14"
msgid "Ah, a few more moments and I'll have your sorry ass in a sling. Hey, wait a minute. This can't be right... I've got you somewhere on the mainland."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:171
msgid "That's right, sucker. Right where you can't get me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:172
msgid "That can't be right. I'm at the comm desk right across the hall from you....Made you look. What a rube."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:173
msgid "Yeah, I'm at the Poseidon Oil power plant number 12. Come and get me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:174
msgctxt "powr15"
msgid "I've got you, at Poseidon Oil, reactor number 5. Ah, well, why don't you just sit tight and I'll order up a little celebration for ya. Including fireworks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:175
msgid "Oh, goodie. I just lo-ove fireworks. Send me a lot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:176
msgid "I'm the Chosen One. You just better make sure you say that with a smile."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:177
msgid "I'm not anyone important. I'm going to go now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:178
msgctxt "powr16_a"
msgid "Yeah well, whoever you are, I just dispatched a verti-assault team to your location. Have a nice day."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:179
msgid "Gee, if the video worked you could see me tremble."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:180
msgid "And what are they going to do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:181
msgid "Well, I better get going then. I'd hate for them to show up before I get the red carpet all unrolled. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:182
msgctxt "powr17"
msgid "Usually they just go in shooting. They let someone else sift through the ashes to figure out what was going on."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:183
msgid "Yeah, well, they aren't going to catch me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:184
msgid "Oh, now you've got me all scared. I need to change my undies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:185
msgid "Well, I'd hate to think I spent all day yesterday polishing my guns for nothing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:186
msgid "Yeah, sure. I've killed better. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:187
msgctxt "powr18"
msgid "Goodbye. Next news on you will be when I read the after-action report."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:188
msgid "What? You can read!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:189
msgid "Yeah, sure whatever."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:190
msgid "Hey, you just went on my list."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:191
msgctxt "powr19_a"
msgid "You had to get out? Why? You're on the coast. You got great defenses. I didn't hear anything about that....Hey, who the hell is this anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:192
msgid "I am the great and powerful Willie. Kneel before me and entreat my forgiveness and I may yet spare thee."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:193
msgid "Nobody important. Where's this Navarro again?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:194
msgid "Yeah, well, we took Navarro and I found those nude pictures of your mother. Or was that just your dad cross-dressing again? No wonder you're so fucking ugly. Goodbye, asshole."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:195
msgctxt "powr20"
msgid "Yeah, you can say that again. And everything's always tighter out here at ENCLAVE and the fuckin' President's watching us like a hawk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:197
msgid "Out here? Where are you exactly?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpacoff.msg:198
msgid "Well, that's how things go. Well, I better get back to work. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:100
msgid "You see a short ghoul."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:101
msgid "You see Percy Crump, the successful ghoul merchant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:102
msgid "You see a shorter and rather stout ghoul. He's nattily attired-uh, for a ghoul, that is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:103
msgid "By gosh and by golly. I just shore cain't thank you enough fer gettin' my friend back. Gee-whillikers. I've got to give ya sumpin' fer yer troubles."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:104
msgid "I was glad to help you out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:105
msgid "What do I get?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:106
msgid "Well, it better be worth it. That sure was a lot of work, and a lot of travelling too. Hazardous, that's what it was. I coulda been hurt."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:107
msgid "You shore you don't want to help ole Percy out with his problem? I shore could use the help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:108
msgid "Uh, let me think about it a bit longer. In the meantime, got anything to trade?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:109
msgid "Well, why don't you tell me about it again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:110
msgid "I didn't know you were going to pester me about that every time I came in. Sheesh. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:111
msgid "You find Woody yet? I'm a-gettin' real worried-like. He ain't never been gone so long afore."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:112
msgid "Uh, not yet, but I'm still looking. Hey, do you have anything I could barter for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:113
msgid "No, I sure haven't. I better get back out there and keep looking."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:114
msgid ""
"Hello there, Percy Crump here, Master Merchant in this locality. But you kin call me just plain ole Percy. Yes, you can.\n"
" Heck, everybody does. Now, what can I do ya' for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:115
msgid "What can ole Percy do fer ya?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:116
msgid "I was just wondering what's going on here in town."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:117
msgid "I was wondering if you had anything I could buy or trade for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:118
msgid "Uh, nothing really, I was just looking around. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:119
msgid "Trade?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:120
msgid "Goo? Me go bye-bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:121
msgid ""
"Jist wanna congra-chew-late you fer makin' our atomic reactor run so purdy. She's a purrin' like a kitten now.\n"
" Anyhow's, t'other than that, my friend Woody's done gone missin'."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:122
msgid ""
"I gotta be thankee-kindly for fixin' up our Atomic Reactor. That dang fool Festus tweren't never no darn good.\n"
" Anyhow's, t'other than that, my friend Woody's done gone missin'."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:123
msgid ""
"Not a whole lot new here in town. I hear Wooz rooked some newbie out of a Black Orchid the other day. Heh, heh, hee.\n"
" Anyhow's, t'other than that, my friend Woody's done gone missin'."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:124
msgid "Well, tell me more about that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:125
msgid "Oh, that's too bad. Well, I hate sad tales. I'll leave you alone with your grief. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:126
msgid "Why I shore do, heck, got all kinds of stuff here fer the right price I do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:127
msgid "Get everything you need or do you want some more?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:128
msgid "Me want stuff?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:129
msgid "Hmm, let's see what you've got."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:130
msgid "Let me take another look at your wares."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:131
msgid "That's it for me. Thanks, Percy. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:132
msgid "Oog. Me go bye-bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:133
msgid ""
"This big ole chest of antee-radee-ation medicine shore ain't doin' me no good. Jist about a hunnert-sumpin' years too\n"
" late fer me ta use it. Heh, heh, heee. Here ya go, I'm findin' that friends is worth more'n more every year. Thanks... friend."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:134
msgid "I was glad to help you and Woody. Thanks for the meds."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:135
msgid "Cool, easy job for lotsa loot. I like it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:136
msgid ""
"Well you see, I had a friend, name o' Woody. That Woody, he can sleep like nobody I ever did see. What's worse, he\n"
" likes to travel. Really likes to kick up the dust that one does."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:138
msgid ""
"Well, that ain't so much of a problem, 'round here that is. But, last I heard Woody was goin' to take a stroll over\n"
" to the Den. You know where the Den is?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:139
msgid "Yes, I know where the Den is. Go on."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:140
msgid "Actually, I don't know where the Den is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:141
msgid "Oh, it's real easy to get to. Here: I'll mark it in for ya on your little mappy-thing-doohickie."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:142
msgid "Hey, be careful with that! Okay, go on now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:143
msgid ""
"Well, anyhows, like I been sayin' that ain't so much of a problem 'round Gecko. But, ya see, people in other parts\n"
" ain't so usta the way we look."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:145
msgid ""
"Cain't ya put two an' two ta-gether? I'm worried that Woody might have takin' himself a nap in the Den - it's a long\n"
" trip after all - and then they woulda buried the poor cuss alive! I need someone to go look fer 'im there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:146 dialog/ncrenesc.msg:760 dialog/rchoffy.msg:169
msgid "And...?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:147
msgid "Well, I miss 'im. That's why. (Percy blinks, moistly, at you) Oh, I see, you wanna know what's in it for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:148
msgid "This is usually the part where I get more interested. Tell on."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:149
msgid ""
"Well, I know where I kin get ahold of a heck of a lot of pre-war stock of, jan-u-wine, Rad-X and RadAway. Don't do me\n"
" no good no how, but I figure that outgha be worth sumpin to a smoothy like you. You gonna take the job fer me or not? I'll\n"
" only pay ya off if'n I know Woody's safe."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:150
msgid "Just how much is a heck-of-a-lot?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:151 dialog/gcpercy.msg:155
msgid "Yes, I'll do it. I'll get back to you soon."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:152 dialog/gcpercy.msg:156
msgid "No, I don't think I want to help you out right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:153 dialog/gcpercy.msg:157
msgid "Let me think about it. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:154
msgid "It's a darn sight more'n you'll ever need, that's how much it is. You gonna do it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcpercy.msg:158
msgid "Thankee-kindly for findin' my pal Woody. Now what kin ol' Percy do fer ya?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:100 dialog/gcrguard.msg:100
msgid "You see someone whose skin has been very badly burnt. It seem to be standing guard here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:101 dialog/gcrguard.msg:101
msgid "You see a ghoul acting as a guard."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see someone whose skin seems to have been burned with radiation. That much radiation looks\n"
" as though it should have killed it, but it seems well enough. It looks as though it's\n"
" standing guard here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:110
msgid ""
"Welcome to the atomic power plant. Just a warning to you: if anything goes wrong while you're\n"
" inside, we're going to blame you, smoothskin."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:111
msgid ""
"Hello, friend. I have to let you know that if anything goes wrong, any non-ghouls -- like you --\n"
" are going to be blamed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:112
msgid "Blook?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:113
msgid "I'll be careful. I'm looking for something, and I wonder if you could direct me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:114
msgid "That's only fair, I suppose. I'll be careful. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:120
msgid "You're back, huh? Take a wrong turn?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:121
msgid "Brugah."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:122
msgid "Actually, I do need directions to something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:123
msgid "I thought I saw people living in here. Is that safe?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:124
msgid "Uh, no. That's all right. I'm just kind of looking around. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:130
msgid ""
"Oh. Well, what did you want help finding? The reactor control room, the supply room, the robot\n"
" control room, or the reactor pit?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:131
msgid "The reactor control room."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:132
msgid "The supply room."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:133
msgid "The robot control room."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:134
msgid "The reactor pit."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:135
msgid "I guess I don't need directions after all. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:140
msgid ""
"I think Jeremy has a key. The guards at the security doors have keys, as do some of the people\n"
" that live here in the reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:142 dialog/gcrdesk.msg:154 dialog/gcrdesk.msg:162
#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:183 dialog/gcrdesk.msg:194
msgid "Thanks. That's all I needed to know. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:150
msgid ""
"The reactor pit is just past the control room and then past Festus' room. But you're going to\n"
" need a Red Keycard to get in there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:151 dialog/gcrdesk.msg:191
msgid "Where's the reactor control room?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:153 dialog/gcrdesk.msg:182 dialog/gcrdesk.msg:193
msgid "I need a keycard? How do I get one of those?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:160
msgid ""
"The supply room is through the door to the left of the one that you came into the building\n"
" through. You need to talk to Jeremy in there if you want to get supplies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:161
msgid "Thanks. I need to know where something else is, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:170
msgid ""
"Well, we tend to like the background radiation leakage here. The Glowing Ones really like it.\n"
" None of us would feel very well without it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:172
msgid "Background leakage?!?!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:173
msgid "Oh, okay. Well that's all I needed to know. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:180
msgid ""
"The reactor control room is through the door to the right of the one you entered the building\n"
" through. Then through a door at the end. Past the Yellow Security Door. Then you go off to the right.\n"
" You'll need a keycard for the security door, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:190
msgid ""
"Don't know why you'd want to go there. Damn maintenance robot hasn't worked right in years.\n"
" It's just past the reactor control room, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:200
msgid ""
"Well, I wouldn't worry unless you plan to stay here for more than a couple of weeks. Most of\n"
" the radiation that the reactor leaks goes into the coolant water, and we pump that back underground.\n"
" The little bit that leaks aboveground just feels good to us, somehow."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:201
msgid "Oh, well, that doesn't sound so bad. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:202
msgid "Hmm, I think I better be moving along. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:300
msgid "Sure. What else would you like to know?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrdesk.msg:301
msgid "I need directions to someplace else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrghoul.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see someone whose skin seems to have been burned with radiation. That much radiation looks\n"
" as though it should have killed 'em, but it seems well enough."
