#: dialog/gcrobot.msg:100 dialog/kcrob.msg:100
msgid "You see a robot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrobot.msg:101
msgid "You see the Reactor Maintenance and Repair Robot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrobot.msg:102
msgid "You see a robot. It appears to be functional."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrobot.msg:200 dialog/geckpwpl.msg:300
msgid "The robot has repaired the power plant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcrobot.msg:300
msgid "You programmed the robot to start a meltdown."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:100
msgid "You see a ghoul wearing old, grease-stained clothing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:101
msgid "You see Skeeter, the Ghoul Gadgeteer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a grubby but intelligent-looking ghoul, wearing greasy overalls with a micrometer\n"
" sticking out of his pocket."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:110
msgid "Just don't touch anything -- you might hurt yourself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:111
msgid "I thought tribals were just unsophisticated."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:112
msgid "You can watch. You might learn something, but I doubt it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:113
msgid "Well, ain't you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:114
msgid "Are you just pretending to be dumb, or are you really that stupid?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:120
msgid ""
"Funny you should ask that. Ya see, cars use replaceable fuel cells, or batteries, for fuel. What\n"
" usually broke down was the Fuel Cell Controller. Most amateur mechanics jist assume that it's the\n"
" battery itself. But you know what ass-uming things does, dontcha?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:121
msgid "No, I don't. What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:122
msgid "So does that mean you have a Fuel Cell Controller?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:130
msgid ""
"Well, assuming something makes an ass out of you and me. Get it? That's still a good one, ain't\n"
" it? Heh heh! I haven't used that for years."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:131
msgid "Uh, thanks for the lesson. Now, do you have a Fuel Cell Controller?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:140
msgid "Yep. Sure do. Got it right here. Jist waitin' fer a car to be put into. You got a car?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:141
msgid "I know where one is. What's it going to cost me to get that Fuel Cell Controller?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:142
msgid "I might have one. Maybe I just like old chipsets. How much for the Fuel Cell Controller?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:143
msgid "I wish I did. If I find one, I'll know where to come for a new Fuel Cell Controller. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:144
msgid "Actually, I have another question for you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:150
msgid "Well, money's nice, but I need sumthin' else right now. Sumthin' I cain't get for myself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:151
msgid "What do you need?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:160
msgid ""
"Great. You've got my Plasma Regulator. Thanks. Now I owe you some free work. What did you want\n"
" me to work on? I'll tell you how much it would've cost, but this one's already paid for."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:161
msgid "Let me see what you can work on."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:162
msgid "I think I'll take a raincheck on that for now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:170
msgid ""
"Thanks for fixin' up our atomic reactor. It shore needed some work. I woulda show'd 'em how, but\n"
" they don't trust me in there anymore. They got that idjit loudmouth Festus doin' all the work now. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:171
msgid "Well, I was glad to help. Right now I need something, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:172
msgid "It sure would have been easier if they'd let you fix it. Oh well, it's done now. See you later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:180
msgid "Did you get my 3-Step Plasma Transformer yet?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:181
msgid "I haven't yet, but I'm still working on it. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:182
msgid "Not yet. But I will. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:190
msgid "Hello there, I'm Skeeter. I sort of put things together here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:191
msgid "Hello there. Whatcha lookin' fer?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:192
msgid "Whaddya need?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:200 dialog/rclou.msg:112
msgid "Have you heard of something called a Garden of Eden Creation Kit?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:201
msgid "Do you have a battery that I could use to fix a car?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:202
msgid "I have some things that I want you to take a look at."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:210 dialog/gcskeetr.msg:600
msgid "What do ya want me to look at?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:211
msgid "Ready for me to take a gander at something else? What do ya want me to look at now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:212
msgid "I've got this telescope thing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:213 dialog/gcskeetr.msg:214 dialog/gcskeetr.msg:215
#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:216
msgid "I've got an 'X'"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:217
msgid "Can I swap the parts around later?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:218 dialog/gcskeetr.msg:605
msgid "I don't need anything else. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:220
msgid "Hmm, I can attach this scope you've got to that rifle of yours."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:221
msgid "Well, I can attach this scope to one of your rifles. Which one do you want me to attach it to?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:222
msgid "How much is it going to cost to attach this scope to my Hunting Rifle?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:223
msgid "How much is it going to cost to attach this scope to my Assault Rifle?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:224
msgid "How much is it going to cost to attach this scope to my Sniper Rifle?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:225
msgid "Let me ask you about another item."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:226 dialog/rcdick.msg:152 dialog/rcmodjes.msg:152
msgid "I think that's all I need to know. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:230
msgid ""
"Hmm, I thought so. Well, ya see, I cain't do nuthin' with your [Selected partname]. You need to\n"
" have sumthin' else for me to do sumthin' with it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:231
msgid "Hmm, what about a different item, then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:232
msgid "What part do I need?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:233
msgid "I guess I better come back when I have something else. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:240
msgid "There ya go. I think that ought to work for you all right. Anything else?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:241
msgid "Yes, could you take a look at another item for me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:242
msgid "That's all I need right now. Thanks. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:250
msgid ""
"Hmm, you don't have enough money to cover the cost of working on that. Got sumthin' else ya\n"
" want me ta look at?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:251
msgid "How much would it cost to combine something else?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:252
msgid "I don't think so. Thanks anyhow. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:260
msgid ""
"Mostly I jist sorta tinker with things. Take 'em apart an try to put 'em all back t'gether...\n"
" mostly. Make 'em work better... sometimes. Keepin' myself outta trouble. Know what I mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:261
msgid "I guess. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:262
msgid "Well, I think I better go do something myself. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:270
msgid ""
"You're lookin' fer a GECK, huh? Well, I don't rightly know where ya might find one of them thar\n"
" things. I know that Vault City prolly used ta have themselves one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:271
msgid "Vault City had one?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:272
msgid "Hmm. Well, let me ask you something else then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:273
msgid "Oh well, I better keep looking. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:280
msgid ""
"They sure did. That's how come they're so darn well off. It sure ain't 'cause they know what to\n"
" do. It's 'cause the GECK done started up their crops, and got their town running when they came outta\n"
" the Vault."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:281
msgid "Who would have an unused GECK?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:290
msgid ""
"Well, lemme see here now. As I recollect, most Vaults were s'posed to have themselves a GECK.\n"
" You might try lookin fer another vault somewheres."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:291
msgid "Thanks for the advice. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:292
msgid "Well, I better get looking then. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:300
msgid ""
"Ta be right-honest with ya, I jist dunno. If'n I get all da parts together, I jist get sort of a\n"
" feel fer how they all goes together. Know whatta mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:301
msgid "Uh, you mean you're doing this by guesswork?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:302 dialog/gcskeetr.msg:312
msgid "How about taking a look at something else, then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:303 dialog/gcskeetr.msg:313
msgid "Well, I guess that makes sense. I better go look for another part, then. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:310
msgid "Well, yup. But you see, it's right edu-ma-cated guesswork. That's what it is. Know whatta mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:311
msgid "I don't know what you mean exactly, but I guess I'll go look for another part. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:320
msgid ""
"These days, good tools is harder to git than parts is. I need myself a bran' new Super Tool Kit.\n"
" Snap-sumthin brand's best."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:321
msgid "A new tool kit? Where can I get that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:330
msgid ""
"I reckon that the best place to go an' git that would be down in Vault City somewheres. They've\n"
" got all kinds of tools, but they sure as heck wouldn't give 'em to a ghoul, no how."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:331
msgid "So, you want me to bring you a Super Tool Kit, and then you'll give me the car part?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:340
msgid "Egg-zactly. That's the deal. One Super Tool Kit for one Fuel Cell Controller."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:341
msgid "Sounds like a fair deal, I guess. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:342
msgid "What if I just do this the easy way? I kill you and take the part I need."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:343
msgid "I think I'm going to walk around a bit and think about it. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:360
msgid ""
"Well, now. You could do that, maybe. Then agin, you might be in fer a little surprise there. I\n"
" might be tougher than you think. Then again, mebbe you'd jist be slittin' yur own throat. I kin be\n"
" pretty useful puttin' items together. Always nice to know someone's able to do that, ain't it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:361
msgid "Well, maybe you're right. I'll let you live, for now. Tell me something else, though. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:362
msgid ""
"You sure have a lot of answers, don't you? Hope you have an answer for what's in the afterlife,\n"
" 'cause I'm sending you there -- right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:363
msgid "I'll have to think about that one. Goodbye, for now. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:370
msgid ""
"I see that you've got a mighty fine tool kit there. Snap-off, ain't it? I'll trade you this Fuel\n"
" Cell Controller for it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:371
msgid "Hey there! Yur back with my repair kit. Mmm, Snap-off -- they're the best. Ready to trade?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:372 dialog/hcrsuper.msg:118 dialog/hcseymor.msg:141
#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:118
msgid "It's a deal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:373
msgid "Not right now. I'm holding on to this for a while. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:380
msgid ""
"That's a mighty fine trade. You should be able to jist plug that sucker in and git your car\n"
" a'workin'."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:381
msgid ""
"That's a mighty fine trade. You should be able to jist plug that sucker in and git your car\n"
" a'workin'. You know I could do you another favor by fixin' up some of yur stuff for free, too."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:382
msgid "Really? For free, huh? What do I need to do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:384
msgid "I'm going to go try that right away. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:390
msgid ""
"Well, ya see, I need a darn 3-Step Plasma Transformer. An the only place I can figger to git one\n"
" is from the supply room."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:391
msgid "Why don't you just get it from there, then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:400
msgid ""
"I kinda wore out my welcome there. An it was only a little fire, too. Coulda happened to jist\n"
" anyone. Anyhow, they won't let me anywhere's inside the reactor building now. I need someone else to\n"
" git my part for me. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:401
msgid "How do I get the Plasma Transformer for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:410
msgid ""
"Youz gotta git yourself a Supply Requisition Form. Once you have that, jist give it to Jeremy in\n"
" the Supply Room and he'll give you any darn thing you want. You can get Supply Requisitions from\n"
" Harold or Festus."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:411
msgid "Where are Harold and Festus and will they just give me the form I need?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:420
msgid ""
"Harold's in the Settlement, and Festus is in the reactor control room. But you might have to\n"
" kind of get the forms on the sly, if ya know what I mean."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:421
msgid "You mean I have to steal the Requisition Form, don't you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:430
msgid "Well, err, yeah. I guess so. You might ask them, but I wouldn't put your chances too high there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:431
msgid "Well, I'll see what I can find out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:432
msgid "I don't think I want any part of this. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:440
msgid "Didja come here to take me up on that work I owe you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:441
msgid "I sure did. Let me see what you can work on for me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:442
msgid "Not yet. Just came by to see if you're still here. Well, Goodbye for now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:450
msgid "I'm sorry. You don't have anything that I can use that with. Anything else?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:451
msgid "Take a look at something else I have."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:452
msgid "I guess that's it for now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:460
msgid ""
"Let's see. It's going to cost you $[Cost of combining item a with item b]. Do you want to do\n"
" that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:461
msgid "Yes. I do. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:462
msgid "I don't think that I want to do that after all. What about something else?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:463 dialog/gcskeetr.msg:472
msgid "I guess I don't want you to work on anything right now after all. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:470
msgid ""
"Once I put things together they stay put. You cain't pull 'em apart later and attach 'em to\n"
" other things. Better pick right the first time, I guess."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:471
msgid "OK, I understand. Take a look at something for me, then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:500
msgid ""
"I was wunderin' where the heck my Repair Kit is. You did say you were gonna git it, didn't ya?\n"
" I cain't rightly do much fer ya without that. Sorry. Should be plenty of 'em available in Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:501
msgid "I'll have to come back when I have that. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:502
msgid "I don't think I need your help with anything right now, anyway. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:601
msgid "I have a pistol here and I was wondering...."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:602
msgid "It sure looks as though you could bolt an accessory to this long arm here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:603
msgid "Sometimes I like to get up close and personal. Anything you can do to improve my powered melee weapon?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:604
msgid "Uh, maybe later. Let me ask you about something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:610
msgid "[Spots your magnum revolver.] I can rig a speed loader on that there magnum for $"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:611
msgid "Hmm, that Desert Eagle would sure be a sweet rig with an expanded magazine. I can do that for $"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:612 dialog/nceldrid.msg:352
msgid "Put the speed loader on the magnum."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:613
msgid "Expand the magazine in my Desert Eagle here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:614
msgid "Actually, I had another weapon in mind...."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:615 dialog/rclou.msg:191
msgid "Hmm, let me ask you about something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:616
msgid "Maybe I'll come back later on."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:617 dialog/gcskeetr.msg:627 dialog/nceldrid.msg:357
#: dialog/vcmainwk.msg:250
msgid "Too rich for my blood. I'll be back when I have more cash."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:620
msgid "[Skeeter studies your long arm, and nods slowly.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:621
msgid "I can put a nice all-weather scope on that hunting rifle for $"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:622
msgid ""
"Nothing like having an assault rifle with an expanded magazine. I can fix\n"
" yours up with one for $"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:623
msgid ""
"That FN FAL is a good gun. Hey, I got a low-light scope for that. It's yours\n"
" for $"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:624 dialog/nceldrid.msg:369
msgid "All right then... put a scope on the Colt hunting rifle."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:625 dialog/nceldrid.msg:370 dialog/vcmainwk.msg:236
msgid "Expand the magazine of the AK-112 assault rifle."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:626 dialog/nceldrid.msg:371 dialog/vcmainwk.msg:238
msgid "Attach that low-light scope on the FN FAL."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:630
msgid "You want that melee weapon juiced up? I can *supercharge* it for $"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:640
msgid ""
"[Skeeter takes the item and looks it over with a weird gleam in his\n"
" eye.] Well, this is a mite challengin', but I think I can fix this up real nice\n"
" for ya. Just sit tight for a while. [Skeeter takes the weapon over to his\n"
" workbench and locks it in a really big vise.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:650
msgid ""
"[As you wait you can see Skeeter's back as he works on your weapon. You\n"
" don't know exactly what he's doing but that weird chuckle and all the pounding are\n"
" making you nervous.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:660
msgid "[More pounding and cackling as you wait some more....]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:661
msgid ""
"[You whistle tunelessly and make shadow-puppets against the back wall of\n"
" Skeeter's workshop....]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:670
msgid ""
"There you go. [You wake suddenly as Skeeter takes your weapon from the\n"
" workbench - you can see a number of small shiny, metal parts lingering on the\n"
" bench as Skeeter returns your weapon to you.] That *should* do it, I reckon. Give\n"
" 'er a try."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:671 dialog/nceldrid.msg:411
msgid "Thanks. Can you upgrade any of my other weapons?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:672
msgid "Thanks, Skeeter. Uh, let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:673
msgid "Thanks, Skeeter. I'll go try it out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:680
msgid "[Spots your magnum revolver.] I can rig a speed loader on that there magnum for free."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:681
msgid "Hmm, that Desert Eagle would sure be a sweet rig with an expanded magazine. I can do that for free."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:682
msgid "I can put a nice scope all-weather on that hunting rifle for free."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:683
msgid ""
"Nothing like having an assault rifle with an expanded magazine. I can fix\n"
" yours up with one for free."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:684
msgid ""
"That FN FAL is a good gun. Hey, I got a low-light scope for that. It's yours\n"
" for free."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:685
msgid "You want that melee weapon juiced up? I can *supercharge* it for free."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:700
msgid "You delivered the part to Skeeter."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcskeetr.msg:710
msgid "You delivered the repair kit to Skeeter."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:100
msgid "You see a tall ghoul with long hair."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:101
msgid "You see Wooz."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:102
msgid "You see an extremely tall and lanky ghoul with long hair."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:110
msgid "I am Wooz. What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:111
msgid "What do you want now? Are you dumb?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:112
msgid "Hello. What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:113
msgid "Booze, Wooz."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:116 dialog/kcmaida.msg:242 dialog/rcmarge.msg:129
#: dialog/rcmcgrew.msg:111
msgid "Have you ever heard of something called a Garden of Eden Creation Kit?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:117
msgid "I don't want anything from you. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:120
msgid ""
"I just told you that every Vault has one. Does this look like a Vault to you? Are you dumb? Why\n"
" are you looking for a GECK here? Try a Vault. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:121
msgid "Where is the nearest Vault?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:122
msgid "I'll show you dumb. Talking to me like that is dumb. I'm the Chosen One, you know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:123
msgid "Uh, well, I was going to... and I thought you might... oh, never mind. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:130
msgid ""
"A Garden of Eden Creation Kit? You mean the device included with every vault that is supposed\n"
" to be used when the people leave the vault in order to reestablish civilization?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:131
msgid "Yes! That's it! Where can I find one?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:132
msgid "Uh, no, I meant some other Garden of Eden Creation Kit."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:140
msgid "I run this place. Are you dumb? I sell drinks, trade for things, tell stories, and play Tragic."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:141 dialog/hczaius.msg:169 dialog/rcwade.msg:109
msgid "What do you want now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:142
msgid "I want a drink."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:143
msgid "I want to trade."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:144
msgid "Tell stories?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:145
msgid "Play Tragic?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:146 dialog/kcardin.msg:177 dialog/kcmaida.msg:239
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:803
msgid "I guess I don't need anything right now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:150
msgid ""
"Trade? I'm always ready to trade Tragic cards. I've got a couple of old Vox Mubies, a Black\n"
" Dahlia, and some Rare Earths."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:151
msgid "I suppose you just want to trade stuff, huh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:153
msgid "Uh, I don't know what you're on, but I hope you have some in inventory to trade."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:154
msgid "Yes, I'd like to trade."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:155
msgid "Hmm... let me ask you about something else, first."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:156
msgid "I don't need to trade right now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:160
msgid "Not much to tell, really. Just a bunch of ghouls clinging tenaciously to the ass-end of life."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:161
msgid "No, I meant tell me about this bar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:162
msgid "Well, that describes a lot of people. Nothing new in that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:170
msgid ""
"You want a drink, huh? Well, we've got our very own Gamma Gulp Beer at $5/bottle and, for\n"
" special occasions, our Roentgen Rum at $12/bottle."
msgstr ""
"Vill du ha en drink? Vi har vår egen Gamma-Glufs-öl för $5/flaska och, för\n"
" speciella tillfällen, vår Röntgen-Rom för $12/flaska."

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:171
msgid "What'll it be?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:172
msgid "Gulp?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:173
msgid "I'd like a Gamma Gulp Beer. Is it supposed to glow like that?"
msgstr "Jag skulle vilja ha en Gamma-Glufs-öl. Är det meningen att den ska lysa så där?"

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:174
msgid "This is a special occasion, of a sort. I'd like a bottle of your Roentgen Rum."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:175
msgid "I want to buy a round of your fabulous Gamma Gulp Beer for everyone here."
msgstr "Jag vill köpa en omgång av er fantastiska Gamma-Glufs-öl till alla här."

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:176
msgid "Uh uh, goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:180
msgid "You don't have enough money. Are you dumb?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:181
msgid "Umb?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:182
msgid "Oops. Sorry. Let me buy something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:183
msgid "Okay, let me ask you a question, then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:184
msgid "I guess I am dumb. Sorry. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:185
msgid ""
"Dumb? Talking like that to me is pretty stupid, pal. You might just hurt yourself that way.\n"
" Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:186
msgid "Sorry. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:190
msgid ""
"You want to buy a round of drinks for everyone here? You must really be hard up for friends.\n"
" That'll cost you $35."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:191
msgid "Cost is no object, my good man. I'd like a round of drinks for everyone here, Wooz."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:192
msgid "Wooz, old chum, I want to buy a drink for all my friends here. These guys are the greatest."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:193
msgid ""
"Wooz, com'ere... theesh guys are the besht friends a person could ever have. Gimme another round\n"
" for all my friends."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:194
msgid ""
"Wooz! Gimme another round for all o' my pals. Theesh guys are the best. I LOVE YOU GUYS! Group\n"
" hug!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:195
msgid ""
"On second thought, I must have a hole in my head for wanting to buy drinks for a bunch of\n"
" rotting zombies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:196
msgid "I guess I'd rather just buy a drink for myself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:200
msgid "I've got this great story. It's really funny. You see there's this head, right?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:201
msgid "A head?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:202
msgid "Uh, I think I've heard this one already. I don't have the time to listen to this now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:210
msgid "Are you dumb? Tragic the Garnering is the most addictive thing since Jet."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:211
msgid "It's like I was saying. Tragic the Garnering is the game to play."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:212
msgid "Tell me more about this Tragic the Garnering."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:213
msgid "What's Jet?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:214
msgid "I guess I'll take your word for that. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:220
msgid "Hmm, sorry. That's the only one I know of. By the way, have you seen an apple, lately?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:221
msgid "An apple?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:222
msgid "I'm too disappointed to talk right now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:230
msgid "I just love apples, but there aren't many left anywhere. I hardly ever see them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:231
msgid "I didn't know you were such a fruit fetishist. Tell me something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:232
msgid "I've heard that you could really savor an apple because they were so slow to eat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:240
msgid ""
"Slow?!? You are dumb. Fuck you! Apples are just as fast to eat as any other fruit. Apples\n"
" rule. If it weren't for a conspiracy on the part of fruit manufacturers we'd all have apples."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:241
msgid ""
"You're crazed, aren't you? I think you've been sampling too much of your own brew here. Tell me\n"
" about something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:242
msgid ""
"Oh, yes... apples really are wonderful. (you back away slowly) Yes, that's right. Good Wooz, easy\n"
" there. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:250
msgid "I think we were able to come to an understanding. Need anything else?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:251
msgid "Actually, I think there is something else that I could use. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:252
msgid "That's all the trading I want to do right now. I do have some questions, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:253
msgid "I don't need anything else right now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:260
msgid ""
"Oh, the Chosen One. Oh my, I didn't realize. I'll just try to stop shaking long enough to tell\n"
" you something then. (Wooz smiles) Come closer and I'll whisper it to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:261
msgid "Well, that's more like it. I deserve a little more respect around here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:262
msgid "I'm not getting any closer to you, you scrawny freak. Get away. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:270
msgid ""
"Nearest Vault? Gee, I don't know. Maybe you could ask the people in Vault City where a Vault\n"
" might be. Vault City's just south of here. You are dumb, aren't you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:271
msgid "I knew that. I was just testing you. Gee, Wooz, you're so smart. Tell me something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:272
msgid "I am not! You're the one that's dumb. I'm leaving. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:280
msgid "(Wooz beckons you closer) Let me whisper in your ear..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:282
msgid "I don't think so; you're just trying to eat my brains, aren't you? I'm leaving. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:290
msgid "FUCK YOU!!! Now get out of my bar. Chosen one. Sheesh, what a loser."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:291
msgid "I don't want to stay in your stupid bar, anyway. You didn't have to yell like that. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:292
msgid "That's it, you fucking leper. Time to give you a little lead inoculation."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:300
msgid "Fuck you! You're dumb. What the hell do you want here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:301
msgid "Uh, I'm really sorry I pissed you off, Mr. Wooz. I just wanted to ask you something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:302
msgid "Fuck me? Fuck you! Your bar sucks. I'm out of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:303
msgid "Uh, nothing. Sorry, Wooz."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:304
msgid "Uh, did I tell you how much I really just love apples?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:310
msgid ""
"Really? I didn't know that. Well, if you love apples, I guess you can't be all bad. Now, what the\n"
" hell do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:311
msgid "I had some questions for you Wooz."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:320
msgid ""
"Zombies? Fuck you! We're ghouls. Zombies are a type of undead with no free will. Although we\n"
" share certain physical characteristics -- most notably, the rotting flesh and characteristic morbidity --\n"
" we are creatures of free will. Allow me to demonstrate."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:330
msgid ""
"I am demonstrating my free will by telling you to GET OUT! Damn smoothskin bigot. Go back to\n"
" Vault City, where you belong."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:331
msgid "Ghouls, zombies, who cares? You're all freaks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:340
msgid ""
"Well, Tragic the Garnering isn't just a game -- it's an obsession. Not a cologne, either. Some\n"
" think that the way it changes a person's life is tragic, but they just don't understand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:350
msgid "Jet's a drug that comes from New Reno. Were you born yesterday, or are you just dumb?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:351
msgid "Oh, that Jet. Well, sure I knew about that. Tell me more about this Tragic the Garnering."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:360
msgid ""
"No, really. It's wonderful. You should play. Just once. The first box of cards is free. A little\n"
" something from me to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:361
msgid "Thanks. Hey, these look great. (you tear the wrapping off) Mmm, I just love that smell."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:362
msgid "I just say 'No' to Tragic. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:370
msgid ""
"Hello there. Looks like you're another Tragic player. Have time for a game? Or are ya yeller?\n"
" I'm a-callin' you out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:371
msgid "I really don't have time for a... well, how long could one little game take..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:372
msgid ""
"Sure, just let me... No! Must stop. (your hand reaches for your deck, seemingly of its own\n"
" volition) Noooooo!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:375
msgid "I'd play Tragic with you but it looks like I'm all out of decks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:376
msgid "Wait until next week I'll put together a deck that can't be beat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:377
msgid "You took some of my best cards. I hate this game!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:380
msgid "That's just the first part. Now that you're one of us, want to play a game?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:381
msgid "Sure, but you're going to have to show me how."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:382
msgid "I don't think I really have time for that right now. Let me ask you something, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:383
msgid ""
"I'd love to stay and trade Tragic cards with you, but I've got things to do. You know, in real\n"
" life? Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:390
msgid ""
"Well, it's simple, really. Even someone dumb can understand it. First, you build a play deck out\n"
" of the cards that you have, and then you..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:391
msgid ""
"Uh, huh. You say you deal to the third player unless it's Thursday? OK, I think I've got it now.\n"
" Let's play."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:392
msgid "Maybe I'll play later. Thanks for telling me how, though. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:400
msgid ""
"You won? Fuck you! I need a ruling on that. You just got lucky, this time. This deck of mine\n"
" just didn't work. I've got to build a better one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:401
msgid "Thanks for the cards, Wooz. And I thought you knew how to play this game? I guess you're dumb."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:402
msgid "Well, them's the breaks, Wooz. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:410
msgid ""
"I won! Fuck you! You are dumb. I have crushed you. Now I can build an even better deck with your\n"
" cards."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:411
msgid "Uh, yeah. You won. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:412
msgid "What a surprise. Well, at least I didn't have to listen to one of your stories. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:420
msgid "No time at all. Let's go. I've got a new deck that I want to try."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:421
msgid "Okay. Let us play then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:422
msgid "No, I must resist the siren's call. Get thee behind me, Tragic! Must ask something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:430
msgid "I know what you mean. I can stop anytime I want. Just not today."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:431
msgid "You're not kidding. Actually, I wanted to ask you about something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:432
msgid "Arrrgh! Must leave while I still can. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:440
msgid ""
"Well, the Harp's named after a favorite hangout that I used to have before the war. I guess it's\n"
" just a reminder of times past. Sort of a joke on the only way we're going to get a better deal, too."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:441
msgid "Before the war? But that was a long time ago."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:442
msgid "Better deal? What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:450
msgid "That may be so, but not everyone has a city full of lunatics thirsting for their blood."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:460
msgid ""
"It sure was a long time ago. How do you think ghouls are made? You think some of us just got up\n"
" one fine day and said to ourselves: \"Gee, I wonder what it'd be like to have my flesh rotting off my\n"
" fucking body?\""
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:461
msgid "Well, no, I didn't. Say, how do you make a ghoul?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:462
msgid "You know, I just don't give a flying fuck what made you that ugly. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:470
msgid ""
"Those assholes in Vault City. If anyone's going to cap us, it's them. They're fucking crazed.\n"
" Anyone's not just as fucked up in the head as they are and they want to kill them. I'd watch myself\n"
" around them, if I were you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:471
msgid "Sounds like good advice. I'll be careful. Let me ask you something, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:472
msgid ""
"I think they've got the right idea. Just a little genetic cleansing. I hope they start with you.\n"
" Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:473
msgid "Well, right now they're pretty crazed about the village nearby. Do you know anything about this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:480
msgid ""
"'Bout the only way us ghouls are going to get an even break is when we're toting a harp of our\n"
" own."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:481
msgid "I didn't know that ghouls were especially musical."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:482
msgid "Oh, I see. Heh, heh. Let me ask you something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:490
msgid ""
"With silver-bells and cockleshells and... Boy, you are dumb, aren't you? Severe radiation. That's\n"
" how. How do you think? You know, many bombs go boom, flash of light and heat, flesh burns off, but you\n"
" don't-quite-die-type severe radiation?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:491
msgid "Uh well, I mean..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:500
msgid ""
"Well, I didn't think so. Fuck you very much for bringing back all those intensely painful\n"
" memories. Asshole. We're a town of fucking leftovers -- slightly overcooked leftovers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:501
msgid "I prefer medium-rare myself. Hey, let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:502
msgid "Well, I uh, um. Sorry. I'll just let you wallow in self-pity, then. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:510
msgid ""
"Well, usually I just pound on the hollow heads of my customers -- sort of like bongos. How the\n"
" hell did they ever let you out of your village? You're a danger to yourself and others."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:511
msgid "Bongos?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:520
msgid "You fell out of the stupid tree and hit every damn branch on the way down, didn't you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:521
msgid "Tree? I guess I'm just not hip to your lingo... man. Uh, let me ask you something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:530
msgid "Yeah, it's a head. But it's not attached to a body. You see, it's been severed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:531
msgid "A severed head. I see. And this becomes entertaining when?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:540
msgid ""
"Just hold on a minute. This severed head, you see, it's in Hell. (hah, hah) And it flies around\n"
" there, you know, in Hell. And it runs into all kinds of famous people there... (ho, ho, ho)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:541
msgid "Wait, a severed head is in Hell, and it flies around... doing what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:550
msgid ""
"Well, it's doing stuff. (hee, hee) You know. It's got, things that it wants to do, or maybe\n"
" things it's forced to do. The point is, it's doing stuff, you know, there in Hell. Oh God, (hah, hah,\n"
" hah) I just can't stand it!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:551
msgid ""
"You kind of obsess about this, don't you? Hmm. Were you and your mother close? Did you ever have\n"
" problems with bed-wetting?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:560
msgid ""
"No, you just don't understand. It's all about a severed head. Get it? Heh, heh, heh, It's funny!\n"
" How can you think about a severed head, in Hell of all places, and not laugh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:561
msgid ""
"Wooz, I don't know you very well, and I'm pretty sure I don't want to. However, I think I can\n"
" say, without fear of exaggeration, that you need help. Immediate, competent help. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:562
msgid ""
"Oh. I see. Why, yes. Of course; that's very funny. Heh heh. I just can't contain my amusement...\n"
" But enough enjoyment -- oh, my splitting sides -- I need to ask you something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:570
msgid ""
"Fuck you! You're just like all the rest of them. I tell, you it's hilariously funny. It's not my\n"
" fault that you don't have a sense of humor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:571
msgid ""
"You're right, Wooz. I guess I'm just not as clever as you are. You're truly a pearl amongst\n"
" swine. Now tell me something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:572
msgid "I have enough of a sense of humor to recognize the absence of one in others. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:600
msgid "Are you dumb? I already told you all about Tragic. You must have a really short memory."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:601
msgid "See? I told you it was funny. Is there anything else you need?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:700
msgid "Are you dumb?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:701
msgid "Give me a giant cola!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:702
msgid "I need a ruling on that!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:703
msgid "Kick me in the jimmy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:704
msgid "Hi, shills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:706
msgid "I wouldn't shit you on this one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:707
msgid "Let's play Tragic."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:708
msgid "I am the worst Tragic player in the world."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:709
msgid "STRONG!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:710
msgid "I suck at all games."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:711
msgid "I am the dumbest person I've ever met."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:712
msgid "HATE!!!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:713
msgid "Where's the horde a' short women?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:714
msgid "Ever seen a grown man NAKED?!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:715
msgid "Nah, maybe some other time Wooz. I got some questions though..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:716
msgid "Hmmm... Say, maybe you should call it a day and put those Tragic cards away. I think you have played enough for today."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:717
msgid "NEVER! BRING FORTH THE GARNERING!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:718
msgid "MOOAHAHAHAH!!! I AM VICTORIOUS!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:719
msgid "NOO!! HOW COULD I HAVE LOST!? Ahhhgghhhgh."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:720
msgid "Yeah... just can't seem to stop. Just one more game..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:721
msgid "Yeah, Gamma Gulp Beer. You deaf or something?"
msgstr "Ja, Gamma-Glufs-öl. Är du döv eller?"

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:722
msgid "Yeah, it is. One Gamma Gulp coming right up."
msgstr "Ja, det är det. En Gamma-Glufs-öl på väg."

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:723
msgid "Alright, enjoy. Anything else?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:724
msgid "Special occasion, huh? Well lah-de-dah, aren't we special today. One Roentgen coming right up then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:726
msgid "Yeah, what else do you have?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:727
msgid "Whatever, I'll take one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:728
msgid "Right. Let me get something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:729
msgid "I think I'll be heading out now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:730
msgid "You have become addicted to the game of Tragic. Many sleepless nights await you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:731
msgid "Alright, done. Anything else?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:732
msgid "Yeah, another round for everyone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:740
msgid ""
"Heh, yeah I heard those assholes are getting attacked by molerats who're protecting those smoothskins. Serves 'em right for fucking with other people's\n"
" business. I don't really know much more than that though. Lumpy over in the junkyard might know more. That smoothskin's always hearing things."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcwooz.msg:742
msgid "Good to know. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:100
msgid "You see a ghoul with some kind of talisman around its neck."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:101 dialog/gcworshp.msg:111
msgid "You see a member of the Renewal Cult."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:102
msgid "You see a contented-looking ghoul."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:110
msgid "You see a Glowing One with some kind of talisman around its neck."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:112
msgid "You see a contented-looking Glowing One."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:120
msgid "One of us, one of us..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:121
msgid "Renew, comrade! Renew!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:122
msgid "The time for lastday is here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:123
msgid "Soon we will all be smoothskins like you, comrade."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:124
msgid "The Atom gives us the power."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:125
msgid "Hello, comrade. The Brain knows all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:126
msgid "Renewal is almost at hand, comrade."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:127
msgid "Together we shall be bonded as one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:128
msgid "Down with free radicalism, comrade."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:129
msgid "We will all be Renewed together."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:130
msgid "Hello, friend. The Brain knows all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:131
msgid "You are favored by the Brain -- soon you will be one of us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:132
msgid "You seek word of Renewal, friend?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:133
msgid "Sit at his pink feet and hear of the Renewal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:134
msgid "The wise seek his wisdom."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:135
msgid "Hello, friend. Do you seek Renewal with us?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:136
msgid "Renew! Renew!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:137
msgid "If only we had a wheel for him. (sigh)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:138
msgid "Hail, friend. Renewal is at hand for the chosen."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:139
msgid "To be a friend of the Brain is a wondrous thing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:140
msgid "Hello. You just better be careful."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:141
msgid "We're watching you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:142
msgid "Seek enlightenment in the Brain's wisdom."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:143
msgid "I don't know why we let smoothskins down here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:144
msgid "You better go directly to him."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:145
msgid "You're here to see the Brain?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:150
msgid "Hello, smoothskin. Do you seek Renewal?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:151
msgid "His Sleekness wishes to see you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:152
msgid "You too can Renew!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:153
msgid "Join us and Renew!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:154
msgid "He wants to see you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:155
msgid "Renewal is open even to smoothskins."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gcworshp.msg:156
msgid "Smoothskins may Renew, too."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gczamok.msg:100
msgid "You see a larger than average Ghoul."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gczamok.msg:101 dialog/gczomak.msg:101
msgid "You see Zomak, known to some as the Destroyer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gczamok.msg:102
msgid "You see a big, burly, Ghoul whose face, beneath a sharply sloping forehead, reflects vast reserves of simpleminded superiority."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gczamok.msg:110
msgid "Renew Comrade! I am Zomak. Some call me Zomak the Destroyer. What is your business here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gczamok.msg:111
msgid "Renew Comrade! What are you doing here? State your business to Zomak the Destroyer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gczamok.msg:112 dialog/gczomak.msg:112
msgid "Renu!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/gczamok.msg:113 dialog/gczomak.msg:113 dialog/kctorr.msg:270
#: dialog/rcfern.msg:120 dialog/rcnord.msg:120 dialog/rcvelani.msg:120
