#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:532
msgid "Whoa! I've never seen that happen before!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:599
msgid "I found a note in the tunnels with the names Francis and Zaius on it. Looks like you've been committing some crimes."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:600
msgid ""
"Damn it. Zaius left notes lying out again, eh? Well, human, let me tell you this: I\n"
" knew there are people trying to kill mutants in this town, and I knew that Marcus would only\n"
" arrest them with evidence. I just wanted to make it happen with as little bloodshed as possible."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:601
msgid "So you killed innocents, huh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:602
msgid "Sure. So what do you propose to do about it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:603
msgid ""
"Innocents? Ha! The people I killed were trying to kill ME! I just returned the favor\n"
"  and made sure their deaths served another purpose - one that might further the cause of peace."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:604
msgid ""
"But this way you're still nothing more than a criminal and a murderer - and I only\n"
" have your word that there's a conspiracy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:605
msgid ""
"The only thing that'll satisfy the cause of peace is for all the murderers to die.\n"
" And I'm going to do my part by killing you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:606
msgid ""
"If you talked to some of the people in town about your hatred of mutants,\n"
"  you'd find out about the conspiracy. I know two wrongs don't make a right, but I call it self-defense.\n"
" I did something wrong, and I admit it. I can't stay here. I'll set out to find a way to atone for my actions...\n"
" That satisfy your sense of justice?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:607
msgid "It'll have to."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcfranci.msg:608
msgid "No, it doesn't. I'm going to kill you myself."
