#: dialog/zidcegrl.msg:255 dialog/zidcegrl.msg:271 dialog/zidcegrl.msg:272
msgid "Hey, "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcphil.msg:306
msgid "You again, "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcphil.msg:307
msgid "No problem, pal. Here's your drink, too. Hey, anything else I can do ya' for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcphil.msg:308
msgid ""
"Hey pal, thanks for all the tips. Lemme' give you one in return. I've heard that Liz, the owner of the General Store,\n"
" keeps a stash of weapons in her basement. But you didn't hear it from me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcphil.msg:309
msgid "Gee, thanks Phil. I'll keep that under my... uh... hat, or something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcphil.msg:1981
msgid "A couple of loons've been locked up for spreading hate propaganda."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcphil.msg:1982
msgid "Mine's purifiers are down."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcphil.msg:1983
msgid "Caravans all over the place. That's about normal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:100
msgid "You see a bemused man in a lab coat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:101
msgid "You see the Professor. He looks like he's engaged in some madcap scheme."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:102
msgid "You see a bemused man in a lab coat surrounded by laboratory equipment. There's an insane gleam in his eye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:103 dialog/scelise.msg:104 dialog/scfelix.msg:104
#: dialog/scggcap.msg:108 dialog/scgunthr.msg:104 dialog/scmerk.msg:126
msgid "You again?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:104
msgid "What is it you want? Out with it! I'm a busy man!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:105
msgid "Noo beezy?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:106
msgid "Test!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:107
msgid "Who are you? And what's with the scorpion?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:108
msgid "I'd like to take one of your tests."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:110
msgid "Ah, a test subject! Would you like to take a test, my friend?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:113
msgid "You wish to take a test, eh? Do you want to test your hands, your eyes, or your brains?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:114
msgid "'Ands!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:115
msgid "Yeyes!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:116
msgid "Rains!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:117
msgid "None!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:118
msgid "Then why are you wasting my time? I told you I'm busy, didn't I? I have too much to do to stand around wasting time talking to people like ... why am I still talking to you? Good day!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:119
msgid "Byeeeeee!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:120
msgid "Err... yeah. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:121
msgid "You wish to take a test, eh? Do you want to test your manual dexterity, your perception, or your intelligence?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:122
msgid "I'd like to test my agility."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:123
msgid "Let's test my eyes."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:124
msgid "How about my smarts?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:125
msgid "Hmm. None of them. Forget it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:126
msgid "Very well. I'll be matching you against the scorpion. You will both attempt to unlock those boxes. Good luck."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:129
msgid "Right. You'll stand behind this rail, and you and the scorpion will tell me the letters you read, from top to bottom, left to right."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:131
msgid "Got it. Let's go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:132
msgid "You and the scorpion will be playing a game of my own devising. I call it \"chess\". Are you ready?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:134
msgid "Yep. I'm ready."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:135
msgid "I am the Professor. What I do is applied intelligence testing. I create chemical compounds to increase intelligence. I'm trying some out on this radscorpion here, after my failure with the plant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:136
msgid "You tried it out on a plant?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:137 dialog/hcprof.msg:142
msgid "I'd like to take a test."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:138
msgid "Have you made anything that works?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:139
msgid "I see. That's all I wanted to know. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:140
msgid "Of course I tried it out on a plant! I'm trying to increase intelligence from the ground up!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:141
msgid "I see. Have you made anything that works?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:143
msgid "That's all I wanted to know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:144
msgid "Yes, I have, thank you very much! You ever hear of \"Mentats\"? I helped develop a method for easy mass-production of that drug! And others! Lots of others!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:145
msgid "All right, all right. Say, I'd like to try out my skills against your scorpion."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:146
msgid "All right, I believe you. I'll just be leaving."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:147
msgid "How... how could you kill my scorpion like that? I was close... so close..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:200
msgid "Woo hoo! Beat THAT, Mr. Exoskeleton."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:201
msgid "Wooooooo Hoooo!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:202
msgid "Damn it!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:203
msgid "Aaaargh!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:204
msgid "::click clack::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:205
msgid "How the hell did you pick a lock with CLAWS?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:206
msgid "How U pik wiff CLAWS?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:207
msgid "::chitter::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:208
msgid "Well, that was a tie."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:209
msgid "You lose. Scorpion: "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:210 game/proto.msg:544
msgid ", "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:211
msgid ": "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:213
msgid "Errr?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:214
msgid "You have proven that you are just as agile as the radscorpion."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:215
msgid "Here, take these Mentats. You appear to need them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:300
msgid "E... Z...W... T...O... D...F... E..R... T...F... P...Y... J...M"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:301
msgid "Yes, that's correct."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:302
msgid "M... O...O... Moo?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:303
msgid "Uh... no, I'm sorry. That's way off."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:304
msgid "::chitter chitter:: ::click clack:: ::chirp (tail swing)::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:305
msgid "Correct! Good boy! Gooooood boy! Your Morse code skills are improving nicely."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:306
msgid "You have proven that you are just as perceptive as the radscorpion."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:400
msgid "Checkmate ::click::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:401
msgid "WHAT? You cheated!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:402
msgid "Ecmat?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:403
msgid "Don't be a sore loser."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:404
msgid "And... checkmate!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:405
msgid "Chekmaaate!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:406
msgid "::chitter:: Kill plant! ::click-clack-click::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcprof.msg:407
msgid "You have proven that you can subvert a radscorpion that is more intelligent than you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:100 dialog/hcsuper.msg:100
msgid "You see a weird mutant thing with splotchy skin and a ghastly smile."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:101 dialog/hcsuper.msg:101
msgid "You see the refinery supervisor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:102
msgid "You see a ghoul. Its skin looks like it's ready to slough off the creature. It also looks like it's readily accepted by the other townsfolk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:103
msgid "You're not supposed to be here! "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:106 dialog/hcsuper.msg:106
msgid "Dunno."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:107 dialog/hcsuper.msg:107
msgid "I have some ore to be refined."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:110 dialog/hcrsuper.msg:123 dialog/hcrsuper.msg:128
#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:110 dialog/hcsuper.msg:123 dialog/hcsuper.msg:128
msgid "I want some uranium."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:113
msgid "Look son, I'm sorry that you've got no mind. But you can't be here. Run along now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:115 dialog/hcsuper.msg:115
msgid "You can't be here. It's dangerous. Run along now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:117
msgid "Great. That'll be $1000, no haggling. You might think that's pricey, but it's a steal considering what you'll get for the finished product."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:119 dialog/hcsuper.msg:119
msgid "$1000? That's ridiculous. Forget it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:120 dialog/hcsuper.msg:120
msgid "I'm the supervisor of this refinery. What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:122 dialog/hcrsuper.msg:127 dialog/hcsuper.msg:122
#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:127
msgid "I want some ore refined."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:125
msgid "This is the refinery of Broken Hills. This is where we purify the ore dug from the mine. What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:130 dialog/hcsuper.msg:130
msgid "You don't have enough money. Come on back when you do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:132 dialog/hcsuper.msg:132
msgid "All right. Give us a day and we'll have it ready for you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:134
msgid "Good luck getting it refined any place else. The process is dangerous -- only a professional should do it. You want it or not?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:137 dialog/hcsuper.msg:137
msgid "Fine. You don't have any business here. Please leave so we can get our jobs done."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:139 dialog/hcsuper.msg:139
msgid "That's ridiculous. We're not giving you any."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:140 dialog/hcsuper.msg:140
msgid "Then die."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:142 dialog/hcsuper.msg:142
msgid "Hey! Get away from there or you'll suffer the consequences!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:143
msgid "Get out of my refinery. Now!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:144
msgid "We're still working on it. Give us time. This isn't instantaneous."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:145 dialog/hcsuper.msg:145
msgid "I want to ask you something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:147
msgid "It's done. Before you take it, listen. Our town really needs this ore. If you donate it to the town, I'll refund your money. What do you say?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:150 dialog/hcsuper.msg:150
msgid "Fine. Be that way. Here's your ore. Now get out of my refinery."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcrsuper.msg:152
msgid "Thanks! Here's your money back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:100
msgid "Look out! It's a radscorpion!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:101
msgid ""
"Looking closer, this scorpion appears to be wearing wire-rimmed glasses.\n"
" It actually looks quite intelligent and non-threatening."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:102
msgid "::click:: ::click clack::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:103
msgid "Can I help you with something? You're disrupting my experiments!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:104
msgid "::scuttle:: ::click click click::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:105
msgid "What? What do you want with him?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:106
msgid "Hiss!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:107
msgid "Good boy! Stand up for yourself!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:108
msgid "[it regards you warily]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:109
msgid "[it makes gestures with its claws]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:110
msgid "[it almost looks friendly]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:111
msgid "Please don't bother the scorpion. He's had a rough day."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:112
msgid "He's a little under the weather right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:113
msgid "::scuttle::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:114
msgid "::click::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:115
msgid "::click-clack::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:116
msgid "::sharpen::"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcscorp.msg:117
msgid "Looking closer, this scorpion appears to be quite intelligent and non-threatening."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:100
msgid "You see a spore plant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:101
msgid "You see Seymour the spore plant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:102
msgid "You see a spore plant that somehow radiates an aura of intelligence."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:103
msgid "Hi! Nice weather we've been having, huh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:104
msgid "Yoo talk?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:106
msgid "Excuse me, but is this the plant that's talking?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:107
msgid "Are you connected with that scientist in any way?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:109
msgid "Yes, I do talk. Better than some people, it seems. I'd smile at you right now, but I just don't have a mouth. [it laughs] Say, could you do me a big favor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:110 dialog/hcseymor.msg:125
msgid "'Es."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:112
msgid "I'm looking for a better place to be. Right here is nice and all, but frankly, these plants aren't much for conversation. I was thinking over there, by the building with all the ghouls in it... Would you replant me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:114 dialog/hcseymor.msg:126 dialog/hcseymor.msg:167
#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:129
msgid "Nuh!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:116 dialog/hcseymor.msg:169
msgid "I think not."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:117
msgid "Great! All you have to do is find a shovel, dig me up, and plant me over there. When you do, I'll tell you a secret."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:119 dialog/hctyphon.msg:111 dialog/hctyphon.msg:202
msgid "Nuh uh."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:120
msgid "All right. Well, um... I'll be waiting here for you. Not like I really have a choice, you know. So long!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:121
msgid "Byeeee!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:122
msgid "If you should happen to change your mind, you know where to find me. I've put down roots here. Ha ha ha! Just a little plant humor for you. Oh, don't let me keep you. So long!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:124
msgid "Well said, well said! How delightful to see a homo sapiens use its brain to its fullest extent. My dear friend, would you be willing to do me a favor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:127
msgid "Why, yes! Yes, it is! Very astute, friend, very astute. I can see you didn't germinate yesterday! My fine-stemmed companion, would you be so kind as to do me a favor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:130
msgid "Deee-lightful! I'm very, very pleased. Just find yourself a shovel and come on back. When you're done, maybe I can tell you a secret. My friend, I do hope you continue to flower."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:131
msgid "Um, right. So long."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:133
msgid ""
"Oh, yes, the Professor. He grew me from a tiny spore and nurtured me... but I realized from an early age that if I were to act as smart as I truly\n"
" am, he'd cut me into pieces to examine me. So, I played dumb and got planted out here. It's nice... but I'd like to branch out a little.\n"
" Y'know, maybe get planted someplace else..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:134
msgid "\"Branch out.\" Indeed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:135
msgid "Right. What do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:136
msgid "Uh... huh. I gotta go. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:137
msgid ""
"So does he still have the scorpion? That thing is a mean chess player... it has a lot of bark and plenty of bite,\n"
" if you know what I mean... but I know how to beat him. If you do me a favor, I'll tell you how."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:138
msgid "Really? How?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:139
msgid "That's fascinating. A chess-playing plant. How prosaic. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:140
msgid "My fine friend, if you will replant me near the ghouls' home over there, I will be happy to impart my deep-rooted knowledge of chess."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:142
msgid "No thanks. I'll handle the scorpion on my own."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:143
msgid "Ahh, my friend, you have returned. This is quite a delightful place here. The shade is perfect, and the company is simply dazzling. That Typhon, what a kidder! He really makes my intellectual sap flow!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:144
msgid "Chess?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:145
msgid "What was that you mentioned about chess?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:147
msgid ""
"Well, it was about how to beat the professor's scorpion at chess. My friend, it is simplicity itself.\n"
" The Flying Liver Attack is like a flytrap to that bug - it walks right into it and then can't extricate itself. I guarantee your success."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:148
msgid "'Anks! Bye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:149
msgid "I appreciate the information! Bye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:150
msgid "My friend! Has the sun been shining upon you? How does your day flower? Are you ready for the move? I certainly am!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:152
msgid "Nuh uh! No move!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:154
msgid "I've changed my mind. I don't want to help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:155
msgid "I'm so excited I could release a spore cloud all over myself! Let's go!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:157
msgid ""
"That's a pity, that's a pity indeed. I do hope you'll change your mind at some point. Perhaps the pollen of your\n"
" indecision will blow my way again. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:159
msgid "Good day indeed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:160
msgid ""
"Oooh... the soil here feels so... different. Cleaner, somehow. Probably because I don't have to share it with\n"
" those other plants. Ahhh. Oh! Yes! If you ever run across the Professor and his scorpion, remember this chess\n"
" maneuver: It's called the Flying Liver Attack, and the scorpion cannot stand against it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:161
msgid "'Anks!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:162
msgid "Thanks. I'll try that out. Bye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:163
msgid ""
"I would also like to tell you that I happen to know the ghoul Typhon inside this building knows the whereabouts\n"
" of a treasure trove. Perhaps that might be useful to you someday."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:164
msgid "'Anks! Byee!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:165
msgid "Have you had time to reconsider? Would you like to help me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:170
msgid "Alas, you do not appear to have a shovel. Until you can find one, I can't go. I await your return with bated pistil."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:172
msgid "Psst! Hey! Hey, pal! Over here!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:173
msgid "C'mere! I promise I won't hurt you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:174
msgid "Come on. You scared of a plant?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:175
msgid "Over here! Let's get to it!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:176
msgid "Yes, I'm a talking plant. Get over it and talk to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:177
msgid "Whoa, friend. Don't just start digging. We've got to strategize the move first. Let's talk it over."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:178
msgid "You replanted Seymour by the old-ghouls home."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:179
msgid "Haf shuvl! Plant now!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcseymor.msg:180
msgid "It just so happens I have a shovel right here. Let's go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:100
msgid "You see a smiling man dressed in leather armor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:101
msgid "You see Steve, the greeter for Broken Hills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a friendly man in leather armor. He looks like he stands here all day waiting for\n"
" someone to talk to."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:103
msgid ""
"Hi there! I'm Steve. I'm the guy who can tell you where's where and what's what in this fine\n"
" town. Can I direct you someplace, or give you any help today?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:104 dialog/scwestin.msg:106
msgid "Duh..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:105
msgid "Noken Heel?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:107 dialog/hcsteve.msg:156
msgid "Who lives here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:109 dialog/hcsteve.msg:153
msgid "What's new here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:110 dialog/hcsteve.msg:157
msgid "What services do you have here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:112
msgid ""
"Oh dear. Another poor child of the wastes. Well, come in. You'll find we're just as hospitable\n"
" as any of the other towns in the wasteland."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:113
msgid "Guyyyyyyyyyy!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:114
msgid "Indeed. Good luck, wanderer. And good bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:115
msgid "Nood eye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:116
msgid "Broken Hills. We're a mining town. We dig for things. Then we sell them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:117
msgid "Bedig?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:118
msgid "Stell!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:119
msgid ""
"That's right. Out of the ground. We have a mine. I don't think they have a job for you there,\n"
" though. If you want one, talk to the Outfitter."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:120
msgid "Oh-kay."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:121
msgid "Sell stuff?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:122
msgid ""
"We sell what we dig to other towns around here. They find it useful. If you want to sell\n"
" something, you can talk to many of the merchants here. Anyway, I have to get back to work. You be good\n"
" and careful here, okay?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:123
msgid "Oh-kay! Byeeee!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:124
msgid "I have to get back to work. You be good and careful here, okay?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:125
msgid "You again? Well, you know what you have to do -- be good and careful. Take care!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:126
msgid "Oh-kay! Byeeeeeeeee!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:127
msgid ""
"Put your weapons away, partner. You won't get any answers from me while you're waving them\n"
" around like that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:128
msgid ""
"We're a small mining community. We were founded several decades ago by our sheriff, Marcus, and\n"
" a man named Jacob. The two of them chose this site because it was near some uranium deposits. Would\n"
" you like to hear more?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:131
msgid ""
"We're a collective of humans, mutants, and ghouls. We don't have the racial tensions that\n"
" plague Vault City; in our eyes, everyone's equal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:132
msgid "You live next to mutants? Don't you know they're evil?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:133
msgid "Equal?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:135
msgid ""
"Nominally, Sheriff Marcus is in charge of the city. He helped found it, and he helps us through\n"
" our crises. In truth, though, everyone in the city has a voice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:136
msgid "That seems unworkable."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:137
msgid "That sounds like a good way to run things."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:139
msgid "The guy who helped create the city's still in charge? That would make him very, very old."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:141
msgid "Aside from the mutants all being DEAD and this town being DOOMED..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:142
msgid "Aside from the mutants being dead and our only source of livelihood destroyed..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:143
msgid "Aside from you being a hero for exposing the corruption in our midst..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:144
msgid "Aside from realizing we have a cancer in our midst with the escape of Franc and Manson..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:145
msgid "Aside from Chad's betrayal of the city and your justice -- for which everyone's grateful -- "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:146
msgid "Not too much, really."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:149
msgid "Oh. You again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:151 dialog/vcgatgrd.msg:122
msgid "Welcome back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:152
msgid "You want to know more?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:159
msgid ""
"We make our living by refining the ore we dig from the hills, and selling it to nearby\n"
" communities like Vault City, Gecko, and the New California Republic. We use some ourselves for our\n"
" own power. More?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:162
msgid ""
"Everyone's equal. We all came from humans; we all have the same core underneath the exterior.\n"
" To say that someone's evil just because of their appearance indicates only ignorance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:163
msgid "You calling me ignorant?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:164
msgid "That's true."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:165
msgid "Not necessarily. Who knows what the virus that mutated him has done to his mind?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:167
msgid "We find that it works fine for our purposes. Plus, Marcus is eminently fair."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:168
msgid "Where I can find Marcus?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:170
msgid ""
"He is old. But he's holding up well. See, he's a mutant, and apparently they live longer than\n"
" most other folks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:171
msgid "You're letting a MUTANT run this place? What are you, nuts?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:172
msgid "Really? I would have thought most of them would have died off by now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:173
msgid ""
"A mutant sheriff, eh? I'll bet most folks here are pretty law-abiding, then. That must work out\n"
" well."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:175
msgid ""
"So now we're eking out a living, creating our own version of civilization, and doing our best\n"
" to avoid giving in to Vault City or NCR -- we don't need their style of government. That's all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:178
msgid ""
"If you're going to persist in believing you can judge someone's mind by what you see on the\n"
" outside, then yes. You are undeniably ignorant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:179
msgid "To hell with you, pal. YOU'RE the ignorant one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:180
msgid "Oh, all right. You've got a point."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:181
msgid "Anyway, that's all I wanted to say. Welcome to Broken Hills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:184
msgid ""
"If the mutants intended us harm, they'd have moved on us before now. They're not going to last\n"
" forever -- in fact, most of them are going senile now. Building a community isn't going to help them\n"
" achieve their aims."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:185
msgid "You have a point."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:186
msgid "They're still evil."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:188
msgid ""
"Pal, the more I talk to you, the dumber I feel myself becoming. With an attitude like that, you\n"
" won't be too welcome in Broken Hills. Excuse me. I have a job to do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:189
msgid "Jerk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:190
msgid "Time to die, jerk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:191
msgid ""
"We have a mine, a refinery, a tavern, a hotel -- which, by the way, has lost its owner, so we\n"
" just let people stay there free -- a hospital, a general store, and a chemist. We grow our own food."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:194
msgid ""
"Well, many of them have. Since mutants are sterile... or so I'm led to believe ... they're dying\n"
" out. The ones who are left seem to be getting senile, too. Not Marcus, though. He's still as sharp as\n"
" ever."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:198
msgid "Marcus, are you sure you don't want to stick around and lead us for a while?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:199
msgid "Marcus: Ain't no future in it. You'll do fine without me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:201
msgid "Pal, you're not wanted here. You've done enough damage."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:300
msgid ""
"You can usually find Marcus near the bank -- that also serves as a tougher jail -- or at the\n"
" Jail. Sometimes he's in the tavern or at home, but he's usually working."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:301
msgid "Bummer!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:303
msgid "Hooray!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:304
msgid "Scoundrels!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsteve.msg:305
msgid "That rat bastard!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:100
msgid "You see a man dressed in robes."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:101
msgid "You see Ashton. He is in charge here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:102
msgid "He has a smirk on his face."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:200
msgid "Greetings. My name is Ashton, and I'm in charge of things here. Were you sent here for security detail?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:201
msgid "Yeah, actually, I was."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:202
msgid "No, I was sent by AHS-9 to check on everything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:210
msgid "Excellent! Never can have too much security with what we have stored here, I say. Good to have you here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:211
msgid "Really? That's... interesting. You're free to look around, of course. I'm sure you'll find that everything is in order."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:220
msgid "Thanks. What exactly are we storing here, anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:221
msgid "Alright then. See you around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:230
msgid ""
"As you're certainly aware, every donation to the Church of Hubology over the last several decades is stored here -- and I must say,\n"
" it's quite a stash. Some donations are small; others quite large. We get all kinds of stuff, from weapons and ammunition, to jewelry,\n"
" and antiques, and even a few old vehicles. Why, just a few months ago, actor Don Ravolta donated a genuine 20th century Harkley Sports\n"
" motorcycle -- best of its time. Heck, a working Howitzer was even donated to the Church. Our most common donation, however, is money -- lots and\n"
" lots of money."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:240
msgid "Impressive. It sounds like the Church does quite well for itself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:241
msgid "Yes, of course -- and for good reason. Advertising campaigns and a massive space shuttle aren't cheap activities you know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:242
msgid "Yeah, I can imagine. So, how large is this place?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:243
msgid "I know what you mean. Well, I must be going. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:250
msgid ""
"The structure we're standing in is an older bunker, probably built for private use rather than military. There's two levels below us.\n"
" Directly below us is the living area -- we got some beds there, bathrooms, exercise machines, security equipment. Below that is what I call the \"vault.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:251
msgid "A vault?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:252
msgid "It's not *really* a vault, I just call it that. It's more of a storage room full of goods. That's where we keep all the donations. It's guarded all day, everyday."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:260
msgid "Interesting. Well, I'm going to have a look around. See you later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:270
msgid "So, how large is this place?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:300
msgid "Hello again. Help you with something?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcstldr.msg:301
msgid "Nope, just looking around. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:100
msgid "You see a tall, graying, man with a tankard of beer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:101
msgid "You see John L. Sullivan. The pugilist."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:102
msgid "You see a tall, older, man with muscular arms and a gray, but neatly groomed, handlebar mustache."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:103
msgid "Sure now, you've had a wee bit too much already."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:104
msgid "Begorah, but aren't you a stupid one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:105
msgid "You'd give Torr a good run for his money."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:106
msgid "On your way now, ya wee strange one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:107
msgid "Ach, another tribal tiched in the hayed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:108
msgid "(Looks you up and down appraisingly) Well now, what have we here? Looks as though you dinnay know much about the sweet science at all do ye?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:109
msgid "If you would get off your wee high horse, I could see helpin' ye a bit with your skills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:111
msgid "Uh, yeah, whatever, mister. See you around. Maybe."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:112
msgid "Well, it's just my educated opinion but I can see by the way you move that you could do with a few pointers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:113
msgid "Pointers? With what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:114
msgid "I don't think so, old man. I doubt that *you* could teach me anything. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:115
msgid "About the sweet science, of course. The sportin' art."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:116
msgid "Uh, the art? Are you talking about magic!?! Can you teach me magic spells?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:118
msgid "(he grins broadly) Sure and begorah, I could teach you about the wee folk, leprechauns, spriggans, Ban'sidhe and the like. Would you like that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:119
msgid "That sounds great. Teach away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:120
msgid "Pugilism, the manly art of hand-to-hand combat. That's what I mean."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:121
msgid "Pugilism, the manly, uh, and womanly art of hand-to-hand combat. That's what I mean."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:122
msgid "Well, I guess I could use some help with that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:123
msgid "I think I already know more about that than you could possibly teach me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:124
msgid "(talking to those around you) Did ye hear that? I got myself a live one here. Wants to hear bout the fairies and wee goblins and such. (Hooo, haah, haah-he doubles over in laughter) Here lad, have a drink on me, that's your ticket to the realms of the fay folk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:125
msgid "(talking to those around you) Did ye hear that? I got myself a live one here. Wants to hear bout the fairies and wee goblins and such. (Hooo, haah, haah-he doubles over in laughter) Here lass, have a drink on me, that's your ticket to the realms of the fay folk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:126
msgid "All I need is a drink? That's great. Thanks for the tip."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:127
msgid "Somehow, I feel as though you're pulling my leg a bit."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:128
msgid "Well, the drink's just a start. You have to find a fairy mound. (winks at the surrounding patrons)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:129
msgid "What then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:130
msgid "Well, you sit by the mound and wait until you can see the fairy circle in the dew. If you jump into the fairy ring, you'll be made to dance until dawn with the wee folk. If you survive, they'll steal you away to the land of fairie. (heee, hah, hah, hah)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:131
msgid "Wow, how'd you find this out?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:132
msgid "Somehow, I think you're pulling my leg."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:133
msgid "Oh, it's in me blood, of course. Erin go bragh! (he hefts his tankard aloft)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:134
msgid "Yeah, go brag about Erin. Okay. Thanks for the tips. Hey, let me ask you about something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:135
msgid "Somehow, I think you're pulling my leg about this whole thing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:136
msgid "Uh, well, uh, I can see that you're a busy man. See you later. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:137
msgid "(He looks you over.) Mebbe' so. Mebbe' so. Well then, suit yourself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:139
msgid "Well, mebbe' I am at that. Ne'er-the-less, you were a bonny good sport about it. Here's a beer, on me, for takin' it so well."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:140
msgid "Thanks. Now what were you saying about the sweet science?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:141
msgid "I'm not taking a beer from you. I know more than you could teach me, you old drunk. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:142
msgid "Well, let's go outside and see what I can teach you. You see, it's all about getting your whole wee body to snap just like a whip..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:143
msgid "Uh, huh."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:144
msgid "I don't have time for this right now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:145
msgid "(Several, sweaty, hours later) So you see what you were doin' wrong then?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:146
msgid "Yes, I do. Thanks for taking the time to help me out, Mr. Sullivan."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:147
msgid "That was great. Let me give you $10 for some brew on me. It's the least I can do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:148
msgid "Yeah, I guess so. Thanks. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:149
msgid "It was me very own pleasure. You take care o' yourself now. And if anyone asks... you just tell 'em that Fightin' John Sullivan taught you how to fight that way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:150
msgid "Will do, John. Thanks. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:151
msgid "No, no, no. I could nay take money from ye. It was my very own pleasure to teach what I know. You take darn good care of yourself now. You've got real potential."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:152
msgid "That's great, let me ask you one thing though. Where'd you learn how to fight like that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:153
msgid "Thanks, John. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:154
msgid "That was a long time ago. When I was a wee young lad, an' dinnay have any sense in me thick head. A place called Reno. You keep your nose clean and stay away from the likes o' that place."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:155
msgid "Where's Reno?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:156 dialog/hcsulvan.msg:163
msgid "Oh, okay. Thanks, John. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:157
msgid "I dinnay want to tell ye. You get on now. Just keep out o' harm's way. Goodbye now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:158
msgid "OK, thanks again. Goodbye, John."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:159
msgid "Keep yourself outa trouble. I've taught you all I know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:160
msgid "Thanks. You mentioned something about the art before?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:161
msgid "Thanks, John. I sure appreciate it. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:162
msgid "I mean the art of pugilism. I was just pulling your leg about the other stuff. I'd best be getting' back to me cup now. Good luck to ye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsulvan.msg:164
msgid "John Sullivan has helped you improve your Melee and Unarmed Combat skills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:113
msgid "Look, son, I'm sorry that you've got no mind. But you can't be here. Run along now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:117
msgid ""
"Great. That'll be $1000, no haggling. You might think that's pricey, but it's a steal\n"
" considering what you'll get for the finished product from an interested buyer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:125
msgid ""
"This is the refinery of Broken Hills. This is where we purify the ore dug from the mine. What\n"
" do you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:134
msgid ""
"Good luck getting it refined any place else. The process is dangerous -- only a professional\n"
" should do it. You want it or not?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:143
msgid "Get out of my refinery! Now!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:144
msgid "We're still working on refining your ore. Give us time. This isn't instantaneous."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:147
msgid ""
"Your ore's done. Before you take it, listen - our town really needs this ore. If you donate it to the\n"
" town, I'll refund your money. Hell, if you want more money for it, I can even give you an extra $500 to make it worth your time.\n"
" Please. With the fiasco at the mine, Broken Hills needs this to stay afloat. What do you say?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:149
msgid "Sure. Don't worry about the extra $500. You probably need it more than I do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:152
msgid "Thanks! Here's your money back. Broken Hills won't forget this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:154
msgid "I told you to get out of here!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:155
msgid "..little bastard comes in here and <grumble> <rant>..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:156
msgid "An extra $500? Sure, I'll take it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:157
msgid "Thanks! Here's your money back with an extra $500."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:158 dialog/vcmclure.msg:331
msgid "Great. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:159
msgid "You figured out how to get uranium ore refined in Broken Hills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:160
msgid "You gave the refined ore back to Broken Hills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hcsuper.msg:161
msgid "You sold the refined ore back to Broken Hills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:100
msgid "You see an old ghoul."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:101
msgid "You see Typhon, son of Set."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:102
msgid "You see an old ghoul with intelligence fairly gleaming from his eyes."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:103
msgid "Howdy there, kiddo, and welcome to the Old Ghouls' Home!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:104
msgid "Nol Ghul?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:105
msgid "Old Ghouls' Home?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:107
msgid "Hey, you ever heard of a GECK?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:109
msgid "Another waste-baby, huh? Hey, kid, you want to know a secret?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:110
msgid "Yeh!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:112
msgid ""
"Back in my running days, I won quite a few races, made quite a bit of cash. Long time ago, I stashed all of my winnings not too far from\n"
" here. If someone was t'do me a favor or two, I might tell 'em where that \"treasure\" is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:113
msgid "Tell!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:114
msgid "No care."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:115
msgid "What kind of treasure?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:116
msgid "What kind of favor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:119
msgid "Heh. All right, then. I ain't got nothin' for you. Go on, git."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:121
msgid "Kid, y'got to do me a favor, first."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:122 dialog/hctyphon.msg:128
msgid "Okey!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:123
msgid "Nuh uh!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:126
msgid "I'm an old guy, an' I don't get out too much. Ain't got much chance for action, y'know what I mean? So what I want is a Cat's Paw magazine. Find me one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:127
msgid "'Ere! [Give Cat's Paw to Typhon.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:130
msgid "Here you go. [Give Cat's Paw to Typhon.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:131
msgid "All right. I'll be back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:133
msgid "Thanks for the mag, kid. Let me get back to you in an hour or so."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:135
msgid "I ain't done yet, kid! Sheesh! Can't an old ghoul have his privacy?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:137
msgid "What kind o' treasure? Money, kid, lots and lots of money. Enough to satisfy any sane person."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:139
msgid "I don't need money."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:140
msgid "You're back, eh? You want to know about that treasure, kid?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:142 dialog/hctyphon.msg:168 dialog/kcsulik.msg:123
#: dialog/kcsulik.msg:325 dialog/kcsulik.msg:757 dialog/kcsulik.msg:957
msgid "Nuh-uh."
msgstr "Näe."

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:143
msgid "What kind of treasure is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:144
msgid "Yeah, tell me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:145
msgid "I had other questions for you first."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:148
msgid "This is the Old Ghouls' Home?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:149
msgid "You ever heard of a GECK?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:151
msgid "Anything else you can tell me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:152
msgid "It's kind of a joke. There ain't any ghouls but old ghouls. We're all sterile, see, but we're incredibly long-lived. We're the first and last generation of ghouls. This is a place for those of us who just wanna rest for a while."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:153 dialog/hctyphon.msg:158 dialog/hctyphon.msg:164
msgid "I see. I had other questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:155
msgid "I'm Typhon. Y'ever hear of Set? He used to run the old-time town of Necropolis. I'm his son. Got born before the radiation hit us, so I grew up mutated. Ain't never been any other way for me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:156
msgid "Tell me about Set."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:157
msgid "Set? I heard he was a total bastard!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:160
msgid "Yep. Used to have some, but all the pure-strain humans stole 'em to make their own little Gardens of Eden. Vault City might be your best bet to find one. Either there or NCR to the south."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:161
msgid "Damn. Okay, I had more questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:162
msgid "Damn. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:163
msgid "\"Total bastard\" would be a fine way to describe the old man. Being turned into a ghoul from the radiation didn't do much for his sense of humor or sense of authority, let me tell you. 'Course, it kinda screwed up everyone's brains. I think growing up ghoulie made it a little easier on me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:166
msgid "Well? Do you have my Cat's Paw magazine yet?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:167
msgid "'Es. [Give Cat's Paw to Typhon.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:169
msgid "Yup. Here you go. [Give Cat's Paw to Typhon.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:170
msgid "Not yet. I had other questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:172
msgid "Well, hurry it up! I'm an old, old ghoul, and I tell you, I gotta have relaxation! Now go, go, go!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:174
msgid "Kid, that magazine stirred up the ol' juices, and I figure that for the sort of treasure I'm talkin', you can hunt me down a few more things. Go git me a blow-up doll. You can probably find one in New Reno."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:175
msgid "Okey! Bye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:176
msgid "Nuh-uh!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:177
msgid "Here go! [Give Blow-Up Doll to Typhon.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:178
msgid "All right. I had more questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:181
msgid "Got it right here. [Give Blow-Up Doll to Typhon.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:182
msgid "This, kid, will hit the spot. Gimme a few hours and we'll talk more. Go on. [He eyes the doll lustfully.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:184
msgid "Can't a guy get a little privacy! Git! Git! G'wan!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:186
msgid "I'm all tuckered out now. Go get me some rotgut and we'll talk about the treasure. Phil the bartender should be able to take care o' that for you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:187
msgid "Rite! Bye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:189
msgid "Take! [give Rotgut to Typhon]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:190
msgid "Got it. Here you go. [Give Rotgut to Typhon.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:191
msgid "Is that going to be it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:194
msgid "I'll probably want... oh, one more thing. I'll tell you what it is when you get me my damn rotgut, all right?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:195
msgid "Fine. I'll do it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:197
msgid "That really hit the spot, kid. I was gonna ask you for a plant, but hey, I'll give you a break."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:198
msgid "'Ank you!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:199
msgid "Thanks. I had other questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:200
msgid "That's a bit vague, but thanks. See ya."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:201
msgid "You find that treasure yet, kid?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:204
msgid "Nope. I had some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:206
msgid "Well, keep lookin'. You're bound to get it eventually."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:208
msgid "Guess so. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:209
msgid "How's the treasure, kid?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:210
msgid "Bad! Caps!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:211
msgid "It was all bottle caps! It's worthless!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:212
msgid "Ha ha. Funny. I had some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:214
msgid "Poo! Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:215
msgid ""
"What, they don't use caps as money anymore? You mean all that collectin' and hidin' and worryin' someone's gonna steal my\n"
" stash was for nothing? God DAMMIT! Sorry to make you run around like that, kid. If I'd'a known..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:216
msgid "'S okay. Bye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:217
msgid "Yeah, well, you made your last mistake, old ghoul. Time to die."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:218
msgid "Suppose it could happen to anyone. I had some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:219
msgid "Yeah, yeah. Okay. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:220
msgid "Guess it was an honest mistake. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:221
msgid "Gud. Where munnee?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:222
msgid "Gee, Typhon. You're so thoughtful. So, where's the cash?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:223
msgid ""
"All right. I remember stashing the cash somewhere downtown. It's been so many years, though, and the buildings have been\n"
" built and rebuilt over and over, that I'm not sure exactly where it is. If it helps any, I remember thinkin' I should put it\n"
" somewhere that wasn't likely to be torn down or plowed over. Somewhere indispensable, ya' know? Good luck to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:224
msgid "You finally got Typhon to spill his guts about location of the hidden loot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:300
msgid "But Hegel's dialectic doesn't account for..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:301
msgid "Hegel, Hegel, Hegel! You're always on about Hegel!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:302
msgid "So then the woman says, \"That's not a rabbit, vicar!\""
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:303
msgid "Ha ha ha ha!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:304
msgid "And the first proton says, \"Yeah, I'm positive!\""
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:305
msgid "[groan] That's SO bad, I'm wilting."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:306
msgid "It's not easy being green."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:307 dialog/vcdrtroy.msg:233
msgid "Tell me about it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:308
msgid "But it's completely apparent that this is a philosophical dead end!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:309
msgid "That's only because you haven't examined all the ramifications of it. Now, if you..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:310
msgid "You want some fruit?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:311
msgid "Feed me, Seymour."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:312
msgid "Brains... braaaaaains... sorry, old habit."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:313
msgid "That's okay. I don't have one, remember?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:314
msgid "Well, certainly manure works well, but there's nothing like a rotting corpse for compost."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:315
msgid "So that's why you wanted to move over here! Easy pickings."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:316
msgid "Let me tell you, there's nothing like a good fast run."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:317
msgid "You really feel the wind through the wisps of your hair, yes?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:318
msgid "I haven't pollinated in years!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:319
msgid "Imagine being trapped in THIS body! No action! No action at all!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:320
msgid "Maybe if you gave photosynthesis at chance..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:321
msgid "I'm not responsible for my evolutionary roots, you green bastard!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:322
msgid "Whoo-ee! I sure hope you can process methane!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:323
msgid "My leaves! My poor leaves! Aaaaagh!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:324
msgid "I like this place. I'm thinking of putting down roots here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:325
msgid "Okay, enough with the endless plant jokes, pal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:326
msgid "I wonder how my cousins in Arroyo are doing? I hope they're flourishing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:327
msgid "Of course they are! Unless some rat-bastard slaughters them all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:328
msgid "Well, I think I'll go open a door or something..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:329
msgid "I think I have opposable thumb envy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:330
msgid "Not to go out on a limb here..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:331
msgid "Aaaaaaaaaaaaaagh! No more plant jokes!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:332
msgid "Check out the grains on that wheat stalk! Woo woo!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:333
msgid "Down boy! I don't think your vacuoles can take it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:334
msgid "Want me to read you a story?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:335
msgid "How about The Giving Tree? Jack and the Beanstalk? Catcher in the Rye?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:336
msgid "A GECK? Yeah, there was a guy who..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:337
msgid "Shhh! Shh! Someone's listening!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:338
msgid "It's the great cycle of life, you see... life feeds on life feeds on life..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:339
msgid "Uh huh. But YOU still eat manure. Sheesh... plant philosophy..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:340
msgid "Can I play with your power armor someday?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:341
msgid "You mean that old suit I keep in the closet? Tee hee..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:342
msgid "Yeah, I've dabbled in cross-pollination."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hctyphon.msg:343
msgid "Not that there's anything WRONG with that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:100
msgid "You see a tough-looking old mutant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:101
msgid "You see Zaius, the mine foreman."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:102
msgid "On closer examination, you see a tough old mutant with a pickaxe and miner's helmet."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:103
msgid "You the new guy in town?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:104
msgid "Eek, oog og!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:105
msgid "New! Me! Town!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:107
msgid "Yeah, rolled in a little while back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:108
msgid "No, genius, I've been living here all along and you never noticed me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:109
msgid "Heard you're having a little trouble with the mine."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:111
msgid ""
"Ummm... riiiight. Tell you what. Here's a couple of dollars. Head on down to the saloon and get\n"
" yourself something to drink."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:112
msgid "Yagga? Ogg? Gronk!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:113
msgid ""
"Can't understand you, pal. Why not head on down to the saloon? Hell, maybe Francis will\n"
" arm-wrestle with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:114
msgid "Wessle? O-KAY!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:115
msgid ""
"Right. Well, I'm Zaius. Now that we're introduced... You any good with your hands? We've got a\n"
" problem with our air purifier on the lower level of the mine, but we haven't got the parts to fix it\n"
" or the protective gear to avoid being overwhelmed by the radon gas that's been building up."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:116
msgid "I'm not too good. Sorry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:117
msgid "Not too shabby. What'll it take?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:118
msgid "Well, I'll hope that you enjoy your stay here in Broken Hills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:119
msgid "(more)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:120
msgid "Ha. Ha. Funny. Nothing better than a smart guy to solve a problem."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:121
msgid "Smarter than anyone else in this shithole town."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:122
msgid "Oh? There's a problem? What is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:123
msgid "The main problem here is that you're an idiot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:124
msgid "That's me. Smart guy. What's your problem?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:125
msgid ""
"Our air purifier's broken. It's on the bottom level. We've got no parts, and we've got no\n"
" protective equipment. Without the parts, we can't fix it. Without the protection, the radon gas'll nail us. Are you any\n"
" good with your hands?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:127
msgid "No. Not really."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:128
msgid "You again, eh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:129
msgid "Ork! Ooo! Ug ug!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:130
msgid "Hi! HIIIII! Me "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:131
msgid "Pal, I already gave you some money. Go bother someone else, eh?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:132
msgid ""
"Hi again. Why not go check out... umm... the bank in town? I'm sure there are plenty people there\n"
" who'd love to talk to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:133
msgid "Well, if you ever happen to think of a way, let me know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:134
msgid "Really? Would you do it for me... and, more importantly, for Broken Hills?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:138
msgid ""
"Izzat so? Well, my brainy friend, why not fix the air purifier down below? You'll need the\n"
" parts, and you'll need to find a way to breathe the gas. Until you can show me you can do that, I think\n"
" I'll just assume the only thing smart about you is your mouth."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:141
msgid "Are you kidding?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:142
msgid ""
"The main problem is that I'm an idiot. I'm repeating this because I don't believe that your\n"
" asshole just spouted something that sounded like words. Get out of my sight, maggot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:143
msgid ""
"Aside from the jerks who keep harassing me, the problem is the air purifier in the mine. It's\n"
" busted, and we don't have the protective gear to breathe the radon and we don't have the parts to fix it.\n"
" You can, though, right? Because you're so smart?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:146
msgid "Are you kidding? No way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:147 dialog/hczaius.msg:300 dialog/hczaius.msg:301
msgid ". How's that sound?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:148
msgid "Like shit. I want more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:149
msgid "Sounds good to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:151
msgid ""
"Great! You'll need the parts, of course. Go to New Reno and look for Renesco. He's got tools\n"
" lying around the shop. Tell him Zaius sent you. Tell him that I said, \"The canary's kicked the\n"
" bucket.\" I don't know where to get protective equipment for the gas. I suppose you could go in without any\n"
" but you'll be hurting. Again, thank you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:153
msgid "No? Well, if you should change your mind, you know where to find me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:155
msgid ""
" it is, then. Take half now. I'll give you the other half when you're done. Go to New Reno and\n"
" look for Renesco. He's got tools just lying around his office. He should be able to help you with the\n"
" parts."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:157
msgid "Sorry. That's the limit. Take it or leave it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:159 dialog/nceldrid.msg:459
msgid "I'll leave it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:160
msgid "Fine. Leave it, then. No thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:162
msgid "Hi, friend!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:163
msgid "Oh, good. It's you again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:164
msgid "Howdy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:165
msgid "Y'know, I knew those bastards Franc, Manson, Jacob, and Aileen had it out for us. Well done! So..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:166
msgid "I hope you've given some thought to giving the ore back to the town... so..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:167
msgid "Thanks for selling the ore. It's not like we couldn't use it or anything. So..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:168
msgid "Thanks so much for returning that ore. You don't know how hard we work for that stuff."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:170
msgid "Can you tell me about the town?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:171
msgid "I hear you're having trouble with the mine."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:172
msgid "How're things?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:173
msgid "You get along all right with the humans?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:174
msgid "You changed your mind about trying to fix the mine yet?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:179
msgid "How's it coming? I hope you're going to take care of this soon..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:180
msgid "It's coming along all right."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:181
msgid "I'm a busy man. I haven't gotten around to it yet."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:182
msgid "I should be able to let you know soon."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:183 dialog/hczaius.msg:186
msgid "You've got the parts? Great... I hope you've got some protective gear. The fumes can take you down."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:184 dialog/hczaius.msg:187
msgid "I'm ready to go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:185 dialog/hczaius.msg:188
msgid "I'll be going soon."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:189
msgid ""
"You've fixed it? Excellent! Say, I know you were doing this for free, but... I couldn't let you\n"
" do that. So me and the guys got together and got you this. It's a combat shotgun. Good luck. And\n"
" thank you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:190
msgid "No problem. Thanks!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:191
msgid "You've fixed it? Excellent! As agreed, here's the remainder of what we owe you. Thank you again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:192
msgid "You bastard. You're going to die now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:193
msgid "Good, good. Please hurry, though... our town needs what we get out of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:194
msgid "Sure thing. See ya."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:195
msgid "Don't rush me. I'm a busy man. Jerk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:196
msgid ""
"Well, I'm sorry, Mr. High and Mighty, but I think that the town's survival might be a little\n"
" more important. Hurry it up, will you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:197
msgid "Bite me. I'll get it done. See ya."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:198
msgid "That's the last straw. Goodbye, dead man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:199
msgid "Please hurry. The mine is our town's lifeblood."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:201
msgid ""
"Well, the best person to talk to about that would be Marcus, over at the bank, or Steve, the\n"
" greeter for the town."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:202
msgid "Hmm. All right, thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:203
msgid "I'll go ask them, then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:204
msgid "I'd have to say they're all right. Still... they could always be better."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:205
msgid "Heh. Thanks for all the information."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:206
msgid ""
"Well, as the mutants are not only getting old and senile -- the gas keeps them young, or\n"
" something -- I'd have to say things are pretty good. I mean, we don't want to kill everyone, and as\n"
" far as I can tell, the humans don't think too poorly of us. 'Course, that's not including the humans\n"
" from the other places around here... now those are some bastards."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:207
msgid "All right, thanks. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:381
msgid "I'm a busy woman. I haven't gotten around to it yet."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:382
msgid "Don't rush me. I'm a busy woman. Jerk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:383
msgid ""
"Well, I'm sorry, Mrs. High and Mighty, but I think that the town's survival might be a little\n"
" more important. Hurry it up, will you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:400
msgid "I've got a note with your name on it. Found it on a dead woman in the tunnels. Would you care to comment?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:401
msgid ""
"Hey, I just received the note. Go talk to Francis about it, all right? He's the one\n"
" who wrote it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:402
msgid "If you had a hand in killing those people, I want to know about it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:403
msgid "All right. See ya."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:404
msgid ""
"No! We're just protecting ourselves from the conspiracy. Marcus believes in law and\n"
" evidence, and even though he knows these people are dangerous, he doesn't know who they are-\n"
" and he's too honorable to plant evidence. My part is keeping Francis restrained from all-out\n"
" revenge."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:405
msgid "Sounds too tidy. I'm going to check this out with Francis."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:406
msgid ""
"I knew Francis couldn't handle exposure. He knew the risks of what he did, but I guess he\n"
" didn't figure on ever being caught. He'll be all right eventually. I hope the same will be true of\n"
" Broken Hills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:407
msgid "I hope so too. I have some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hczaius.msg:408
msgid "Me too. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hicavein.msg:100
msgid "The mine has caved in."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hicavein.msg:101
msgid "The explosion of the air purifier caused the entire mine to collapse."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hicdshlf.msg:103
msgid "As you search through the records in the dresser, you notice a thin leather briefcase stuffed carefully deep in the back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hicdshlf.msg:108
msgid ""
"Inside the briefcase you find papers documenting a whole year's worth of skimming money from\n"
" caravans by Chad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hicdshlf.msg:109
msgid ""
"Wow, it really looks like Chad was skimming money. Apparently he is preparing to skip town as well,\n"
" better tell Marcus all this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hicdshlf.msg:110
msgid ""
"30 minutes pass and you find nothing of importance. All that you have found out is that Chad has records\n"
" documenting every moment of his life. He's a pretty boring guy actually."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hichaddr.msg:101
msgid "This door is made of a solid wood. It seems to be built with a new locking system."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hichaddr.msg:102
msgid "This door is firmly locked."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hichaddr.msg:103
msgid ""
"Using the technique you learned from Max, you carefully undo the trigger mechanism and\n"
" effortlessly lockpick the door."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hichaddr.msg:104
msgid "Something seems different about this lock. You decide to leave it alone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hichaddr.msg:105
msgid ""
"You are about to get to work lockpicking when you notice a small little trigger mechanism in the locking system.\n"
" If triggered, you never would have been able to lockpick the door. You skillfully remove it and then in a matter of\n"
" seconds you have the rest of the door lockpicked."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hiconsol.msg:100
msgid "You see a computer console for the power station."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hiconsol.msg:101
msgid "This console must be used to divert and regulate power in Broken Hills."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hiconsol.msg:102 dialog/hiconsol.msg:105
msgid "You probably shouldn't touch this equipment without a good reason."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hiconsol.msg:103
msgid "Unscientifically fiddling with the controls isn't going to get Eric his extra power."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hiconsol.msg:104 dialog/hiconsol.msg:110
msgid "You've already routed more power to Eric's home."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hiconsol.msg:106
msgid "You attempt to increase the power flow to Eric's home, but are unsuccessful."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hiconsol.msg:107
msgid "In your bumbling attempt to figure out how to regulate power flow, you incur a massive electrical shock."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hiconsol.msg:108
msgid "You manage to figure out how to route more power to Eric's home."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hiconsol.msg:109
msgid "You successfully route more power to Eric's home. In addition, you optimize Broken Hills' entire power grid."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hidead.msg:100
msgid "You see a dead body. It appears to have been chewed by animals."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hidead.msg:101 dialog/hidead.msg:104
msgid "Upon closer inspection it appears this person was shot before being chewed by animals."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hidead.msg:102
msgid "You see the body of a young Broken Hills woman."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/hidead.msg:103
msgid "There appears to be a piece of paper of some kind sticking through the lining of her clothing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/himanhol.msg:100
msgid "You successfully entered Liz's hidden weapons cache."
msgstr ""

