msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:400
msgid "Dad!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:401
msgid "Uh-oh!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:402 dialog/mcmiria.msg:402
msgid "I surely do!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:405 dialog/mcmiria.msg:420
msgid "Uncle Biff!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:410 dialog/mcmiria.msg:410 dialog/scmrkgrd.msg:104
#: dialog/scslvgrd.msg:104
msgid "Uhh..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:411 dialog/mcmiria.msg:411
msgid "Uhhh... Continue, please..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:412 dialog/mcmiria.msg:412
msgid "I sure the hell..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:413 dialog/mcmiria.msg:413
msgid "Um... I do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:450
msgid "Uhhh, I'm not the one you should be talking too."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:500
msgid "Oh boy, I get to be the one that's in charge here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1000
msgid "Yes, my sweet."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1001
msgid "What can I do for you, lover boy?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1005
msgid "You don't understand. I just don't want you clinging on me so much when we're walking around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1006
msgid "What you're doing wrong is I need you to walk far behind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1007
msgid "But... But... What did I do wrong?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1008
msgid "What is it you want from me, my dearest?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1009
msgid "Thanks, it was starting to chaff anyway. So now what, lover?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1010
msgid ""
"I used to skin the brahmin at the slaughterhouse, so I'm pretty handy with the\n"
" knife. Also dad had me beat a brahmin to death with a crowbar once. I guess I could use\n"
" a club if I need to. Uhhh, oh yeah, dad took me to shoot a pistol once, but I got\n"
" scared and almost shot him by accident."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1020
msgid "I need a little space, Davin."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1100 dialog/mcmiria.msg:1100
msgid "I'm completely healed and ready to go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1200 dialog/mcmiria.msg:1200
msgid "Hardly more than a scratch left on me now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1300
msgid "Well, I'm mostly healed but I could use more healing when we get a chance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1400 dialog/mcmiria.msg:1400
msgid "I healed myself as much as I could but I'm still pretty badly hurt."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1500 dialog/mcmiria.msg:1500
msgid "No, baby; I wanna come with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1600 dialog/mcmiria.msg:1600 dialog/scrobo.msg:1600
msgid "Sure thing, I'll put it away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1700
msgid "OK, I'm right behind you all the way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1800
msgid "Then I wouldn't be able to protect you. No, I better stay close."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:1900
msgid "Is that it? No way. I'm not letting you out my sight, you little sex pistol."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:2000
msgid "Owie. I think I broke a limb. Can you kiss it and make it better?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:2001
msgid "Ugh, I feel like I am burning up. I think I am radiated."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdavin.msg:2002
msgid "Ugh, I feel so sick. I think I am poisoned."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdthclw.msg:100
msgid "You see Rose's chicken."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcdthclw.msg:110
msgid "Sounds like something BIG is moving around inside."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:100
msgid "You see an old man. He makes a prune look fresh."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:101
msgid "You see Farrel."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:102
msgid "You hear the sound of dry twigs cracking every time he moves."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:150 dialog/scwesgrd.msg:134
msgid "Hey, get away from there!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:153
msgid "I didn't steal the watch, so stop coming over here and harassing poor old Farrel!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:154
msgid "Cornelius says you stole his gold watch."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:155
msgid "Where'd you get the money for the new tools?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:156
msgid "What can you tell me about Modoc?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:157 dialog/mcmiria.msg:156 dialog/vced.msg:114
#: dialog/vced.msg:152 dialog/vcmsmith.msg:105
msgid "What do you do around here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:158
msgid "Watch? What are you talking about?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:159
msgid "Now what!?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:162
msgid "What are you hiding in the wall safe?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:165
msgid "Can you take me to your garden?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:166
msgid "I cleared out all the vermin from your garden."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:167
msgid "You mentioned something about a watch earlier."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:168
msgid "Is this the watch you were looking for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:169
msgid "All furries dead!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:170
msgid "Gar -- din?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:171
msgid ""
"Not again! How many people is Cornelius going to send over to look for his watch? I didn't do\n"
" it! In fact, I was probably the victim of the same thief. Around the same time his watch disappeared,\n"
" some of my tools were stolen. I'm sure you don't believe me, so you might as well have a look\n"
" around, otherwise you'll never go away. Well, go on!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:172
msgid "I think I will have a look around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:173
msgid ""
"Did Miria tell you that? I'll have to spank her bottom for spreading rumors again! Look, I may\n"
" be poor, but I have my pride. I helped one of the traders fix his wagon, and in return he gave me some\n"
" tools."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:174
msgid "Admit it - you're guilty!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:175
msgid "What proof do you have that what you say is true?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:176 dialog/mcfarrel.msg:180
msgid "Do you expect me to believe that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:177
msgid "My honor alone is proof enough that my words are true. I can offer nothing more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:178
msgid "If you didn't take it, then who do you think took it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:179
msgid ""
"I suspect a thief passing through town took the watch, and has since moved on. Although I can't\n"
" for the life of me think of a reason he would want my old tools..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:181
msgid "No, but since I know I didn't do it, that's the only theory I could come up with."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:183
msgid ""
"HA! If you think I'm so guilty, why don't you just shoot me and get it over with. You little\n"
" punk, come and get me!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:184
msgid ""
"How did you find it? I hid that safe so nobody would be able to find it. You must be a\n"
" professional thief. Hmm... where were you when the gold watch disappeared? I think you'd better leave,\n"
" and nothing better be missing from the safe or I'll have Sheriff Jo on ya. Now get out!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:185
msgid ""
"Modoc is a small community of farmers and ranchers. We supply most of the food for the\n"
" surrounding towns and cities by trading our crops for various essentials. It's actually a very nice\n"
" arrangement. However, this could all change with the drought. We can barely keep ourselves fed, let\n"
" alone have surplus to trade."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:187
msgid ""
"Well, mostly I putter around in the garden, trying to make those damn plants grow without\n"
" water. I can't do that now because something big has moved in and I can't seem to get rid of it.\n"
" And to top it all off, nobody will help me because they think I stole Cornelius's gold watch."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:188
msgid ""
"Well, mostly I putter around in the garden, trying to make those damn plants grow without\n"
" water. But I can't do that now because something big has moved in and I can't seem to get rid of it.\n"
" Without food from my garden, I'll surly starve."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:189
msgid "I can help you, for a price."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:190
msgid "I'll be happy to help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:191
msgid "Admit you stole the watch and I'll help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:193
msgid ""
"Look around! I'm just a poor old man. I can barely afford to keep myself fed, let alone reward\n"
" you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:194
msgid "I'll be glad to help you anyway."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:195
msgid "Sorry, I can't help you then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:196
msgid ""
"That would be wonderful. I can't thank you enough. My garden is little ways east of here. Come\n"
" with me, I'll show you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:197
msgid ""
"Thank you! You are truly a hero amongst heroes. Not many people would risk their lives for a\n"
" total stranger. Thank you! Thank you! Thank you... [You get this warm fuzzy feeling all the way down to\n"
" your toes.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:199
msgid "I'd rather starve than tarnish my good name! Go to hell!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:200
msgid ""
"Everybody is accusing me of stealing my best friend Cornelius's gold pocket watch. Me and\n"
" Cornelius have been friends as long as I can remember; I would never take his watch. I've searched\n"
" everywhere hoping to find it so we can be friends again, but I've had no such luck."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:201
msgid "I'll be around for awhile. If I come across it, I'll let you know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:202
msgid "That's really too bad. Can I ask you some more questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:203
msgid ""
"Would you really? Nobody will help me because they think I stole the watch. It would be nice to\n"
" have somebody on my side, for once. I've already questioned everyone about it, but it won't hurt to ask\n"
" everybody again. Maybe they'll tell you something they wouldn't tell me. It also won't hurt to poke yer\n"
" nose around Rose's Bed and Breakfast; Cornelius is notorious for putting stuff down and forgetting\n"
" where he put it a minute later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:205
msgid ""
"Let me see that! Yes, this is it! You said a rat living down the sewage hole stole it? And you\n"
" climbed down there and retrieved it? EWWW! I'm going to give this to Cornelius right now! Now we can be\n"
" friends again. Thank you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:206
msgid ""
"Ooga right back at ya. How would you like to do old Farrel a favor, my slope-foreheaded little\n"
" friend? I have this little vermin problem in my garden. Make the little pests go away and I'll give\n"
" you a reward."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:207
msgid "No, no, no... me no do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:208
msgid "Yep. I do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:209
msgid "Bye bye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:210
msgid "Then get out, you dimwitted cave dweller!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:211
msgid ""
"So good of you, my dear fellow. [He takes your hand and walks you to the garden.] Wouldn't want\n"
" you to get lost. Come back and see me when you finish killing the pests."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:212
msgid ""
"My dear, sweet, woman. You're so kind to an old man. [He takes your hand and walks you to the\n"
" garden.] Wouldn't want you to get lost. Come back and see me when you finish killing the pests."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:213
msgid ""
"Fantastic! And here is your reward. [He digs in his pants and produces a half eaten cookie.] Now\n"
" be a good little caveman and take your cookie outside and play."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:300
msgid "I'm gonna kill that bastard."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:301
msgid "I hate him..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:302 dialog/scrobo.msg:110
msgid "Grrr..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:501
msgid "I didn't steal yer stupid watch!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:502
msgid "I'm innocent, I tell ya!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:503
msgid "You couldn't hit the broadside of a barn!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:550
msgid "He's not paying attention to what you're saying."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcfarrel.msg:600
msgid "You have peacefully solved the feud between Farrel and Cornelius."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:100
msgid "You see a very active old man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:101
msgid "You see Grisham."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:102
msgid "You can't quite place him, but he looks familiar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:151
msgid "I told you you'd get yours!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:152
msgid "Bwahahaha!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:154
msgid "I'm busy!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:155
msgid "I knew my daughter was odd."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:156 dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1156
msgid "Different people, different tastes, I suppose."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:157
msgid "I think I'm going to be sick."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:158
msgid "I knew my son was odd."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:159
msgid "You take good care of my daughter."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:160 dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1159
msgid "I guess you're family, now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:161
msgid "You take good care of my son."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:162
msgid "The name's Grisham. Welcome to my slaughterhouse. You dropping off or picking up?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:163
msgid "I guess picking up? I'm interested in buying some traveling provisions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:164
msgid "You wouldn't have happened to have seen a gold watch lying around here somewhere?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:166
msgid "I would like to buy some of your famous jerky."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:168
msgid "Can you tell me a little bit about the slaughterhouse?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:169
msgid "I see the drought hasn't affected your business yet."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:170
msgid "I knew you'd be able to handle it. Let's see now, I owe you $1000 for completing the job. Of course, "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:171
msgid " brahmin got killed due to your carelessness. At $100 per brahmin your reward is "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:172
msgid ""
". Don't even bother to lie about the number of brahmin killed -- I had one of my boys follow you\n"
" out and watch from a distance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:173
msgid "You never said anything about charging me if any brahmin died!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:174
msgid ""
"Why, you conniving, dried up old coot. Arg! Mark my words - this is the last time you get the best\n"
" of me!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:175
msgid "Thanks, pops; pleasure doing business with ya."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:176
msgid ""
"How dare you show your face around here. I lost ten brahmin due to your cowardice. However, if\n"
" you wish to make amends, $1500 would do a lot to cover my losses."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:177
msgid "Those brahmin weren't worth more than a $1000."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:178
msgid ""
"I don't have that kind of money, and if I did, I wouldn't give it to a little trickster like\n"
" you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:179
msgid "I've left my money in my room; let me go get it for you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:180
msgid ""
"Ah! Of course, of course. Let's see, for traveling, I recommend our world famous dried brahmin\n"
" strips. Won't spoil on the road and it's tasty, too. Only $10 a package. You interested?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:181
msgid "Sounds good; give me one package."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:182
msgid "No thanks, maybe later. I would like to ask you some questions, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:183
msgid "A pleasure doing business with you. Is there anything else I can do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:185
msgid ""
"Wait! You look to be a capable traveler. I don't suppose you'd be interested in making some\n"
" money?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:186
msgid ""
"Are you sure you're not interested in making some money? I'm quite sure you'd be able to solve\n"
" my problem quite easily."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:187
msgid "That depends. How much, what do I have to do, and most importantly, HOW MUCH?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:188
msgid ""
"Smart as whip! You remind me of myself when I was young. Simple... some wild dogs have been\n"
" coming down out of the hills lately looking for food. I think they find brahmin easy prey and have been\n"
" attacking my herds nightly. Wipe out their pack, and I'll give you $1000."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:189
msgid "You're holding something back, you old coot. What's the catch?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:190
msgid ""
"Perceptive as well as smart. I knew I wouldn't be able to pull anything on you. The catch is\n"
" that for every brahmin you let get killed, I charge you $100. I pay well for success and I also charge\n"
" for failure. That's the risk you take working for me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:191
msgid ""
"Great! Head out to the pastures at night and kill the pack of wild dogs that are attacking my\n"
" brahmin. Come back here when you finish the job."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:192
msgid ""
"Great jumping horny jacko-snatchers! Is Cornelius still looking for his lost watch? Why can't he\n"
" accept that it's gone? That dang watch never worked anyways, and I'll be a brahmin's uncle if it was\n"
" actually made of gold. Give it up; you'll never find it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:193
msgid "Actually, Farrel asked me to look for it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:195
msgid "Thanks all the same, but I'll keep looking."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:196
msgid ""
"I didn't? Are you sure? I could have sworn I told ya... maybe next time you won't go accepting\n"
" jobs until you know all the details. Now if you don't mind, I have other work to attend to."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:197
msgid "Hehehe. Now that all depends. Are you planning to stay in town much longer? Bwahahahaha!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:198
msgid "I see you're no fool. OK - $1000 then, and we call it even. Shake on it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:199
msgid "[SHAKE HANDS WITH GRISHAM]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:200
msgid ""
"Now hold on a minute. Now that I think of it, those brahmin looked a bit thin. How about $750,\n"
" instead?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:201
msgid "I changed my mind, I don't want to pay you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:202
msgid "[Gives you a big toothy smile.] Good to see you're a person of character."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:203
msgid "[Grisham turns beet red and talks to you with teeth clenched.] OK, $750 then. Give me the money!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:204
msgid ""
"You know, $750 still seems kind of expensive. Those brahmin would have died anyway if the dogs\n"
" didn't get them first. But I'm not totally selfish; I'll give you $50."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:206
msgid "FINE! GIVE ME THE MONEY AND GET OUT!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:207
msgid "[LEAVE WITHOUT PAYING]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:208
msgid "Mark my words, you'll get yours. If not by me, then by someone else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:209
msgid ""
"[Grisham smiles at you in such a way that you involuntarily take a step back.] Why don't you\n"
" just keep your money? I have feeling you might have need of it later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:210
msgid ""
"Not much to tell. I run the slaughterhouse in Modoc; you want something slaughtered, you bring\n"
" it to me. I'll kill it for ya and make it into some of the best jerky you've ever tasted."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:211
msgid "What about the hides and other parts of the animal?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:213
msgid ""
"Actually, it has kind of helped my business. Nobody has been able to grow sufficient\n"
" food for their brahmin, so they are severely culling their herds. But that's just a temporary thing;\n"
" you have to look at the big picture. With the decline in the brahmin population, my business can only\n"
" suffer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:215
msgid ""
"[Grisham walks around you, pokes you a couple of times and then opens you mouth and checks your\n"
" teeth.] Ah! A fine, healthy specimen. You'll do fine. Ahem... Bad doggies, killing good brahmin. Go kill\n"
" the bad doggies for your friend Grisham. Grisham will give big reward. OK?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:216
msgid "No, me like doggies. Only bad man no like doggies. Me go away from bad man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:217
msgid "I do it. Go there now!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:218
msgid "Good! Remember, bad things go 'Woof! Woof!' Good things go 'Moo.' Try not to kill the good things."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:219
msgid ""
"You seem to be a little short of money. I don't take credit and I certainly don't believe in\n"
" giving something for nothing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:221
msgid "That's what I get for sending a Neanderthal. Just go!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:222
msgid "Uh... snarf ick unga bunga. Now take your money and be a good little Neanderthal and leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:223
msgid ""
"You are quick, aren't you? Well, if you ask you can retrieve any part of the animal you want.\n"
" Balthas will usually buy the hides, and Rose will buy whatever scraps you don't want. She uses it to\n"
" make soup and feed her dogs."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:225
msgid ""
"You've got to be kidding. Everyone knows Farrel took the watch. Why would he ask you to search\n"
" for it... unless Farrel didn't steal the watch after all! Or maybe this is a trick to convince everyone\n"
" he didn't take it. I need to think this out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:228
msgid ""
"Boy, don't even try to explain this. I don't want to hear it. I'm gonna get the preacher, make\n"
" this all lawful like, and you will leave and take my son with you when you go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:229
msgid ""
"I can't say I'm not just a little turned on by this, but I can't have her living in this house\n"
" now that I've seen it. You two are going to have to get hitched and leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:230
msgid "You mind explaining what yer doing with my daughter?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:231
msgid "You mind explaining what yer doing with my son?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:232
msgid "Let me explain it to you gently, pops. There are these birds and bees, you see... "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:233
msgid "I'm a doctor, and I was just giving her a complete physical."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:234
msgid "I'm a doctor, and I was just giving him a complete physical."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:235
msgid "This isn't what it appears to be."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:236
msgid ""
"That's just great. I'm going to have a smart-ass as son-in-law. Well, come on... son. Let's get\n"
" this over with."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:237
msgid ""
"That's just great. I'm going to have a smart-ass as a daughter-in-law. Well come on... daughter. Let's get\n"
" this over with."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:238
msgid ""
"Let me see. It looked to me that you and my daughter were imitating the brahmin during mating\n"
" season."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:239
msgid ""
"Let me see - it looked to me that you and my son were doing the horizontal tango between the\n"
" sheets."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:240
msgid ""
"OK, maybe it is what it appears to be. But it's only sex, it's not like there's love involved or\n"
" anything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:241
msgid "I understand perfectly. Hormones, and it being that special time of the year."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:242
msgid "I'm glad you understand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:243
msgid ""
"I understand. I hope you understand that you both are gonna hafta get hitched. Can't have rumors\n"
" flying about town, you know. Come along and let's go get the preacher. Don't make me fill ya full of\n"
" buckshot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:244
msgid "Really? Then why were you both naked?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:245
msgid "Germs? I mean GERMS! Very important to be clean when doing these examinations."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:246
msgid ""
"Well as long as yer a doctor, I guess it's OK. You best get dressed; rumors tend to start\n"
" because of misunderstandings like this. While you're here, I've been having these pains down in my\n"
" anus and was wondering if you could take a look at it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:247
msgid "Err... I'll take a look at that later. I have another patient waiting for me. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:248
msgid ""
"Yeah. Why don't you just come with me to get the preacher? Don't try anything funny, or you will\n"
" need a doctor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:260
msgid ""
"I knew you'd be able to handle it. Let's see now, I owe you $1000 for completing the job. Here\n"
" you go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:300
msgid "What the hell is going on here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:301
msgid "Uhhh... Sir, I was just..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:302
msgid "You keep your damn hands off of her..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:350
msgid "[Looking at Bessy] Dropping off."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:360
msgid "I'd like you to make some jerky for me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:400
msgid "What's going on in here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:402
msgid "Holy shit! I knew "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:403
msgid "How dare you sully the honor of my "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:404
msgid "Uh, Jo, can we just skip to the vow tying parts?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:406
msgid "Boy..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:407
msgid "Missy..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:410
msgid "Don't make me make "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:414
msgid "Uh, Bo, can we just skip to the vow tying parts?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:420
msgid "You're not going anywhere, boy!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:421
msgid "You're not going anywhere, missy!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:452
msgid " was different, but there's only one way to make this right!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:453
msgid ". There's only one way to make this right!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:460
msgid " a widow."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:461
msgid " a widower."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:500
msgid ""
"Why, that's a fine looking animal you have there. Should make some fine jerky. Tell you what,\n"
" I'll just keep some of the jerky as payment. What do you say?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:501
msgid "No way! I love Bess. Nobody is going make jerky out of her."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:502
msgid "Sounds good to me. When can I come back to pick up my jerky?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:503
msgid "Forget it, gramps. I'm outta here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:510
msgid ""
"Oh... you're one of those. Wouldn't want to take your 'friend' away from you. Nights out in the\n"
" desert would probably be awfully lonely without her. I don't have time for this; I have work to do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:515
msgid ""
"Great! Come back in about a week. You can pick up your jerky in the smokehouse located just\n"
" outside of the slaughterhouse. I'll leave it in a sack for you. Good doing business with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:600
msgid "Howdy "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:601 dialog/ncbisgrd.msg:229 dialog/ncbismen.msg:230
#: dialog/ncsalmen.msg:180 dialog/ncsalmen.msg:185
msgid "Well, if it isn't "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:602
msgid "Uhhh, he's dead."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:603
msgid "Uhhh, she's dead."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:604
msgid "Miria was alive when I left her, but I'm pretty sure she's dead by now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:605
msgid "Davin was alive when I left her, but I'm pretty sure she's dead by now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:606
msgid "Davin, uhhh, couldn't make the trip, but I'll let him know you said, \"Hi,\" when I see him again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:607
msgid "Miria, uhhh, couldn't make the trip but I'll send her your love when I see her again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:700
msgid "Aggg... [A shocked look comes over Grisham's face as he suddenly grasps his chest and collapses to the floor.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:750
msgid "Well, I have to get back to work now. I'll see you around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:800
msgid "You have saved Grisham's brahmin."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1101
msgid "You see Uncle Biff."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1155
msgid "I knew my niece was odd."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1157
msgid "I'm glad Grisham ain't alive to see this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1158
msgid "I knew my nephew was odd."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1160
msgid "You take good care of my niece."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1161
msgid "You take good care of my nephew."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1228
msgid ""
"Boy, dont even try to explain this. I dont want to hear it. I'm gonna get the preacher, make\n"
" this all lawful like, and you will leave and take my nephew with you when you go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1229
msgid ""
"I can't say Im not just a little turned on by this, but I've got to do what Grisham would've\n"
" wanted. You two are going to have to get hitched and leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1230
msgid "You mind explaining what yer doing with my niece?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1231
msgid "You mind explaining what yer doing with my nephew?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1232
msgid "Let me explain it to you gently, Uncle Biff. There are these birds and bees, you see "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1236
msgid ""
"That's just great. I'm going to have a smart-ass as an in-law. Well... come on nephew, let's get\n"
" this over with."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1237
msgid ""
"That's just great. I'm going to have a smart-ass as an in-law. Well... come on niece, let's get\n"
" this over with."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1238
msgid ""
"Let me see. It looked to me that you and my niece were imitating the brahmin during mating\n"
" season."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1239
msgid ""
"Let me see. It looked to me that you and my nephew were doing the horizontal tango between the\n"
" sheets."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1403
msgid "How dare you sully the honor of my brother's "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1412
msgid "daughter."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1413
msgid "son."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1600
msgid ""
". I hope you're taking good care of my daughter, Miria. She is the light of my life and it\n"
" would break my heart if anything were to happen to her. Where is she by the way? I was sure hoping\n"
" to see her again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcgrisha.msg:1601
msgid ""
". How's the married life treating you? I see my son Davin isn't traveling with you. I sure\n"
" do miss him. Maybe the next time you visit you can bring him along. It sure would make an old man\n"
" happy if he could see his only son again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:101
msgid "You see an average person, of average height, of average complexion. Nothing out of the ordinary."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:102
msgid "You see Jo."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:103
msgid "You see Trader Jo."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:104
msgid "You see Sheriff Jo."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:105
msgid "You see Mayor Jo."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:106
msgid "You see Justice of the Peace Jo."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:150
msgid "We killed everyone. Even the children... [sob]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:151
msgid "Meet us at the Ghost Farm. We attack immediately."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:152
msgid "Thank you for saving the residents of Modoc."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:154
msgid "Hey! Leave that alone!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:156
msgid "Sorry, this trading post is closed indefinitely due to the drought."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:157
msgid "So who says I'm here to trade?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:158
msgid "I'm new here. What can you tell about this town?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:159
msgid "I don't suppose you have a gold watch for sale?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:160 dialog/mcjo.msg:168
msgid "GECK!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:162
msgid "I'm looking for a certain item, and I was wondering if you might be able to help me locate it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:164
msgid "I'm looking to buy a gold pocket watch. Do you know where I can get one?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:169
msgid "You're back! What did you find out about the farm?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:170
msgid "I cleaned out your Ghost Farm problem. You can take over the farm any time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:171
msgid "I have a message for you from the leader of the Slags."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:172
msgid "Mess-aj."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:173
msgid "Farm?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:174
msgid "Bad things all gone!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:176
msgid "I'll be back when I have more to report."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:179
msgid "There's a drunkard in the Den who matches Karl's description. Says he used to be a farmer too."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:180
msgid "Those bodies are fake. Just dummies covered in Brahmin guts. They were there to scare you away from the crops."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:181
msgid "What am I supposed to do again?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:182
msgid ""
"What? Oh, you must be new around here. Welcome to Modoc. My name's Jo, I run the trading post\n"
" here at Modoc."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:183
msgid "I am on a quest. I seek the holy GECK. Do know where I might find it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:186
msgid ""
"Well, you're in luck. I just happen to know where it is. I guess we have some business to\n"
" discuss after all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:187
msgid "Business? Just tell me where I can find the holy GECK and I'll be on my way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:188
msgid ""
"Our only business is that you will tell me where the holy GECK is located before something bad\n"
" happens."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:189
msgid "What do you want for this information?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:190
msgid ""
"Ah yes, what I want... If you hadn't noticed yet, our little farming community is experiencing one\n"
" of its worst droughts ever. The rainy season was unusually short this year, and our crops are dead or\n"
" dying from lack of water. To put it bluntly, our community is on the verge of withering away with our\n"
" crops."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:191
msgid "Umm... You do know I can't make it rain, right?!?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:192
msgid ""
"[He chuckles softly] No, no... of course not. I wouldn't ask you to do something as impossible as\n"
" that. You really can't make it rain, can you... No, of course you can't! Anyway, like I was say'en, we're\n"
" in trouble and we could use your help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:193
msgid "OK, I'm listening."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:194
msgid ""
"There's this farm at the outskirts of town, where no farm should be. Some years back it just\n"
" 'appeared' out of nowhere."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:195
msgid "Are you saying that this farm just sprung up overnight? Yeah, right!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:196
msgid ""
"A group of us were out hunting when we noticed the new farm. But that wasn't the strange thing.\n"
" Soon after, some of us got together to visit our new neighbor, only to discover that there wasn't\n"
" anybody there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:198
msgid ""
"After many months of trying to contact the owners with no success, it was decided that the farm\n"
" must have been abandoned soon after it was built. So instead of letting the crops rot in the fields,\n"
" young Karl moved in."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:199
msgid "Hmm... "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:200
msgid ""
"That's when things got bad. Karl started to tell stories of seeing strange glowing figures\n"
" tending the crops and feeding the animals at night. We all laughed at him, thinking he was making up\n"
" stories. Then one day Karl stopped coming into town."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:201
msgid "What happened to him? Did you look for him?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:202
msgid ""
"Of course we did! We went up there as soon as we suspected something was wrong. [He starts to\n"
" tremble violently.] The horror. Bodies strewn everywhere. Some crucified, while others were\n"
" left to rot out in the sun. I still wake up screaming in the middle of the night from the horrible\n"
" images I saw that day."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:203
msgid "So, let me guess. You want me to go to this farm and find out what happened."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:204
msgid ""
"Normally, I would just leave that cursed place be, but for some reason the crops at this farm\n"
" are still flourishing despite the drought. We'll starve if we don't get food soon. Will you help us\n"
" rid the farm of these ghosts?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:205 dialog/mcvegeir.msg:174
msgid "What do I get out of this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:206
msgid "In return for helping us, I'll tell you where you can find what you seek."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:207
msgid "OK, then let's seal the deal. Cut off your right pinky finger."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:208
msgid "Then it's a deal. Show me where this Ghost Farm is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:209
msgid ""
"What?!? Is that how you seal a deal where you're from? We're desperate and I believe you're the\n"
" only person that could pull this off. So, I guess it's a small sacrifice, if it'll save our town. [Jo\n"
" takes out a knife and proceeds to cut off his right pinky finger!]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:210
msgid ""
"[You stop him just in time.] Wait! I see now you were telling the truth and are truly in need of\n"
" help. I'll help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:211
msgid "Now, take your finger and saute it in a light garlic sauce. Very tasty dish!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:212
msgid ""
"This farm is about a day's travel northeast of here. [He pulls out a map and points to a spot\n"
" northeast of Modoc.] Come back when you've found something."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:213
msgid ""
"[Jo calmly wraps his hand in a bandage and then proceeds to pull out a shotgun!] Let's see if\n"
" you can laugh this off, smart ass!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:214
msgid "[BOOM!]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:215
msgid ""
"You've got to be joking! I'm not going to cut my finger off. I'm desperate, not stupid! Now, do\n"
" you want the job or not?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:216
msgid "OK, I'll do it anyway. Where's this farm located?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:217
msgid "You're obviously not desperate enough. I'll pass."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:218
msgid "What was that? Did you say GECK?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:219
msgid "Unh. GECK."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:222
msgid ""
"My name's Jo. Can you say Jo? No matter; you see that rectangular thing over there? That's a\n"
" door. Be careful not to let it hit you on the way out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:223
msgid "[You don't quite understand everything he's saying, but you grin and turn to leave.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:224
msgid ""
"[He seems to mull something over for a bit and then smiles and looks up at you.] Maybe we can\n"
" work out a trade after all. My name is Jo; I run this here trading post. I have some information about\n"
" GECK. You interested?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:225
msgid "[You nod your head up and down.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:226
msgid "[You swing your head left to right.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:227
msgid ""
"Fantastic! There's this Ghost... er, farm at the edge of town. It's about a day's walk northeast of\n"
" here. Bad things happen there. Make bad things stop, then come back and I'll tell you about GECK."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:228
msgid "I go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:229
msgid "Well then, we have nothing more to talk about. The door is right over there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:230
msgid ""
"Yup, that's one big chip on yer shoulder. Why don't you come back when that chip isn't quite so\n"
" big? You have a nice day, and watch out for that door on yer way out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:231
msgid ""
"Well, then -- welcome to Modoc. My name's Jo and I run this here trading post. We don't have\n"
" much; just a few farms, a slaughterhouse, Rose's Bed and Breakfast, and a tannery. Just enough to\n"
" produce goods to trade. Although that could all change with this drought."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:232 dialog/mcmiria.msg:157
msgid "What can you tell me about the slaughterhouse?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:233
msgid "Rose's Bed and Breakfast?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:234
msgid "Tell me about the trading post."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:235
msgid "Where's the tannery?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:237
msgid ""
"The slaughterhouse is run by Grisham and his son Davin. It's just east of here. He makes the\n"
" best damn jerky this side of the Rockies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:242
msgid ""
"Rose's Bed and Breakfast is on the north side of town. Travelers from all over come just to\n"
" sample her world-famous omelets. Some say her omelets can cure people of what ails them. Frankly, I\n"
" think that's just a bunch of nonsense."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:247
msgid ""
"Just follow your nose and you'll find it. Can you smell that foul stench in the air? That's the\n"
" tanning vats just north of here. If you overlook the smell, you'll not find a better place to get\n"
" leather goods. Balthas can work miracles with leather."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:252
msgid ""
"Like I said before, my name's Jo and I run the trading post for Modoc. I organize trade between\n"
" Modoc and other cities in need of food and leather goods. But with this drought, that could all come to\n"
" an end real soon. We're getting desperate."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:257
msgid ""
"What do you want to talk about? The slaughterhouse, Rose's Bed and Breakfast, the tannery or the\n"
" trading post?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:262
msgid ""
"Well, spit it out. I can't help you if you don't tell me what you're looking for, and I sure\n"
" ain't going to stand here and try to guess what you're looking for."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:263
msgid "I am looking for the holy GECK."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:265
msgid ""
"Since I rely heavily on the products of the people of Modoc, I don't have much to trade for. You\n"
" know, with the drought and all. You still interested?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:266
msgid "Let's do some business."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:267
msgid "No thanks, but can I ask you some more questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:268
msgid "No, maybe later. I have to go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:269
msgid ""
"Now that's a good question. Mostly, I just run this here trading post. But on occasion, I'm the\n"
" sheriff, mayor, judge, and any other official you can think of."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:270
msgid "Wow; you must be a very popular fellow to be entrusted with all those duties."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:271
msgid "Thanks for the info; I'll be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:272
msgid ""
"Nah... I just drew the short straw. It seems I was out getting some supplies and when I came back,\n"
" I found out the townsfolk went and elected me. Seems no one else wanted the job. Except for the\n"
" occasional argument, I really don't have to do anything -- which suits me fine."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:274
msgid ""
"What! Are you trying to be a wise ass? Everyone knows old Corny lost his gold pocket watch.\n"
" He even had me search his best friend's house looking for it. If you know what's good for you, you'd\n"
" keep your nose out of this. Good day!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:275
msgid ""
"[He takes the message from the Slags.] What's this? It's from the people living at the Ghost\n"
" Farm. This is incredible; have you read... oops, of course you didn't. There are still some things that\n"
" need to be worked out between the Slags and Modoc, but it's much too complex for your tiny brain to\n"
" understand, so you needn't worry about it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:276
msgid "GECK now!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:277
msgid ""
"Well, that could be a little difficult. You see I really don't know what a GECK is. But, I do know\n"
" of a place called Gecko, I've never been there myself but I hear it's somewhere east of here. I feel\n"
" really bad about deceiving you. I wish I could give you more in the way of compensation than this,\n"
" but the best I can offer you is a discount on goods. I'm not too stocked up right now, but I'm\n"
" sure things will pick up around here soon and I'd be honored to help stock you up."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:278
msgid "Jerk!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:280
msgid ""
"I don't blame you for being mad at me, but I'm not sorry I did it. We needed someone for the job\n"
" and you fit the bill. All I can say is \"thanks,\" and send you on your way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:282
msgid "Yes... faaarmm. Farm northeast. Go farm. Make bad things go bye-bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:283
msgid ""
"That's great! I'll send some people over immediately to start harvesting the crops. You've saved\n"
" us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:284
msgid "Show GECK!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:285
msgid ""
"Slags? Who are they? What's this? [Jo opens and reads the message.] This is incredible! They've\n"
" been living underground all this time. They say they'd be willing to trade food for medical supplies\n"
" and other stuff. I don't know if they can be trusted. After all, they killed Karl and all those other\n"
" people. What do you think?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:286
msgid ""
"All those bodies are fake. Nothing but dummies covered in brahmin innards. They just wanted to\n"
" keep you from stealing their crops."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:287
msgid ""
"They're extremely sensitive to light. I think a small group of people armed with flares would\n"
" be able to wipe their whole community out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:288
msgid ""
"I found Karl at the Den. He left because no one would believe him about the ghosts and he was\n"
" scared."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:289
msgid "They're holding little Jonny hostage! We need to attack now!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:290
msgid ""
"Fake! But, I saw the bodies with my own eyes. In any case, Karl is still missing. How do they\n"
" explain that? I won't trust them until I'm certain they are on the up and up."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:292
msgid "They said the person that moved in some years ago left suddenly."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:293
msgid ""
"Karl wouldn't do that. They probably killed him! No, until I find out what happened to Karl, I\n"
" don't think we can trust them. I was hoping it wouldn't come to this, but we're just going to have to\n"
" take over their farm. It's either us or them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:294
msgid ""
"No wait! Let me try and find out what happened to Karl. There must be an explanation for his\n"
" disappearance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:295
msgid "I agree we should attack! Their weakness is their eyes."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:296
msgid ""
"I didn't agree to this. I've found out what's happening at the Ghost Farm. Now tell me where I\n"
" can find the holy GECK."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:297
msgid ""
"I'll give you one month to find out what you can about Karl. If you don't come back within that\n"
" time, I'll mobilize the residents of Modoc and we'll take the farm by force."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:298
msgid "OK, one month! Don't do anything rash until then. I'll be back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:299
msgid "I need more time. It'll be impossible to find him in such a short period of time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:300
msgid ""
"One month, no longer! I told you we were desperate. Our food supply is running critically low.\n"
" We have enough for one month; after that we all start starving. I'm going to start organizing the\n"
" townspeople immediately. You best hurry!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:301
msgid "Please don't do anything rash until I return!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:302
msgid ""
"[Shocked] The Den! I-I guess we were a little hard on him. I can imagine what he went through at\n"
" the Ghost Farm, with nobody believing him and all. You say he's a drunkard now, at the Den? If you could\n"
" give him the message that we believe him and that he should come home, I would be most appreciative. In\n"
" the meantime, I believe it's about time the Slags and the residents of Modoc get acquainted."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:303
msgid ""
"I believe I have fulfilled my part of the bargain. How about telling me where I might find the\n"
" holy GECK?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:304
msgid ""
"[Acting a little embarrassed.] Um... well, you see, I don't really know anything about this holy\n"
" GECK thing you're looking for. You have to understand; we were desperate! However, I do know of a place\n"
" called Gecko. It's a ways east of here somewhere. If I were a betting man, I would wager your GECK gizmo\n"
" is located there. I wish I had more I could give you, but we're still a poor community with not\n"
" much in the way of offerings. The best I can do is offer you goods at basically my cost. But\n"
" I'd be honored to help keep you stocked for your journeys when I have the goods and I'm sure any\n"
" of the other residents would be equally grateful if you asked them. Thank you! You've saved us all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:305
msgid ""
"Well, they did kill Karl along with all those other people staked out in front of their farm.\n"
" OK, let's do it. You've seen their hideout and seem quite capable; will you lead us to victory over\n"
" those treacherous Slags?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:306
msgid "Of course! For such a just cause, I would be happy to help you defeat the Slags."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:307
msgid "Maybe this isn't such a good idea; let's think of another way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:308
msgid "That's great; I'll get the townsfolk together and we'll meet you there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:309
msgid ""
"You saw Jonny there! We've been searching everywhere for him. Those monsters, they're stealing\n"
" our children. We won't be safe until they're all dead. I'll get the townspeople together and we'll\n"
" storm their hideout. Meet us at the Ghost Farm as soon as you can."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:310
msgid ""
"How can you live with yourself? We are in a crisis here and all you can think of are your own\n"
" selfish needs. Very well, why don't you go to Gecko; it's to the east of here somewhere. If anyone knows\n"
" about this GECK thing, I'm sure they would. Now if you don't mind, I need to meet with the townspeople so\n"
" we can figure out what to do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:311
msgid "That's great. What were those things, anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:312
msgid "Just a community of mutants. If they weren't ghosts before, they are now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:313
msgid ""
"They were ghosts. They're gone. That's all you need to know. Now, tell me where I can find the\n"
" holy GECK."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:314
msgid ""
"You mean you just went in and killed everyone?! I didn't mean for you to do that. You were sent\n"
" to investigate what was happening at the farm and then return with the information. I think you better\n"
" leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:315
msgid ""
"We're going to attack, but only as the last resort. We only have a month's supply of food left\n"
" before we start to starve. You have until then to find out what is going on. I won't negotiate with\n"
" them unless I know for certain that they didn't do anything to Karl."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:316
msgid ""
"We're going to attack, but only as the last resort. We only have a month's supply of food left\n"
" before we start to starve. You have until then to find out what is going on. I won't negotiate with\n"
" them unless I know for certain that they didn't do anything to Karl and I have to know their reason\n"
" for staking all those people out in front of their farm. I won't deal with savages."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:317
msgid "I think you enjoy killing people just a little too much for my taste. I think you'd better leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:318
msgid ""
"[Shocked] The Den! I-I guess we were a little hard on him. I can imagine what he went through\n"
" at the Ghost Farm, with nobody believing him and all. You say he's a drunkard now, at the Den? If you\n"
" could give him the message that we believe him and that he should come home, I would be most\n"
" appreciative."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:319
msgid ""
"I also found out that all those bodies surrounding the Ghost Farm are fake. Dummies, covered\n"
" with brahmin guts."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:320
msgid "Now will you talk to the leader of the Slags?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:321
msgid "That's all I know for now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:322
msgid ""
"Fake! That's impossible; I saw them with my own eyes. Blood and gore everywhere. But... I guess\n"
" it's possible, we didn't... I mean... well [Jo's face turns beat red.] We all kind of turned tail and ran\n"
" when we saw the bodies. No one actually had the guts to examine them closely."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:326
msgid ""
"Yes, I believe the Slags and the people of Modoc will be able to come to some kind of mutually\n"
" beneficial agreement. Thank you for saving the people of Modoc."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:327
msgid "There's this little thing about my reward? You said you'd tell me where the holy GECK was."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:328
msgid "You need to find out who those people staked out in front of the Ghost Farm are. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:329
msgid "Karl disappeared from the farm some time ago. Find out what happened to him."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:330
msgid "Thanks, I'll see what I can find out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:400
msgid "[Letting him cut his finger off] OK, now I'll help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:410
msgid "What's the big white building in the middle of town?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:500
msgid ""
"Oh, that's our town church. The people of Modoc built it to show their faith. Lately,\n"
" there hasn't been much to be thankful for, so nobody attends the sermons anymore."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:600
msgid "Dearly Beloved: We are gathered here..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:602
msgid "[Jo turns some pages in his book.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:603
msgid ""
"OK, um... Before we begin, is there anyone in this room who knows any reason why these two\n"
" here before us should not be joined together in holy matrimony?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:604
msgid "Do you "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:605
msgid " take "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:606
msgid " to be your lawfully wedded "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:607
msgid "Then by frontier law, I pronounce you attached. You may now kiss the bride."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:608
msgid "Then by frontier law, I pronounce you attached. You brides may now kiss."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcjo.msg:609
msgid "Then by frontier law, I pronounce you attached. You may now kiss the other."
