msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcprotec.msg:156
msgid "Yes, I need to see Vegeir immediately."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcprotec.msg:160
msgid "You're dumber than dirt, aren't you! If you want to see Vegeir, you can just go find him yourself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcprotec.msg:200
msgid "I don't trust \"surfacers.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcprotec.msg:201
msgid "Vegeir said not to harm you... YET!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcprotec.msg:202
msgid "We are charged with protecting our people."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcprotec.msg:203 dialog/vccrtcit.msg:114
msgid "I'm watching you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcprotec.msg:220
msgid "I guess you're OK... for a \"surfacer.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcprotec.msg:221
msgid "Maybe we can get along with the \"surfacers.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcprotec.msg:222
msgid "I'm glad I was wrong about you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:100
msgid "You see a pleasantly plump woman."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:101
msgid "You see Rose."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:102
msgid ""
"Her gray hair is done up in a loose bun, and she walks with a slight waddle. You can't help but\n"
" feel relaxed around her."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:150
msgid "I'm sorry, we're closed. There's been a death in the family. [sniff]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:151
msgid "Hey! I'm the only one allowed to go through the lost and found box."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:152
msgid "I'm beginning to think you're a thief!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:153
msgid "Thief! Thief! Thief!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:154
msgid ""
"Welcome to Rose's Bed and Breakfast. My, aren't you the strapping young man. What can Rose help\n"
" you with today?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:155
msgid ""
"Welcome to Rose's Bed and Breakfast. Oh my, what a pretty young lady you are. What can Rose do\n"
" for you today?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:156
msgid "I'm starved! What do you have to eat around here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:157
msgid "I'd like to rent a room for the night."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:158
msgid "You must hear things working here. Mind if I ask you a few questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:159
msgid "[You smack your lips with a loud POP]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:160
msgid "Glad to see you again! What can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:165
msgid ""
"Oh my! It's you. Everyone is talking about how you risked your life for us, and solved the\n"
" mystery of the Ghost Farm. Know that you are always welcome here, and of course all your meals are on\n"
" the house. You may also rummage through the lost and found box and take whatever you wish as a special\n"
" reward."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:166
msgid "It's the hero of Modoc! Welcome back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:167
msgid "I'd really love to have one of your delicious omelets right about now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:168
msgid ""
"That's what I like to hear. A growing young boy needs to eat to keep up his strength, and I can\n"
" tell you haven't been eating properly. You just sit right down and look at the menu."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:169
msgid ""
"And so you should be. When was the last time you had a good meal, young lady? Why, you're as\n"
" thin as a rail. You just look at the menu and tell Rose what you would like to eat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:170
msgid "Brahmin fries. [$5]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:171
msgid "Wasteland omelet. [$25]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:172
msgid "Water. [$1000]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:173
msgid "Brahmin dogs. [$5]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:174
msgid "Canis burgers. [$7]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:175
msgid "Shepherd's stew. [$3]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:176
msgid "No thank you; I'm not hungry right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:177
msgid "Oh, I'm sorry, but you don't seem to have enough money. Why don't you come back later?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:178
msgid "But I'm starving! Maybe I can order something cheaper."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:179
msgid "Wait! Can I ask you a few questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:180
msgid ""
"Back for some more, I see. You must really like brahmin fries. I'm sorry; since you hold the\n"
" record, you can't enter the contest again until somebody else breaks your score."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:181
msgid ""
"Brahmin fries it is, then. We have a contest on who can eat the most Brahmin fries; so far, the\n"
" record is 36. If you break the record, you don't have to pay the tab for your meal. You look like\n"
" you'd be able to beat the record with no problem. Are you interested in trying?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:182
msgid "That's okay, I'm willing to pay to eat your delicious fried brahmin scrotum."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:183
msgid "I'm so hungry I can probably double that score. Bring it on."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:184
msgid "No thanks; just one order, please."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:185
msgid ""
"Oh, that's just grand. Each order consists of 10 pieces. I'll have to ask you for the money up\n"
" front. I'll refund it as soon as you break the record. That'll be $20, please."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:186
msgid "I don't have that much. Why don't I try for the record later? I'll just get one order. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:187
msgid "Sure, I'll get it back when I break the record."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:188
msgid ""
"[Rose takes the money and comes back with a heaping platter of brahmin fries. They are not\n"
" quite what you expected. They appear to be about the size of golf balls, covered in batter and fried in\n"
" oil to a deep, golden brown. You take a tentative bite of one of the fries. These are delicious! You\n"
" start into the meal with zeal.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:189
msgid ""
"[At around the 34th fry, you start to feel the effects of overeating. A crowd has gathered to\n"
" witness the historic event of the old record being broken. In an attempt to regain your composure, you\n"
" strike up a conversation with Rose.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:190
msgid ""
"[You pop a fry into your mouth.] 'Mmff... splt... mnch...' Don't talk with your mouth full, dear. [You\n"
" swallow.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:191
msgid ""
"How do you prepare these? If it's not a secret or anything, I know some people back home who\n"
" would love these."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:192
msgid ""
"Oh, it's no secret. You just dip them in batter, add some salt and fry in grease. [You pop\n"
" another one in your mouth.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:193
msgid ""
"How do you prepare the brahmin meat? It has such a unique texture. [You pop yet another one in\n"
" your mouth. These are good!]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:194
msgid "That's 37! You just broke the record! [The crowd cheers!]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:195
msgid "[You feel like you've gotten you're second wind and pop another fry into your mouth.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:196
msgid ""
"[The crowd yells, \"38!\"] Well, what makes ours taste so special is that you have to harvest it\n"
" while the brahmin is still alive. You just grab the brahmin by the scrotum and 'snip' four with one\n"
" cut. You've got be careful; the brahmin usually gets riled up at that point."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:197
msgid ""
"[The 38th brahmin tidbit must have been going at the speed of light as it is suddenly and\n"
" forcefully propelled from your mouth.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:198
msgid ""
"We can't count that last one, but you broke the record at 37! Here's your money back.\n"
" Congratulations!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:199
msgid "[You feel sick.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:200
msgid ""
"Ah, that's my specialty. I hope you're hungry; I guarantee you've never tasted an omelet like\n"
" this one anywhere. [She leaves and returns with the biggest damn omelet you've ever seen.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:201
msgid "[You feel revitalized after such a big meal.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:202
msgid "[She quickly disappears behind the counter and returns with your order.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:203 dialog/vcconnar.msg:154
msgid "Can I ask you a few questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:204
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, sweetie, I'm quite busy serving customers. Maybe if you ordered something I'll have\n"
" time to chat with you between orders."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:205
msgid "In that case, I'm starving. What do you have to eat?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:206
msgid "Sure, but make it quick, dear. I don't want to keep the other customers waiting."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:207
msgid "What can you tell me about Cornelius's missing watch?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:208
msgid "Have you ever heard of a GECK?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:209
msgid "What do you know about the Ghost Farm?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:210
msgid ""
"I've never seen an omelet the size of the one you served me. What kind of animal lays such a\n"
" large egg?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:211
msgid "What's a canis burger made of?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:212
msgid ""
"Oh dear! Have you been talking to my husband Cornelius? This whole business with the watch is\n"
" just terrible. Cornelius has got the whole town believing that his best friend, Farrel, took his watch.\n"
" If you've talked to him, I'm sure you've noticed his mind isn't quite functioning properly. I'm pretty\n"
" sure the poor dear just left the watch somewhere and forgot where."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:213
msgid "Now, if you don't need anything else, I have other customers to serve."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:215
msgid "One moment, I'm still hungry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:216
msgid ""
"Did you say GECK? No, I can't say that I have. I have heard of good soup recipe that requires\n"
" three geckos. But no, I haven't heard of anything about a GECK."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:217
msgid ""
"[She shivers involuntarily.] Stay away from there! I've heard tales from travelers about\n"
" rotting bodies tied to stakes, and glowing shapes moving through the fields at night. I don't know how\n"
" much of this is true, but I do know a while back Karl moved out there and hasn't been seen since."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:218
msgid ""
"Ah, you've had the desert omelet. Delicious, wasn't it? Some people say it has healing\n"
" properties. [She looks around nervously.] Oh! Some customers just came in. I'll be right back. [Hmm...\n"
" She never answered your question.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:220
msgid ""
"Our burgers are made of nothing but the choicest, select, grade-A dog. The meat is ground up and\n"
" made into half-pound patties. And to give it that unique smoky flavor, they are slow grilled over dried\n"
" brahmin dung."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:221
msgid ""
"You poor thing. You look half starved. Come sit down and let Rose get you something to eat. [She\n"
" leaves and returns with a large omelet.] Now, you don't move from that spot until you finish every bit\n"
" of that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:222
msgid "Sorry, we're full up. A large caravan has all the rooms rented."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:225
msgid ""
"Really!? You must be really thirsty. I raised the price to discourage customers from ordering it.\n"
" Drinking water is at a premium out here, with the lack of rain and the well drying up. Do you still want\n"
" some?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:226
msgid "Yes! I need water desperately."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:227
msgid "Actually, I'm really hungry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:228
msgid "I'm sorry, we stopped serving omelets. Some fool broke into our coop and killed our... chicken."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:229
msgid "I'm really hungry, so let's see what else you have."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:230
msgid "I was really looking forward to your world-famous omelet. I guess I'll go hungry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:231
msgid "Ahh! Oogie!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcrose.msg:300
msgid ""
"[She quickly returns with a glass of some brownish liquid substance. It appears that there is\n"
" more dirt than water in the glass. However, you are so thirsty that you drink it anyway.] I brought\n"
" a cookie for you to enjoy with that, sweetie."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:100
msgid "You see a scruffy little lad hard at work caring for the brahmin."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:101
msgid "You see the stable boy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:150
msgid "He seems to be busy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:200
msgid "Sorry, the stables are full. You'll have to look elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:201
msgid "I'm really busy right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:250
msgid "Smell? I guess you get used to it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:251
msgid "It doesn't smell that bad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:252
msgid "I guess I don't have to fertilize the fields this year. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:300
msgid "This one needs some fresh hay."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:301
msgid "Got to get some more water."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:302
msgid "Whew! Time to get the shovel."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:303
msgid "Everything seems okay with this one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:304
msgid "Better keep an eye on this one. Looks a little sick."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:350
msgid "Zzz... I'm sleeping... Zzz..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:351
msgid "*YAWN* I've gotta be up early."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:352
msgid "Hey, I'm still growing. I need my sleep."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:353
msgid "Why don't you go talk to someone else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcsblboy.msg:354
msgid "Boy, I sure am sleepy. If only someone wouldn't keep talking to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:102
msgid "We're being attack by the surfacers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:104 dialog/scpeaon.msg:122 game/cmbatai2.msg:32543
#: game/combatai.msg:32543 game/combatai.msg:36809 game/combatai.msg:41337
msgid "Can't we all just get along?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:150
msgid "Go back where you came from."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:152
msgid "All you surfacers are alike."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:153
msgid "You will not escape."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:201
msgid "Boo!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:202
msgid "Moaaaaaaan."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:203
msgid "*Clank*"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:204 dialog/nimcgslt.msg:204
msgid "*Clink*"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:250
msgid "We used to live above ground."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:251
msgid "What's it like above ground?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:252
msgid "It's so BIG up there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:253
msgid "What's the sun look like?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:254
msgid "Hello, surfacer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslag.msg:300
msgid "I knew we could trust you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslgext.msg:200
msgid "Vegeir says you can't leave just yet."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslgext.msg:210
msgid "Vegeir said it's alright to let you through."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:100
msgid "Seems to be a guard of some sort."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:101
msgid "You see a Protector."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:150
msgid "Besides the pale skin and enlarged pupils, he looks to be an ordinary person."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:201
msgid "Oooh! Now that's gotta hurt."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:210
msgid "You do know you can enter from the back door..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:211
msgid "Bwahahahaha!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:212
msgid "I'm not going to say a word."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:213
msgid "Oh god! You're killing me! Do it again!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:215
msgid "Hahahaha!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:220
msgid ""
"We have been instructed to take all surfacers to Vegeir. You will not be harmed. Please\n"
" come with us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:221
msgid "Go to hell, I'm not going anywhere with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:222 dialog/ocariel.msg:115 dialog/shtandi.msg:143
msgid "I'd like to ask you some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:224
msgid ""
"Let me elaborate on my previous statement. You will not be harmed UNLESS you resist. Are\n"
" you resisting?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:225
msgid "Yes, I am absolutely going to resist you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:226
msgid "No, I know resistance is futile. I'll go with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:230
msgid "Vegeir will answer all your questions. Please come with us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:231
msgid "Okay, I'll go with you peacefully for now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:232
msgid "No, I'm not going anywhere with you unless I get some answers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:240
msgid ""
"Hmm... I wonder if this is an exception to the rule. No, no, no. Vegeir said ALL surfacers,\n"
" even the idiots. Come with me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:241
msgid "[Go with the guards.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:242
msgid "[Kill them all and let whatever gods they worship sort them out.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:250
msgid "I'm sorry; you can't leave this way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:251
msgid "This entrance is for the workers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:252
msgid "It takes too much effort to set up the ramps for just one person."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:253
msgid "If you want to leave, ask Vegeir."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcslggrd.msg:260
msgid "Ogey Dogey."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:100
msgid "Rose makes the best omelets."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:101
msgid "Psst... Stay away from the brahmin fries."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:102
msgid "I stop by Rose's every chance I get."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:103
msgid "Have you tried Rose's omelets?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:110
msgid "Do you smell something?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:111
msgid "Good god! What the hell have you been rolling in!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:112
msgid "Could you please stand downwind? I'm trying to eat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:120
msgid "Do you mind? I'm trying to get some sleep."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:121
msgid "Hey, what are you doing in my room?!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:122 dialog/vclynett.msg:113 game/cmbatai2.msg:32645
#: game/combatai.msg:32645
msgid "Get out!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:130
msgid "Rose is out of omelets."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:131
msgid "I'll kill the person who let her chicken escape."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:132
msgid "There's no point in coming here if I can't get an omelet."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:140
msgid "I don't know why I bother to come here to trade."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:141
msgid "This town is dying."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:142
msgid "This used to be a prosperous farming town."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:150
msgid "I hear Modoc 'acquired' a prosperous farm northeast of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:151
msgid "I don't know if I want to trade for food grown at the Ghost Farm."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:152
msgid "The crops at the Ghost Farm are probably cursed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:160
msgid "I hear they slaughtered innocent women and children."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:161
msgid "I don't want to trade with savages who kill recklessly."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:162
msgid "After I heard what they did, I almost puked."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:163
msgid "Whatever their reason, I don't think I'll be coming by Modoc to trade anymore."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:164
msgid "The people of Modoc are killers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:170
msgid "Looks like things are looking up around here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:171
msgid "I'll probably need to hire another team to carry all the food from here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:172
msgid "It looks as if Modoc is going to be alright after all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mctrader.msg:500
msgid "You see a trader."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:100
msgid "You see the leader of the Slags."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:101
msgid "You see Vegeir."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:102
msgid "A tall, stately man. His movements remind you of a cat stalking its prey."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:150
msgid "You may leave through the trap door located at the rear of this building."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:151
msgid "Please deliver the message to Modoc."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:152
msgid "Modoc is south of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:154
msgid "No, the other south."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:155
msgid ""
"A visitor - how convenient. I've been contemplating on a way to make contact with the surfacers,\n"
" but now I don't have to worry about that -- thanks to your timely arrival. Welcome to the home of the\n"
" Slags."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:156
msgid ""
"How good of you to return. I take it you have delivered the message to Modoc, then. How was it\n"
" received?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:157
msgid "They need time to think it over."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:158
msgid "They have some reservations."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:159
msgid "I want to take Jonny home to his parents."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:160
msgid "Have you reconsidered helping us?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:161
msgid "I need to ask you some questions, first."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:162
msgid "The answer is still no."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:163
msgid "I have decided to help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:165
msgid ""
"Thank you for helping us. You will always be welcome here. For your services, I offer this as a\n"
" reward. [Vegeir hands you an assault rifle.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:166
msgid "Thank you for helping us. You will always be welcome here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:167
msgid "Would it be all right to take Jonny home to his parents?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:168
msgid ""
"Please let me apologize for the unpleasant circumstances under which we meet. Normally, the\n"
" Protectors would have tried to scare you off. Usually rattling chains and some low moaning is\n"
" enough to scare anybody off, but recently they have been instructed to bring any surfacers they find\n"
" to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:169
msgid "That's all right. I'll just be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:170 dialog/mcvegeir.msg:301
msgid "What do you want with me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:171 dialog/mcvegeir.msg:303
msgid "Ghosts?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:172
msgid "You will go IF and WHEN I decide you can go. Not before."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:173
msgid ""
"A simple request. We need to make contact with the town to the southwest; I believe it is called\n"
" \"Modoc.\" Would you do us this favor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:175
msgid "I have many questions to ask before I can possibly take this mission."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:176
msgid ""
"Fair enough. I wouldn't expect anyone to blindly accept tasks from strangers without first\n"
" learning a little bit about them. Ask your questions, and I will answer them as best I can."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:177
msgid "Why don't you send one of your own people to deliver the message?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:178
msgid "Tell me about your people."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:179
msgid "What are your defenses?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:180
msgid "I have heard enough. I am ready to make my decision."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:181
msgid "Ask your questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:190
msgid "Why did you come back to the surface?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:191
msgid "Why the big ghost charade on the surface?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:192
msgid "What is the purpose of your message?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:194
msgid ""
"Since the Sealing, we, as a people, have changed. Few can bear to be on the surface because they\n"
" are not used to having a black sea of nothingness above them. The sensation of falling upward is so\n"
" great for them that they lie frozen, clutching the ground. But that is not the main reason. All of us\n"
" cannot stand the bright light of that which you call the sun; living underground for so long has made\n"
" our eyes too sensitive to light. We cannot travel far from the safety of our homes beneath the ground."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:197
msgid ""
"Once, long ago, we were once like the surfacers. We too dwelled above ground, until the world\n"
" above caught fire. Our ancestors -- who were part of a secret militia -- sealed themselves and their\n"
" families down here for protection. For generations, down here we've remained, safely hidden within\n"
" the womb of Mother Earth."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:200
msgid ""
"Our population steadily increased since the Sealing. It soon became apparent that we could\n"
" no longer survive down here without further supplies. So the Seal was broken, and we once again looked\n"
" to the surface for survival."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:203
msgid ""
"Years ago, someone tried to take over our farm, harvesting crops and stealing animals\n"
" they had no right to. We are not a violent people by nature, but something had to be done. Our\n"
" survival at the time depended on those crops. That's when we came up with the ghost idea. Smearing\n"
" ourselves with glowing fungus, we were able to scare away this person and any other nosy neighbors.\n"
" Unfortunately, this has been a little too effective. Lately, we've been seeking to make contact with\n"
" the surfacers, but no one comes to the farm anymore for fear of the ghosts. Luckily, you dropped by."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:206
msgid "Enough! No more questions. Make your decision now!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:207
msgid "I am sorry; I cannot help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:208
msgid "Yes, I will gladly carry your message to Modoc."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:209
msgid ""
"I am sorry to hear that. Please consider yourself a guest of the Slags. When we finally\n"
" establish contact with the surfacers, you will be allowed to leave. Until then, do not try to\n"
" the leave the caves - the consequences would be most unpleasant."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:210
msgid ""
"With the completion of the new irrigation systems, our food supply far exceeds our needs. We\n"
" wish to establish trade with the surfacers and exchange surplus foods for much needed medicines."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:213
msgid "Please enlighten us with your wisdom."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:216
msgid ""
"I knew you would understand. Here is a message relaying our request. Please take it to Modoc\n"
" and give it to the person in charge. Return here when your task is complete. I will tell the Protectors\n"
" to expect your return. We thank you for doing us this service."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:217
msgid ""
"How typical of surfacers. Never doing anything for anyone unless there is some kind of personal\n"
" gain involved. Obviously, we cannot trust such a person as you. We will find someone else to deliver the\n"
" message. Although we are not a violent people, do not attempt to leave the caves or you will regret it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:218
msgid ""
"Hmm... I understand. Such a decision cannot be made lightly. Please keep me informed of their\n"
" progress."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:219
msgid "Then do not bother me any more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:220
msgid "About what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:221
msgid ""
"They don't trust you. After all, they think you kill passersby and stake the bodies out in front of your\n"
" farm."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:222
msgid "They want to know what happened to the farmer that was living here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:223
msgid ""
"We are a peaceful people, and have killed no one. Those bodies are merely props we manufactured\n"
" to scare off those who try to steal from us. If you examine the bodies closely, you'll notice that they\n"
" are nothing but brahmin guts and dummies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:224
msgid "Then what about poor Karl? You know, the farmer that was living on your farm?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:225
msgid ""
"Was that his name, Karl? We scared him off the farm, nothing more. I assume he went back home\n"
" when he discovered the farm was haunted. The Protectors reported him headed west. You might try\n"
" searching for him that way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:226
msgid "I'll keep you informed of my progress."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:227
msgid ""
"We scared him off the farm -- nothing more. I assume he went back home when he discovered the\n"
" farm was haunted. The Protectors reported him headed northwest. You might try searching for him that\n"
" way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:231
msgid ""
"I see you've met Jonny. We found him wandering in the darkness of one of our deepest tunnels.\n"
" He said he had fallen down a dry well by his house, and then was trapped in a tunnel by a cave in. We\n"
" have treated him as one of our own and he is loved by all -- so you will understand that I am wary of\n"
" entrusting him to a stranger who has yet to prove himself to me as trustworthy. I will return Jonny\n"
" when I am sure he will make it home safely."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:232
msgid ""
"You have proven your trustworthiness without doubt. Despite the fact that we'll miss little Jonny\n"
" down here, we have arranged an escort for you and Jonny to go back to Modoc right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/mcvegeir.msg:233
msgid ""
"Oh boy! No wonder you weren't scared away by our little tricks. You're too stupid to be scared.\n"
" I hate to depend on such an intellectually challenged individual, but we have need of your services.\n"
" Take this message to Modoc. Give to leader of Modoc and try not to get lost."
msgstr ""

