#: dialog/ncbishop.msg:682
msgid "Tribal, my patience is wearing thin. Did you kill Carlson or not?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ncbishop.msg:683
msgid "They're fitting Carlson for a coffin right now. Well, what's left of him, anyway."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ncbishop.msg:695
msgid "(Smiles.) Good job, tribal. I'm impressed... and I'm not an easy man to impress. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ncbishop.msg:705
msgid ""
"Not exactly... (Smiles.) What I got is an OFFER: How about becoming part of the Family? I got big plans, and I could\n"
" use you: you're resourceful, tough, and you get things DONE. That's the kind of soldier I need."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ncbishop.msg:706
msgid "I'm interested. What's in it for me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ncbishop.msg:707
msgid "Thanks, but I can't be tied down... my village and my people are counting on me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ncbishop.msg:715
msgid ""
"Hold on... you didn't think I'd let you just WALK with what you know, did you? Heh. C'mon now... there's skeletons that\n"
" need to be buried before this matter's closed. Letting you walk around... that's just bad policy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ncbishop.msg:716
msgid ""
"Hold on... you didn't think things were settled between us, did you? Heh. C'mon now... by my accounts, you still got a LOT\n"
" you have to pay for. Plus, I can't let you leave with what you know... bad policy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ncbishop.msg:717
msgid "Don't talk stupid, Bishop. Let me go, or I'll turn your backwater casino into an inferno. \"Capiche?\""
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ncbishop.msg:718
msgid "Makes sense. Let me introduce you to my 9mm policy."
