#: dialog/ocariel.msg:167
msgid "Glad you, little one, both okay."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocariel.msg:168
msgid "Me outta here. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocariel.msg:169
msgid "Wow. What a story."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocariel.msg:170
msgid "What a crock of sh... I'm outta here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocariel.msg:171
msgid "Thank goodness that you and your daughter are safe."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocariel.msg:172
msgid "Hello again. How are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocariel.msg:175
msgid "Go away, you bastard! I want nothing to do with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocariel.msg:176
msgid "Go away, bitch! I have nothing to say to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocariel.msg:179
msgid ". Yes, I'm new here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocariel.msg:180
msgid ""
"I was holding Sandy behind me, trying to keep her from the monster that had shot Rand. He stood\n"
" next to my husband's body and laughed at me as he aimed his gun at my head. Suddenly, this huge claw\n"
" came out of the darkness, grabbed him from behind and... well, thank goodness that Sandy didn't see\n"
" what happened next. Anyway, the raiders were being wiped out by this group of deathclaws. The one that\n"
" saved Sandy and me stood near us and talked to me. He kept reassuring me that I was safe, and that he\n"
" was sorry that he couldn't have gotten there sooner to help us. Afterwards, the deathclaws brought us\n"
" here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocbabdth.msg:100 dialog/ocbabdth.msg:101
msgid "You see a baby deathclaw."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocbabdth.msg:102
msgid "It looks like a small version of a deathclaw, with claws and all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocbabdth.msg:103
msgid "Sqwee... Rrr"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocbabdth.msg:104
msgid "Maaamaa"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocbabdth.msg:105
msgid "patater..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:100
msgid "You see a young woman in metal armor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a pretty young woman dressed in metal armor. She watches her surroundings very\n"
" carefully."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:103
msgid "Well, I'll be. How are you doing,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:104
msgid "You Dalia. Me remember you help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:105
msgid "Things ok. Me go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:106
msgid "Dalia! Thanks to you, things worked out great."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:107
msgid "Things are fine, but I've got to go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:108
msgid ""
"Hey, I'm glad to hear that. It was my pleasure to do what I could for you. So, what can I help\n"
" you with?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:112
msgid "Nothing. But it's nice to see you again. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:114
msgid "You prisoner."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:115
msgid "You leave when want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:116
msgid "What know about D'claws?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:118
msgid "Why you worry safe?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:119
msgid "Thanks. Me go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:121
msgid "Can you leave anytime you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:122 dialog/ocgordon.msg:122 dialog/ocjoseph.msg:131
msgid "What can you tell me about the deathclaws?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:123
msgid "How did you come to be here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:124
msgid "Why are you worried about needing a place of safety?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:125
msgid "Thanks. I'll talk at you later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:126
msgid ""
"No, I'm not. I'm here of my own free will and I like it. I think this will be a safe place for\n"
" me to stay for a while."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:130
msgid "I see. Well, I'll be going then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:131
msgid "Yeah, I've been told I'm free to go or stay. I'm staying for now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:133
msgid "Okay then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:134
msgid ""
"I don't know any more about them than you do, I guess. I'm still trying to get used to\n"
" them talking to me instead of tearing my head off and using it for a golf ball. It's scary, you know?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:135
msgid "Yeah, me bothered."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:136
msgid "Na, me used to it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:137
msgid "Yes it is, in a lot of ways."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:138
msgid "No, I've come to accept it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:139
msgid ""
"After I left the Squat I didn't know what to do with myself. I figured I'd just drift into\n"
" another town and another hired gun job... so I was wandering the desert trying to decide exactly where\n"
" I should go. Well, one day I was looking for a good place to camp. It was getting late, and I didn't\n"
" want to be out in the open after dark. Off in the distance a ways, I thought I saw a campfire -- so I\n"
" decided to see who was there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:142
msgid ""
"When I let you by me in the Squat, I broke my contract with my employer. I was sure that I'd be\n"
" hunted down and killed because of it. Seeing you here convinces me that I don't have to worry about\n"
" that. I can only assume that my previous employer is no longer in any condition to be concerned with me\n"
" or my whereabouts."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:143
msgid "You safe now. Dalia no worry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:144
msgid "You're safe now, Dalia. You'll have no need to worry about any retribution."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:145
msgid "Thanks,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:149
msgid "I'll see ya."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:151
msgid "Hello again. How's it going?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:152
msgid "I have no quarrel with you. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:153
msgid ". I hope everything worked out for you at the Squat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:154
msgid ""
"So, I sneak up on this camp site and there are these two deathclaws sitting around the fire just\n"
" chatting away. Idiot that I am, I let out a little cry of surprise, jumped up, and turned to run -- right\n"
" into the arms of another deathclaw standing right behind me. Anyway, to make a long story short, it\n"
" took awhile for me to realize that I wasn't about to be put on a spit and barbecued. Instead, I was\n"
" brought here and 'interviewed' by Gruthar. Now I can live here if I want."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdalia.msg:155
msgid ". That takes a load off my mind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:101
msgid "You see Dar, the Deathclaw."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:102 dialog/ocgrunt.msg:102 dialog/ocjul.msg:102
#: dialog/octhearn.msg:102 dialog/ocvaldis.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a typical deathclaw. The creature is huge, with a powerful body, sharp teeth, and long\n"
" claws."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:103
msgid "Hello, human."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:105
msgid "Hi. Who you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:106
msgid "Why you here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:107
msgid "You smart like rest?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:108
msgid "Me bored, me go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:109
msgid "Sorry to bother you, but who are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:110
msgid "What is your job at the vault?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:111
msgid "Please don't take offense, but how educated are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:112 dialog/octhearn.msg:112 dialog/ocvaldis.msg:111
msgid "Well, just passing the time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:113
msgid "I Dar, warrior."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:115
msgid "You all same. Me leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:117
msgid "I see. Well I've got to go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:120
msgid "Warrior! Ha! That's a good one. Know any more?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:121
msgid "Dar guard hall and keep peace. Nothing more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:122
msgid "Me hear before."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:124
msgid "Well, you're doing fine, Dar. Just keep it up."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:125
msgid "Yeah, I figured as much."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:126
msgid "Nothing new here. I guess I'll be going."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:127
msgid "With a face like yours, how can you keep the peace?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:128
msgid "You not nice. Go away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:129
msgid "Not much but I learn. Gruthar -- he leader -- tell us all learn."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:130
msgid "Elder in village do same me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:131 dialog/ocgordon.msg:152 dialog/octhearn.msg:129
msgid "Ah."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:132
msgid "Gruthar is right; you should all try to educate yourselves."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:134
msgid "So, you're so stupid that someone else has to force you to educate yourself. How nice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:135
msgid "Hello. You pack friend."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:136
msgid "Grrrrrrrrr! Argggggghhhh."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdar.msg:138
msgid ", Dar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:100
msgid "You see a sad, older man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:101
msgid "You see Dave, \"Mr. Depression.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a grumpy, older man in his early sixties. He has a weathered face and looks as if he\n"
" has had his fair share of abuse."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:103
msgid "Oh. I didn't see you standing there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:104
msgid "How not see? Me big."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:105
msgid "Look sad. Why?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:106
msgid "Me go bye bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:107
msgid "That's ok, we all space out at times. Say, you look rather down. May I ask why?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:108
msgid "Yeah, whatever. Why are you so down?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:109
msgid "Should I hit you with a board to get your attention next time?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:110
msgid "Whatever. I just remembered some place I've got to be."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:111
msgid "Hey, shit happens -- and when it does, it happens to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:112
msgid "Uh... me be leaving now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:114
msgid "Nice attitude. What caused it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:115
msgid "I can tell I want to be elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:116
msgid ""
"I was born two months premature. When I was one, I was dropped on the porch. When I was two, I\n"
" had pneumonia. When I was three, I got the chicken pox. When I was four, I fell down the stairs and broke\n"
" six ribs. When I was five, my uncle was decapitated by a watermelon. When I was six, my parents hit me\n"
" in the head with a shovel. When I was seven, I lost my right index finger to my pet rat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:117
msgid "Uh, me hear someone call. Bye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:118
msgid "Sorry things bad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:119
msgid "Past bad, no talk. Things good now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:120
msgid "Wow! I'm sure glad that I'm not you!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:121
msgid "Ok, I get the picture. What's currently bothering you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:122
msgid "I'm truly sorry that you've had so much pain in your life. Hopefully things have gotten better?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:123
msgid "Wait a minute. I forgot I have something else to do right now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:124
msgid "Yeah, well, shit happens -- and when it does, it happens to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:125
msgid "What happen now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:126
msgid "Me hear before. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:127
msgid "So what's going on now to upset you so much?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:128
msgid "I really don't want to hear this. I think I'll be leaving."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:129
msgid ""
"Well, there I was, traveling through the desert, when suddenly my brahmin falls over dead. About\n"
" then I realized I was low on water and hadn't had a drink in quite a while. Later, my bones began to\n"
" ache, my head started to hurt, my bowels became loose, and I got this rash that just wouldn't go away.\n"
" It was time to sit down and die."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:130
msgid "Me... uh... you... You no have wife or child?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:131
msgid "You no talk no more. Me go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:132
msgid "I don't want to hear anymore. I've got to get out of here and away from you. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:133
msgid "Please tell me that you don't have any children."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:134
msgid "Nope. When I turned twenty-two this strange fungus started to grow on my test..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:135
msgid "Arrg! You talk no more! Me go!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:136
msgid "Stop! I don't want to know!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:137
msgid "Oh. Hi. What can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:138
msgid "Uh, what you story again?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:140
msgid "I was wondering if I could hear your tale once again?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:141
msgid "Wait a minute, I thought you were someone else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:142
msgid "At last, my time has come. Are you going to kill me now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:145
msgid ""
"When I was eight, my dog Spike got hit by a tractor. When I was nine, my mother lost her arm to a\n"
" rabid brahmin. When I was ten, my sister was torn to bits by a pack of dogs. When I was eleven, my\n"
" grandfather killed himself because I was ugly. When I was twelve, my grandmother killed herself because\n"
" I was ugly. When I was thirteen, my father poked out his eyes with a pitchfork in a drunken stupor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:146
msgid ""
"When I was fourteen, my brother lost his hand to a wallaby. When I was fifteen, my aunt choked to\n"
" death on a chicken bone. When I was sixteen, I lost my cousin to a badger. When I was seventeen, I cut\n"
" off my left big toe with a hoe. When I was eighteen, my father lost his right leg to the same tractor\n"
" that killed my dog. When I was nineteen... "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:147
msgid ""
"Well, there I was sitting in the desert, waiting for the world to swallow my miserable existence,\n"
" when a pack of deathclaws shows up. Well, I'm thinking to myself, this is it. Now I can die. I can wind up\n"
" as a pile of deathclaw shit in the middle of the desert. But no... fate had yet another cruel\n"
" card to play against me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:148
msgid ""
"You see, the deathclaws didn't kill me. Instead they gave me water, brought me here, gave me\n"
" this room, gave me food, cleaned me up, and now they won't let me leave. I know they're fattening me up\n"
" for some unknown, horrible fate. I keep telling them that I would probably taste better if I was\n"
" leaner, but it does no good. They just smile -- if you can call it that -- and pat me on the head and\n"
" say 'Don't worry, human, things will get better.' Ha! We both know what that means."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocdave.msg:149
msgid ""
"Anyway, to make matters worse, then they started giving me some sort of medication. It was\n"
" making me gassy, so I stopped taking it -- and it's a good thing I did. I think it was some sort of\n"
" 'mind control' pill, because I started to feel like things weren't actually as bad as I thought!\n"
" Anyway, that's about it. I'm just waiting for the dinner bell to chime, so that they can feast on my\n"
" bloated body."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:100
msgid "You see a lean man in long robes. He appears to be in deep thought."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:101
msgid "You see the Shrine Keeper."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a lean man in long robes. He is in his late forties, and his features are soft and\n"
" unweathered. He appears to be meditating."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:103
msgid "Welcome, traveler. I am called Gordon, and I am the Shrine Keeper. What can I help you with?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:104
msgid "Shrine?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:105 dialog/ocmatt.msg:104
msgid "Me ask questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:106
msgid "Uh... not remember. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:107
msgid "It's a pleasure to meet you, Gordon. I'm"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:108
msgid "You call this a shrine? Whoever it's dedicated to must be turning in their grave!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:109
msgid "Well, sorry to have disturbed you. I'll be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:110
msgid ""
"Yes. A shrine is a place of worship that is usually dedicated to a god, a saint, or other being\n"
" of power."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:111
msgid "Ah. Ok. Me ask questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:113
msgid "Certainly you may."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:115
msgid "Who shrine for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:116
msgid "How long you here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:117
msgid "D'claws bad?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:118
msgid "Why you stay?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:120
msgid "Who is this shrine dedicated to?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:121 dialog/ocgoris.msg:125
msgid "How long have you been here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:123
msgid "Why do you stay here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:124
msgid "Thanks, Gordon. Good-bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:125
msgid ""
"This shrine is dedicated to an unnamed hero known only as the Vault Dweller. He, or she, was the\n"
" savior of all who lived here several decades ago. We do not know what became of our savior, but he, or\n"
" she, lives on in our minds and hearts."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:126 dialog/ockerith.msg:144
msgid "That nice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:127
msgid "Me thank you. Wavy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:128
msgid "What a joke! A shrine to someone you can't even remember!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:129
msgid "I see. Well, I have other questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:130
msgid "Very commendable, Gordon. Can I ask you some more questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:131
msgid ""
"I have lived all my life here in this vault. I have been a Shrine Keeper for most of those\n"
" years."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:132
msgid "You here before D'claws?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:133
msgid "Ah. Need know more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:135
msgid "You are a very dedicated man. May I ask you some more questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:136
msgid "That's a long time. Can you answer some more questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:137
msgid "It's your life to waste as you see fit, bud."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:138
msgid "Then you were here when the deathclaws took over?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:139
msgid ""
"No, my friend, I was not. I left a few months ago to visit the statue of the Vault Dweller\n"
" erected in the central court of the NCR (the New California Republic east of here). When I returned to\n"
" the vault, I found the deathclaws were already here. Needless to say, I was in shock. However, I am\n"
" convinced that they are not responsible for what happened to my fellow citizens. If, by chance, you\n"
" want more information on this matter, you can seek out Goris in the library."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:142
msgid "I'll keep this in mind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:143
msgid "I don't need you telling me where to go or who to see."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:144
msgid "Thank you for your help. I have more questions, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:145
msgid ""
"I have lived with the deathclaws for several months now. They seem to be honorable and\n"
" forthright in their dealings with me and the other humans who live here. I trust them and, in time, I\n"
" think you will as well."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:146 dialog/ocgoris.msg:190
msgid "Uh... Okay."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:147
msgid "Humph. Me go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:148
msgid "I'm willing to give them the benefit of the doubt for now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:149
msgid "You can trust the lizards if you want to, but I'll reserve my opinion for now, thank you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:150
msgid "Thank you. I need to know more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:151
msgid "My place is here at the Shrine. I will not leave it willingly."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:153
msgid "Me leave you now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:155
msgid "You are either dedicated or a dumbass. I vote for dumbass!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:156
msgid "Your dedication is admirable."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:157
msgid ""
"You are a rude and verbally abusive individual. Perhaps if one of the guards were present with\n"
" us, you would curb your tongue."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:158
msgid ""
"I warned you earlier that I would not tolerate your abuse. Obviously you have chosen to ignore\n"
" that warning. (Gordon looks towards the door) Guards! To the Shrine, please!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:159
msgid ""
"So you still choose to be an ass. (Gordon motions toward the deathclaw guard) Guard, please take\n"
" out the trash."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:160
msgid "Bring on your stooge! I can kick both your asses in the wink of an eye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:161
msgid "Sorry, I'll curb my tongue."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:162
msgid "My apologies to you, Gordon. Please forgive my outburst."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:163
msgid "I'm sorry. I forgot myself. Please forgive me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:164
msgid "Ooops, sorry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:165
msgid "I've been looking forward to doing some lizard plinking!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:166
msgid "Guards! To the Shrine!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:169
msgid ""
"So, you've returned. Well, I had you removed once and I can have you removed again. Guards! To\n"
" the Shrine! The trash is back!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:172
msgid "Hello again. What can I do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:173
msgid "Ask question?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:174
msgid "Me been here before? Sorry. Got go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:175
msgid "I wanted to talk with you once again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgordon.msg:177 dialog/ocjimmy.msg:181
msgid ". Can I ask you some questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:100
msgid "You see a robed figure."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:101
msgid "You see Goris the scholar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a humanoid figure wearing a long sleeved, hooded robe. There is something unnatural\n"
" about his stance, but you're not sure exactly what it is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:103
msgid "Hello, I'm Goris. I don't recognize you; are you new here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:106
msgid "Yeah, so what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:107
msgid "Hi. I'm"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:108
msgid ""
"Hello, Goris. Gruthar said I should look you up. He seems to think you're the man with the\n"
" answers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:109 dialog/vcgreg.msg:137 dialog/vcmclure.msg:117
#: dialog/vcmclure.msg:167 dialog/vcnancy.msg:164 dialog/vcstark.msg:158
msgid "Can I ask you some questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:111 dialog/ocjimmy.msg:117
msgid "It's a pleasure to meet you,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:112
msgid ""
"So you've talked with Gruthar. He has a rather inflated opinion of me. I don't really know half\n"
" as much as he thinks I do. Anyway..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:113
msgid ""
"So you're an outsider! I've seen a few like you; some are staying here in the vault, but you\n"
" look different. You appear to be more 'seasoned,' if you know what I mean. I'll bet you've been around\n"
" a bit and accomplished things. Am I right?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:114
msgid "Uh... 'seasoned'?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:116
msgid "Sorry, but I think I'll be leaving."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:117
msgid ""
"Yes, I've had some adventures. Say, if you wouldn't mind answering some questions for me, I\n"
" could tell you some of my adventures in return."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:119 dialog/vcrandal.msg:194 dialog/vcrandal.msg:206
msgid "Mind if I ask you some questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:120
msgid "It's a deal! I would love to hear anything you can tell me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:121
msgid "Besides, I couldn't refuse a friend of Gruthar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:126
msgid "What can you tell me about the deathclaws here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:127
msgid "Do you know what happened to the people who used to live here in the vault?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:128
msgid "What can you tell me about Gruthar?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:129
msgid "Do you think the deathclaws are a threat to humans?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:130
msgid "Do you have any information on this Enclave you spoke of?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:131
msgid "What do you know about this virus?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:132
msgid "You mentioned you wanted to do some traveling. How about joining me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:133
msgid "Sorry, but I've got to go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:134
msgid "Hmm... I'm surprised Gruthar didn't tell you about me. Oh well. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:135
msgid ""
"I'm a student of sorts. I'm trying to learn as much as I can about the world and the different\n"
" cultures that have developed. Right now I'm studying the culture the deathclaws are forming and\n"
" comparing it to human development along similar lines. I've acquired just about all the information I\n"
" need here. It would help my research a great deal if I could do some traveling. However, I don't want\n"
" to go it alone, if you know what I mean."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:136
msgid "Interesting. Can I ask you some more questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:137
msgid "So, you're a scholar. That's quite an accomplishment in today's world."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:138
msgid "How boring. Oh, well... it's your life to waste as you see fit. I need more info, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:139
msgid ""
"No, I can leave any time I like. I haven't done so because I don't want to travel alone. I'm\n"
" pretty tough and can take care of myself, but I would still be one person alone in the desert if\n"
" anything happened."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:141
msgid "Ah, too much of a wimp to make it on your own. I got it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:142
msgid "I don't like traveling alone either, so I can't blame you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:143
msgid "Uh... a few months actually. I came here from the coast a while back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:144
msgid "Wow, you're pretty new here yourself. If you don't mind, I need to know more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:145
msgid "You weren't long on that answer. Care to tell me more?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:146
msgid "I see. I need to ask a couple more questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:147
msgid ""
"These aren't your average deathclaws, as I'm sure you noticed. They've had their intelligence\n"
" enhanced by some means not understood by them. It was done by a group of humans known as 'The\n"
" Enclave.' It seems this Enclave needed an army and they chose deathclaws because of their ferocity,\n"
" physical prowess, and... well, you get the picture. Anyway, the only thing lacking in deathclaws was\n"
" their intelligence. They needed to be smart enough to understand complex commands, but not so smart\n"
" that they'd be a threat to 'those in charge.'"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:148
msgid "That sounds like the biggest crock of shit I've ever heard in my life!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:149
msgid "That's incredible. You seem very knowledgeable. Can I ask you more?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:150
msgid "Hmm... Okay."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:151
msgid ""
"::sigh:: They were captured by The Enclave. Gruthar and the pack were forced to aid in their\n"
" capture. They had no choice since they were slaves at the time. The fate of the humans has weighed\n"
" heavily on Gruthar's mind. He's never really forgiven himself for his complicity in the affair. The\n"
" humans were taken alive, but who knows what has happened to them since?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:152
msgid ""
"(Sigh) They were captured by a group called 'The Enclave.' Gruthar and the pack were forced to\n"
" aid in their capture. They had no choice since they were slaves at the time. The fate of the humans has\n"
" weighed heavily on Gruthar's mind. He's never really forgiven himself for his complicity in the\n"
" affair. The humans were taken alive, but who knows what has happened to them since."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:153
msgid "Hmm... I need to ask some more questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:154
msgid "I knew the damn deathclaws were responsible somehow! I need some more information, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:155
msgid ""
"Sometimes we're forced into doing distasteful things by situations outside of our control.\n"
" Gruthar should learn to forgive himself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:156
msgid ""
"Gruthar is not the monster that he appears to be. He genuinely cares about all of us here, and\n"
" is doing everything he can to ensure our safety and survival. All of us trust him with our lives. I\n"
" don't know what else I can say about him. You would have to get to know him and judge for yourself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:157
msgid "I'll not make any snap decisions about him. He deserves better."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:158
msgid "Sure. Let's talk about some other things."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:159
msgid "He's a deathclaw. I find it hard to believe that he can have any redeeming qualities."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:160
msgid ""
"Well... the potential is there, especially when you take their new intelligence into account.\n"
" However, I don't think that Gruthar and his pack pose a threat. They all seem to respect life and\n"
" personal freedom above all else. Now, I don't expect you to take my word on this. I would ask you to\n"
" judge for yourself. There are others who live here whom you can ask your questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:161
msgid "Only a dumbass would fail to see the threat potential of these deathclaws!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:162
msgid "Thanks for the advice; I will ask around. Can I ask you a few more questions, though?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:163
msgid "Hmm... Okay, how about a few more questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:164
msgid "No, only what I've told you. Wait, there is one other thing. The Enclave showed an interest in some ruins to the west of here. Why, I don't know. That's about it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:165
msgid "Well, every little bit of information helps, and I thank you for it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:166
msgid "This happens to be a very important subject to me and you've let me down!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:168
msgid ""
"I think it's called the FEV virus. The Enclave is, or was, doing extensive research on it. I'm\n"
" sorry, but I don't know anything more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:169
msgid "That's okay; on to other things."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:170
msgid "You should be sorry. I was told you were a font of knowledge!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:171
msgid "You've been more than helpful, Goris."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:172
msgid ""
"I've kept my part of our bargain and answered all of your questions. Now, how about those\n"
" adventure stories you promised?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:173
msgid "Gladly. It's a pleasure to talk to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:174
msgid "Promise? What promise?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:176
msgid ""
"(Goris hesitates and you get the feeling you are being carefully scrutinized.) I would be\n"
" honored to join you!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:177
msgid ""
"(Goris hesitates and you get the feeling you are being carefully scrutinized.) I'm sorry, but I\n"
" don't think that you and I share the same ideals. A joint venture would not be in our best interest."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:178
msgid "Okay, you lose."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:179
msgid "I understand. Perhaps you'll reconsider later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:180
msgid "What? I'm not good enough for your company? Screw you!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:181
msgid "Ok, I understand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:182
msgid "I have nothing to say to you. Do not bother me again."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:183
msgid "I asked you not to bother me again. Perhaps violence is the only language you understand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:185
msgid ""
"Yeah, you know, well traveled... knowledgeable... experienced... You don't have a clue what I'm\n"
" talking about, do you? "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:186
msgid "Food seasoned, not me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:188
msgid ""
"Uh huh. Well, your IQ may be smaller than your shoe size, but you obviously have something\n"
" going for you to have survived in the world this long... Ok, let's try this. Me want leave this place.\n"
" Me want travel with you. Ok?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:189
msgid ""
"Uh huh. Well, your IQ may be smaller than your shoe size but you obviously have something going\n"
" for you to have survived in the world this long... it must be that mean streak I can sense in you. Oh,\n"
" well. Good-bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:192
msgid "I'm sorry, I didn't mean to pry into your private affairs."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:193
msgid "Yeah, well, see that you don't do it again!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:194
msgid "Whatever. I need some information from you, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:195
msgid "I'm sorry, Goris. I'm a bit jumpy today. I wanted to ask you a few questions, if you don't mind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:196
msgid ""
"You have had some interesting times. You are the stuff that heroes are made from, and I\n"
" envy you. Thanks for telling me everything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:197
msgid "Well... you are a walking quest for carnage, and I think I'll be going now. Thanks, and bye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:198
msgid "You're welcome, Goris."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:199
msgid "Hello again. What's up?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:200
msgid "You come me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:201
msgid "Uh... me lost. Me go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:202
msgid "Just thought I'd stop by and say hello. See ya later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:203
msgid "Hey, I'm looking for a traveling companion. You up for it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:204
msgid "What can I do for you,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:205
msgid "You bad thing! Why no tell?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:206
msgid "You're a deathclaw? Is there a reason you didn't mention this to me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:207
msgid ""
"How do I put this... Bad thing you kill, no talk. Me not tell you so you see me good thing. Not\n"
" kill me. Okay me stay with you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:208
msgid ""
"I'm sorry to have deceived you, but humans have a habit of shooting deathclaws on sight. I felt\n"
" that it would be to my advantage to hide my identity until you could see for yourself that I am on your\n"
" side in this venture. If you want me to leave, I'll do so. But I would rather stay and help you on your\n"
" quest. I want to show that humans and deathclaws can work together as friends, not enemies."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:209
msgid "Me not like, you go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:210
msgid "Okay, you stay."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:211
msgid "I'm sorry, but I don't like being deceived. You should leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:212
msgid ""
"I understand why you felt it necessary to hide your identity. I think we can work together, so\n"
" please stay -- but don't deceive me again, Goris."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:213
msgid ". Me new here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:214
msgid ". Yes, I'm from outside the vault."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:217
msgid ""
"So, the Enclave started messing with a virus, or some such thing, and injected the deathclaws\n"
" with it. This virus was known to mutate humans into some sort of super beings, so the Enclave wanted\n"
" to see what it would do to deathclaws. Well, the result was a breed of deathclaws so smart that they\n"
" could see they were destined for slavery. So, they played dumb until they could gain their freedom.\n"
" And here they are!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:218
msgid "I am against attacking any deathclaw."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:219
msgid "I suddenly sense that my pack is in trouble. I am sorry to leave you, but I must check on my brothers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:221
msgid "The security cameras recorded what has happened. You should go check it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:222
msgid "You see a gray deathclaw. It's Goris."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:223
msgid "You see a humanoid figure wearing a long sleeved, hooded robe. It's Goris."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1000
msgid "Yes,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1003
msgid "Uh... no weapon now. Okay?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1008
msgid "You D'claw? Why you no tell?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1012
msgid "Make sure you don't have a weapon ready, Okay?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1017
msgid "You're a deathclaw? Is there a reason you didn't mention this to me before?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1019
msgid "I'm healed and ready to go,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1020
msgid "I'm almost completely healed,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1021
msgid "I'm mostly healed, but I could use some assistance when we get the chance,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1022
msgid "I've healed myself as much as I can, but I'm still pretty badly hurt,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1041
msgid "I'll be waiting here for you when you get back,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1060
msgid "I do my best to look inconspicuous,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1079
msgid "I'll stay as close as I can,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1098
msgid "I'll move out a bit and give you room to breathe,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1117
msgid "I'll hang back and give you some room,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1136
msgid "I'm sorry,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1137
msgid "I've learned a lot from our travels together. I'll gladly come with you, "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1158
msgid ", but you've got too many people with you now. I'll wait here until a position opens."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1159
msgid "I think I will do better on my own."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1160
msgid "Your not anyone I want to be around I am leaving."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1161
msgid "I wish to avenge my brethren."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1162
msgid "All right. Let's do it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1163
msgid "Maybe you should do this one on your own."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1164
msgid "You right we kill."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1165
msgid "You go alone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1166
msgid "Lets change up the distance between us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:1167
msgid "Me think you need to move different."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:2000
msgid "I think I broke a limb. Medical assistance is required."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:2001
msgid "I believe I am suffering from radiation poisoning. Do you have anything to aid me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgoris.msg:2002
msgid "I believe I have been poisoned. Do you have anything to aid me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrunt.msg:100 dialog/ockerith.msg:100 dialog/zcldthcl.msg:100
msgid "You see a deathclaw."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrunt.msg:101
msgid "You see a deathclaw guard."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrunt.msg:104
msgid "Hello again. No can talk. Me on guard duty."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrunt.msg:105
msgid "Enemy of pack must die!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:100
msgid "You see a large deathclaw. The creature is composed of rippling muscle, sharp teeth, and claws."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:101
msgid "You see Gruthar, leader of the deathclaws."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see the most impressive deathclaw you could imagine. The creature must be unique among its\n"
" kind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:103
msgid ""
"Do not fear me, human. I do not intend to harm you. I am Gruthar, leader of this deathclaw pack.\n"
" Why have you come here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:104
msgid "Why have you come here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:106
msgid "To kick your ass!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:107
msgid "How is it possible that a deathclaw can talk... and so well?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:108
msgid "I want to know what happened to the people who once lived here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:109
msgid "I'm looking for something called a GECK. I was told I could find one here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:110
msgid "I've been asked to eliminate a den of dangerous deathclaws..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:111
msgid "I'm investigating raids on the local brahmin ranches. Do you know anything about this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:112
msgid "I think I'll be leaving now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:113
msgid ""
"You are no idiot, human. I can see the truth of this in your eyes. Please do not try to deceive\n"
" me. I have no patience for such games."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:114
msgid ""
"Very well. If you wish to be thought of as an idiot, then so be it. Return to me if you change\n"
" your mind."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:115
msgid ""
"My apologies. You seem to be intellectually challenged. You are no threat to me or the pack. You\n"
" are welcome here, and may consider this place a safe haven from the outside world. Harm no one, stay\n"
" out of trouble, and you will always be welcome here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:116
msgid ""
"Forgive me. I do not mean to be rude, but I do not see that this is relevant to our conversation.\n"
" I can speak your tongue, I can read your written word. What more needs be said?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:118
msgid "I don't mean to pry, but surely you can understand my interest in this matter."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:119
msgid "Yeah, well, how about letting me decide what is or is not relevant?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:120
msgid ""
"Yes, I certainly can. Very well. If we part as friends, human, you should speak with Goris. He\n"
" has more understanding in this matter than I. He can usually be found in the vault library."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:121
msgid "Thank you. I look forward to meeting Goris."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:122
msgid "I have no intention of adding a deathclaw to my list of friends. Bye!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:124
msgid ""
"They are gone, human. We did not kill them and take their home. It is not our way to kill. I\n"
" understand that you may not believe me, but I hope that you will judge me by my actions toward you and\n"
" not out of fear or prejudice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:125
msgid "Hey, maybe you figure I can kick your ass?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:126
msgid "You seem to be an honorable being, Gruthar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:128
msgid ""
"A geck. Is that not a small lizard... no, wait... that is a gecko. I am sorry, but I do not know\n"
" what a geck is, nor where it can be found."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:129
msgid ""
"Yes, I believe you mentioned this once before. I do not know what a geck is, nor where it can be\n"
" found."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:130
msgid "Will you let me in to look for it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:131
msgid "Hey, that small lizard comment was really funny. That a relative of yours?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:132
msgid "It's obvious that talking to you is a waste of time. Good-bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:133
msgid ""
"To be honest with you, I'm not exactly sure what it is myself. Would it be all right with you if\n"
" I looked for it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:134
msgid ""
"I am sorry, but I do not allow just anyone to wander these halls. I am responsible for the\n"
" safety of all who live here and I must exercise caution. However, I will look for this geck, and if I\n"
" find it, I will let you know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:135
msgid ""
"I am sorry, but I do not allow just anyone to wander these halls. I am responsible for the\n"
" safety of all who live here and I must exercise caution."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:136
msgid "Look. It's not like you own the place. Maybe I'll look around whether you like it or not!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:137
msgid "I understand, Gruthar, and I'll respect your wish for privacy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:138
msgid ""
"I can understand your concern. You don't know me well enough to trust me. What if I could help\n"
" you out somehow, and in return you allow me to look around?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:139
msgid ""
"(Gruthar stares at you intently for a moment.) You would be interested in helping us? Yes, I\n"
" sense little evil in you. Very well, I shall place my trust in you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:140
msgid ""
"(Gruthar stares at you intently for a moment.) I think not. I can sense the evil in you, human.\n"
" I cannot risk the lives of those I protect by taking a chance with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:142
msgid "Fine. I think a bullet lobotomy is a viable solution to my problem."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:143
msgid "Sorry you feel that way, Gruthar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:144
msgid "I'll be leaving, then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:145
msgid ""
"There are many machines here, machines built by humans. Deathclaw hands cannot use these\n"
" machines. However, there is one machine that understands questions. I ask it to run the other machines\n"
" and it obeys. This machine no longer listens. It will no longer run the other machines. We are running\n"
" out of food and water. I have ordered raids on the human lands so that we may survive. I am not proud\n"
" of this and I would put an end to it. If you repair this machine, I will be able to feed my people once\n"
" again. I will gladly stop the raids. Will you agree to this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:146
msgid "Sorry, I have no idea how to fix such a thing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:147
msgid "I'm no tech, but I can give it a try."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:148
msgid "Hmm... sounds like the voice recognition module has gone bad on you. Let's go take a look."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:149
msgid "I've changed my mind. I'll have to think about this some more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:150
msgid "I will do what I can for you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:151
msgid "I refuse to help deathclaws."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:152
msgid ""
"Thank you. The machine is in the vault control center on the third level. If you can repair it,\n"
" please do so. I am placing my trust in you. Please do not betray it. You are welcome here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:153
msgid "I won't let you down, Gruthar. You have my word on that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:154
msgid "Thanks. I'll get on it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:155
msgid "There really is one born every minute..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:156
msgid ""
"I see... Well, deathclaws are dangerous by nature and great care must be taken when encountering\n"
" them in the wild. However, I am certain that you have noticed that we are an exception. My pack poses\n"
" no threat to you or your human communities. We have evolved beyond our base cousins and wish simply to\n"
" be left alone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:158
msgid ""
"Your heightened intellect could make you even more of a threat than the average deathclaw,\n"
" Gruthar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:159
msgid "I can see that you are not the savage killers that deathclaws are known to be."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:160
msgid ""
"I have spent many sleepless nights, deep in thought, pondering just such issues. I have finally\n"
" come to the conclusion that the burdens and responsibilities associated with the gift of intelligence\n"
" are countless. There are only two choices available to any thinking being. Either accept life as it\n"
" comes and make the best of it for yourself and others, or simply cease to be. I have chosen to accept\n"
" the challenges of life. If this makes me a threat to humankind, then I pity the small mind that finds\n"
" it so..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:161
msgid "Yes, well... I may have a small mind but I also have a BIG weapon."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:162
msgid "I couldn't agree with you more. I don't think you're a threat, Gruthar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:163
msgid "Uh... yeah. What you said."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:164
msgid ""
"(Gruthar pauses and seems to be carefully considering his response to you) I am sorry to say\n"
" that I ordered the raids on the human lands. I am responsible for the lives of many here. We are\n"
" running out of food, water, and other supplies. Until I can get the situation corrected, I need to take\n"
" what I, a deathclaw, cannot ask humans for."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:165
msgid "Well, now that I know the source of the raids, I'll just eliminate it!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:166
msgid ""
"I'm sorry to hear that. Is there some way that I may be able to help you so that you can stop\n"
" the raids?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:167
msgid "I've heard enough for now. I need some time to think."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:168
msgid "I see..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:169
msgid ""
"I am displeased with your decision but I accept it. You may leave, but please return if you\n"
" reconsider."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:171 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:177
msgid "Hello"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:172
msgid "No. I'll get to it, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:173
msgid "I'm sorry, Gruthar. The voice module has gone bad. I'll have to go get one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:174
msgid "I do not understand the workings of such things but I trust you,"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:176
msgid "I shall return, you have my word."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:179
msgid "Yes, and here it is!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:181
msgid ""
"You have restored my faith in humans. I thank you for all that you have done for the pack. Is\n"
" there something that I can do for you in return?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:182
msgid "You said you would let me know if you found a GECK here. Did you locate one?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:183
msgid "Yes, I am looking for a GECK. I have been told that I could find it here. Do you know where it is?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:184
msgid "No, thank you. I have everything that I need."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:185
msgid "Ah, let me see. [He leaves, then returns a moment later, awkwardly clutching some kind of metallic case in his large claws.] Yes, there was a geck in the vault storage room. It is yours with many thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:186
msgid ""
"Yes, there was a geck in the vault storage room. However, it is missing. I am sorry\n"
" that I cannot give it to you as a reward for all your generous help."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:188
msgid "Uh... that's okay. I'll try to locate one elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:189
msgid "Hello again, human. I hope that you do not intend to play the fool with me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:190
msgid "I want to apologize and start over, Gruthar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:191
msgid "Sorry, I gotta go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:192
msgid "Uh, me sorry."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:193
msgid "Greetings, human. Have you reconsidered? Will you help me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:194
msgid "Hell, no. I just wanted to listen to you butcher the language some more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:196
msgid "Yes, Gruthar. I will help you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:197
msgid "Greetings, friend. Have you examined the machine yet?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:198
msgid "Not yet, but I'll get on it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:199
msgid "Hello, my friend. You have saved the pack and we thank you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:205
msgid ""
"I have no quarrel with you, human, and I do not want one. I am trying to deal with you civilly.\n"
" Please return the favor!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:206
msgid "All right, let's talk then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:207
msgid "You're a deathclaw and that means a death sentence... for you, that is!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:208
msgid "I'm sorry, Gruthar. Let's talk."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:209
msgid "Whatever. I'm gone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:210
msgid "No. I am leader here, so I decide. If you do not like this, you can return to your human lands!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:211
msgid "Blow me!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:212
msgid "OK, I'll be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:213
msgid "Of course, Gruthar. I forgot myself for a moment."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:214
msgid ""
"I assure you that I was not trying to be funny or toy with you. Please excuse me if I gave you\n"
" that impression. I would help you if I could."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:215
msgid "Well, thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:216
msgid "I'm sorry, I didn't mean to smart off like that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:217
msgid "Give up the civilized act, bud. It doesn't work on me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:218
msgid ""
"(Gruthar emits a guttural series of growls) I may not own this place, human, but it is my home\n"
" and the home of others who rely on me for their protection. Do not push me to the point that either of\n"
" us will regret it!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:219
msgid "I'm sorry; I've been impolite and overstepped my bounds."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:221
msgid "Whoa! I'm outta here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:222
msgid "Thank you. Please go to the control room and replace the module."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:223
msgid "Consider it done!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:225
msgid "You are not welcome here at this time. You may leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:226 dialog/ocgrutha.msg:227
msgid "Good-bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:229
msgid "Apology accepted, human. Have a nice day!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:231
msgid ". Have you examined the machine?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:232
msgid ". I will wait for your return."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:233
msgid ". Have you found the part to fix the machine?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:235
msgid "I hope you are enjoying your stay."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:236
msgid "Unfortunately, it had to come to this. I allowed him to stay unharmed as long as he presented no threat to the pack. He chose his path. I hope you understand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:237
msgid "You bad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:238
msgid "I understand, Gruthar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocgrutha.msg:239
msgid "Yes. Matt no good."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:100
msgid "You see a tall, lanky man with thick glasses."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:101
msgid "You see Jimmy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:102
msgid "You see a tall, lanky man wearing thick glasses. His brow is furrowed in deep thought and he talks to himself as he wanders about the room."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:103
msgid "Oh, hello there. I'm Jim, or Jimmy. Whatcha up to?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:104
msgid "Me look around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:106
msgid "Uh... Me wander about. Me go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:108
msgid "Hi, Jim. I'm"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:109
msgid "None of your business, four eyes. Back off."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:110
msgid "I'm just wandering about. I'll be leaving now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:111
msgid "Feel free to look all you want but please don't touch anything. There's some sensitive equipment in here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:112
msgid "Me just look around. Me no touch."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:113
msgid "I'm just looking around. I won't bother anything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:114
msgid "You're annoying. Go away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:115
msgid "Hey, sorry. I didn't mean to step on your toes. I'll leave you to your business."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:120
msgid "What all this machine?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:121
msgid "Vault have overseer. This overseer room?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:122
msgid "You here in vault cause you want be?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:123
msgid "What you think about D'claws?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:124
msgid "Computer need part. You know where get?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:125
msgid "Me know enough. Me go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:127
msgid "What's all this machinery for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:128
msgid "Isn't this the vault overseer room?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:129
msgid "Are you here in the vault because you want to be?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:130
msgid "What do you think about the deathclaws?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:131
msgid "The computer needs a part. Do you know where I might be able to get it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:132
msgid "I think I'll be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:133
msgid "Well... we're having some computer problems and I'm looking into it. Unfortunately my forte is software, not hardware."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:134
msgid "What problem?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:135 dialog/vcmsmith.msg:117
msgid "What's the problem?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:136 dialog/ocjimmy.msg:143
msgid "Yes, Gruthar mentioned this to me and asked me to take a look. Do you mind?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:137
msgid "The voice interface to the mainframe has failed so Gruthar can't give the system instructions for running the vault. The food and water processors have already shut down. The power systems could very well be next."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:138
msgid "Why you no use keebored?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:139
msgid "Why not just give it keyboard input?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:140
msgid "Well, you see, that's the weird part. The system refuses to accept keyboard input. I'm at a loss as to what to do at this point."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:141
msgid "Okay me look?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:142
msgid "Mind if I take a look at it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:144
msgid "Well... no offense, but are you sure you're qualified? Oh, never mind. You can't possibly make matters any worse than they already are. Go right ahead."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:145
msgid "You can't make matters any worse than they already are. Go right ahead."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:146
msgid "Okay, but me ask more questions first."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:147
msgid "All right, but I need to ask you a couple of things first."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:148
msgid "This is a mainframe computer system and related support devices. From here all functions of the vault are remotely controlled."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:151
msgid "Normally the vault overseer would be stationed here but Vault 13 has been fully automated."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:153
msgid "Okay, me ask more."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:154
msgid "Why? I mean, isn't that unusual?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:155
msgid "I see. Let's change the subject."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:156
msgid "I don't know the full story but at one point in the vault's history there was a rebellion. The overseer was either killed or overthrown, I'm not sure which. Anyway, the leaders of the revolution didn't want to entrust the fate of the people to another overseer so they installed this mainframe. The records say it was purchased from... oh, what was that name... Ah, I remember, the 'Brotherhood of Steel.'"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:157
msgid "You tell about Brotherhood?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:158
msgid "Can you tell me anything about this Brotherhood?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:159
msgid "No, I'm sorry, but I have no information on them. This all happened ages ago and I've never found any references to them other than this one. However, it's my understanding that the Brotherhood was a military outfit and there are some ruins of what appears to be a military base west of here. That may be what's left of them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:160
msgid "Ok. Me ask other thing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:161
msgid "All right. Let me ask you some other things then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:162
msgid "Oh yeah. I've liked it here ever since I stumbled upon the place and I don't really want to leave. I've always been a loner and don't much care for people, no offense intended."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:163
msgid "Me take none."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:164
msgid "None taken."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:165
msgid "Well... In some ways I admire them for what they are and what they are trying to become. In other ways they scare the hell out of me. I don't think I'll ever get used to the fact that they are just as smart as I am... well, some of them are that smart."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:166
msgid "You think they threat to people?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:167
msgid "Do you think they are a threat to human society?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:168
msgid "Oh, absolutely. They are far superior to us physically and they are our equals mentally. That makes them a pretty big threat. However, it all comes down to morals and ethics in the end. Fortunately, they seem to be ethical and morally well developed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:170
msgid "Yeah, I see what you mean."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:171
msgid "Hi there. It's good to see you again. What can I help you with?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:172
msgid "Need ask question."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:173
msgid "Just say hi. Me go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:175
msgid "Just saying hi."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:176
msgid "Well, let's see... I suppose the best place to look would be Vault City since they're the most modern place I can think of. You might want to give New Reno a try though. They're closer and they do a lot of trading with Vault City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:178
msgid "Thanks for fixing the computer. You've saved all our butts."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:179
msgid "I've got better things to do than shoot the likes of you, but everyone needs a vacation!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:180
msgid ". Me ask question?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:182
msgid ". I'd be happy to answer some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjimmy.msg:183
msgid "You should let Gruthar know that you fixed the computer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:101
msgid "You see Joseph, the herbalist."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:102
msgid "You see a short man with a book called \"Herbs and Their Medicinal Uses.\""
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:103
msgid "Hello, I'm Joseph the herbalist. What can I help you with?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:114
msgid ""
"Why, certainly. Hmmm. You'll need to take some of this. I'll apply this balm to the wound.\n"
" Now just lie back and rest for a couple of hours."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:117
msgid ""
"Why, certainly. Hmmm. This will take a while, so you'll have to stay here overnight. You'll\n"
" need to take this, drink this -- all of it, I know it tastes foul. Now, just lie back and I'll wake\n"
" you in the morning."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:119
msgid "Thanks. That did the trick."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:120
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, but I'm not a medical doctor and I can't perform surgery. I would suggest that you\n"
" go to one of the bigger cities and see a surgeon. Try the New California Republic. It's east of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:126
msgid "What you know about D'claws?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:134
msgid ""
"No, I'm not a prisoner. I stay because I'm needed here. I've learned to accept the fact that\n"
" some of my patients are deathclaws."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:139
msgid "That's a decision that I can't agree with, but it's your life."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:140
msgid ""
"Yes I can, and often do. I have to collect my herbs from time to time, and I've never been\n"
" stopped. I used to wonder if the deathclaws were secretly following me and whether or not they would\n"
" stop me if I tried to leave. So one day I put the theory to test."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:143
msgid "You took a foolish chance and you're lucky it paid off."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:145
msgid "Good idea. I'm glad to see it worked."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:146
msgid ""
"Well, let's see... Deathclaws appear to be mutated Jackson's Chameleons, the horned variety.\n"
" There are a lot of similarities still present, but an even greater number of differences. The mutation\n"
" factor is quite high. This species is highly intelligent, about the equivalent of an eight-year-old,\n"
" with some individuals reaching human normal level. Their learning capacity is very high and they are\n"
" capable of abstract thought and reasoning."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:150
msgid "Wow, I'm impressed with your knowledge."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:151
msgid "Sounds like a bunch of hogwash to me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:152
msgid ""
"I was gathering some herbs one night when a voice called to me out of the darkness. 'I have been\n"
" watching you,' it said, 'and I know that you are a healer. Are you dedicated to your art enough to heal\n"
" someone foreign to you? Someone whom many would consider an enemy?'"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:155
msgid "What a waste to be here when you could be helping others."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:156
msgid "You are truly a dedicated man who deserves recognition."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:159
msgid ""
"I traveled to another town and stayed there a week or so before returning. When I got back, I was\n"
" warmly welcomed. Gruthar, the pack leader, came to me privately and personally thanked me for coming\n"
" back. No, I am definitely here because I want to be."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:160
msgid ""
"Although they do not have vocal chords, the deathclaws seem to mimic human speech much the same\n"
" as a parrot does. I have yet to discover the exact mechanism behind this, so I am unable to say more at\n"
" this time. Socially, they are pack animals with a very rigid code of ethics. They are led by an 'alpha\n"
" male' who rules with the mutual consent of the pack. They appear to be extremely loyal to the pack as a\n"
" whole, treating it as a family unit rather than having individual families as humans do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:161
msgid ""
"Their sense of right and wrong is very well defined. They do follow a code of ethics that is\n"
" enforced by the pack as a whole. Violence is never used as a solution to a problem among the pack as\n"
" far as I can see. There have been no 'capital crimes' committed here, so I can't say how those are\n"
" handled. Hmmm. That's about all I can think of for now. I hope this helps you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjoseph.msg:162
msgid ""
"I answered that I respected all life and would do my best to heal the injured, regardless of who\n"
" or what they were. I thought it was some thief or raider who had gotten himself hurt and needed\n"
" a doctor. You can't begin to imagine my surprise when a couple of deathclaws stepped out of the\n"
" night with an injured companion. Somebody had shot him up real good. I told them I couldn't work on him\n"
" where we were, so they blindfolded me and brought me here. I've been here from that day forward."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:101
msgid "You see Jul, the Deathclaw."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:103
msgid "Stop. You not go here. This place off limits."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:107
msgid "All right, I'll leave"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:108
msgid "I go where I please, lizard breath!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:111
msgid "This hatchery. Pack mother inside. Eggs inside. I guard. All of pack guard."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:112 dialog/ocjul.msg:132
msgid "Me want talk mother."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:115
msgid "I'll be leaving then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:117
msgid "I'd like to speak to the mother."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:118
msgid "I Jul. Pack warrior. I guard hatchery. I guard mother."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:121
msgid "Guard mother important job. You important."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:123
msgid "Guarding mother is a position of great responsibility. You must be an important pack member."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:124
msgid "I guess I'll be leaving now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:125
msgid "You wait. I ask mother."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:127
msgid ""
"Mother say she talk to you. You go in. You not cause trouble. I not want hurt you, but I hurt\n"
" you bad if you cause trouble."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:128
msgid ""
"Mother say she talk to you. You go in but you go alone; friends stay here. You not cause\n"
" trouble. I not want hurt you, but I hurt you bad if you cause trouble."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:130
msgid "You think so? I not look at it that way. That make me feel good. I like. Thank you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:131
msgid "You welcome. Me go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:133
msgid "You're welcome. I've got to go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:134
msgid "May I talk to mother?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:135
msgid ""
"Lizard breath... Oh, I get it. Ha ha! Now you get this. I guard here because I meanest,\n"
" toughest, ruthless son of bitch in whole damn vault. Screw with me, you screw with best.\n"
" You leave here or I rip you head off and make you watch me crap down throat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:137
msgid "Oh yeah? Let's see just how tough you are!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:138
msgid "It you again. What you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:139
msgid "Me say hi. Me go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:140
msgid "Who you say you be?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:142
msgid "Just dropped by to say hello."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:144
msgid "Who are you again?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:145
msgid "You already dead. You just too dumb to fall over."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:146
msgid ". Me want talk mother."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocjul.msg:147
msgid ", Jul, and I'd like to talk to the mother, please."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:101
msgid "You see Kerith, the deathclaw mother."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a typical deathclaw. The creature is huge, with a powerful body, sharp teeth, and long\n"
" claws. This one appears to be female but you cannot tell with any certainty. You notice the scars of several injuries on her torso."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:103
msgid "A human visitor is an unexpected but not unwelcome event. I am Kerith."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:105
msgid "You D'claw mother?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:106
msgid "Who D'claw father?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:107
msgid "Door look like crap. What happen?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:108
msgid "Who build nest room?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:110
msgid "So, you are the deathclaw mother?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:111
msgid "Who is the deathclaw father?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:112
msgid "What happened to the door? It looks like it has seen better days."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:113
msgid "Who built this hatchery?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:114 dialog/ocmatt.msg:114
msgid "I'll be leaving now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:115
msgid "Yes. I am the current pack mother. After my eggs hatch, the other mothers will have their turn."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:117
msgid "Other mothers?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:119
msgid "There are other mothers?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:120
msgid ""
"Yes, there are more mothers. Should anything happen to me, one will be chosen to take my place.\n"
" The pack must survive."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:121
msgid "Uh, me understand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:123
msgid ""
"These eggs were sired by Gruthar, the pack leader. It is Gruthar who decides who will mate and\n"
" who will not. The pack will be made strong by Gruthar."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:125
msgid "Hmmm. I see. Selective breeding to improve the strain."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:126
msgid ""
"That is a painful memory. A treacherous human sneaked in here and planted a bomb among the eggs\n"
" while I was asleep. Fortunately he was not as stealthy leaving and I awoke to find the bomb. There was\n"
" not enough time to deal with the device properly, so I threw it at the door and placed myself between\n"
" it and the eggs. The eggs and I survived. The door did not."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:127 dialog/ockerith.msg:139
msgid "What happen to human?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:128 dialog/ockerith.msg:134
msgid "How get by guard outside?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:129 dialog/shtandi.msg:170
msgid "Me got more questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:130
msgid "What happened to the person who did this?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:131 dialog/ockerith.msg:136
msgid "How did this person get by the guard outside?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:133
msgid ""
"His name is Matt, and he is a prisoner here. Personally, I wanted him dead -- but Gruthar would\n"
" not allow it. I do not see the wisdom in this, but Gruthar's word is law and he will be obeyed. Should\n"
" you talk to this human, take care. He cannot be trusted!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:138
msgid ""
"The guard was added after this incident occurred. We were more trusting back then. Now we are\n"
" more careful."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:141
msgid "What happened to this person?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:143
msgid ""
"We built the cave portion, and a human friend installed the door. He got the parts from a settlement\n"
" north-east of here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:145 dialog/ocsandy.msg:134
msgid "That's nice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:146
msgid "Hello again. It is good to see you. What can I help you with?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:147
msgid "Me just say hello. Me go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:148
msgid "Just saying hi. I'll be going now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ockerith.msg:149
msgid "It saddens me to have to kill you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:100
msgid "You see a tall, slender man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:101
msgid "You see Matt."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a tall, slender man with short hair and a wild look in his eye. You can feel him staring\n"
" back at you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:103
msgid "Is there something that I can help you with, stranger?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:105
msgid "No, wavy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:106
msgid "Yes, I'd like to ask you some questions."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:107
msgid "No, I'll be leaving."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:115
msgid "My name is Matt. Does it matter?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:116
msgid "Guess not."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:117
msgid "Humph. Me go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:118
msgid "Okay, I'll just leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:120
msgid ""
"Yes, as a matter of fact I am. I stumbled upon this place and got myself captured by the deathclaws.\n"
" They give me freedom of movement within the lower levels of the vault, but I can never go to level 1 where the exit is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:123
msgid "Me outta here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:127
msgid ""
"Because, unlike the rest of the sheep who live here, I recognize them as a threat to humanity.\n"
" They know that if I get out of here I will see to it that they are wiped off the face of the earth!\n"
" Look: They can think for themselves, they can learn, they can read and even write if they dip a claw\n"
" in ink. They are fast, tough, perceptive, and deadly. If their numbers grow large enough, they will be\n"
" the greatest threat that the human race could ever face. Think about it. They need to be eliminated!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:128
msgid "Hmm. You make sense."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:129
msgid "Me think you wrong."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:130
msgid "I realize that they are a potential threat, but I trust them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:131
msgid "You do have a point. What should we do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:132
msgid "Alone I don't stand a chance, but together we can fight our way out of here. How about it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:135
msgid "Arrgh! You're a fool to trust them. If you change your mind come back and get me."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:137
msgid "Have you changed your mind? Will you help me get out of here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:140 dialog/ocmatt.msg:143
msgid "You seem to have bought yourself a shit storm!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:141
msgid "Me not here about escape. Me here because someone break computer. You do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:142
msgid "I'm not here to talk about escape plans. Someone sabotaged the mainframe computer interface. Know anything about that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:144
msgid "Yeah. I destroyed the voice module and then I disabled all keyboard input."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:146
msgid "With the mainframe offline the vault will eventually shut down. Without food or water the deathclaws will be forced to begin raiding human lands for their needs. Eventually they will be discovered and their threat to humanity can be dealt with."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:147
msgid "Others here. They need food, water. You no care about them?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:148
msgid "What about the others who live here. Aren't you concerned with their fate?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:149
msgid "Not in the least. They are simply casualties of war."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:151
msgid "Me think me shoot you now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:152
msgid "Good job."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:154
msgid "I think I'll shoot you now. You are obviously dangerous."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocmatt.msg:155
msgid "Good job!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:100
msgid "You see a small girl wearing a yellow dress."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:101
msgid "You see Sandy, the child."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see a small girl wearing a yellow dress with flowers on it. She appears to be meowing like\n"
" a cat. She has on a name tag that says \"Sandy\"."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:103
msgid "Meow... meow... I am a cat. And I have special powers that only cats have. What are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:104
msgid "Me doggy! Woof! Woof! Who you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:105
msgid "Urrrh? (confused puppy look)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:106
msgid "You strange. Me gone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:107
msgid ""
"I'm the person that's gonna kick your ass if you don't stop this cat nonsense and tell me your\n"
" name."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:108
msgid ""
"I'm just a normal person who is quite impressed with your special nature. Can you tell me your\n"
" name?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:110
msgid ""
"(Giggles) You look funny! Meow... I'm Sandy. I'm not really a cat. I just like to play like I\n"
" am."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:111
msgid "(Screams) Mommy! Mommy! Mommy!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:112
msgid "I'm Sandy. I'm not really a cat, I just like to play."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:113
msgid "Me play too. Me ask you questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:115
msgid "I see. Can I ask you some questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:116
msgid "Okay, I'm history."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:117
msgid "What do you want to ask me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:118
msgid "You forced stay here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:119
msgid "You like be here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:120
msgid "You safe here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:121
msgid "Never mind. Me leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:122
msgid "Are you forced to stay here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:123
msgid "Do you like it here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:124
msgid "Are you safe here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:126
msgid ""
"Yeah. My mom always tells me where I can and can't go. She tells me where I can play and when\n"
" to eat and when to go to bed and when to go potty and when to go to school and everything. I don't think\n"
" it's fair that she can do anything she wants but I've gotta do what she says all the time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:128
msgid "Me got leave now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:130
msgid "I think I've heard enough for now. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:131
msgid ""
"I guess. I miss not having other kids to play with but Mom says that will change some day. She\n"
" thinks other kids will come to live here. Until they do I like to play with Valdis. He's funny and he\n"
" gives me piggy back rides. Mom says I should leave Valdis alone. He's busy and doesn't have time to\n"
" play but he always plays with me when I ask him. I just don't tell Mom about it anymore."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:132
msgid "Piggy... (confused puppy look)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:135
msgid "Ok, see ya."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:136
msgid "Yeah. Mommy takes care of me and Valdis wouldn't let anyone hurt me. I'm safe here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:137
msgid "Ok. Me go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:138
msgid "Good; I'll be leaving then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocsandy.msg:140
msgid "Go away! I don't like you!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:101
msgid "You see Thearn, the Deathclaw."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:103
msgid "Forgive. I no speak well. I try talk you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:104
msgid "You want what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:107
msgid "How smart you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:111
msgid "No offense, but just how smart are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:113
msgid "I Thearn. Who you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:115
msgid "Me leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:117
msgid "It's a pleasure to meet you, Thearn. I'm"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:119
msgid "Now that I think about it, I don't give a radrat's ass who you are."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:120
msgid "I guard hall. Safety of pack goal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:121
msgid "Oh... Uh..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:122
msgid "Guard? What?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:124
msgid "Well, continue on. I'll be leaving now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:125
msgid "You're doing a great job!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:126
msgid "You call yourself a guard? Ha!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:127
msgid "What are you guarding the hall against?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:128
msgid "Intruder. Human, deathclaw, whatever. Pack threatened, I attack."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:131
msgid "I'd be surprised if you're smart enough to tell a friend from a foe."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:132
msgid "I feel sorry for any intruders who happen upon you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:133
msgid "Never mind. I'll be seeing you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:134
msgid ""
"How I judge? Not know. Some things understand much. Some things understand little. Lot things\n"
" understand not."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:135
msgid "You, me, same."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:136
msgid "Yeah, well that describes me as well."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:137 dialog/ocvaldis.msg:133
msgid "You're doing ok."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:138
msgid "In other words, you're a dumbass."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:139
msgid "You pack friend. You save pack by fix machine."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:140
msgid "Hello again. I still guard here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/octhearn.msg:142
msgid "Arrrrrrrrrgggh! Die!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:101
msgid "You see Valdis, the Deathclaw."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:103
msgid "Greetings, human."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:104
msgid "How may I serve you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:105
msgid "Who you be?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:107
msgid "Brain hurt. Me come back later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:108
msgid "Hello, who are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:109
msgid "What's your job?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:110
msgid "No offense to your fellow deathclaws, but you sound more... educated, shall we say?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:112
msgid "I am called Valdis. And you are?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:113
msgid "Me human."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:114
msgid "Oooo! Something shiny. Me go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:115
msgid "Hey, I'm the one asking the questions here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:117
msgid "Glad to meet you, I'm"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:119
msgid "I am currently guarding this area of the vault against any unauthorized personnel."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:120
msgid "Un awe thor iced person el?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:121 dialog/vicencom.msg:211
msgid "Uh... sure."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:122
msgid "You talk funny. Me leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:123
msgid "I'll be leaving now, Valdis."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:125
msgid "Well, you certainly seem to know your job well."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:126
msgid "Do you have the brains to decide who is or is not 'authorized?'"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:127
msgid ""
"Why yes, I do. I also have enough brains to decide who is or is not an asshole -- and I have\n"
" concluded that you excel in that category! Now, why don't you leave before I dance on your face for\n"
" half an hour?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:129
msgid "Bad lizard. Now I have to shoot you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:130
msgid "Hey, I'm sorry. I'll watch my tongue from now on."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:131
msgid ""
"Yes. We are quite diverse in our levels of education. I am doing my best to continue mine in my\n"
" spare time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:132
msgid "An iguana with a goal. How freaking cute."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:134
msgid "That's an excellent goal. Keep it up."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:135
msgid "Huh? I am well aware that you are human. I was inquiring about your name."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:136
msgid "Not ask name, ask 'you are.' I are human."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:137
msgid "Me know. Me just test you. Uh... you pass."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:138
msgid "Hear someone call. Me go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:139
msgid "I see. Let us try this again. Hello. I am Valdis. What is your name?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:142
msgid "Unauthorized personnel. Meaning 'people who do not have permission to be here.'"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:144
msgid "Me get another of those headaches. Me go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:145
msgid ""
"My goal is to maintain as much patience as I can, in light of the fact that you are being rude.\n"
" If you cannot deal with me civilly, then please leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:146
msgid "Sorry, I'll try to be more civil."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:147
msgid "Shove it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:149 dialog/rcgenpes.msg:120 dialog/vcgenvil.msg:103
msgid "Good day to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/ocvaldis.msg:150
msgid "I regret the fact that I must kill you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:101
msgid "You see the voice interface terminal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:102
msgid "You see a standard computer terminal, modified for voice commands."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:103
msgid ""
"You examine the computer terminal, but cannot find anything obviously wrong with it. What do\n"
" you do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:104
msgid "Hit it in that 'special' way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:105 dialog/oscomptr.msg:110
msgid "Kick it in that 'special' spot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:106 dialog/oscomptr.msg:111 dialog/oscomptr.msg:115
msgid "Run the diagnostic program."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:107 dialog/oscomptr.msg:112
msgid "Open it up and look inside."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:109
msgid ""
"You gaze at the console for a while and decide upon the best spot to place a punch. After giving\n"
" it your best 'this'll fix it' hit, the monitor flashes a couple of times and then stabilizes. There is\n"
" no other effect. What do you do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:114
msgid ""
"This well-known repair method produces two results. First, the monitor seems to go haywire for\n"
" several seconds and then stabilizes. Second, you hear a breaking metal type of sound and the panel you\n"
" kicked falls to the floor. What do you do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:116
msgid "Damn thing's open. Might as well look inside."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:118
msgid ""
"You are certain that the system should have a set of diagnostic routines available. However, the\n"
" keyboard input seems to have been disabled. The unit accepts voice commands only. What do you do?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:119
msgid "The only thing left is to look inside."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:121
msgid ""
"Peering into the mass of cables and circuit boards, you find that the system has been deliberately sabotaged.\n"
" One of the circuit boards, the voice recognition module, is beyond repair and must be replaced.\n"
" Now all you need to do is find a replacement module."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:124
msgid "You install the module in the terminal. The system is repaired."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:125
msgid "The terminal needs a voice recognition module installed before it can become operational."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:127
msgid "The system is working fine now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:128
msgid "Accessing security footage, loading holographic playback..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:129
msgid "You are the last, Gruthar. The stain of your kind will soon be wiped clean."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:130
msgid "You tell your so-called President that he will burn for this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:131
msgid "Whatever. You were never anything more than a talking animal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:132
msgid "That may be, but we were created through your experimentation. You gave us life!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:133
msgid "And now I give you death."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:134
msgid "Take his body. The doctor wanted a specimen."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:135
msgid "Their blood will run like the Nile!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:200
msgid "Welcome, Vault Dweller. For your convenience, this Vault-Tec terminal has been modified to respond to vocal commands. Please vocalize your command now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:201
msgid "Oh, you've got me confused with someone else. You see, I'm not the Vault Dweller, I'm the Chosen One. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:202 dialog/oscomptr.msg:211 dialog/oscomptr.msg:311
msgid "Run diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:203 dialog/oscomptr.msg:212 dialog/oscomptr.msg:312
msgid "Switch to keyboard input mode."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:204 dialog/oscomptr.msg:213 dialog/oscomptr.msg:313
msgid "Access security footage."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:206
msgid "Urk?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:210
msgid ""
"[A light blinks on the terminal as it makes various clicking and whirling sounds. After several seconds, text\n"
" appears on the monitor.] Sorry, I did not understand your command. Please repeat your command, making sure to speak\n"
" directly into the microphone in a clear and precise manner. Vault-Tec apologizes for any inconvenience. Thank you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:220
msgid ""
"Please wait while I initiate diagnostic checks..Vault-Tec appreciates your patience... Thank you for waiting... Diagnostic\n"
" checks complete. All systems are working properly. After all, you're using Vault-Tec. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:230
msgid ""
"Switching to manual interface mode... manual interface mode initiated. For the convenience of others, this\n"
" terminal will automatically revert to vocal interface mode once you have logged off. Please input command."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:231
msgid "Search database for anything of interest."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:240
msgid ""
"After a bit of searching, you discover three files that might be worth a look: Vault Dweller's Survival Guide\n"
" (Abridged Version), Vault 13 Timeline, and Overseer Logs."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:241 dialog/oscomptr.msg:277
msgid "Access Vault Dweller's Survival Guide (Abridged Version). "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:242 dialog/oscomptr.msg:267
msgid "Access Vault 13 Timeline. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:243 dialog/oscomptr.msg:268 dialog/oscomptr.msg:278
msgid "Access Overseer Logs."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:250
msgid ""
"Welcome to Vault-13, the latest in a series of public defense works from Vault-Tec, your contractor of choice\n"
" when it comes to the best in nuclear shelters. Vault-Tec, America's Final Word in Homes."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:252
msgid ""
"The Vault series of survival shelters are designed from the ground up to provide the best chance for a good life\n"
" following nuclear armageddon. It is the duty of every American citizen to learn and use the skills necessary for a comfortable Vault life. The best place to start is with a description of your new home."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:254
msgid ""
"IMPORTANT VAULT 13 STATISTICS\n"
"                                    Starting construction date: August 2063\n"
"                        Ending construction date: March 2069\n"
"                             Starting Budget: $400,000,000,000\n"
"                                Final Budget, with interest: $645,000,000,000\n"
"                   Total number of occupants: 1,000 (at capacity)\n"
"                 Total duration: 10 years (at capacity)\n"
"                            Number of living quarters: 100 (hot bunking required if at maximum capacity)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:256
msgid ""
"To help Vault Dwellers record information (and information is extremely valuable, in fact, it might be the most\n"
" valuable weapon we have against the end of civilization, so pay attention!) Vault-Tec has selected the RobCo Industries RobCo Pip-Boy 2000 as the Personal Information Processor of choice for its Vault Dwellers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:258
msgid ""
"The RobCo Pip-Boy 2000 is a handy device that you wear on your wrist. It's small, especially by today's standards, and it will store a goodly amount of information for you. And using modern super-deluxe\n"
" graphics to boot! Please refer to your Pip-Boy manual for more information."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:260
msgid "The key to a successful reintroduction of civilization following a massive scale nuclear war is people. Here at Vault-Tec, we are working to ensure to your fellow man (and woman) is up to the task of bringing America back from the dead."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:262
msgid "We believe that a positive attitude is one of the best tools at our disposal. Should you encounter any fellow Vault Dwellers displaying a less than positive attitude, you are encouraged to report them to your Vault's Overseer. Remember, once the doors are sealed, the Overseer's word is law."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:264
msgid "Vault-13 comes prepared with the latest in survival equipment. The items in your storage containers will last 1,000 people over 10 years in comfortable and modern surroundings. When it is time to leave the Vault, and return to rebuild America, your friends at Vault-Tec have provided you with everything that you will need."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:266
msgid "Thank you for taking the time to read The Vault Dweller's Survival Guide (Abridged Version). We at Vault-Tec feel confident that you'll love your new underground dwelling."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:270
msgid "As you read over the beginning of the timeline, you find it interesting that no reason is given for why the Vault didn't open 10 years after the Great War, as it was originally designed to. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:272
msgid "Browsing ahead, you don't find much of interest until the year 2161, when the Vault's only working water chip breaks down. You feel a surge of pride as you read about your grandfather being selected for the important task of leaving the Vault and scouring the wasteland for a replacement water chip. However, it feels a little odd seeing your tribe's most revered legend told in a simple bullet point format."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:274
msgid "Continuing down the timeline, you read of your grandfather's success and subsequent exile, and how several other vault dwellers chose to join him rather than remain in the relative safety of the Vault. You also discover that the Overseer was eventually tried and executed by the remaining vault dwellers."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:276
msgid "The final entry in the timeline is dated May of 2242. It seems that, for the first time, Vault 13 was sent an \"all clear\" signal from an unknown source. After some debate, the vault dwellers decided to open the Vault doors and see what awaited them on the surface world. There is no record of what happened to them after that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:280
msgid "Authorization required. Please enter password. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:282 dialog/oscomptr.msg:292
msgid "[Guess password]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:283 dialog/oscomptr.msg:293 dialog/oscomptr.msg:302
msgid "[Attempt to hack into it.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:290
msgid "Incorrect. Please enter password."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:300
msgid "Incorrect. You are now locked out of these files. Vault-Tec apologizes for any inconvenience."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:310
msgid "[You try everything you can think of, but you're unable to gain access. With a sigh of defeat, you return to the main menu.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:320
msgid "Password correct. All entries but one have been removed from the system. Final entry in the Overseer's Logs is still accessible."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:321
msgid "[After several long minutes of working your technical magic, you manage to hack your way into the Overseer's Logs. However, it seems that every entry except for the final one has been deleted.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:322
msgid "Alright, let's see what this Overseer had to say. [Read Log.] "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:323
msgid "Eh, whatever. [Logoff.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:330
msgid "This is it. Consider these my final words, as I doubt I'll live to write another entry. Oh no, the people of the Vault have spoken, and they've made it quite clear that they want my head. I knew this day would come, ever since HE managed to rile them up by doing the impossible. Sure, he saved all our lives, but he also ruined everything."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:332
msgid "Let it be known that I took little joy in exiling our \"great hero\", but I had no choice in the matter. His adventures in the outside world had changed him too much. He was too great a threat to the project. Had I let him remain among us, he might have uncovered the true nature of the Vaults and jeopardized the experiment. Even if he didn't, he'd at least inspire others to venture outside, which would be just as bad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:334
msgid "He simply had to go. There was no other option. But even that wasn't enough. No, I'm afraid the damage had already been done. I allowed his most stubborn supporters to follow him into exile, and then tried to reassert my control over those who remained. But it was no use -- I'd already been vilified. So be it. The only thing I'm guilty of is an entire lifetime of carrying out the demands of our Great Nation."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:336
msgid "My only regret is that Vault 13 is not likely to complete the social experiment. Once I've been disposed of, I feel certain the others will leave the Vault. Not right away, of course -- I've instilled too much fear in them of the outside world. But eventually, they're bound to overcome that fear. I have very little faith that Vault 13 will remained closed until 2277, as the experiment dictates."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:338
msgid "I'm afraid I have failed my duty as Overseer. I can only hope that the rest of the public Vaults involved in the Societal Preservation Program have been more successful. To my superiors, who I'm certain will one day read this: forgive me. And may God bless America."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:339
msgid "Search for any other files that contain information on \"Societal Preservation Program\"."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:350
msgid "After hours of scouring through the computer's archives, you're unable to find anything else that mentions the Societal Preservation Program. As you give up your search, you vow never again to waste so much time staring at a computer monitor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:360
msgid "After hours of scouring through the computer's archives, you're able to locate a few hidden documents concerning the Societal Preservation Program. As you read over them, you uncover a rather disturbing truth about the Vaults: they were never intended to save the population of the United States."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:362
msgid "Incredibly, all 122 of Vault-Tec's public Vaults were part of a grand social experiment orchestrated by the US government. Only 17 of those Vaults, dubbed \"control Vaults\", were designed to function correctly (it seems Vault 8 was one of the lucky few). The rest were meant to have various critical flaws, so that the government could study the pre-selected occupants, and see how they react to the stresses of their situations, and how well they're able to re-colonize once their Vaults open."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:364
msgid "It seems Vault 13's role in the experiment was to remain closed for 200 years to test the effects of prolonged isolation. Apparently, the breaking down of the water chip was un-intended, and forced the Overseer to improvise by selecting your grandfather to go out and fetch a new chip. After some more digging around, you manage to find descriptions of some of other Vault experiments."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:366
msgid "Vault 12's door was designed never to close, so that the assholes behind this experiment could \"study the effects of radiation on the selected population\". If you recall the legend correctly, Vault 12 was located under the ghoul filled city of Necropolis, where the Vault Dweller finally found the water chip. It seems quite likely that the ghouls were the result of this experiment."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:368
msgid "Vault 15, another key location in the Vault Dweller's quest, was to be populated by people with \"radically diverse ideologies\" that would be sealed in the Vault together for 50 years. Vault 27 was to be purposely overcrowded with 2,000 people -- double the maximum capacity. That couldn't have been pretty. Vault 29 was to be populated only by those under the age of sixteen, with their parents \"purposely redirected to other Vaults\"."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:370
msgid "Vault 34's experiment involved an armory overstocked with weapons and ammo, and, of course, not provided with a lock. How pleasant. Vault 36 suffered from food extruders that were designed to produce only \"a thin, watery gruel\", while Vault 42 was outfitted only with dim lighting--no light bulbs of over 40 watts were provided."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:372
msgid "Vault 53's equipment was designed to break down every few months. While repairable, the constant breakdowns were meant to test the stress of the inhabitants. You wonder how many expert mechanics and technicians that Vault produced. Vault 55 would have all its entertainment tapes removed, while Vault 56 would have all its entertainment tapes removed, with the exception of one featuring a particularly bad comic actor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:374
msgid "Vault 68 was to be occupied by 999 males and only one female. You can only imagine the horrors that took place there... Vault 69, on the other hand, was to be occupied by 999 females and only one male... interesting. Vault 70's jumpsuit extruders were designed to fail after 6 months. And finally, Vault 106 was designed so that 10 days after being sealed, it would begin \"releasing psychoactive drugs into the air filtration system\"."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:500
msgid "You learn about the Vault Experiments and the roles of the various Vaults."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:510
msgid "You learn about the history of Vault 13 and the Overseer's role in the Vault Experiments."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/oscomptr.msg:520
msgid "I'm sorry, I did not understand that."
msgstr ""

