msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:117
msgid "I'm Martin, over here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:118
msgid "Hey, you, I'm Frobisher. Here!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:119
msgid "Over heeeere!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:120
msgid "Helloooooo!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:121
msgid "Come here!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:122
msgid "I can tell you what you want to know."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:123
msgid "My name's Martin."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:125
msgid "Hello there, I'm Martin Frobisher. I speak for these people. Thank God you're here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:127
msgid "Nice outfits, just like mine. Who are you people?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:128
msgid "What are you people doing here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:129
msgid "Are you the Overseer?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:130
msgid "How did you people get here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:131
msgid "Nice to meet you Martin, but I've got people to free. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:132
msgid "Yes, I'd hoped that's why you were here. You've got to free us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:133
msgid "Free you? I was just going to free my tribe."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:134
msgid "Of course, I wouldn't let anyone stay trapped in this place."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:135
msgid "What are you people doing here anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:136
msgid "They're using us to test some sort of antidote for a fatal virus."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:137
msgid "What kind of virus?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:138
msgid "That doesn't sound good. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:139
msgid "Lucky you. Maybe now you know the pain my ancestor, the Vault Dweller, felt. I hope you all burn. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:140
msgid "They call it the FEV toxin. It does horrible things to people, before it kills them. The only *good* thing about it is that it kills so quickly. Sure looks painful though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:141
msgid "That sounds nasty. Why are they using your people for a test?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:142
msgid "They took us all from our vault because they wanted test subjects for the antidote. They needed people from outside the Enclave, and who were still pure-strain-humans. So they took us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:143
msgid "They took you? How, from where?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:144
msgid "They came to the front door of the vault. Somehow they already knew the security code. They just opened the door and their armored troopers marched us into vertibirds and flew us here. Then the experiments began. (He shudders.)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:145
msgid "That sounds bad. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:146
msgid "The vault? Which vault are you from?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:147
msgid "Why, Vault 13, of course."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:148
msgid "I went there looking for a GECK."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:149
msgid "I went there to ask for your GECK to save my people. But you were already gone. Only the GECK remained."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:150
msgid "I was looking for that. Hey, are you the Overseer?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:151
msgid "A GECK? We must have a couple of them. You're welcome to one. I think I saw some troopers loading one of our GECKs into a vertibird."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:152
msgid "You saw them load a GECK? Do you know where they put it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:153
msgid "That's okay. I already helped myself to a GECK from our vault. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:154
msgid "I don't know exactly where they put it but I did hear them say that they were going to leave it in the barrier level, just below this level, I think."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:155
msgid "That's great. Thanks. I better be going."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:156
msgid "Ah, I see. Let me ask you something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:157
msgid "Wait! You've got to get us out of this place."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:158
msgid "I plan to. I'm going downstairs to the power plant to shut the power off and free you. When the fields are down, run topside for the ship I've got there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:159
msgid "How can I do that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:160
msgid "You should have thought of that *before* you kicked my ancestor out of the vault. I hope you all rot here. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:161
msgid "Thank you. Godspeed and good luck to you friend."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:162
msgid "Goodbye and good luck to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:163
msgid "Thanks, but let me ask you something else first."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:164
msgid "I've got a feeling I'll need it. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:165
msgid "To turn off these forcefields, I think you're going to have to turn off the main power supply."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:166
msgid "How the heck am I going to manage that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:167
msgid "I've been listening and I think that the power reactor is controlled by a large computer three levels below us. If you manage to blow that up, it should turn off the power and we can go free."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:168
msgid "Great idea. I can use my explosives to blow up the computer. Then you can run topside to my ship. I'll be right behind you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:169
msgid "Great idea but I don't know how I can blow up the reactor. I don't have any explosives."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:170
msgid "I'm sure that wherever the guards have their barracks that they must have an arsenal. They'll have explosives there, I'm certain of it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:171
msgid "Good idea. I can get the explosives and use them to blow up the computer. Then you can run topside to my ship. I'll be right behind you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:172
msgid "We don't use that term anymore. There used to be an overseer, many years ago, but he did a bad thing and many of our people left the vault - only to die in the wastes, I'm sure. He was tried and sentenced to death for his crime. We haven't used the title since."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:173
msgid "I don't blame you. I understand that an overseer kicked my ancestor, the Vault Dweller, out into the wastes. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:174
msgid "The Vault Dweller? How long ago was that? Say, about eighty years perhaps?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:175
msgid "Yes, It was eighty years ago. How did you know that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:176
msgid "Eighty years ago, a hero saved our vault and then the Overseer exiled him. Others followed him into exile and they were never heard from again. We remember the event with shame."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:177
msgid "Hey! You're talking about *my* ancestor and the people who founded my village. They all came from the Vault of the Holy 13."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:178
msgid "As well you should. Let me ask you about something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:179
msgid "I don't think you've suffered enough for that yet. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:180
msgid "Incredible, that's our vault! Once again, the people of the vault must rely upon - uh, this time - the great grandson, of the Vault Dweller to save us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:181
msgid "Incredible, that's our vault! Once again, the people of the Vault must rely upon - uh, this time - the great granddaughter, of the Vault Dweller to save us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:182
msgid "I wish I knew how to save you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmartin.msg:184
msgid "What a bizarre coincidence! Let me ask you about something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:101
msgid "You see Tom Murray, the head of the Atomic Energy Commission."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:102
msgid "You see a very nervous old man in a pristine lab coat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:103
msgid "My machine! My beautiful machine gone. (Sob, sob.)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:104
msgid "We're doomed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:105
msgid "Without the computer online the reactor will meltdown!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:106
msgid "I can't even swim."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:107
msgid "Maybe I can fix it..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:108
msgid "What's the alarm ringing about?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:109 dialog/vcoldjoe.msg:124
msgid "What's going on here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:110
msgid "Don't panic, anyone. DON'T PANIC!!!!!!!!!!!!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:111
msgid "OK, stay calm. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:112
msgid "Maybe this is just a drill."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:113
msgid "Get back to the detention level."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:114
msgid "You really can tell the difference."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:115
msgid "Your forehead is quite beetling."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:116
msgid "Your cranial capacity isn't quite up to snuff is it?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:117
msgid "If you're good, I'll make sure you get a cracker when you get back to your cell."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:118
msgid "You there, you're not supposed to wear that stuff in here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:119
msgid "I'll wear my armor wherever I want to."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:120
msgid "Oh, sorry, sir. I'll be going then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:121
msgid "You will, huh? Well, I'll just have to report you then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:122
msgid "Go ahead. Make my day."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:123
msgid "Oh, please don't do that. I'm leaving now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:124
msgid "I'm Tom Murray, head of the Atomic Energy Commission. I control our atomic power plant here. Who the hell are you and what are you doing here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:125
msgid "What the hell do you want now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:126
msgid "I need to shut down your atomic reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:127
msgid "I was just curious as to how your reactor works."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:128
msgid "I need to exterminate you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:129
msgid "Help! Help me! Help!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:130
msgid "Intruders! Alert!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:131
msgid "Run for your lives! The primitives are loose!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:132
msgid "Guards! Heeeeeeelllllp!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:134
msgid "Shut it down? Are you crazed? You're not going to shut down *my* reactor."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:135
msgid "Yes, I am. You better tell me how, or I'll shut you down, permanently."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:136
msgid "Did I say shut down? I'm sorry, I just wanted to know how your reactor works."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:137
msgid "Oh, it's yours? I'm sorry, I didn't realize that. Well, Goodbye then."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:138
msgid "Here, I tell you what. I'll do it for you. But if you try to shut it down too fast it'll overheat."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:139
msgid "I don't care about that. Just shut down the reactor, or I'll gut you like a fish."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:140
msgid "That sounds dangerous. Well, OK, just forget it. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:141
msgid "You're bluffing. You wouldn't dare."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:142
msgid "Yes, I would. If you don't help me, you're a dead man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:143
msgid "I tried to let you cooperate, but you wouldn't do it. Oh well, can't let you sound the alarm. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:144
msgid "Hey, I was just kidding. How does your reactor work anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:145
msgid "Yeah, I guess you're right. You better just keep quiet for a while after I'm gone though. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:146
msgid "Okay, okay. I'll do it. Just take it easy now. But I'm telling you - it's going to overheat as soon as I put the containment rods down. If we perform a crash shutdown like this we'll have to scram the whole reactor-or we better learn to speak Chinese."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:147
msgid "Yeah, whatever. Just shut the damn thing down right now!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:148
msgid "That sounds dangerous. Maybe I better look for another way. I sure don't want to hurt anything here. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:149
msgid "I'm not going to risk the lives of everyone here. No way. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:150
msgid "I'm sorry to hear that. I guess I'll have to kill you then. Nothing personal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:151
msgid "How would that risk everyone's life? How does your reactor work anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:152
msgid "I guess I'll just have to find another way to shut down the power. You better not make any noise after I'm gone. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:153
msgid "You got it. Okay, uh, slide this to green. (He fiddles with a control panel for a few minutes while he mutters to himself.) Okay, you got it, but it sure isn't going to stay stable for very long."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:154
msgid "You did the right thing. Now, I've got to be going. You better just keep quiet in here for a while."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:155
msgid "Good job. Now, I've got to kill you. Sorry, but I can't leave any witnesses."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:156
msgid "I've got to be going. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:157
msgid "I don't control that much of the reactor's operation. The central computer just north of the reactor controls most of the power plant functions. If that weren't there, we'd have no power at all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:158
msgid "No power at all?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:159
msgid "Well, not enough for much. The lights, life-support, and defenses would work for a while but forcefields and other power intensive devices would be shut down immediately."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:160
msgid "Sounds as though you'd really be crippled."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:161
msgid "Well, it wouldn't be good. All kinds of watertight security doors close when that happens. No way in the world to open them once they're closed by the power shut-off. That's a safety feature."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:162
msgid "Interesting. There's something else I wanted to know though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:163
msgid "That's all I need to know. Thanks you've been a big help. You just better keep quiet after I leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcmurray.msg:164
msgid "Thanks. Too bad you won't live to see that. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:100
msgid "You see a somewhat plump, blonde secretary in a tight dress."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:101
msgid "You see the President's *personal* private secretary."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:102
msgid "You see a plump but not unattractive intern, uh, secretary. Her hair is a little mussed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:103
msgid "Yeah? Whatcha want, honey?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:104
msgid "Not again, I just cleaned my dress."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:105
msgid "So what's Mr. Important up to?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:106
msgid "They don't call him *Dick* Richardson for nuthin'."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:107
msgid "I do too know how to type."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:108
msgid "You oughta knock before barging in like that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:109
msgid "I need some mouthwash."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:110
msgid "Where's that washcloth?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:111
msgid "I think it's time for a raise."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:112
msgid "Do those Secret Service agents always have to hover like that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:113
msgid "Come back later. I'm gonna be busy in a minute here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:114
msgid "I don't think I'll wash this dress - it might come in handy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:115
msgid "The President says I kiss the best."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:116
msgid "You're not taping me, are you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcprssec.msg:117
msgid "Where are my kneepads? Heh, heh, just kidding."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcsecbot.msg:100
msgid "You see a security robot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcsecbot.msg:101
msgid "You see a heavily armed security robot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcsecbot.msg:102
msgid "It looks like one of these is more than enough to waste a squad."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcsecbot.msg:103
msgid "It does not respond to you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcwrkbot.msg:101
msgid "This robot appears to have been designed to carry heavy supplies and equipment around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcwrkbot.msg:200
msgid "Beep."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcwrkbot.msg:201
msgid "*Click*"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcwrkbot.msg:202
msgid "*Beeboop*"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qcwrkbot.msg:203
msgid "Proceed through work area with caution."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:100
msgid "You see a man in a suit. He's staring into space. Like he's lookin' at you but he ain't lookin' at you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:101
msgid "You see the head of the free world, the President of the United States."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:102
msgid "You see a thin, nervous, older man who looks as tired and frayed as the suit he's wearing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:103
msgctxt "prs1a"
msgid "You there, what are you doing outside of the reconditioning center?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:104
msgctxt "prs1b"
msgid "Do I know you? What project are you on?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:105
msgctxt "prs1c"
msgid "And who do you think you are barging into my office?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:109
msgctxt "prs2a"
msgid "Ah, affected by the test serums, I see. Um, I'll get you some help. Guards!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:110
msgctxt "prs2b"
msgid "Doctor, I think you've been exposed to the FEV. Poor soul, I'll get you some help. Guards!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:111
msgctxt "prs2c"
msgid "Now be a good mutant and stay put. Guards!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:113
msgid "Uh uh. Bye bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:114
msgid "Just wait right here. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:115
msgid "Uh, stay calm. Someone will be right along. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:116
msgid "Everything is fine."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:117
msgid "Damn it! Will somebody come and get this... person?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:118
msgid "Oh, guards! There's an idiot in my office... No, not the veep."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:119
msgctxt "prs4"
msgid "Hello, there. I'm President Richardson and I'm damn proud to meet you. Ah, Vault 13. You've been doing your country an invaluable service."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:120
msgid "President? Who are you anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:121
msgid "A service to my country? Just what's going on here anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:122
msgid "Uh, I guess I took a wrong turn on my way to the lab. Sorry, sir. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:123
msgctxt "prs5a"
msgid "Hello, doctor. Do you have a report? Good news, I hope. Our salvation is in your team's hands."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:124
msgctxt "prs5b"
msgid "You there, shouldn't you be working on the Project? Mankind's salvation depends on you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:126
msgid "Salvation? Just what's going on here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:127
msgid "Sorry, sir. Wrong turn on my way back to the lab. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:128
msgctxt "prs6"
msgid "Oh, that's quite all right. All those inoculation shots would disorient anyone."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:129
msgid "Inoculation shots? What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:130
msgid "I guess I do feel a bit groggy. But knowing that I'm helping my country makes it all seem worthwhile."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:131
msgid "You can say that again. Well, I better get going."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:132
msgctxt "prs7"
msgid "Let me get one of the Secret Service to escort you back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:133
msgid "That's kind of you but I think I can make it on my own. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:134
msgid "That would be nice of you. Thanks."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:135
msgctxt "prs8"
msgid "It's no problem at all. (talking to intercom) Hello. I could use a little assistance here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:136
msgid "Uh. Gee, thanks sir."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:137
msgid "You better not call your guards if you want to leave this room alive."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:138
msgctxt "prs9"
msgid "Ah... well. I'm sure we can work something out. What's on your mind?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:139 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:151
msgid "I want to know what's going on here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:140
msgid "I just want to leave quietly. Keep your hand off the alarm until I'm out of here. Or else...."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:141
msgid "I'm leaving here and taking you as a hostage to make sure my people get out safely."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:142
msgctxt "prs10"
msgid "Do you really think you can intimidate the President of the United States?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:144
msgid "Maybe not, but I suggest you stay out of my way until I leave."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:145
msgctxt "prs11a_a"
msgid "For your information, the guards have orders to shoot me rather than let anyone or anything endanger the Project. I... wouldn't be of any use as a hostage."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:146
msgctxt "prs11b"
msgid "You don't really expect that to work do you? Ha! If you try it, my guards have orders to shoot me rather than let anything, or anyone, endanger the Project. I'm staying right here. Now, are you going to shoot me or not?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:147
msgid "Maybe not, but I'm leaving. Don't touch that buzzer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:148
msgid "The Project? What Project?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:149
msgid "Yes, it will. I'll enjoy it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:150
msgctxt "prs12"
msgid "Uh, now, now, now. Now, let's... let's... Uh, Wh-wh-what is it you want, anyway?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:152
msgid "I want to know just who the hell you are."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:153
msgid "I want you dead."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:154
msgctxt "prs13"
msgid "Okay, okay, whatever you say. I'll just sit here quietly. It's, uh, nice to meet you. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:155
msgid "That's too easy. Before I go, I'd like to know just what you're doing here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:157
msgid "Nice to meet you, Mr. President. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:158
msgctxt "prs14"
msgid "Ahhh. Ahhh. Guards? Guards!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:159
msgid "Say goodnight, Mr. President."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:160
msgctxt "prs15"
msgid "I am the President of the United States of America. The Vice-President is in the office outside. If you belonged here you'd know that. Who are you and what are you doing here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:161
msgid "You're the President of what United States?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:162
msgid "You're a loony."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:163
msgid "Vice-President? You mean that drooling idiot next door?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:164
msgid "What a coincidence, I'm Emperor of the planet Quetzel, here for the surrender of Earth."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:165
msgid "I'll just let you get back to business Mr., uh, President. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:166
msgctxt "prs16"
msgid "Ah-ha. Oh, of course, your eminence. Why don't I just call for... some refreshments? We can talk and work things out - can't we all just get along?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:167
msgid "That sounds just grand."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:168
msgid "Nice try, Mr. President."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:169
msgctxt "prs17"
msgid "Uh, well, just one second. (into intercom) Ahh, I'd like refreshments for myself and an *unexpected guest*. A very important - unexpected - guest. Right away?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:170
msgid "Thanks. I guess you're not such a bad guy after all."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:171
msgid "That was stupid. Now someone's going to have to get hurt."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:172
msgctxt "prs18"
msgid "Somebody's loony here, all right. Oh yeah. Oooooh yeah."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:173
msgid "Don't look at me. I'm not claiming to be the President of a United States that fell long before either of us was born."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:174
msgctxt "prs19"
msgid "I am the elected representative of the people. The United States does still exist. God bless us, every one. We've just had to adapt in order to survive after the war."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:175
msgid "I don't understand. What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:176
msgctxt "prs20a"
msgid "You really don't know, do you? Let me tell you about mankind's salvation. A little history first..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:177
msgctxt "prs20b"
msgid "A, hmm, a little history...."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:178
msgid "Go on, Mr. President...."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:179
msgid "First, why do you have a base at Navarro?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:180
msgid "Before you get into that... I saw some of your vertibirds doing some trade with New Reno. What's that all about?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:181
msgid "I don't have time for this lunacy now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:182
msgctxt "prs21a"
msgid "Well, hello there. Glad to make time for one of our gallant troopers. But, I am rather busy. So, uh, what can the President of the United States of America do for you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:183
msgctxt "prs21b"
msgid "You're back? What is it you want?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:184
msgid "You can tell me just what's going on here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:185
msgid "I, uh, I'm just checking this area, sir. Security check. Yeah. Everything's fine here. Uh, goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:186
msgctxt "prs22a"
msgid "Hello. I'm the President of the United States of America, and you are...?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:187
msgctxt "prs22b"
msgid "Hello there. I'm the President of the United States of America and I must say I've seldom seen a stranger, or sorrier, delegation of misfits in all my life. Just who are you to barge in on me this way?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:188
msgid "I'm damn curious as to what's going on here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:189
msgid "I'm your executioner."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:190
msgid "The President? What are you talking about?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:191
msgid "I'm lost. I can see you're a busy man Mr. President. I'll just be leaving now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:192
msgctxt "prs23"
msgid "That's a shame. A conversation with a genuine mutant like you? It'd certainly paint me a picture of what life's like in that radioactive hell on the mainland."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:193
msgid "Mutant? Why are you calling me a mutant?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:194
msgid "Radioactive hell? You don't get out much, do you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:195
msgid "That's it. Enough talk. Time to die."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:196
msgid "Yeah, well, we all have to learn to live with disappointment. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:197
msgctxt "prs24"
msgid "There was a great war long before we were born. Our gallant soldiers fought from the Yukon to the Yangtze."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:198
msgid "Yeah, I knew about that part. Go on."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:199
msgctxt "prs26"
msgid "Vice-President Bird may look like a drooling idiot, but I'll have you know that man's a national hero."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:200
msgid "To you, probably."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:201
msgctxt "prs27"
msgid "He's one of the bravest men I know. He volunteered to try one of the early versions of the FEV toxin antidote. (sigh) Unfortunately, it didn't quite work out the way we'd hoped."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:202
msgid "You mean that wasn't what you'd hoped for?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:203
msgctxt "prs28"
msgid "It's tiny mocking minds like yours that prove the superiority of real humans over mutants."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:204
msgid "He's still a gibbering idiot."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:205
msgid "Why are you calling me a mutant?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:206
msgctxt "prs29"
msgid "He may yet come around. In fact, there may even be some unforeseen benefits. His spelling ability has actually improved."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:207
msgid "I'm happy for you. But why did you call me a mutant?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:208
msgctxt "prs30"
msgid "Because you are. Your tribe's DNA has changed since your ancestor left the vault. Unavoidable. All that background radiation you've been exposed to."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:209
msgid "OK, so I'm a mutant. Guess what smart guy, you're about to become a dead pure-strain human."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:210
msgid "So we're mutants. So what?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:211
msgid "Creatures change all the time. It's called evolution. Without that change you and I would still be two bits of protoplasmic goo."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:212
msgctxt "prs31"
msgid "We try to keep ourselves safe and secure from radiation. That's what separates humans - like me - from mutants like you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:214
msgid "Enough talk. Time for you to face that great electoral college in the sky."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:215
msgid "I've killed men for less than that. But I'm in a hurry today. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:216
msgctxt "prs32"
msgid "We were winning, too. And then those damn Reds launched. We barely got our birds up."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:217
msgid "Doesn't seem as though it helped us much."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:218
msgctxt "prs33"
msgid "Well, no it didn't. But at least it knocked the damn Red menace back into the stone age. (chuckles)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:219
msgid "And us with it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:220
msgctxt "prs34"
msgid "Well, no. No... not quite. You see, we had planned ahead. We were ready. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:222
msgctxt "prs35"
msgid "We had a number of sanctuaries that would enable the glorious American civilization to endure. This facility - the vaults - were part of the great plan."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:223
msgid "Those damn vaults didn't work the way they were supposed to. A lot of people in them died."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:224
msgctxt "prs36"
msgid "Actually, they worked almost exactly the way they were supposed to. You might call it a social experiment on a grand scale."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:225
msgid "An experiment?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:226
msgctxt "prs36a"
msgid "The vaults were set up to test humanity. Some had not enough food synthesizers, others had only men in them, yet others were designed to open after only 6 months. They each had a unique set of circumstances designed to test the occupants."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:227
msgid "What about Vault 13? What was its purpose?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:228
msgctxt "prs37"
msgid "Ahh. Vault 13 is a special case. It was supposed to remain closed until the subjects were needed. Vault 13 was, in scientific parlance, a control group."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:229
msgid "But they would all have died if my ancestor didn't get them a replacement water chip. That doesn't seem to fit in with your plan."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:230
msgctxt "prs38"
msgid "An unfortunate, and unforeseen accident. However, as it turns out a rather fortuitous one."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:232
msgctxt "prs39"
msgid "As it turns out we needed test subjects from untainted, pre-war, human stock - your ancestors in Vault 13 - and some freshly mutated stock - the villagers from Arroyo."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:234
msgctxt "prs39a"
msgid "For the Project. It's almost ready. Humanity's salvation is almost at hand and the United States of America will be the progenitor of that rebirth."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:235
msgid "Rebirth? What do you mean?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:236
msgctxt "prs40a"
msgid "The only way for true humans, and democracy, to be safe is to cleanse the mutants from the globe. We humans will take back that which is rightfully ours."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:237
msgctxt "prs40b"
msgid "The Project will cleanse all the mutants from our fair land - and the rest of the globe. Once again, America will be the world's policeman."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:238
msgid "I'm a true human, too."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:239
msgid "Cleanse the mutants? That sounds a bit drastic. How are you going to do that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:240
msgctxt "prs41"
msgid "We found a research facility in operational shape about 70 years ago. A former military base that had been used to research a special virus."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:241
msgid "A virus?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:242
msgctxt "prs42"
msgid "Yes, the FEV virus. It was originally developed to turn soldiers into super-warriors but it failed. The warriors were tough and strong, but far too stupid. However, our brilliant Chemical Corps altered it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:243
msgid "Altered the virus? Why?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:244
msgctxt "prs43"
msgid "To turn it into a staggeringly effective killer. Any humanoid that isn't inoculated against its effects before its release will die. That is the Project."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:245
msgid "That's insane."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:246
msgctxt "prs43a"
msgid "No, no. That's humanity's last, best, hope. That's what we've been working towards all these years."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:247
msgid "Great, so you have all this poison and no way to spread it around."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:248
msgctxt "prs44"
msgid "We've run short of certain critical chemicals. We can get them from the drug labs of New Reno. If the mutant-mobsters use our guns to kill each other, (snorts) just saves us the trouble."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:249
msgid "Everything works in your favor, huh? Tell me the rest of the story."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:250
msgctxt "prs45"
msgid "Simple. Navarro is an isolated base. Our vertibirds have a limited range. They refuel there."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:251
msgid "Makes sense."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:252
msgctxt "prs46a"
msgid "I'm sure you think so. But tests performed on your tribesmen have all shown that you are guilty of mutation. And it's a damn good thing the Project is ready."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:254
msgctxt "prs46b"
msgid "Some of the members of your tribe are showing some extremely interesting changes. If the danger to true humanity weren't so great I would think about studying them. But (sighs) that's not to be."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:255
msgid "Not to be? Why not?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:256
msgctxt "prs47"
msgid "Oh, but that's one of the advantages of the FEV virus. We can release it right here and the jet stream will carry it worldwide. It'll have plenty of time to cleanse every nook and cranny of the globe."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:257
msgid "OK. Then why did you have to kidnap my villagers and the people from Vault 13?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:258
msgctxt "prs48"
msgid "Test subjects. Your villagers are all descended from vault stock and we had to make sure that the FEV toxin was still effective. The subjects from Vault 13 test that and an inoculation against the FEV."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:259
msgid "You're not testing the inoculation on my people?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:260
msgctxt "prs48a"
msgid "It's hardly necessary. I'm sure we could and it would work, but there's no reason to do so."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:261
msgid "Did it ever occur to you that what you're doing is wrong?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:262
msgctxt "prs49"
msgid "Never. Part of the president's job is to make the tough decisions. A lot of near-humans will sacrifice their lives for the return of humanity. Humans will prevail."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:263
msgid "There's no way in hell that I can let you do this."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:264
msgid "Just because everyone out there doesn't have an exact copy of your DNA that doesn't give you a license to exterminate them."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:265
msgctxt "prs50"
msgid "You can't stop it. The tests are complete and the toxin is ready for release. In hours, your villagers will be the first to make the ultimate sacrifice. The other mutants will follow. An unfortunate footnote in the continuing history of the human race."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:266
msgid "Why don't we start that footnote off with your epitaph, Mr. President?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:267
msgctxt "prs51"
msgid "Oh, I don't relish this decision. If there was another way- but there isn't. No price is too high for the survival of the human race. If you were human, you'd feel the same way."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:268
msgid "You really believe that, don't you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:269
msgctxt "prs53"
msgid "Yes, I do. Even killing me won't help you. There's nothing you can do to stop the release."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:270
msgid "Maybe I'll just figure out a way to give you a taste of your own medicine."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:271
msgid "We'll just see about that. I've got things to do. Goodbye, President Richardson."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:272
msgid "I disagree, Mr. President. I think killing you will help. I'll feel a lot better."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:273
msgctxt "prs54"
msgid "You could try, I suppose, but soon the staff of the Enclave and Navarro will be inoculated."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:274
msgid "They aren't already?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:275
msgctxt "prs55"
msgid "We just have to distribute the supplies. A matter of hours. Besides, the Enclave is a sealed unit. No air or contaminants get in or get out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:276
msgid "We'll see. In the meantime, I'm taking you out of the picture, personally."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:277
msgctxt "prs56"
msgid "You might find that tougher than you think. If you do, I'll go to my reward knowing that I died a patriot and a servant of humanity."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:278
msgid "Time for your reward."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:279
msgid "Right now, I'll let you think about your coming death. Don't touch the alarm. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:280
msgctxt "prs57"
msgid "Very moving. But the radical changes your villagers and other mutants show is a far cry from the gradual changes of natural evolution."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:281
msgid "Maybe we're changing into a better version of the human race. Did you ever think of that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:282
msgctxt "prs58"
msgid "Very possible, indeed. In which case, our mission is even more vital to the survival of the human race. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:283
msgid "Huh? What do you mean by that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:284
msgctxt "prs59"
msgid "That's the spirit. God bless America. You should probably get back to your isolation ward now, though."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:285
msgid "Uh, yes, sir. Whatever you say, sir."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:286 dialog/qhprzrch.msg:290
msgid "Oh, I'll be able to find my own way back, sir. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:287
msgctxt "prs60"
msgid "Why, against the FEV toxin, of course. Damn brave sacrifice you and the other members of Vault 13 are making. On behalf of the United States government, and all humanity, I thank you. Now, we better get you back to your ward."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:288
msgid "FEV toxin? What the hell are you talking about? What's going on here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:289
msgid "Uh, yes sir. Whatever you say, sir."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:291
msgctxt "prs61"
msgid "So what? If your kind is allowed to flourish it'll mean the end of the human race as we know it. We can't allow radioactive freaks to squeeze humans into extinction."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:292
msgid "I think you're overestimating things a bit."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:293
msgctxt "prs62"
msgid "Not at all. Look to the future. Sure muties and men could get along for a while, but before you know it, the numeric pressure of your kind would tell. No, a line must be drawn in the sand - the buck stops here."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:294
msgid "What do you intend to do about this so called threat?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:295
msgid "I don't have time to listen to your bigoted, mad ravings. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:296
msgctxt "prs63"
msgid "The government of the United States of America has been working towards a solution for quite some time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:297
msgid "How so? What are you doing here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:298
msgctxt "prs64"
msgid "I assure you, I'm quite sane, as is everyone on the Project. We're dedicated to the salvation of the human race. You can call single-minded dedication to a cause madness, I suppose, but if so, it's divine madness."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:299
msgid "What are you talking about? What are you doing here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:300
msgid "How about my single-minded dedication to killing you right now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:301
msgid "You're mad. I don't have time for your lunacy right now. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:302
msgctxt "prs65"
msgid "I don't think this tired old Planet's big enough for two top dogs. If it's us or you.... Well, I'm going to choose us."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:303
msgid "I don't think you get to make that kind of choice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:304
msgctxt "prs66"
msgid "As the embodiment of the executive branch, I bear the burden of ensuring the survival and prosperity of the United States and of humanity itself. A heavy burden and yet if it means the return of the earth to our children and to their children, I bear it gladly."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:305
msgid "How do you intend to do that? What are you doing here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:306
msgid "Let me remove your burden. Permanently."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:307
msgid "It must be nice in your dimension. See you later, Mr. Nutcake."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:308 dialog/vclynett.msg:802
msgid "To the North"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:309 dialog/vclynett.msg:806
msgid "To the Northwest"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:310 dialog/vclynett.msg:805
msgid "To the West"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:311 dialog/vclynett.msg:808
msgid "To the Southwest"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:312 dialog/vclynett.msg:803
msgid "To the South"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:313 dialog/vclynett.msg:809
msgid "To the Southeast"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:314
msgid "To the East of here"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:315 dialog/vclynett.msg:807
msgid "To the Northeast"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:318
msgid "Ouch"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:319
msgid "(cry of pain)"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:320
msgid "Why are you talking to me like that?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:322
msgid "You're not very nice."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:323
msgid "Thank-you. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:328
msgid "You people are crazy."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qhprzrch.msg:338
msgid "Actually, Mr. President, I'm back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qibstdr1.msg:100
msgid "There is no apparent locking mechanism on the door."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qibstdr1.msg:101
msgid ""
"It does not appear as though conventional explosives will open\n"
" these doors."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qibstdr1.msg:102
msgid ""
"You see sturdy blast doors. They seem to meld into the floor and\n"
" ceiling."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qibstdr1.msg:103
msgid "You see no way in which to open the door."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qienddor.msg:100
msgid "You see no way in which you could open the door."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:101
msgid "This computer appears to control the nuclear bombing sitting nearby."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:200
msgid "Welcome to PoseidoNet. This terminal controls the operations of the MK-17 Fusion Bomb. Current Status of bomb is: Deactivated."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:201 dialog/qinuke.msg:226
msgid "Activate bomb."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:210
msgid ""
"Activation of the bomb requires two forms of security overrides. Override 1: Red Reactor Keycard, given only to\n"
" top U.S. Research officials. Override 2: Presidential Security Passkey, given only to the President of the United States."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:220
msgid "Looks like I don't have all of these keycards."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:221
msgid "Insert Red Reactor Keycard."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:222
msgid "Keycard accepted. Security override 1 complete. Level 2 Security still activated."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:223
msgid "Insert Presidential Security Passkey."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:224
msgid "Looks like I am still missing a keycard."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:225
msgid "Keycard accepted. Security override 2 complete."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:228
msgid ""
"Bomb has been activated and will detonate in T-minus 5 min. Error in countdown procedure. Countdown restated at\n"
" T-minus 5 seconds. Please make sure you are at least 80 miles from the blast area. Have a great day."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qinuke.msg:229
msgid "Mother of God..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qipzldor.msg:100
msgid "You see a tightly sealed door."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qipzldor.msg:101
msgid ""
"This door appears to be electro-magnetically sealed. Perhaps you can open it\n"
" elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qipzldor.msg:105
msgid "You temporarily bypass the electric field."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qipzldor.msg:106
msgid " temporarily bypasses the electric field."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qipzldor.msg:110
msgid "You fail miserably on disarming the electric field."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qipzldor.msg:111
msgid " fails miserably on disarming the electric field."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qipzldor.msg:115
msgid "You fail on disarming the electric field."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qipzldor.msg:116
msgid " fails on disarming the electric field."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/qipzldor.msg:120
msgid "You encounter an electric field."
