msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:267
msgid "A delightful place, really. Killers, thieves... the usual Outsider scum. A place where one such as yourself would feel right at home."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:272
msgid "Thought I'd ask anyway. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:273
msgid "*Thanks.* Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:274
msgid "Broken Hills is a mining town to the south. As I understand it, mutants mine the uranium, and they ship it here by caravan."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:275
msgid "They seem a bit shifty, but nice enough... well, nice enough for Outsiders, anyway. No offense."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:276
msgid "Out of curiosity, how much do you pay for your uranium?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:279
msgid "Uh, yeah... look, I had some other questions for you..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:280
msgid "None taken. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:281
msgid "It's a mining town far to the west. The caravans from there were the most pleasant to deal with, but recently the shipments of ore have slowed considerably. It has us a bit worried... we depend on their ore a great deal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:282
msgid "I know why the shipments from Redding have slowed."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:287
msgid "You have? This is excellent news! Please go tell Councilor McClure right away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:288
msgid "You have? That is excellent news! Let me give you a Day Pass so you can speak with Councilor McClure. The pass is only good during the day; at night you will be asked to leave. Now go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:291
msgid "I'll go speak to him at once."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:292
msgid ""
"Funny you should mention that. The price has been going up of late... nothing we can't afford,\n"
" mind you. We're certainly getting a better deal than Gecko. Those filthy scavengers need the uranium\n"
" much more than we do."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:296
msgid "Hmmm. Interesting. Thanks for the information."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:297
msgid "Our First Citizen is Joanne Lynette. She has done many good things for our city in her ten years of service."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:299
msgid ""
"She has kept our city untainted by the outside world. Even with NCR pressuring us to join the\n"
" Republic and the raider attacks, she has kept our city strong. Now there are the troubles with Gecko...."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:300
msgid "What is the NCR?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:302
msgid "What is the problem with Gecko?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:304
msgid "Sorry to hear it. Maybe I can hear more about it some other time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:305
msgid ""
"NCR is the \"New California Republic.\" They claim they are attempting to unify all of California\n"
" under one Government, but we can see right through their pathetic ruse."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:306
msgid "\"Ruse?\" Is that some weapon that NCR h--?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:307
msgid "Ruse? Are you sure?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:308
msgid ""
"Even if they were sincere, why would we want to share our resources with the cutthroats\n"
" and thieves that live outside these walls? I think *not.*"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:309
msgid "I see. What were you saying about raiders before?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:310 dialog/vcwalace.msg:317
msgid "What troubles is Vault City having with Gecko?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:312
msgid "That's a little more than I needed to know. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:313
msgid ""
"Recently we have experienced a rash of particularly brutal raider attacks. We have had attacks in\n"
" the past, but nothing like this. I fear these raiders might eventually breach our laser turret defenses."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:314
msgid "You won't have to worry about those raiders anymore. I wiped them out."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:315
msgid "Can you tell me anything else about these raiders?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:316
msgid "Uh, sorry to hear it. What was that you said about the NCR?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:318
msgid "They sound like a real problem. I wish you luck."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:319
msgid ""
"Not much. We can't seem to find where they are striking from. Our Citizen Sergeant Stark\n"
" may know more, but he's in the Corrections Center inside the city."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:320
msgid "If I track down these raiders, will you let me in the City?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:322
msgid "I'll go see what I can find out about these raiders."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:324
msgid "Certainly. If you can find the raiders base camp, I'll grant you a Day Pass."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:325
msgid "I'll see what I can do. But first, I had some other questions..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:326
msgid "It's a deal. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:327
msgid "You have? That is excellent news! Please go tell the First Citizen right away."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:328
msgid ""
"You have? That is excellent news! Let me give you a Day Pass so you can tell the First Citizen.\n"
" Here you go. The pass is only good during the day; at night you will be asked to leave. Now go."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:329
msgid "Before I leave, can I ask you another question?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:330
msgid "I'll go do that."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:332
msgid "Oh, uh, that's not my place to say. You'd have to speak with the First Citizen about such matters."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:333
msgid "What were you saying about NCR?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:334
msgid "What were you saying about raiders?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:335
msgid "Uh, okay... can I ask you some other questions?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:337
msgid ""
"A GECK? Well, that means nothing to me... and if means nothing to me, it will certainly mean\n"
" nothing to the First Citizen. Now was THAT what you wished to see the First Citizen about or\n"
" was it something else?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:338
msgid "I'm looking for a GECK to save my village."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:339
msgid "Look, let me in now, and I'll let you keep breathing. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:340
msgid "Nevermind. Maybe we'll talk later."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:341
msgid "Thank you for your assistance, Outsider."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:342
msgid "Well, as promised, here is your Day Pass... but you step out of line, I'll have it revoked. You hear me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:343
msgid "Oh, uh... well, I am a merchant. I had planned on trading with the other merchants in the city. Can I get a Day Pass from you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:344
msgid "You are a merchant? Really. And what would you happen to be selling? Ore? Some of those filthy wasteland lizard skins? "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:345
msgid "(Glances at your companion.) Or are you looking to sell some Servants?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:346
msgid "Yes, I am looking to sell some Servants in the City."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:347
msgid "I'm selling some of those... uh... filthy Gecko pelts."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:348
msgid "Actually, I have some fine Golden Gecko pelts with me. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:349
msgid "I'm selling some gold ore."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:350
msgid "I'm selling some uranium ore."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:351
msgid "I don't have any of those things... yet. Maybe I'll be back."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:352
msgid "Actually, I misspoke. Sorry to bother you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:353
msgid "Hmmmm. Well, let's see what you have. Once I inspect your stock, I can process the paperwork for your Day Pass. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:354
msgid "All right. Uh, all I have is a sample of my stock here. The rest is in... uh, my caravan. Outside the city. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:355
msgid "Hmmmm. Very well."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:356
msgid "Well, this sample is adequate."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:357
msgid ""
"There IS a Day Pass fee for merchants, five hundred dollars. That includes full daytime trading privileges within\n"
" Vault City walls and is good for up to five years after its issue date."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:358
msgid "All right. I'll take it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:359
msgid "Hmmm... That's a little steep. I'll pass for now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:360
msgid "Five hundred's a little more than I can afford right now. Maybe some other time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:361
msgid "Excellent. Here you go... again, it is only good during the day - at night you will be asked to leave the city. Citizens also reserve the right to cancel the Day Pass privileges at any time, so behave yourself."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:1255
msgid "I found the raiders' camp and convinced their guide to not help them. They won't be able to find their way without him."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vcwalace.msg:1314
msgid "You won't have to worry about those raiders anymore. I convinced their guide to leave and without his help, they will never find their way through the mountains."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vialocom.msg:100 dialog/vialocom.msg:102
msgid "A computer terminal, displaying various bits of data."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vialocom.msg:101
msgid "You see a terminal. "
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vialocom.msg:103 dialog/vialocom.msg:105
msgid "You see the Vault City Allocation Computer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vialocom.msg:106
msgid "This is the computer the Pip-Boy said to use."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vialocom.msg:108
msgid "With the help of the information on your Pip-Boy, you access the computer."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vialocom.msg:109
msgid "Whoa."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vialocom.msg:110
msgid "You have learned TONS of information about Fallout 2."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/viautdoc.msg:100 dialog/viautdoc.msg:102 dialog/viautdoc.msg:105
msgid "You see an Auto-Doc."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/viautdoc.msg:101 dialog/viautdoc.msg:103
msgid "You see an ancient-looking Auto-Doc. Despite its age, you have managed to coax it back into working order."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/viautdoc.msg:104 dialog/viautdoc.msg:106
msgid "You see an ancient-looking Auto-Doc. It is clicking and whirring unhealthily, and a great deal of heat is emanating from it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/viautdoc.msg:107
msgid "This ancient Auto-Doc looks badly in need of repair. It looks several decades past its scheduled maintenance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/viautdoc.msg:108
msgid "The damage wasn't as bad as it seemed. Some interior cables needed to be replaced and the diagnostic board cleaned. No problem."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/viautdoc.msg:109
msgid "You examine the Auto-Doc, but you can't seem to figure out the problem."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/viautdoc.msg:110
msgid "You have already fixed the Auto-Doc. It is running smoothly. You think."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:100
msgid "You see the caravan master."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:101
msgid "You see Mr. Baron, the master of this caravan."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:200
msgid "Hello Traveler, name's Robert Baron, master of this here caravan. Are you looking to make a trade?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:201
msgid "Sure. Let's see what you've got."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:202
msgid "Actually, I wanted to speak with you on behalf of a nearby village."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:203 dialog/vibaron.msg:222
msgid "Nope. I'll be on my way now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:204
msgid "Robert Baron, huh? Ever think about going by Bobby Baron? That's got a nice bounce to it, don't you think?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:210
msgid "I think your mom might've bounced you on your head a couple times. Now, do you want to trade, or not? I'm a busy man."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:220
msgid "Alright. Anything else?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:221
msgid "Yes actually, I wanted to speak with you on behalf of a nearby village."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:230
msgid "[He furrows his brow.] Village? Not sure what your--oh! Are you talking about that rat infested little shit-hole down the way?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:231
msgid "Uh, maybe."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:233
msgid "It's not a shit-hole. They're a struggling community that's making some real progress."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:240
msgid "Look, I already met with them, and I'm going to tell you the same thing I told them. They're simply too small for me to bother with. Besides, that place is fetid as all hell."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:241
msgid "Alright. I gave it a shot. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:242
msgid "Oh, come on, it's not that far out of your way. You pretty much pass right by it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:243 dialog/vibaron.msg:262 dialog/vibaron.msg:282
msgid "Is there *any* way I could get you to change your mind?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:250
msgid "Now what? If you're not going to trade, then stop wasting my fucking time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:252
msgid "Sorry, I'll go now."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:253
msgid "I think I'll waste *you* asshole."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:254
msgid "Is there *any* way I could get you to change your mind about trading with the village?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:260
msgid "So what if I do? I don't care if it's only a *minute* out of my way, it's just not worth the hassle."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:261 dialog/vibaron.msg:281
msgid "Alright. I see it's useless to reason with you. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:263
msgid "That's too bad, because a smart merchant would jump on this opportunity. But hey, if you're not interested, I suppose I'll have to go elsewhere..."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:270
msgid "Now just hold on a moment. I didn't say for certain that I wasn't interested. What's this opportunity you speak of?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:271
msgid "You see, that village might not be much to look at now, but I've got some insider information that all but guarantees that place is going to be the new hot spot. Trust me, it's going to be booming in the coming years. So if I were you, I'd want to build up relations now, before they get too big and you miss your chance."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:280
msgid "Haha! You expect me to believe that shit-hole is going to turn into something worthwhile? I think I'm about done wasting my time with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:290
msgid "You're not kidding, are you? Hmm, I suppose it couldn't hurt to take a little detour over there now and then. Hell, it's hardly even out of my way. Thanks for the tip, friend."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:291
msgid "No problem. See ya."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:300
msgid "[He seems to consider your question.] Perhaps . . . exactly what are we talking here?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:301 dialog/vibaron.msg:371
msgid "You make that village a regular stop on your route, and in return, I'll pay you $500."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:302 dialog/vibaron.msg:372
msgid "You make that village a regular stop on your route, and in return, I'll do my part to ensure nothing \"unfortunate\" happens to your caravan."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:303
msgid "You make that village a regular stop on your route, and in return, I'll show you a good time you'll never forget."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:304
msgid "You make that village a regular stop on your route, and in return, my wife here will show you a good time you'll never forget."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:305
msgid "Actually, never mind. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:310
msgid "Now you're speaking my language! Alright, it's a deal. [He greedily snatches the money from you and shakes your hand.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:320
msgid "$500? Not worth it. Make it $1,000 and you've got a deal."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:321
msgid "I don't have that much. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:322
msgid "Alright, fine. $1,000 it is."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:323
msgid "No deal. Goodbye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:330
msgid "Now you're speaking my language! You've got yourself a deal. [He greedily snatches the money from you and shakes your hand.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:340
msgid "Are you threatening me? No one threatens me and lives! (to his caravan guards) Kill this stupid fuck!"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:350
msgid "Look, I don't want any trouble. If you want me to swing by and trade with that village, fine, no big deal. Hell, it's hardly even out of my way. No problem."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:351
msgid "I'm glad we have an understanding. I'll be watching you. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:352
msgid "You better hope there's not a problem. Cause if there is, I'll solve it. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:353
msgid "[Glare at him intently for a moment, then slowly walk away.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:360
msgid "Ugh! God no! I'd rather fuck a brahmin. Now get out of here and stop wasting my time."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:361
msgid "Fuck you, asshole! [Attack.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:362
msgid "Fine, but you could've just said no. No need to be a jerk about it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:363
msgid "You don't know what you're missing."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:364
msgid "[Bury your ugly face in your hands and run away crying.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:370
msgid "Eh, sorry girl. I'm just not in the mood right now. You got anything else to offer?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:380
msgid "[He looks you up and down, then grins.] I think you've got yourself a deal. Do you take it in the backdoor?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:381
msgid "Baby, I take it any way you want to give it."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:382
msgid "You'll just have to find out, won't you?"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:383
msgid "Ugh! Hell no! Now let's hurry up and get this over with before I puke."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:390
msgid "[The merchant grins at you as he refastens his belt.] Holy shit, you sure know how to drive a good bargain. If you ever need to talk a merchant into doing something else, you make sure and look me up. Now, I should really be going. It was a pleasure doing business with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:391
msgid "[Shudder.] Once was enough. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:392 dialog/vibaron.msg:412
msgid "Anytime. Bye."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:400
msgid "[He looks Miria up and down, then grins.] I think you've got yourself a deal. [He shakes your hand, then puts his arm around Miria and walks her to someplace more private.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:401
msgid "[Tap your foot while you wait.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:402
msgid "[Whistle while you wait.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:403
msgid "[Check your weapons while you wait.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:404
msgid "[Stand there silently and make awkward eye contact with the caravan guards while you listen to the sounds of your wife being defiled by the merchant master.]"
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:410
msgid "[An hour later, you see Robert Baron and Miria, now sweaty and disheveled from their sexual romp, walking back towards you. You notice Miria is walking with a slight limp. The merchant grins at you as he refastens his belt.] Holy shit, you sure know how to drive a good bargain. If you ever need to talk a merchant into doing something else, you make sure and look me up. Now, I should really be going. It was a pleasure doing business with you."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:500
msgid "You convince the merchant to add the village to his trade route."
msgstr ""

#: dialog/vibaron.msg:510
msgid "You kill the merchant, thus ensuring that the village won't be able to trade."
msgstr ""

